{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-232","properties":{"name":"Brooklyn, NY","date":"2006-02-24","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 305","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":19.920167922973633,"median_income_tract":51696,"summary":"Feb 24, 2006: 4 killed, 1 injured. Brooklyn, NY.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nArson trapped a mother and her two kids in an apartment building. Another woman died jumping from the fourth floor. Six years later, prosecutors charged Samuel Martinez with murder. In 2014, the charges were dismissed.\nCensus Tract 305 (ACS 2006-2010): 19.9% in poverty, median household income $51,696, 22.5% white, 53.7% Black, 15.5% Hispanic/Latino, 9.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"New York - Presbyterian Brooklyn Methodist Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.08,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.29,"nearest_level1_center":"Kings County Hospital Center","nearest_level1_km":2.81,"nearest_level1_miles":1.75,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.959496,40.679249]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-95","properties":{"name":"Detroit, MI","date":"2006-03-15","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Shelter/Drug house","tract":"Census Tract 5351","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":26.83289909362793,"median_income_tract":32120,"summary":"Mar 15, 2006: 4 killed. Detroit, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Shelter/Drug house · Offenders: 1\nFour Detroit residents, including a pregnant woman, were found shot at a vacant city-owned house that had been raided repeatedly as a drug den. No arrests have been made.\nCensus Tract 5351 (ACS 2006-2010): 26.8% in poverty, median household income $32,120, 2.0% white, 97.8% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 15.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sinai Grace Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":5.66,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.52,"nearest_level1_center":"Henry Ford Hospital","nearest_level1_km":7.16,"nearest_level1_miles":4.45,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.171928,42.368149]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-162","properties":{"name":"Cumming, GA","date":"2006-03-19","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1305.10","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":7.217939853668213,"median_income_tract":93333,"summary":"Mar 19, 2006: 4 killed, 3 injured. Cumming, GA.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 3\nSeven people were shot or stabbed in a Forsyth County farmhouse. Four died. Convicted: Jason McGhee, sentenced to life without parole; and Frank Ortegon, sentenced to 20 years in prison.  Marcin W. Sosniak was sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 1305.10 (ACS 2006-2010): 7.2% in poverty, median household income $93,333, 81.6% white, 4.1% Black, 7.9% Hispanic/Latino, 5.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Wellstar North Fulton Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":17.14,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.65,"nearest_level1_center":"Wellstar Atlanta Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":47.46,"nearest_level1_miles":29.49,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.17057,34.15522]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-96","properties":{"name":"Seattle, WA","date":"2006-03-25","killed":6,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Shelter/Drug house","tract":"Census Tract 81","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":39.25925827026367,"median_income_tract":33592,"summary":"Mar 25, 2006: 6 killed, 2 injured. Seattle, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: Shelter/Drug house · Offenders: 1\nKyle Aaron Huff, 28, attended a Seattle rave and an after-party at a house, then left. He returned with a handgun and a shotgun that he used to kill six people before killing himself. He left an assault rifle in his car.\nCensus Tract 81 (ACS 2006-2010): 39.3% in poverty, median household income $33,592, 65.9% white, 11.1% Black, 4.2% Hispanic/Latino, 17.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.66,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.41,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":0.66,"nearest_level1_miles":0.41,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.332069,47.606209]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-94","properties":{"name":"Cleveland, OH","date":"2006-04-04","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1187","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":48.29812240600586,"median_income_tract":15246,"summary":"Apr 4, 2006: 4 killed. Cleveland, OH.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nFour children--ages 3 to 8--died in a Cleveland house fire set by a man who was angry at their mother, a former girlfriend. Lorenzo Collins, 42, was sentenced to 111 years in prison. Collins Bennett, 39, his accomplice, also was convicted and given a 16-\nCensus Tract 1187 (ACS 2006-2010): 48.3% in poverty, median household income $15,246, 48.0% white, 31.4% Black, 3.2% Hispanic/Latino, 18.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Hospitals Cleveland Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.36,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.84,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospitals Cleveland Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.36,"nearest_level1_miles":0.84,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.615425,41.515614]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-102","properties":{"name":"Modest, VA","date":"2006-04-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 904","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":14.480488777160645,"median_income_tract":40412,"summary":"Apr 7, 2006: 4 killed. Modest, VA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAfter smoking crack, Ronald Shrieves, 32, stabbed his parents and a niece and nephew in Modest Town, VA. He pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life in prison without the possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 904 (ACS 2006-2010): 14.5% in poverty, median household income $40,412, 34.0% white, 41.8% Black, 23.0% Hispanic/Latino, 14.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Tidalhealth Peninsula Regional, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":61.14,"nearest_trauma_miles":37.99,"nearest_level1_center":"Children'S Hospital Of The King'S Daughters","nearest_level1_km":124.14,"nearest_level1_miles":77.14,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.564926,37.812904]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-106","properties":{"name":"Leola, PA","date":"2006-04-12","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Strangulation","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 131.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":7.841484069824219,"median_income_tract":59125,"summary":"Apr 12, 2006: 6 killed. Leola, PA.\nCause: Blunt force, Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJesse Wise, 21, beat and strangled his grandmother, an uncle, two aunts and two cousins. Surviving relatives asked prosecutors not to seek the death penalty. Wise was sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 131.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 7.8% in poverty, median household income $59,125, 91.5% white, 0.0% Black, 2.5% Hispanic/Latino, 5.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Lancaster General Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":11.1,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.89,"nearest_level1_center":"The Lancaster General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":11.1,"nearest_level1_miles":6.89,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.184952,40.087875]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-199","properties":{"name":"St. Louis, MO","date":"2006-04-18","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 1256","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":11.617217063903809,"median_income_tract":45870,"summary":"Apr 18, 2006: 4 killed, 1 injured. St. Louis, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nUpset over payroll deductions for child support, Herbert Chalmers Jr. 54, killed his ex-wife and an ex-girlfriend. He took a bus to the caterer where he was considered a good worker and killed the co-owner, her daughter and himself.\nCensus Tract 1256 (ACS 2006-2010): 11.6% in poverty, median household income $45,870, 59.8% white, 35.1% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 24.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ssm Health Saint Louis University Hosp","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.58,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.22,"nearest_level1_center":"Ssm Health Saint Louis University Hosp","nearest_level1_km":3.58,"nearest_level1_miles":2.22,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.197891,38.627274]}}
