{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-103","properties":{"name":"Baton Rouge, LA","date":"2006-05-21","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"House of worship","tract":"Census Tract 7.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":20.321081161499023,"median_income_tract":31319,"summary":"May 21, 2006: 5 killed, 1 injured. Baton Rouge, LA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: House of worship · Offenders: 1\nAt his Baton Rouge, LA, church, Anthony Bell, 25, opened fire, killing four. He fled with his family at gunpoint. He killed his wife but released their three kids unharmed. He was sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 7.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 20.3% in poverty, median household income $31,319, 9.8% white, 84.6% Black, 1.6% Hispanic/Latino, 9.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Our Lady Of The Lake Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":9.55,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.93,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_level1_km":116.38,"nearest_level1_miles":72.31,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-91.128212,30.487511]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-104","properties":{"name":"Berlin, CT","date":"2006-05-27","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Vehicle crash","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 4001","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":3.797128677368164,"median_income_tract":84469,"summary":"May 27, 2006: 5 killed. Berlin, CT.\nCause: Vehicle crash · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nA woman driver was pursued by her ex-boyfriend and father of her child at speeds up to 120 mph. A crash killed her and four co-workers. Kevin Cales, 32, was convicted of the crime and was sentenced to 79 years in prison. Less than two months later, Cales\nCensus Tract 4001 (ACS 2006-2010): 3.8% in poverty, median household income $84,469, 88.4% white, 2.6% Black, 1.6% Hispanic/Latino, 1.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Connecticut Children'S Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":15.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.71,"nearest_level1_center":"Hartford Hospital","nearest_level1_km":15.68,"nearest_level1_miles":9.74,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-72.745651,41.621487]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-121","properties":{"name":"Hoschton, GA","date":"2006-05-30","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns, Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 101.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":4.709418773651123,"median_income_tract":67308,"summary":"May 30, 2006: 4 killed. Hoschton, GA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nHenry Lee Stringer, 34, torched a house, killing his two young kids. Firefighters also found their mother and grandmother fatally stabbed. He accepted life in prison without a chance for parole to avoid the death penalty but offered no explanation.\nCensus Tract 101.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 4.7% in poverty, median household income $67,308, 88.3% white, 1.7% Black, 4.7% Hispanic/Latino, 4.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Northeast Georgia Medical Center, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":23.57,"nearest_trauma_miles":14.65,"nearest_level1_center":"Wellstar Atlanta Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":67.56,"nearest_level1_miles":41.98,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.761284,34.096497]}}
