{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-110","properties":{"name":"Gustine, CA","date":"2006-07-04","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 20","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":18.39606475830078,"median_income_tract":42283,"summary":"Jul 4, 2006: 4 killed. Gustine, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTrevor Branscum, 38, had been drinking and argued with his wife at a market. Later that night, with his blood-alcohol level four times the legal limit for driving, he shot their four children with a rifle before killing himself.\nCensus Tract 20 (ACS 2006-2010): 18.4% in poverty, median household income $42,283, 45.4% white, 0.6% Black, 52.3% Hispanic/Latino, 12.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Doctors Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":45.3,"nearest_trauma_miles":28.15,"nearest_level1_center":"Santa Clara Valley Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":82.87,"nearest_level1_miles":51.49,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-120.998817,37.257717]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-112","properties":{"name":"Kirkland, WA","date":"2006-07-17","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 224","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":5.9754204750061035,"median_income_tract":101027,"summary":"Jul 17, 2006: 4 killed. Kirkland, WA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nConner Schierman, 24, entered a neighbor's house while the man was deployed with the Army National Guard in Iraq. He fatally stabbed the man's wife, two young sons and sister-in-law. He bought gasoline and torched the house. He received a death sentence.\nCensus Tract 224 (ACS 2006-2010): 6.0% in poverty, median household income $101,027, 84.1% white, 0.8% Black, 6.1% Hispanic/Latino, 9.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Evergreenhealth Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":4.45,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.76,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":12.21,"nearest_level1_miles":7.59,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.208733,47.681488]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-91","properties":{"name":"New Orleans, LA","date":"2006-07-24","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 44.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":54.80690383911133,"median_income_tract":21384,"summary":"Jul 24, 2006: 4 killed. New Orleans, LA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nThree brothers and a friend were gunned down on a porch in New Orleans. Two brothers were charged. One was tried but not convicted. The other, Raymond Amison, agreed to a 10-year sentence to avoid the possibility of the death penalty.\nCensus Tract 44.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 54.8% in poverty, median household income $21,384, 2.6% white, 97.4% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 41.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.02,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.63,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_level1_km":1.02,"nearest_level1_miles":0.63,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.072884,29.964895]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-90","properties":{"name":"Fresno, CA","date":"2006-08-23","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 14.10","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":23.703794479370117,"median_income_tract":49090,"summary":"Aug 23, 2006: 4 killed. Fresno, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nFour bodies -- three men and a woman -- were found in a Jeep in a Fresno residential neighborhood. They were bound with duct tape and cable ties. Police said they probably were involved in the illegal drug trade. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 14.10 (ACS 2006-2010): 23.7% in poverty, median household income $49,090, 13.9% white, 4.0% Black, 53.9% Hispanic/Latino, 8.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Community Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.25,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.26,"nearest_level1_center":"Community Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.25,"nearest_level1_miles":3.26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.734314,36.72023]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-89","properties":{"name":"North Charleston, SC","date":"2006-09-30","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 55","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":50.280025482177734,"median_income_tract":17702,"summary":"Sep 30, 2006: 5 killed. North Charleston, SC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMichael Simmons has been confined indefinitely to a state mental hospital. The bodies of his wife and her four children were found by a woman visiting their home. Simmons previously had served time in prison for robbing and beating a disabled man.\nCensus Tract 55 (ACS 2006-2010): 50.3% in poverty, median household income $17,702, 19.4% white, 74.5% Black, 0.5% Hispanic/Latino, 15.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Musc Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":8.05,"nearest_trauma_miles":5,"nearest_level1_center":"Musc Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":8.05,"nearest_level1_miles":5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.974808,32.854618]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-113","properties":{"name":"Nickel Mines, PA","date":"2006-10-02","killed":5,"injured":5,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"School","tract":"Census Tract 143","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":10.089262008666992,"median_income_tract":54910,"summary":"Oct 2, 2006: 5 killed, 5 injured. Nickel Mines, PA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: School · Offenders: 1\nCharles Roberts IV, 32, entered a schoolhouse in an Amish hamlet, dismissed the boys and bound the girls. He carried three guns, a stun gun, two knives, a hammer, 600 rounds. He shot 10, five fatally, before killing himself as police closed in.\nCensus Tract 143 (ACS 2006-2010): 10.1% in poverty, median household income $54,910, 95.3% white, 0.7% Black, 2.9% Hispanic/Latino, 4.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Lancaster General Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":21.42,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.31,"nearest_level1_center":"The Lancaster General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":21.42,"nearest_level1_miles":13.31,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.080414,39.959198]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-108","properties":{"name":"Winchester, VA","date":"2006-10-05","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 505","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":12.33806324005127,"median_income_tract":65259,"summary":"Oct 5, 2006: 4 killed. Winchester, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA mother, 19, her son, 2, her nephew, 17, and her father, 60, were found shot at their home outside Winchester, VA. Her former boyfriend, Jessi A. Jephson, 20, was found guilty and sentenced to life in prison without possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 505 (ACS 2006-2010): 12.3% in poverty, median household income $65,259, 96.5% white, 0.4% Black, 0.5% Hispanic/Latino, 1.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Valley Health Winchester Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":5.47,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.4,"nearest_level1_center":"Inova Fairfax Hospital","nearest_level1_km":96.86,"nearest_level1_miles":60.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-78.249725,39.21677]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-87","properties":{"name":"Louisville, KY","date":"2006-10-06","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 49","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":34.798370361328125,"median_income_tract":21796,"summary":"Oct 6, 2006: 4 killed, 1 injured. Louisville, KY.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSaid Biyad, 42, slit the throats of his four children, who ranged in age from 2 to 8. He also beat his wife with a mallet, suspecting her of infidelity, prosecutors said. She survived. Biyad was sentenced to life in prison without possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 49 (ACS 2006-2010): 34.8% in poverty, median household income $21,796, 40.6% white, 47.0% Black, 4.1% Hispanic/Latino, 25.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Of Louisville Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.47,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.91,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Louisville Hospital","nearest_level1_km":1.47,"nearest_level1_miles":0.91,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.759407,38.254238]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-114","properties":{"name":"Port St. Lucie, FL","date":"2006-10-13","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 3820.08","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":7.37222957611084,"median_income_tract":49005,"summary":"Oct 13, 2006: 4 killed. Port St. Lucie, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 4\nA couple and their two sons were killed at milepost 149 on the Florida Turnpike in a drug trade case. Gunmen Daniel Troya, 23, and Ricardo Sanchez Jr., 23, are on death row. Liana Lopez, 20, was sentenced to 15 years in prison. Their boss, Daniel Varela,\nCensus Tract 3820.08 (ACS 2006-2010): 7.4% in poverty, median household income $49,005, 57.5% white, 13.2% Black, 22.1% Hispanic/Latino, 12.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lawnwood Regional Medical Center And Heart Institute","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":15.36,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.54,"nearest_level1_center":"St Mary'S Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":66.28,"nearest_level1_miles":41.18,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.350327,27.293934]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-86","properties":{"name":"Bonaparte, IA","date":"2006-10-14","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Profit","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9501","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":15.52451229095459,"median_income_tract":40375,"summary":"Oct 14, 2006: 5 killed. Bonaparte, IA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Profit · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA couple and their three teenage daughters were shot with a .22-caliber rifle. Prosecutors said Shawn Bentler, 23, killed his family to gain control of his parents' estate. He is serving life in prison without possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 9501 (ACS 2006-2010): 15.5% in poverty, median household income $40,375, 98.9% white, 0.0% Black, 0.7% Hispanic/Latino, 16.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Van Buren County Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":16.14,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.03,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Iowa Hospitals And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":109.3,"nearest_level1_miles":67.92,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-91.775352,40.692898]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-200","properties":{"name":"Kansas City, KS","date":"2006-10-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 418","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":53.0964469909668,"median_income_tract":9385,"summary":"Oct 14, 2006: 4 killed. Kansas City, KS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nThree women and a man were found shot in a house about 3 a.m. after neighbors reported hearing gunshots. Earnest King and Kenton Williams were arrested the following month. They face charges that carry the death penalty. The case is pending.\nCensus Tract 418 (ACS 2006-2010): 53.1% in poverty, median household income $9,385, 12.2% white, 57.9% Black, 26.6% Hispanic/Latino, 21.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Children'S Mercy Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.47,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.4,"nearest_level1_center":"University Health Truman Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.58,"nearest_level1_miles":3.47,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.627457,39.11417]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-164","properties":{"name":"Riverside County (Cabazon), CA","date":"2006-10-26","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 469","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":23.3883056640625,"median_income_tract":41724,"summary":"Oct 26, 2006: 5 killed. Riverside County (Cabazon), CA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nAuto mechanic Raymond Oyler, 37, was convicted of setting a wildfire that killed five federal firefighters. The 60-square-mile Esperanza fire also destroyed 54 homes and other buildings. He was sentenced to death in 2009.\nCensus Tract 469 (ACS 2006-2010): 23.4% in poverty, median household income $41,724, 40.2% white, 2.7% Black, 54.3% Hispanic/Latino, 54.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Desert Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":47.01,"nearest_trauma_miles":29.21,"nearest_level1_center":"Loma Linda University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":117.37,"nearest_level1_miles":72.93,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-116.050835,33.733353]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-88","properties":{"name":"Reno, NV","date":"2006-10-31","killed":12,"injured":30,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 1.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":34.919708251953125,"median_income_tract":22820,"summary":"Oct 31, 2006: 12 killed, 30 injured. Reno, NV.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nAngry over a fight, Valerie Moore set fire to a mattress outside a hotel room. The blaze spread through the Mizpah Hotel, killing 12 and injuring 30 others. Moore, who was convicted of second-degree murder in 1987, received 12 life sentences.\nCensus Tract 1.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 34.9% in poverty, median household income $22,820, 61.0% white, 3.4% Black, 15.9% Hispanic/Latino, 23.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Saint Mary'S Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":0.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.32,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":178.45,"nearest_level1_miles":110.89,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.813805,39.529633]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-163","properties":{"name":"New Orleans, LA","date":"2006-11-04","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 134","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":21.057119369506836,"median_income_tract":41875,"summary":"Nov 4, 2006: 4 killed. New Orleans, LA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nAuthorities say a family dispute over an inheritance left four family members dead. Felton Bernard received a life sentence in the shootings of his uncles, an aunt, and her boyfriend. Corey Berniard was sentenced to 30 years in prison.\nCensus Tract 134 (ACS 2006-2010): 21.1% in poverty, median household income $41,875, 65.6% white, 20.0% Black, 1.2% Hispanic/Latino, 35.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.9,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.56,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_level1_km":0.9,"nearest_level1_miles":0.56,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.075073,29.954649]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-85","properties":{"name":"Toledo, OH","date":"2006-11-11","killed":4,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 19","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":61.89759063720703,"median_income_tract":16621,"summary":"Nov 11, 2006: 4 killed, 4 injured. Toledo, OH.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nWayne S. Powell, 41, made good on his threat, pouring gasoline inside a home's side door, and lighting it. His ex-girlfriend, her mother, adopted son and a niece were killed. Powell was convicted and sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 19 (ACS 2006-2010): 61.9% in poverty, median household income $16,621, 12.4% white, 72.4% Black, 7.4% Hispanic/Latino, 9.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Health St. Vincent Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.61,"nearest_trauma_miles":1,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Health St. Vincent Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.61,"nearest_level1_miles":1,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.526474,41.676556]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-107","properties":{"name":"Elkhart, IN","date":"2006-11-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Strangulation","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 27","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":24.257633209228516,"median_income_tract":23514,"summary":"Nov 14, 2006: 4 killed. Elkhart, IN.\nCause: Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAngelica Alvarez, 27, strangled her four children, ranging in age from 2 through 8. Psychiatrists debated her mental health and eventually she was ruled competent to stand trial. She was sentenced to life in prison without possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 27 (ACS 2006-2010): 24.3% in poverty, median household income $23,514, 48.4% white, 21.0% Black, 26.6% Hispanic/Latino, 32.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Elkhart General Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":1.41,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.88,"nearest_level1_center":"Bronson Methodist Hospital","nearest_level1_km":74.65,"nearest_level1_miles":46.39,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.976669,41.681995]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-84","properties":{"name":"Kansas City, MO","date":"2006-11-17","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 157","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":17.195613861083984,"median_income_tract":39681,"summary":"Nov 17, 2006: 4 killed. Kansas City, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTerrance Robinson, 22, went into the house, stayed a few minutes, left briefly, and returned to shoot two men and two women, possibly because of an earlier dispute. He was sentenced to eight life terms without the possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 157 (ACS 2006-2010): 17.2% in poverty, median household income $39,681, 75.0% white, 15.7% Black, 4.1% Hispanic/Latino, 20.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Health Truman Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.06,"nearest_level1_center":"University Health Truman Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.71,"nearest_level1_miles":1.06,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.578568,39.099728]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-31","properties":{"name":"Kansas City, KS","date":"2006-12-16","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 404","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":19.703622817993164,"median_income_tract":28797,"summary":"Dec 16, 2006: 6 killed. Kansas City, KS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nHersel M. Isadore, Jr., 28, was \"depressed and acting irrationally\" in the weeks before he fatally shot his longtime girlfriend, four of their children, and a cousin. Isadore then committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 404 (ACS 2006-2010): 19.7% in poverty, median household income $28,797, 3.2% white, 79.6% Black, 16.7% Hispanic/Latino, 26.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"North Kansas City Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":9.44,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.87,"nearest_level1_center":"University Health Truman Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":9.56,"nearest_level1_miles":5.94,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.660004,39.139999]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-30","properties":{"name":"South Bend, IN","date":"2006-12-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 7","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":14.264920234680176,"median_income_tract":25568,"summary":"Dec 21, 2006: 4 killed. South Bend, IN.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 2\nIn January 2007, police found the bodies of four homeless men dumped in manholes. They apparently had stolen scrap metal from the suspects. Daniel Joseph Sharp pleaded guilty and is serving a 65-year sentence. Randy Lee Reeder received a sentence of 260\nCensus Tract 7 (ACS 2006-2010): 14.3% in poverty, median household income $25,568, 76.4% white, 22.1% Black, 1.5% Hispanic/Latino, 20.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Memorial Hospital Of South Bend","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":0.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.09,"nearest_level1_center":"Bronson Methodist Hospital","nearest_level1_km":86.85,"nearest_level1_miles":53.97,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.250008,41.68338]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-28","properties":{"name":"Fishkill, NY","date":"2007-01-19","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 604","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":4.4294657707214355,"median_income_tract":67096,"summary":"Jan 19, 2007: 5 killed. Fishkill, NY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nA plan to steal drugs from an acquaintance ended in his killing and the slayings of his wife and three children. Charles W. Gilleo Jr. received five life sentences without parole, while Mark S. Serrano was sentenced to 50 years to life.\nCensus Tract 604 (ACS 2006-2010): 4.4% in poverty, median household income $67,096, 72.0% white, 2.0% Black, 15.6% Hispanic/Latino, 6.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Luke'S Cornwall Hospital - Newburgh","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":10.27,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.38,"nearest_level1_center":"Westchester Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":50.6,"nearest_level1_miles":31.44,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.899025,41.535648]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-235","properties":{"name":"Omaha, NE","date":"2007-01-28","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 74.08","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":8.07947063446045,"median_income_tract":49234,"summary":"Jan 28, 2007: 4 killed. Omaha, NE.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nRichard Wilkinson didn't get along with his daughter and son-in-law, who lived with him. He argued with her and told friends they were stealing. One night, he shot them and his two grandsons, ages 3 and 6. As police entered his home, he killed himself.\nCensus Tract 74.08 (ACS 2006-2010): 8.1% in poverty, median household income $49,234, 89.8% white, 0.3% Black, 6.9% Hispanic/Latino, 5.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Children'S Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.35,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.94,"nearest_level1_center":"The Nebraska Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":11.06,"nearest_level1_miles":6.87,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.106873,41.230972]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-29","properties":{"name":"Youngstown, OH","date":"2007-01-29","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8023","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":34.72222137451172,"median_income_tract":16480,"summary":"Jan 29, 2007: 4 killed. Youngstown, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour young adults were found shot in the head inside a run-down house. The gunman had forced his way in. Police believe the shooting was part of an ongoing feud between two neighborhood groups. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 8023 (ACS 2006-2010): 34.7% in poverty, median household income $16,480, 2.3% white, 83.7% Black, 9.4% Hispanic/Latino, 32.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Health St. Elizabeth Youngstown Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.91,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.43,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Health St. Elizabeth Youngstown Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.91,"nearest_level1_miles":2.43,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.671928,41.080639]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-27","properties":{"name":"Salt Lake City, UT","date":"2007-02-12","killed":5,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 1140","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":17.96357536315918,"median_income_tract":35375,"summary":"Feb 12, 2007: 5 killed, 4 injured. Salt Lake City, UT.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nAn FBI report found 18-year-old Sulejman Talovic \"\"sought to kill as many people as possible\"\" when he entered Trolley Mall and began shooting. Five died and four were injured. Talovic was killed by police. There is no indication why he went on his rampage\nCensus Tract 1140 (ACS 2006-2010): 18.0% in poverty, median household income $35,375, 58.1% white, 19.1% Black, 21.9% Hispanic/Latino, 32.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Primary Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.55,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Primary Children'S Hospital","nearest_level1_km":4.55,"nearest_level1_miles":2.83,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.891045,40.76078]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-186","properties":{"name":"Immokalee, FL","date":"2007-03-04","killed":5,"injured":5,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 114","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":26.75638771057129,"median_income_tract":38839,"summary":"Mar 4, 2007: 5 killed, 5 injured. Immokalee, FL.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSomeone twice set fire to a trailer in a mobile home park. On the third try, five of 10 occupants died, in part because the owners had covered windows with wire mesh. They settled survivors' claims for $6 million. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 114 (ACS 2006-2010): 26.8% in poverty, median household income $38,839, 2.1% white, 18.1% Black, 79.8% Hispanic/Latino, 33.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lee Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":51.07,"nearest_trauma_miles":31.74,"nearest_level1_center":"Kendall Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":128.28,"nearest_level1_miles":79.71,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.417297,26.41869]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-26","properties":{"name":"Frederick, MD","date":"2007-03-26","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Strangulation","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7502","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":6.323024272918701,"median_income_tract":53500,"summary":"Mar 26, 2007: 5 killed. Frederick, MD.\nCause: Blunt force, Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTwo years after police found the bodies of three suffocated children, the body of their mother was found in a shallow grave 20 miles away. Pedro Rodriguez, 28, who was found hanged in the family's home, is believed to have killed all four.\nCensus Tract 7502 (ACS 2006-2010): 6.3% in poverty, median household income $53,500, 85.8% white, 4.2% Black, 3.8% Hispanic/Latino, 23.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Meritus Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":32.85,"nearest_trauma_miles":20.41,"nearest_level1_center":"Medstar Washington Hospital Center","nearest_level1_km":63.74,"nearest_level1_miles":39.61,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.410538,39.414268]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-24","properties":{"name":"Happy Valley, CA","date":"2007-04-10","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 123.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":9.480687141418457,"median_income_tract":52161,"summary":"Apr 10, 2007: 5 killed. Happy Valley, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFive relatives found dead after a house fire had been shot, the coroner found. A sixth person, Russell Wilcox, who investigators believe killed his family member, died of smoke inhalation. Wilcox was reportedly mentally disabled.\nCensus Tract 123.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 9.5% in poverty, median household income $52,161, 85.8% white, 0.5% Black, 8.4% Hispanic/Latino, 7.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Medical Center Redding","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":13.6,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.45,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":225.89,"nearest_level1_miles":140.36,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.404518,40.449821]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-201","properties":{"name":"Quincy, IL","date":"2007-04-15","killed":5,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":27.56836700439453,"median_income_tract":20125,"summary":"Apr 15, 2007: 5 killed, 4 injured. Quincy, IL.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSeveral hours after arguing with a man at a nightclub, Zachary Q. Meeks set the man's house on fire. Five kids -- ages 5 months to 10 years -- died. Meeks pleaded guilty and was sentenced to five consecutive life terms without possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 7 (ACS 2006-2010): 27.6% in poverty, median household income $20,125, 74.9% white, 14.4% Black, 0.6% Hispanic/Latino, 12.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Blessing Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":0.93,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.58,"nearest_level1_center":"Boone Hospital Center","nearest_level1_km":134.46,"nearest_level1_miles":83.55,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-91.409874,39.9356]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-25","properties":{"name":"Blacksburg, VA","date":"2007-04-16","killed":32,"injured":17,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"College","tract":"Census Tract 207","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":31.070833206176758,"median_income_tract":35944,"summary":"Apr 16, 2007: 32 killed, 17 injured. Blacksburg, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: College · Offenders: 1\nSeung-Hui Cho, an \"angry and disturbed\" Virginia Tech senior, killed two students in a dorm before entering classrooms and shooting others. Thirty-two people were fatally shot by Cho, who then took his own life. A review of the case found that Cho's ment\nCensus Tract 207 (ACS 2006-2010): 31.1% in poverty, median household income $35,944, 75.1% white, 7.7% Black, 6.0% Hispanic/Latino, 8.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lewisgale Hospital Montgomery","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":4.72,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.93,"nearest_level1_center":"Carilion Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":41.8,"nearest_level1_miles":25.97,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.41394,37.229572]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-184","properties":{"name":"Washington, DC","date":"2007-06-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing, Strangulation","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 98.11","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":46.20396423339844,"median_income_tract":21713,"summary":"Jun 1, 2007: 4 killed. Washington, DC.\nCause: Stabbing, Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nBanita Jacks killed her four daughters by stabbing, beating, and strangling them. She lived with their bodies for several months. She was convicted of murder and sentenced to 120 years in jail.\nCensus Tract 98.11 (ACS 2006-2010): 46.2% in poverty, median household income $21,713, 0.0% white, 99.3% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 21.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"George Washington University Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":9.21,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.72,"nearest_level1_center":"George Washington University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":9.21,"nearest_level1_miles":5.72,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.998497,38.82917]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-82","properties":{"name":"Riverdale, GA","date":"2007-06-06","killed":5,"injured":7,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Hotel/Motel","tract":"Census Tract 405.12","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":16.178068161010742,"median_income_tract":39078,"summary":"Jun 6, 2007: 5 killed, 7 injured. Riverdale, GA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Hotel/Motel · Offenders: 1\nSheree Dionne Murphy, a drug addict, argued with a motel tenant and set fire to the motel, killing the man, his fiancé, and several other family members. Seven people were injured. Convicted of murder and arson, Murphy received five life sentences.\nCensus Tract 405.12 (ACS 2006-2010): 16.2% in poverty, median household income $39,078, 14.2% white, 77.7% Black, 1.7% Hispanic/Latino, 15.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":20.16,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.53,"nearest_level1_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":20.16,"nearest_level1_miles":12.53,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.413261,33.572613]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-83","properties":{"name":"Delavan, WI","date":"2007-06-09","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":23.836633682250977,"median_income_tract":48714,"summary":"Jun 9, 2007: 5 killed, 1 injured. Delavan, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAmbrosio Analco had threatened to kill his estranged girlfriend, the mother of his children. He fatally shot three adults and a pair of 6-month-old twins. His 1-year-old daughter survived her injuries. Analco then shot himself in the chest twice.\nCensus Tract 7.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 23.8% in poverty, median household income $48,714, 71.5% white, 0.0% Black, 24.7% Hispanic/Latino, 6.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Walworth Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":9.46,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.88,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercyhealth Javon Bea Hospital - Riverside Blvd Campus","nearest_level1_km":43.31,"nearest_level1_miles":26.91,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.646858,42.629688]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-168","properties":{"name":"Channahon Township, IL","date":"2007-06-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 8833.06","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":2.3414103984832764,"median_income_tract":85208,"summary":"Jun 14, 2007: 4 killed. Channahon Township, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nA man who wanted to abandon his family to live in the Canadian wilderness pulled over their Ford Expedition on an isolated road and shot his wife and three kids. Christopher Vaughn, 32, will spend the rest of his life in prison.\nCensus Tract 8833.06 (ACS 2006-2010): 2.3% in poverty, median household income $85,208, 93.5% white, 0.0% Black, 5.0% Hispanic/Latino, 1.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ascension Saint Joseph - Joliet","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":13.46,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.37,"nearest_level1_center":"Good Samaritan Hospital - Advocate","nearest_level1_km":46.98,"nearest_level1_miles":29.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.228676,41.429474]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-234","properties":{"name":"Philadelphia, PA","date":"2007-07-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 67","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":33.015159606933594,"median_income_tract":28049,"summary":"Jul 22, 2007: 4 killed. Philadelphia, PA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nVonzell Roundtree, high on drugs, saw two men argue with his uncle in a Southwest Philadelphia bar. When he stopped firing his handgun, all three were dead. A fourth man died of his wounds a month later. Roundtree is serving four life prison terms.\nCensus Tract 67 (ACS 2006-2010): 33.0% in poverty, median household income $28,049, 14.6% white, 70.4% Black, 4.2% Hispanic/Latino, 18.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Children'S Hospital Of Philadelphia","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.85,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.39,"nearest_level1_center":"The Hospital Of The University Of Pennsylvania","nearest_level1_km":3.93,"nearest_level1_miles":2.44,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.227577,39.925621]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-81","properties":{"name":"Jonestown, TX","date":"2007-08-24","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 17.80","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":5.155181407928467,"median_income_tract":59911,"summary":"Aug 24, 2007: 6 killed. Jonestown, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nPaul Devoe is sentenced to death in the shootings of four people in Texas. Just before killing his ex-girlfriend and others, he killed two and injured one in Pennsylvania. He initially was found incompetent to stand trial, but after medication was deemed\nCensus Tract 17.80 (ACS 2006-2010): 5.2% in poverty, median household income $59,911, 87.6% white, 2.1% Black, 8.5% Hispanic/Latino, 21.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Cedar Park Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":11.41,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.09,"nearest_level1_center":"Dell Childrens Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":29.8,"nearest_level1_miles":18.52,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.923347,30.495474]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-80","properties":{"name":"Detroit, MI","date":"2007-09-17","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Profit","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5050","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":41.81431579589844,"median_income_tract":12430,"summary":"Sep 17, 2007: 4 killed, 1 injured. Detroit, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Profit · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThe case of Davontae Sanford, who at 14 confessed to killing four people and who later recanted, drew national media attention. Sanford, who is developmentally disabled, was exonerated after seven years in custody. Vincent Smothers, a contract killer, co\nCensus Tract 5050 (ACS 2006-2010): 41.8% in poverty, median household income $12,430, 3.2% white, 96.8% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 37.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ascension Macomb Oakland Hosp - Warren Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":7.25,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.5,"nearest_level1_center":"Ascension St John Hospital","nearest_level1_km":7.88,"nearest_level1_miles":4.9,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.00724,42.440659]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-185","properties":{"name":"Miami, FL","date":"2007-09-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 37.06","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":0,"median_income_tract":0,"summary":"Sep 22, 2007: 4 killed. Miami, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Open space · Offenders: 2\nKirby Archer, 35, and Guillermo Zarabozo, 19, chartered and hijacked the Joe Cool, a Miami-based fishing boat. They shot and dumped overboard its crew of four, planning to flee to Cuba. Archer pleaded guilty to murder and Zaraboso was convicted at trial.\nCensus Tract 37.06 (ACS 2006-2010): 12.2% white, 26.4% Black, 60.2% Hispanic/Latino.","nearest_trauma_center":"Jackson Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.83,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.76,"nearest_level1_center":"Jackson Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":2.83,"nearest_level1_miles":1.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.193657,25.774265]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-79","properties":{"name":"Crandon, WI","date":"2007-10-07","killed":6,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9503","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":21.49007797241211,"median_income_tract":38875,"summary":"Oct 7, 2007: 6 killed, 2 injured. Crandon, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDeputy Sheriff Tyler Peterson, 20, barged into his former girlfriend's locked apartment during a party and shot and killed six people. Two others were injured, including a police officer responding to the shooting.  Peterson shot himself after a standoff\nCensus Tract 9503 (ACS 2006-2010): 21.5% in poverty, median household income $38,875, 74.0% white, 1.3% Black, 2.8% Hispanic/Latino, 34.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Aspirus Rhinelander Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":37.47,"nearest_trauma_miles":23.28,"nearest_level1_center":"Essentia Health St. Mary'S Med","nearest_level1_km":280.83,"nearest_level1_miles":174.5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.902893,45.571907]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-78","properties":{"name":"Detroit, MI","date":"2007-10-18","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5332","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":36.79867935180664,"median_income_tract":26689,"summary":"Oct 18, 2007: 4 killed. Detroit, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTwo children were among the victims of a shooting in what police described as a \"\"known narcotics location.\"\" All four victims were shot as they slept. Patrick Albert Young Smith was found guilty of four counts of murder and sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 5332 (ACS 2006-2010): 36.8% in poverty, median household income $26,689, 2.3% white, 96.1% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 36.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Henry Ford Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.4,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.49,"nearest_level1_center":"Henry Ford Hospital","nearest_level1_km":2.4,"nearest_level1_miles":1.49,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.113548,42.371078]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-76","properties":{"name":"Temecula, CA","date":"2007-11-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 512","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":4.098085403442383,"median_income_tract":43409,"summary":"Nov 11, 2007: 4 killed. Temecula, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nInvestigators say Matthew Blixt, 17, used his father's gun to shoot his father, his father's girlfriend, and the woman's two daughters before turning the gun on himself. Friends said Blixt was upset that his father, who was separated from his mother, was\nCensus Tract 512 (ACS 2006-2010): 4.1% in poverty, median household income $43,409, 56.0% white, 3.1% Black, 35.5% Hispanic/Latino, 7.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Southwest Healthcare System","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":13.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.5,"nearest_level1_center":"Riverside Community Hospital","nearest_level1_km":57.85,"nearest_level1_miles":35.94,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-117.148361,33.493641]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-77","properties":{"name":"Unity, MD","date":"2007-11-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7001.03","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":1.379548192024231,"median_income_tract":169881,"summary":"Nov 22, 2007: 4 killed. Unity, MD.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA woman had twice asked the court to seize her ex-husband's long gun after she filed a protective order against him. David Peter Brockdorff, 40, used the .22-caliber rifle to shoot her and their three children before killing himself on Thanksgiving Day.\nCensus Tract 7001.03 (ACS 2006-2010): 1.4% in poverty, median household income $169,881, 70.0% white, 9.8% Black, 6.1% Hispanic/Latino, 1.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Suburban Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":25.69,"nearest_trauma_miles":15.96,"nearest_level1_center":"Medstar Washington Hospital Center","nearest_level1_km":33.3,"nearest_level1_miles":20.69,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.06942,39.226215]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-99","properties":{"name":"Omaha, NE","date":"2007-12-05","killed":8,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 18","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":27.897350311279297,"median_income_tract":39276,"summary":"Dec 5, 2007: 8 killed, 4 injured. Omaha, NE.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nA 19-year-old with an extensive history of mental health troubles entered Westroads Mall and began firing an assault rifle. Eight people died and four were injured. Robert Hawkins, who declared that \"I'll be famous,\" killed himself.\nCensus Tract 18 (ACS 2006-2010): 27.9% in poverty, median household income $39,276, 65.7% white, 15.1% Black, 11.5% Hispanic/Latino, 14.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Chi Health Bergan Mercy Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.95,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.59,"nearest_level1_center":"Chi Health Bergan Mercy Hospital","nearest_level1_km":0.95,"nearest_level1_miles":0.59,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.93779,41.25861]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-173","properties":{"name":"Colorado Springs, CO","date":"2007-12-09","killed":4,"injured":5,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"House of worship","tract":"Census Tract 23","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":43.70546340942383,"median_income_tract":16034,"summary":"Dec 9, 2007: 4 killed, 5 injured. Colorado Springs, CO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: House of worship · Offenders: 1\nMatthew Murray, 24, was dropped from the missionary program of New Life Church in Arvada, Colo. Five years later, he returned and shot two people then drove 80 miles to the evangelical church itself, where he killed two others before committing suicide.\nCensus Tract 23 (ACS 2006-2010): 43.7% in poverty, median household income $16,034, 78.2% white, 7.3% Black, 9.2% Hispanic/Latino, 4.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Colo Health Memorial Hospital Central","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.24,"nearest_level1_center":"University Colo Health Memorial Hospital Central","nearest_level1_km":2,"nearest_level1_miles":1.24,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.821365,38.833881]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-172","properties":{"name":"Sharonville, OH","date":"2007-12-13","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 235.21","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":4.739109516143799,"median_income_tract":55677,"summary":"Dec 13, 2007: 4 killed. Sharonville, OH.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour bricklayers were beaten, stabbed, and robbed in their apartment, 1,600 miles from home: Villa de Ramos, Mexico. Their roommate Santiago Moreno was convicted in Mexico, which won't extradite citizens facing the death penalty. He received a prison sen\nCensus Tract 235.21 (ACS 2006-2010): 4.7% in poverty, median household income $55,677, 62.6% white, 22.8% Black, 3.7% Hispanic/Latino, 7.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bethesda North Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":4.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.58,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Cincinnati Medicalcenter, Llc","nearest_level1_km":19.68,"nearest_level1_miles":12.23,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.370384,39.28204]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-229","properties":{"name":"Largo, FL","date":"2007-12-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 253.03","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":6.741090774536133,"median_income_tract":44323,"summary":"Dec 14, 2007: 4 killed. Largo, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nOliver Bernsdorff killed himself while driving across the Sunshine Skyway. Police found his ex-wife and her girlfriend dead at their home in Largo. At Bernsdorff's Clearwater home, they found the bodies of his two children, ages 4 and 2.\nCensus Tract 253.03 (ACS 2006-2010): 6.7% in poverty, median household income $44,323, 87.3% white, 3.4% Black, 3.5% Hispanic/Latino, 24.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Johns Hopkins All Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric","nearest_trauma_km":20.54,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.76,"nearest_level1_center":"Tampa General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":30.78,"nearest_level1_miles":19.13,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.770782,27.909161]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-75","properties":{"name":"Carnation, WA","date":"2007-12-24","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 325","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":5.019383907318115,"median_income_tract":80494,"summary":"Dec 24, 2007: 6 killed. Carnation, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nA woman and her boyfriend fatally shot her parents and then also her brother and his family as they arrived for Christmas Eve dinner. Michele K. Anderson and Joseph Thomas McEnroe both were sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 325 (ACS 2006-2010): 5.0% in poverty, median household income $80,494, 83.1% white, 1.6% Black, 7.3% Hispanic/Latino, 10.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Snoqualmie Valley Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level V","nearest_trauma_km":15.18,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.43,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":31.11,"nearest_level1_miles":19.33,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-121.914009,47.647881]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-183","properties":{"name":"Dauphin Island, AL","date":"2008-01-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Pushing/Jumping, Drowning","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 72.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":13.509316444396973,"median_income_tract":51085,"summary":"Jan 7, 2008: 4 killed. Dauphin Island, AL.\nCause: Pushing/Jumping, Drowning · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nAfter arguing with his wife, a Vietnamese immigrant Lam Luong threw their three children plus his wife's child off the 80-foot Dauphin Island bridge to their deaths. Luong appealed his  death sentence. He was then deemed intellectually disabled and his s\nCensus Tract 72.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 13.5% in poverty, median household income $51,085, 91.4% white, 1.0% Black, 2.0% Hispanic/Latino, 57.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Thomas Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":36.11,"nearest_trauma_miles":22.44,"nearest_level1_center":"Usa Health University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":50.23,"nearest_level1_miles":31.21,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.109718,30.255482]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-74","properties":{"name":"Mason, OH","date":"2008-01-11","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 319.03","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":2.6663312911987305,"median_income_tract":119356,"summary":"Jan 11, 2008: 5 killed. Mason, OH.\nCause: Stabbing, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMichel Veillette, 34, hanged himself in jail while awaiting trial on charges that he stabbed his wife to death and then set fire to their house. The couple's four young children, all younger than 9, died from smoke inhalation.\nCensus Tract 319.03 (ACS 2006-2010): 2.7% in poverty, median household income $119,356, 81.2% white, 3.4% Black, 2.9% Hispanic/Latino, 1.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Cincinnati Children'S Hospital Medical Center At T","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.45,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.14,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Cincinnati Medicalcenter, Llc","nearest_level1_km":29.77,"nearest_level1_miles":18.5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.309937,39.360058]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-72","properties":{"name":"Indianapolis, IN","date":"2008-01-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":5,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3508","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":52.1521110534668,"median_income_tract":19195,"summary":"Jan 14, 2008: 4 killed. Indianapolis, IN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 5\nA plan to steal marijuana and cash from a home ended in the shootings of two women, a baby, and a toddler. Five men were convicted in connection to the robbery and slayings. All five assailants pled guilty and were sentenced to prison for various terms r\nCensus Tract 3508 (ACS 2006-2010): 52.2% in poverty, median household income $19,195, 2.3% white, 95.6% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 19.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Indiana University Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.4,"nearest_level1_center":"Indiana University Health","nearest_level1_km":3.86,"nearest_level1_miles":2.4,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.132614,39.815662]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-73","properties":{"name":"Youngstown, OH","date":"2008-01-23","killed":6,"injured":13,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8006","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":42.17473220825195,"median_income_tract":23227,"summary":"Jan 23, 2008: 6 killed, 13 injured. Youngstown, OH.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAngry about two teenagers stealing his cellphone, Michael A. Davis set fire to their home. The blaze trapped two adults as well as four children, all younger than the age of 8. Davis was sentenced to  six consecutive life terms in prison.\nCensus Tract 8006 (ACS 2006-2010): 42.2% in poverty, median household income $23,227, 11.0% white, 63.3% Black, 25.6% Hispanic/Latino, 25.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Health St. Elizabeth Youngstown Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.22,"nearest_trauma_miles":2,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Health St. Elizabeth Youngstown Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.22,"nearest_level1_miles":2,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.619156,41.110363]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-160","properties":{"name":"Tinley Park, IL","date":"2008-02-02","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 8254","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":15.343650817871094,"median_income_tract":59025,"summary":"Feb 2, 2008: 5 killed, 1 injured. Tinley Park, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nThe killer entered a Lane Bryant store on a Saturday morning and announced he was robbing the store. He ordered six women to the back of the store where he bound and shot them. Five died. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 8254 (ACS 2006-2010): 15.3% in poverty, median household income $59,025, 86.8% white, 3.7% Black, 9.3% Hispanic/Latino, 5.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Silver Cross Hospital And Medical Centers","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":16.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.47,"nearest_level1_center":"Advocate Christ Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":17.05,"nearest_level1_miles":10.59,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.784492,41.573368]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-69","properties":{"name":"Cockeysville, MD","date":"2008-02-02","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4089","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":3.649921417236328,"median_income_tract":87132,"summary":"Feb 2, 2008: 4 killed. Cockeysville, MD.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nNicholas Browning, 15, used his father's handgun to kill his mother, father and two brothers while they were sleeping. He then went to a friend's house to play video games. He had been arguing with his father. Browning took a plea and was sentenced to li\nCensus Tract 4089 (ACS 2006-2010): 3.6% in poverty, median household income $87,132, 83.9% white, 1.8% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 8.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sinai Hospital Of Baltimore","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":14.42,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.96,"nearest_level1_center":"The Johns Hopkins Hospital","nearest_level1_km":21.06,"nearest_level1_miles":13.09,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.64386,39.481216]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-177","properties":{"name":"Los Angeles, CA","date":"2008-02-07","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2074","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":0,"median_income_tract":0,"summary":"Feb 7, 2008: 4 killed, 1 injured. Los Angeles, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA month after being fired from his brother's moving firm, Edwin Rivera, 20, shot and killed his father, two brothers and a police officer during a standoff at his home. He was killed by a police sniper's bullet as he fled a fire caused by stun grenades.\nCensus Tract 2074 (ACS 2006-2010): 14.3% white, 20.8% Black, 60.7% Hispanic/Latino.","nearest_trauma_center":"California Hospital Medical Center - Los Angeles","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.64,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.64,"nearest_level1_center":"Los Angeles General Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":3.35,"nearest_level1_miles":2.08,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.243683,34.052235]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-70","properties":{"name":"Kirkwood, MO","date":"2008-02-07","killed":6,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Government/Transit","tract":"Census Tract 2184.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":4.622561454772949,"median_income_tract":80252,"summary":"Feb 7, 2008: 6 killed, 1 injured. Kirkwood, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Other · Location: Government/Transit · Offenders: 1\nAngry at city officials, Charles Lee \"Cookie\" Thornton, 52, entered a City Council meeting and began shooting, killing five, including two council members and two police officers. Months later, the mayor died of his injuries. Thornton was killed by polic\nCensus Tract 2184.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 4.6% in poverty, median household income $80,252, 91.0% white, 5.0% Black, 1.2% Hispanic/Latino, 6.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Missouri Baptist Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.84,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.25,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Hospital St. Louis","nearest_level1_km":7.72,"nearest_level1_miles":4.8,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.406784,38.583385]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-100","properties":{"name":"Dekalb, IL","date":"2008-02-14","killed":5,"injured":21,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"College","tract":"Census Tract 13","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":22.97321319580078,"median_income_tract":37796,"summary":"Feb 14, 2008: 5 killed, 21 injured. Dekalb, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: College · Offenders: 1\nSteven Kazmierczak, a 27-year-old former graduate student, entered a Northern Illinois University lecture hall during a class, shot and killed five people and wounded 21 before committing suicide.  Kazmierczak reportedly had a history of mental illness.\nCensus Tract 13 (ACS 2006-2010): 23.0% in poverty, median household income $37,796, 76.7% white, 6.6% Black, 13.8% Hispanic/Latino, 2.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Northwestern Medicine Delnor Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":34,"nearest_trauma_miles":21.13,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercyhealth Javon Bea Hospital - Riverside Blvd Campus","nearest_level1_km":46.36,"nearest_level1_miles":28.8,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.750366,41.929474]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-68","properties":{"name":"Yorba Linda, CA","date":"2008-02-23","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 218.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":5.141458034515381,"median_income_tract":71769,"summary":"Feb 23, 2008: 4 killed, 1 injured. Yorba Linda, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA 14-year-old boy called police to say his father had shot him and his brother. Police found a woman and three children dead in the home; the teenager survived his injuries. Orland Cho, 41, husband and father of the three, later shot himself.\nCensus Tract 218.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 5.1% in poverty, median household income $71,769, 64.1% white, 0.2% Black, 22.2% Hispanic/Latino, 0.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Children'S Hospital Of Orange County","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level II","nearest_trauma_km":12.94,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.04,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Irvine Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":13.11,"nearest_level1_miles":8.15,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-117.81311,33.888626]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-71","properties":{"name":"Bristol, TN","date":"2008-02-27","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 427.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":22.39472198486328,"median_income_tract":30264,"summary":"Feb 27, 2008: 4 killed, 1 injured. Bristol, TN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nUpset over breaking up with his girlfriend, Rusty Rumley, 26, went to her mother's apartment and shot and killed four people, including  his ex-girlfriend's boyfriend. Rumley then committed suicide when surrounded by police.\nCensus Tract 427.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 22.4% in poverty, median household income $30,264, 92.2% white, 2.7% Black, 3.6% Hispanic/Latino, 5.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bristol Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.18,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.84,"nearest_level1_center":"Johnson City Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":36.43,"nearest_level1_miles":22.64,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.188744,36.595104]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-67","properties":{"name":"Memphis, TN","date":"2008-03-02","killed":6,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 42","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":18.30698585510254,"median_income_tract":54063,"summary":"Mar 2, 2008: 6 killed, 3 injured. Memphis, TN.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJessie Dotson, out of prison five months for an earlier murder, was convicted of killing his brother and five others, including two toddlers. Three other children were badly injured, two of whom testified against Dotson. . Dotson was convicted and senten\nCensus Tract 42 (ACS 2006-2010): 18.3% in poverty, median household income $54,063, 66.5% white, 20.3% Black, 2.2% Hispanic/Latino, 22.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Le Bonheur Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.64,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.02,"nearest_level1_center":"Le Bonheur Children'S Hospital","nearest_level1_km":1.64,"nearest_level1_miles":1.02,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.048981,35.149536]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-64","properties":{"name":"Santa Maria, CA","date":"2008-03-18","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 21.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":22.33169174194336,"median_income_tract":46964,"summary":"Mar 18, 2008: 4 killed. Santa Maria, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nLee Isaac Bedwell Leeds, who had been diagnosed with paranoid schizophrenia, fatally shot his father, two employees and a customer at his family's junkyard. Leeds said that he believed the victims were plotting to kill him. He was found competent to stan\nCensus Tract 21.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 22.3% in poverty, median household income $46,964, 38.4% white, 2.0% Black, 57.9% Hispanic/Latino, 4.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Marian Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.07,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.29,"nearest_level1_center":"Santa Barbara Cottage Hospital","nearest_level1_km":87.33,"nearest_level1_miles":54.26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-120.435722,34.953033]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-65","properties":{"name":"Iowa City, IA","date":"2008-03-23","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 16","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":71.44682312011719,"median_income_tract":16031,"summary":"Mar 23, 2008: 5 killed. Iowa City, IA.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSteven Sueppel, 42, beat to death his wife and four children before killing himself. Sueppel had been indicted a month earlier on charges that he had stolen more than a half million dollars from the bank where he worked.\nCensus Tract 16 (ACS 2006-2010): 71.4% in poverty, median household income $16,031, 87.0% white, 2.4% Black, 1.6% Hispanic/Latino, 3.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Hospital Ic","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":0.36,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.22,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Iowa Hospitals And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":1.44,"nearest_level1_miles":0.9,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-91.530167,41.661129]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-66","properties":{"name":"Charlotte, NC","date":"2008-03-24","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":12.09964370727539,"median_income_tract":76583,"summary":"Mar 24, 2008: 4 killed. Charlotte, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour people were found shot to death in Charlotte's Tree Top apartment complex. More than a decade later, a cold case investigation resulted in the arrest of Dominick Daise. Investigators believe the four victims were \"involved in a lifestyle that put th\nCensus Tract 1 (ACS 2006-2010): 12.1% in poverty, median household income $76,583, 80.2% white, 11.4% Black, 2.4% Hispanic/Latino, 25.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Novant Health Presbyterian Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.42,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.5,"nearest_level1_center":"Atrium Health University City","nearest_level1_km":12.43,"nearest_level1_miles":7.73,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.843124,35.227085]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-236","properties":{"name":"Sitka, AK","date":"2008-03-25","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":3.968573808670044,"median_income_tract":61062,"summary":"Mar 25, 2008: 4 killed, 1 injured. Sitka, AK.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice found Jason Abbott, 18, on his grandparents' porch, a knife to his throat. Inside, they found his grandparents, his aunt, and her fiancé, all fatally stabbed. Another aunt survived. He pleaded guilty and gets schizophrenia treatment in prison.\nCensus Tract 2 (ACS 2006-2010): 4.0% in poverty, median household income $61,062, 60.6% white, 0.4% Black, 3.0% Hispanic/Latino, 9.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sitka Community Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":1.14,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.71,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1368.45,"nearest_level1_miles":850.31,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-135.333557,57.05254]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-62","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2008-04-23","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8432","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":22.05035972595215,"median_income_tract":40133,"summary":"Apr 23, 2008: 5 killed. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 3\nThree men and two women were shot in the head and killed during a Chicago burglary. The three suspects stole money, jewelry and TVs, police said. Torolan Williams and Michael King were found guilty and received life sentences. Arthur Brown pleaded guilty\nCensus Tract 8432 (ACS 2006-2010): 22.1% in poverty, median household income $40,133, 13.7% white, 3.7% Black, 80.4% Hispanic/Latino, 10.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"John H. Stroger Jr. Hospital Of Cook County","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.2,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.99,"nearest_level1_center":"John H. Stroger Jr. Hospital Of Cook County","nearest_level1_km":3.2,"nearest_level1_miles":1.99,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.650055,41.850033]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-63","properties":{"name":"Easley, SC","date":"2008-04-26","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 108.04","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":10.781166076660156,"median_income_tract":39733,"summary":"Apr 26, 2008: 4 killed. Easley, SC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAfter an earlier disagreement with his father about coming home late, Nathaniel Dickson, 18, went to his brother's closet looking for clothes and found his brother's 12-gauge shotgun. He proceeded to shoot and kill his stepmother, stepsister, brother, an\nCensus Tract 108.04 (ACS 2006-2010): 10.8% in poverty, median household income $39,733, 86.5% white, 5.6% Black, 5.9% Hispanic/Latino, 12.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Prisma Health Greenville Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":17.29,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.74,"nearest_level1_center":"Prisma Health Greenville Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":17.29,"nearest_level1_miles":10.74,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.601524,34.829838]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-61","properties":{"name":"Houston, TX","date":"2008-05-10","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1000","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":32.72495651245117,"median_income_tract":56705,"summary":"May 10, 2008: 4 killed. Houston, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSalvador Alfaro, an immigrant from El Salvador, shot and killed a woman and three children in their home and then committed suicide. The woman also was from El Salvador, and they lived together as a family.\nCensus Tract 1000 (ACS 2006-2010): 32.7% in poverty, median household income $56,705, 43.0% white, 33.0% Black, 18.8% Hispanic/Latino, 32.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Joseph Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":1.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.06,"nearest_level1_center":"Memorial Hermann - Texas Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":6.29,"nearest_level1_miles":3.91,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.363274,29.763283]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-60","properties":{"name":"Ingram, TX","date":"2008-06-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9603.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":12.431815147399902,"median_income_tract":41931,"summary":"Jun 1, 2008: 4 killed. Ingram, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJohn David Young, 38, shot and killed his wife, mother-in-law and two children in the middle of the night, and then killed himself. Deputies had been alerted by the mother-in-law, who called police to report \"He's killing us.\"\nCensus Tract 9603.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 12.4% in poverty, median household income $41,931, 81.0% white, 0.1% Black, 15.4% Hispanic/Latino, 17.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hill Country Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":40.14,"nearest_trauma_miles":24.94,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":90.02,"nearest_level1_miles":55.94,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-99.240318,30.077431]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-58","properties":{"name":"Quartz Hill, CA","date":"2008-06-23","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9103.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":6.741293430328369,"median_income_tract":82417,"summary":"Jun 23, 2008: 5 killed. Quartz Hill, CA.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nInvestigators found the bodies of a woman, her two children and her cousin. Her ex-husband Jae Hwan Shim led authorities to a fifth body in Mexico in late 2013. Shim and his friend Tae Won Kwon pleaded guilty, both receiving life sentences.\nCensus Tract 9103.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 6.7% in poverty, median household income $82,417, 77.3% white, 5.8% Black, 11.8% Hispanic/Latino, 7.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Antelope Valley Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":7.23,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.49,"nearest_level1_center":"Providence Cedars - Sinai Tarzana Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":60.14,"nearest_level1_miles":37.37,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.218132,34.645264]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-59","properties":{"name":"Henderson, KY","date":"2008-06-25","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 203","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":32.28438186645508,"median_income_tract":22888,"summary":"Jun 25, 2008: 5 killed, 1 injured. Henderson, KY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nWesley Higdon, upset after his supervisor reprimanded him, shot the man and five co-workers at the Atlantis Plastics plant. All but one died. Higdon then committed suicide at the scene.\nCensus Tract 203 (ACS 2006-2010): 32.3% in poverty, median household income $22,888, 76.7% white, 15.8% Black, 2.3% Hispanic/Latino, 14.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ascension St Vincent Evansville","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":16.07,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.99,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Louisville Hospital","nearest_level1_km":168,"nearest_level1_miles":104.39,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.590012,37.836155]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-203","properties":{"name":"Rock Falls, IL","date":"2008-06-29","killed":8,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Profit","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 15","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":16.511194229125977,"median_income_tract":36435,"summary":"Jun 29, 2008: 8 killed. Rock Falls, IL.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Profit · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTwo men, a young woman and her 2-year-old son were beaten to death in their apartment. Nicholas Sheley was found guilty of murder. Sheley, who faces a trial in the murder of an Arkansas couple, is already serving a life sentence for two other killings.\nCensus Tract 15 (ACS 2006-2010): 16.5% in poverty, median household income $36,435, 83.1% white, 1.4% Black, 14.4% Hispanic/Latino, 12.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercyone Clinton Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":42.36,"nearest_trauma_miles":26.32,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercyhealth Javon Bea Hospital - Riverside Blvd Campus","nearest_level1_km":85.25,"nearest_level1_miles":52.97,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.69133,41.774754]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-57","properties":{"name":"Milwaukee, WI","date":"2008-07-04","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 88","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":47.17348861694336,"median_income_tract":18625,"summary":"Jul 4, 2008: 4 killed, 2 injured. Milwaukee, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 3\nA retaliatory shooting at a Fourth of July street party resulted in the deaths of four victims and injuries to two others. Antonio D. \"\"Cheem\"\" Williams and James R. Washington were sentenced to life in prison. Rosario C. Fuentez pleaded guilty and got 20\nCensus Tract 88 (ACS 2006-2010): 47.2% in poverty, median household income $18,625, 0.7% white, 95.1% Black, 1.9% Hispanic/Latino, 29.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ascension Se Wisconsin Hospital - St Joseph Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":2.48,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.54,"nearest_level1_center":"Childrens Hospital Of Wisconsin","nearest_level1_km":6.6,"nearest_level1_miles":4.1,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.948692,43.064266]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-230","properties":{"name":"Birmingham, AL","date":"2008-07-24","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 104.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":27.514175415039062,"median_income_tract":23412,"summary":"Jul 24, 2008: 4 killed. Birmingham, AL.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nAuthorities found four bodies after putting out a house fire. A couple had been shot execution-style. Two boys survived gunshots but died in the blaze. Two men were charged but found not guilty. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 104.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 27.5% in poverty, median household income $23,412, 27.2% white, 67.8% Black, 4.5% Hispanic/Latino, 23.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Medical West Hospital Authority, An Affiliate Of Uab Health System","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.54,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.58,"nearest_level1_center":"Children'S Hospital Of Alabama","nearest_level1_km":20.55,"nearest_level1_miles":12.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.963692,33.375031]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-231","properties":{"name":"Shelby County/Birmingham, AL","date":"2008-08-17","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":6,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 302.13","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":1.6170016527175903,"median_income_tract":104300,"summary":"Aug 17, 2008: 5 killed. Shelby County/Birmingham, AL.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 6\nFive men were tortured, beaten, electrocuted, and slashed in what authorities said was a contract killing. Members of a Mexican drug cartel were angry over $450,000 that was missing. Six members of the cartel were sentenced to prison.\nCensus Tract 302.13 (ACS 2006-2010): 1.6% in poverty, median household income $104,300, 76.7% white, 7.2% Black, 4.4% Hispanic/Latino, 15.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Grandview Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.56,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.59,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Alabama Hospital","nearest_level1_km":13.7,"nearest_level1_miles":8.51,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.692474,33.423038]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-54","properties":{"name":"Camden, NJ","date":"2008-09-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 6018","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":41.83400344848633,"median_income_tract":26806,"summary":"Sep 1, 2008: 4 killed. Camden, NJ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nLuis Cruz shot and killed his wife, daughter, son, and mother-in-law before committing suicide as they gathered for Labor Day dinner. The killing was precipitated by a \"fierce argument\" with his wife, according to the police.\nCensus Tract 6018 (ACS 2006-2010): 41.8% in poverty, median household income $26,806, 5.3% white, 50.0% Black, 40.4% Hispanic/Latino, 15.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Cooper Hospital University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.74,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.08,"nearest_level1_center":"Cooper Hospital University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.74,"nearest_level1_miles":1.08,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.119621,39.925945]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-56","properties":{"name":"Alger, WA","date":"2008-09-02","killed":6,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 9508","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":2.271535873413086,"median_income_tract":76405,"summary":"Sep 2, 2008: 6 killed, 4 injured. Alger, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nUsing stolen guns, Isaac Zamora killed six people, including a sheriff's deputy. Zamora was sentenced to life and sent to a state mental hospital but later was returned to prison after doctors indicated he posed too much of a threat.\nCensus Tract 9508 (ACS 2006-2010): 2.3% in poverty, median household income $76,405, 89.8% white, 0.1% Black, 8.7% Hispanic/Latino, 8.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Peacehealth United General Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":14.57,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.05,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":112.98,"nearest_level1_miles":70.2,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.34127,48.619831]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-55","properties":{"name":"Irvington, NJ","date":"2008-09-08","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 123","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":10.244941711425781,"median_income_tract":40666,"summary":"Sep 8, 2008: 4 killed. Irvington, NJ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nA robbery ended with the two suspects shooting and killing four people, then setting the house ablaze in an attempt to cover it up. Rolando Terrell was sentenced to life in prison. Lester Hayes worked out a plea deal and received a 20-year sentence.\nCensus Tract 123 (ACS 2006-2010): 10.2% in poverty, median household income $40,666, 0.9% white, 92.0% Black, 3.2% Hispanic/Latino, 10.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.8,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.36,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.8,"nearest_level1_miles":2.36,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.234871,40.732323]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-53","properties":{"name":"Lancaster, CA","date":"2008-09-09","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9008.06","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":37.970314025878906,"median_income_tract":16875,"summary":"Sep 9, 2008: 4 killed. Lancaster, CA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThe bodies of a mother and her three daughters were found in the embers of their home. Corey King, a friend of the woman's son, was found guilty of four counts of first-degree murder and was sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 9008.06 (ACS 2006-2010): 38.0% in poverty, median household income $16,875, 42.4% white, 28.2% Black, 22.1% Hispanic/Latino, 12.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Antelope Valley Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.29,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.42,"nearest_level1_center":"Providence Cedars - Sinai Tarzana Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":68.96,"nearest_level1_miles":42.85,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.136742,34.69804]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-178","properties":{"name":"Wright Township, MI","date":"2008-09-29","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Blunt force","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 201","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":9.31204891204834,"median_income_tract":57163,"summary":"Sep 29, 2008: 4 killed. Wright Township, MI.\nCause: Shooting, Blunt force · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA woman, her two sons, and one of the son's girlfriend were found in the embers of her home. They had died of gunshots or beating. Troy Brake, 31, was convicted of their murders and is serving life in prison without possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 201 (ACS 2006-2010): 9.3% in poverty, median household income $57,163, 92.1% white, 1.1% Black, 5.5% Hispanic/Latino, 6.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Spectrum Health - Butterworth Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":19.53,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.13,"nearest_level1_center":"Spectrum Health - Butterworth Campus","nearest_level1_km":19.53,"nearest_level1_miles":12.13,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.808655,43.110855]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-51","properties":{"name":"Los Angeles, CA","date":"2008-10-05","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1081.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":7.6086955070495605,"median_income_tract":101712,"summary":"Oct 5, 2008: 5 killed. Los Angeles, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nUpset over his finances -- he had lost his job and lost money in the stock market -- Karthik Rajaram, 45, shot and killed his wife, mother-in-law, and three sons, ages 7 to 19, in their home in the upscale Sorrento neighborhood. Rajaram then committed su\nCensus Tract 1081.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 7.6% in poverty, median household income $101,712, 54.1% white, 4.1% Black, 6.2% Hispanic/Latino, 4.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Northridge Hospital Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":7.12,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.42,"nearest_level1_center":"Providence Cedars - Sinai Tarzana Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":12.55,"nearest_level1_miles":7.8,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.550613,34.282192]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-52","properties":{"name":"Jefferson, LA","date":"2008-10-30","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":5,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 246","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":17.231637954711914,"median_income_tract":41117,"summary":"Oct 30, 2008: 4 killed. Jefferson, LA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 5\nFive men entered a bar, intending a robbery. They shot three and, in the melee, a fourth man also was shot. Pedro Duran, 32, Renil Escobar, 29, Mario A. Funes, 26, Rigoberto Funes, 20 and Jose A. Cornejo, 22, all were sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 246 (ACS 2006-2010): 17.2% in poverty, median household income $41,117, 9.9% white, 84.5% Black, 2.1% Hispanic/Latino, 9.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":6.89,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.28,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_level1_km":6.89,"nearest_level1_miles":4.28,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.15313,29.966038]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-158","properties":{"name":"Long Beach, CA","date":"2008-11-02","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Shelter/Drug house","tract":"Census Tract 5760.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":10.104450225830078,"median_income_tract":63503,"summary":"Nov 2, 2008: 5 killed. Long Beach, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Shelter/Drug house · Offenders: 2\nFive men in a homeless camp were killed in a drug-debt dispute, police say. David Cruz Ponce and Max Eliseo Rafael each were charged with five special-circumstance counts of murder. Both pleaded not guilty and were convicted. Ponce was sentenced to death\nCensus Tract 5760.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 10.1% in poverty, median household income $63,503, 54.0% white, 7.4% Black, 22.1% Hispanic/Latino, 17.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Mary Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":1.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.95,"nearest_level1_center":"Lac - Harbor Ucla Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":11.81,"nearest_level1_miles":7.34,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.189232,33.766964]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-50","properties":{"name":"Alton, TX","date":"2008-12-06","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 241.12","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":60.081642150878906,"median_income_tract":19801,"summary":"Dec 6, 2008: 4 killed, 1 injured. Alton, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nRoberto A. Rojas went to his in-laws' house, where his estranged wife was living, and shot and killed his mother-in-law, son, and two stepsons. He shot and beat his wife, who survived. Rojas was sentenced to life in prison without parole eligibility.\nCensus Tract 241.12 (ACS 2006-2010): 60.1% in poverty, median household income $19,801, 1.7% white, 0.0% Black, 98.3% Hispanic/Latino, 7.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mission Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":14.95,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.29,"nearest_level1_center":"Doctors Hospital At Renaissance","nearest_level1_km":17.64,"nearest_level1_miles":10.96,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-98.363297,26.323446]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-49","properties":{"name":"Covina, CA","date":"2008-12-24","killed":9,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4061.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":21.678104400634766,"median_income_tract":56023,"summary":"Dec 24, 2008: 9 killed, 3 injured. Covina, CA.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nBruce Pardo dressed up as Santa Claus and went to his former in-laws' home during a Christmas Eve party. He shot and killed his ex-wife and members of her family before setting the house ablaze, killing  nine and injuring three others. Pardo then committ\nCensus Tract 4061.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 21.7% in poverty, median household income $56,023, 36.2% white, 0.0% Black, 54.2% Hispanic/Latino, 7.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Pomona Valley Hospital Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":12.96,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.05,"nearest_level1_center":"Lac Usc Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":29.49,"nearest_level1_miles":18.32,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-117.890343,34.090008]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-48","properties":{"name":"El Reno, OK","date":"2009-01-12","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Strangulation","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3005","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":24.384870529174805,"median_income_tract":38889,"summary":"Jan 12, 2009: 5 killed. El Reno, OK.\nCause: Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJoshua S. Durcho's girlfriend had threatened to call police on him, so he strangled her, and then strangled her four young children. Durcho, who had been in prison and vowed not to return, pleaded guilty and received five life sentences without parole.\nCensus Tract 3005 (ACS 2006-2010): 24.4% in poverty, median household income $38,889, 72.5% white, 1.5% Black, 19.4% Hispanic/Latino, 23.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Hospital El Reno","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":2.32,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.44,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Health University Of Oklahoma Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":41.45,"nearest_level1_miles":25.75,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.955048,35.532272]}}
