{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-153","properties":{"name":"Brockport, NY","date":"2009-02-14","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 153.04","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":19.039026260375977,"median_income_tract":48942,"summary":"Feb 14, 2009: 4 killed, 1 injured. Brockport, NY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nFrank Garcia, a nursing supervisor, was enraged at two co-workers who accused him of sexual harassment which caused him to be fired. Returning to the hospital, he shot three people, including a nurse and a bystander who attempted to intervene.  Garcia th\nCensus Tract 153.04 (ACS 2006-2010): 19.0% in poverty, median household income $48,942, 81.7% white, 8.5% Black, 5.6% Hispanic/Latino, 7.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Strong Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":27.47,"nearest_trauma_miles":17.07,"nearest_level1_center":"Strong Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":27.47,"nearest_level1_miles":17.07,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.939178,43.213673]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-46","properties":{"name":"Lawrence, NY","date":"2009-02-19","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4116","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":0.8234928250312805,"median_income_tract":123482,"summary":"Feb 19, 2009: 4 killed. Lawrence, NY.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nCaleb Lacey, a rookie volunteer firefighter, was found guilty of setting a fire that killed a mother and her three children. Prosecutors said Caleb Lacey drove to the fire station and donned gear, wanting to be a hero. Lacey was sentenced to 25 years to\nCensus Tract 4116 (ACS 2006-2010): 0.8% in poverty, median household income $123,482, 96.2% white, 0.0% Black, 3.4% Hispanic/Latino, 10.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"South Nassau Communities Hospital Off - Campus Emergency Department","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.94,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.31,"nearest_level1_center":"Jamaica Hospital Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":11.89,"nearest_level1_miles":7.39,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.729576,40.615662]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-45","properties":{"name":"Cleveland, OH","date":"2009-03-05","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1011.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":40.115943908691406,"median_income_tract":17670,"summary":"Mar 5, 2009: 5 killed, 1 injured. Cleveland, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAfter leading police on a daylong manhunt, Davon Crawford, 33, shot himself as officers found him inside a West Side home. The night before, Crawford had killed his wife, his sister-in-law, two nephews, and his niece. He also injured his 7-year-old daugh\nCensus Tract 1011.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 40.1% in poverty, median household income $17,670, 35.1% white, 44.2% Black, 18.0% Hispanic/Latino, 15.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Metrohealth Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.66,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.9,"nearest_level1_center":"Metrohealth Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":4.66,"nearest_level1_miles":2.9,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.745155,41.483017]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-171","properties":{"name":"Hueytown, AL","date":"2009-03-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 100.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":12.32017707824707,"median_income_tract":41077,"summary":"Mar 7, 2009: 4 killed. Hueytown, AL.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Other · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nScott Lamar Abbott has been hospitalized for mental health issues at least four times. He was sentenced to life without parole after stabbing his ex-girlfriend and three others 95 times. Prosecutors said he was angry about the breakup.\nCensus Tract 100.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 12.3% in poverty, median household income $41,077, 69.2% white, 29.1% Black, 1.7% Hispanic/Latino, 4.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Medical West Hospital Authority, An Affiliate Of Uab Health System","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":8.84,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.49,"nearest_level1_center":"Children'S Hospital Of Alabama","nearest_level1_km":18.71,"nearest_level1_miles":11.62,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.996658,33.451221]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-155","properties":{"name":"Samson, AL","date":"2009-03-10","killed":10,"injured":6,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 501","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":21.205575942993164,"median_income_tract":24362,"summary":"Mar 10, 2009: 10 killed, 6 injured. Samson, AL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTen people died and six were injured after Michael McLendon, 28, went to several relatives' homes firing an assault rifle. According to a letter McLendon sent police, he was depressed he could not be a police officer or Marine. He committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 501 (ACS 2006-2010): 21.2% in poverty, median household income $24,362, 84.7% white, 9.2% Black, 4.2% Hispanic/Latino, 19.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mizell Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":27.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":17.31,"nearest_level1_center":"Usa Health University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":200.37,"nearest_level1_miles":124.5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.05159,31.1113]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-44","properties":{"name":"Conover, NC","date":"2009-03-12","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 102.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":11.164073944091797,"median_income_tract":44843,"summary":"Mar 12, 2009: 4 killed. Conover, NC.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nChiew Chan Saevang, 38, and his girlfriend, Yer Yang, 40, decided to steal a drug shipment from their partner in an opium ring. At his home, they killed the partner's wife and three children. A week later, while fleeing police, Saevang fatally shot Yang\nCensus Tract 102.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 11.2% in poverty, median household income $44,843, 73.7% white, 7.2% Black, 15.1% Hispanic/Latino, 12.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Caromont Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":48.78,"nearest_trauma_miles":30.31,"nearest_level1_center":"Atrium Health University City","nearest_level1_km":61.63,"nearest_level1_miles":38.3,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.218697,35.70652]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-175","properties":{"name":"Miami, FL","date":"2009-03-15","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 70.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":22.69215202331543,"median_income_tract":36702,"summary":"Mar 15, 2009: 4 killed. Miami, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA birthday party ended in violence when a woman's estranged husband burst into her house and shot her, her boyfriend, and two members of her family, police said. Guillermo Lopez, 48, set his truck and home on fire before he killed himself.\nCensus Tract 70.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 22.7% in poverty, median household income $36,702, 10.1% white, 0.0% Black, 89.0% Hispanic/Latino, 9.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Nicklaus Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric","nearest_trauma_km":3.75,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.33,"nearest_level1_center":"Jackson Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":7.53,"nearest_level1_miles":4.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.257141,25.737244]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-42","properties":{"name":"Raytown, MO","date":"2009-03-16","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 126","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":10.949511528015137,"median_income_tract":46130,"summary":"Mar 16, 2009: 4 killed, 1 injured. Raytown, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA 14-month-old boy was spared in the slayings of a woman, her boyfriend and two of her nephews. Gevante E. Anderson, the woman's former boyfriend and the father of the child, was found guilty of first-degree murder and sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 126 (ACS 2006-2010): 10.9% in poverty, median household income $46,130, 68.9% white, 15.8% Black, 6.6% Hispanic/Latino, 9.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Research Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":8.17,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.08,"nearest_level1_center":"Research Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":8.17,"nearest_level1_miles":5.08,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.463562,39.008617]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-41","properties":{"name":"Oakland, CA","date":"2009-03-21","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 4093","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":24.90754508972168,"median_income_tract":33772,"summary":"Mar 21, 2009: 4 killed, 1 injured. Oakland, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Other · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nFour Oakland police officers, including two SWAT team members, were killed after a wanted man was pulled over in a traffic stop. Lovelle Mixon, 26, holed up in his sister's apartment and shot at police before he was killed. A fifth officer was injured.\nCensus Tract 4093 (ACS 2006-2010): 24.9% in poverty, median household income $33,772, 3.5% white, 28.6% Black, 59.9% Hispanic/Latino, 11.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Eden Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":8.24,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.12,"nearest_level1_center":"Highland Hospital","nearest_level1_km":8.9,"nearest_level1_miles":5.53,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.172089,37.733795]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-40","properties":{"name":"Santa Clara, CA","date":"2009-03-29","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5049.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":7.046037197113037,"median_income_tract":126774,"summary":"Mar 29, 2009: 5 killed, 1 injured. Santa Clara, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAs a family meal began, Devan Kalathat, 42, shot his wife and two children; his brother-in-law and the brother-in-law’s wife and infant daughter; and finally, himself. Only his wife survived. Police believe a feud fueled the violence.\nCensus Tract 5049.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 7.0% in poverty, median household income $126,774, 20.3% white, 5.0% Black, 5.1% Hispanic/Latino, 5.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Santa Clara Valley Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":9.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.03,"nearest_level1_center":"Santa Clara Valley Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":9.71,"nearest_level1_miles":6.03,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-121.954224,37.398548]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-43","properties":{"name":"Carthage, NC","date":"2009-03-29","killed":8,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Medical facility","tract":"Census Tract 9504.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":12.485164642333984,"median_income_tract":34919,"summary":"Mar 29, 2009: 8 killed, 2 injured. Carthage, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Medical facility · Offenders: 1\nRobert Kenneth Stewart entered a nursing home where his estranged wife worked and fatally shot seven elderly patients and a nurse. He said he had taken too many sleeping pills and could not be held responsible. He was sentenced to at least 142 years.\nCensus Tract 9504.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 12.5% in poverty, median household income $34,919, 75.1% white, 18.0% Black, 4.3% Hispanic/Latino, 20.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Womack Army Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":43.76,"nearest_trauma_miles":27.19,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of North Carolina Hospitals","nearest_level1_km":70.42,"nearest_level1_miles":43.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.416969,35.345985]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-38","properties":{"name":"Binghamton, NY","date":"2009-04-03","killed":13,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 14","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":24.558670043945312,"median_income_tract":28977,"summary":"Apr 3, 2009: 13 killed, 4 injured. Binghamton, NY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nWearing a bulletproof vest, Jiverly Wong, 41, entered a citizenship class and fired 98 shots from two handguns. Wong killed 13 people and injured several more before shooting himself.\nCensus Tract 14 (ACS 2006-2010): 24.6% in poverty, median household income $28,977, 88.6% white, 2.2% Black, 2.9% Hispanic/Latino, 15.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"United Health Services Hospitals Inc - Wilson Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.76,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.34,"nearest_level1_center":"Upstate University Hospital At Community General","nearest_level1_km":103.17,"nearest_level1_miles":64.1,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.917976,42.098686]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-39","properties":{"name":"Graham, WA","date":"2009-04-04","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 731.18","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":12.801115036010742,"median_income_tract":72838,"summary":"Apr 4, 2009: 5 killed. Graham, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJames Harrison, 34, fatally shot his five children, ages 7 to 16, in the middle of the night after a fight with his wife. His wife was with another man and planned to leave Harrison, according to police reports. The next morning, Harrison killed himself.\nCensus Tract 731.18 (ACS 2006-2010): 12.8% in poverty, median household income $72,838, 85.3% white, 1.5% Black, 6.2% Hispanic/Latino, 1.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Multicare Good Samaritan Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":14.05,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.73,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":61.31,"nearest_level1_miles":38.09,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.294281,47.052879]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-182","properties":{"name":"Green Hill, AL","date":"2009-04-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 116.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":19.83184051513672,"median_income_tract":36138,"summary":"Apr 7, 2009: 4 killed. Green Hill, AL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nKevin Garner's divorce hearing was scheduled to begin the next day. His estranged wife, teenage daughter, and his wife's sister and niece were found shot dead in their home. Garner's body was found 70 miles away, in his house, which he set on fire.\nCensus Tract 116.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 19.8% in poverty, median household income $36,138, 98.4% white, 0.0% Black, 1.4% Hispanic/Latino, 8.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"North Alabama Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":22.56,"nearest_trauma_miles":14.02,"nearest_level1_center":"The Huntsville Hospital","nearest_level1_km":89.49,"nearest_level1_miles":55.61,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.512245,34.973137]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-37","properties":{"name":"Middletown, MD","date":"2009-04-17","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7526.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":1.0076903104782104,"median_income_tract":107964,"summary":"Apr 17, 2009: 4 killed. Middletown, MD.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFaced with the possibility of his wife leaving him, Christopher A. Wood shot her and their three young children. He then wrote suicide notes and mutilated the bodies before committing suicide. An autopsy found he was on medication for depression.\nCensus Tract 7526.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 1.0% in poverty, median household income $107,964, 92.3% white, 2.6% Black, 3.0% Hispanic/Latino, 9.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Meritus Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":23.1,"nearest_trauma_miles":14.35,"nearest_level1_center":"Inova Fairfax Hospital","nearest_level1_km":70.61,"nearest_level1_miles":43.88,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.544708,39.443714]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-36","properties":{"name":"Kansas City, KS","date":"2009-06-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 439.05","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":32.88557052612305,"median_income_tract":26667,"summary":"Jun 22, 2009: 4 killed. Kansas City, KS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAdrian Burks went to the house where his girlfriend was staying, got in an argument, and killed her and the other three people who lived there, including a 3-year-old girl. He pleaded guilty to the four shootings and received life in prison.\nCensus Tract 439.05 (ACS 2006-2010): 32.9% in poverty, median household income $26,667, 44.1% white, 44.1% Black, 1.8% Hispanic/Latino, 7.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Providence Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":7.7,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.78,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Kansas Hospital Transplant Center","nearest_level1_km":9.82,"nearest_level1_miles":6.1,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.699547,39.111839]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-35","properties":{"name":"Fayetteville, TN","date":"2009-07-18","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9754","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":16.81524658203125,"median_income_tract":36463,"summary":"Jul 18, 2009: 6 killed. Fayetteville, TN.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJacob Levi Shaffer is serving life sentences for killing six people, including his estranged wife and her teenage son. Hours before killing his wife's family, he beat a man to death at an Alabama marble company owned by his wife's relatives.\nCensus Tract 9754 (ACS 2006-2010): 16.8% in poverty, median household income $36,463, 86.1% white, 11.2% Black, 0.5% Hispanic/Latino, 14.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Huntsville Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":47.89,"nearest_trauma_miles":29.76,"nearest_level1_center":"The Huntsville Hospital","nearest_level1_km":47.89,"nearest_level1_miles":29.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.570549,35.152027]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-34","properties":{"name":"Hancock, MI","date":"2009-07-25","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 6","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":23.5155086517334,"median_income_tract":30048,"summary":"Jul 25, 2009: 4 killed. Hancock, MI.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour residents of an apartment building died in a fire set in the laundry room. A resident heard saying he hated the place was tried twice on homicide and arson charges. The jury deadlocked both times. Charges have been dropped. The case remains open.\nCensus Tract 6 (ACS 2006-2010): 23.5% in poverty, median household income $30,048, 91.3% white, 0.3% Black, 2.9% Hispanic/Latino, 6.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Up Health System Portage","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":1.55,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.96,"nearest_level1_center":"Essentia Health St. Mary'S Med","nearest_level1_km":269.36,"nearest_level1_miles":167.38,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.579933,47.126755]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-33","properties":{"name":"Lawrenceville, GA","date":"2009-08-27","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 505.21","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":15.861798286437988,"median_income_tract":49549,"summary":"Aug 27, 2009: 4 killed, 1 injured. Lawrenceville, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice arrived at a shooting to find a 4-year-old girl who had covered her bullet wounds with Band-Aids telling them \"\"My whole family is dead.\"\" Richard Terrance Ringold pleaded guilty to four counts of murder and is serving life in prison without parole\nCensus Tract 505.21 (ACS 2006-2010): 15.9% in poverty, median household income $49,549, 49.3% white, 17.8% Black, 27.3% Hispanic/Latino, 20.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Northside Hospital Gwinnett","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.85,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Wellstar Atlanta Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":41.57,"nearest_level1_miles":25.83,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.987961,33.956215]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-32","properties":{"name":"Brunswick, GA","date":"2009-08-29","killed":8,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":41.74781036376953,"median_income_tract":33469,"summary":"Aug 29, 2009: 8 killed, 1 injured. Brunswick, GA.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nEight family members, seven of them adults, were beaten to death in a mobile home. A child was injured. Guy Heinze Jr., who reported the slayings to police, was found guilty of eight counts of murder and sentenced to life in prison without parole.\nCensus Tract 9 (ACS 2006-2010): 41.7% in poverty, median household income $33,469, 39.8% white, 39.1% Black, 18.7% Hispanic/Latino, 25.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Winn Army Community Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":80.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":50.32,"nearest_level1_center":"Uf Health Jacksonville","nearest_level1_km":90.63,"nearest_level1_miles":56.32,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.491486,31.149952]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-115","properties":{"name":" Naples, FL","date":"2009-09-17","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 102.05","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":4.2172980308532715,"median_income_tract":84083,"summary":"Sep 17, 2009: 6 killed.  Naples, FL.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMesac Damas slashed the throats of his wife and five children and later fled to Haiti. He was found competent to stand trial and subsequently was sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 102.05 (ACS 2006-2010): 4.2% in poverty, median household income $84,083, 88.0% white, 0.0% Black, 10.2% Hispanic/Latino, 25.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lee Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":46.23,"nearest_trauma_miles":28.72,"nearest_level1_center":"Kendall Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":150.64,"nearest_level1_miles":93.6,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.791756,26.219255]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-197","properties":{"name":"Beason, IL","date":"2009-09-21","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9529","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":9.0128755569458,"median_income_tract":55288,"summary":"Sep 21, 2009: 5 killed, 1 injured. Beason, IL.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nA husband, wife and their three children were bludgeoned with a tire iron. Their former son-in-law, Christopher Harris, did it, according to his brother Jason, who admitted that he watched. Prison sentences: Life and 20 years, respectively.\nCensus Tract 9529 (ACS 2006-2010): 9.0% in poverty, median household income $55,288, 95.8% white, 1.2% Black, 1.8% Hispanic/Latino, 10.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Decatur Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":36.56,"nearest_trauma_miles":22.72,"nearest_level1_center":"St. John'S Hospital","nearest_level1_km":53.74,"nearest_level1_miles":33.4,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.19342,40.14365]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-21","properties":{"name":"Mount Airy, NC","date":"2009-11-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 9304","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":27.607616424560547,"median_income_tract":25407,"summary":"Nov 1, 2009: 4 killed. Mount Airy, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nA romantic dispute led Marcos Chavez Gonzalez to kill his girlfriend's adult relatives and friends with a high-powered assault rifle. Gonzalez pleaded guilty and was sentenced to three life terms without parole eligibility.\nCensus Tract 9304 (ACS 2006-2010): 27.6% in poverty, median household income $25,407, 74.0% white, 10.7% Black, 11.4% Hispanic/Latino, 3.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"North Carolina Baptist Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":53.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":33.54,"nearest_level1_center":"North Carolina Baptist Hospital","nearest_level1_km":53.98,"nearest_level1_miles":33.54,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.610046,36.489349]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-101","properties":{"name":"Killeen, TX","date":"2009-11-05","killed":13,"injured":32,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Government/Transit","tract":"Census Tract 105.03","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":0,"median_income_tract":0,"summary":"Nov 5, 2009: 13 killed, 32 injured. Killeen, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Government/Transit · Offenders: 1\nMaj. Nidal Malik Hasan, an Army psychiatrist, was sentenced to death in shootings at Fort Hood. He entered a military medical center firing a semi-automatic pistol, killing 13 and injuring 32.\nCensus Tract 105.03 (ACS 2006-2010): 56.6% white, 16.1% Black, 17.8% Hispanic/Latino.","nearest_trauma_center":"Carl R. Darnall Army Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.47,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.53,"nearest_level1_center":"Baylor Scott And White Medical Center - Temple","nearest_level1_km":41.85,"nearest_level1_miles":26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.796387,31.1425]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-22","properties":{"name":"Oklahoma City, OK","date":"2009-11-09","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Shooting, Blunt force","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1072.17","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":29.094608306884766,"median_income_tract":30602,"summary":"Nov 9, 2009: 4 killed, 1 injured. Oklahoma City, OK.\nCause: Shooting, Blunt force · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 4\nFour people (two of whom were pregnant) were killed in a drug dispute implicating four assailants. David Allen Tyner and Johnathan Cochran both pleaded guilty and agreed to testify against Denny Phillips and Russell Hogshooter. Tyner was sentenced to six\nCensus Tract 1072.17 (ACS 2006-2010): 29.1% in poverty, median household income $30,602, 45.7% white, 5.5% Black, 34.0% Hispanic/Latino, 15.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Community Hospital, Llc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":4.43,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.75,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Health University Of Oklahoma Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":8.82,"nearest_level1_miles":5.48,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.544212,35.409443]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-19","properties":{"name":"Pearcy, AR","date":"2009-11-12","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 111","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":21.261320114135742,"median_income_tract":45435,"summary":"Nov 12, 2009: 5 killed, 1 injured. Pearcy, AR.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 3\nFive adults were found dead in two trailers that had been burglarized, one was set on fire. Samuel Lee Conway was convicted in 2011, but the conviction was later overturned. In a 2016 retrial, he pleaded guilty to lesser charges and received a 40-year se\nCensus Tract 111 (ACS 2006-2010): 21.3% in poverty, median household income $45,435, 92.9% white, 0.4% Black, 2.9% Hispanic/Latino, 8.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Chi St. Vincent Hospital Hot Springs","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":12.77,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.93,"nearest_level1_center":"Uams Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":87.62,"nearest_level1_miles":54.44,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-93.202194,34.442989]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-117","properties":{"name":"Jupiter, FL","date":"2009-11-26","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":20.146047592163086,"median_income_tract":52279,"summary":"Nov 26, 2009: 4 killed, 2 injured. Jupiter, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPaul Merhige, 35, had been treated for depression and obsessive-compulsive disorder. At Thanksgiving dinner, he shot his aunt, twin sisters and cousin and wounded two others. He pleaded guilty to avoid the death penalty and will spend life in prison.\nCensus Tract 2.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 20.1% in poverty, median household income $52,279, 46.1% white, 4.4% Black, 48.9% Hispanic/Latino, 6.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Mary'S Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":20.08,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.48,"nearest_level1_center":"St Mary'S Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":20.08,"nearest_level1_miles":12.48,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.094208,26.934225]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-20","properties":{"name":"Burlingame, KS","date":"2009-11-28","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 102","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":13.30837345123291,"median_income_tract":47765,"summary":"Nov 28, 2009: 4 killed. Burlingame, KS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJames Kraig Kahler lost his high-paying job after his domestic-assault arrest. His wife of 23 years said he was controlling. He was convicted of killing his wife, two daughters and wife's grandmother, and sentenced to death. His son, 10, was uninjured.\nCensus Tract 102 (ACS 2006-2010): 13.3% in poverty, median household income $47,765, 96.4% white, 0.8% Black, 1.1% Hispanic/Latino, 12.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Stormont Vail Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":35.26,"nearest_trauma_miles":21.91,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Kansas Hospital Transplant Center","nearest_level1_km":111.09,"nearest_level1_miles":69.03,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.834984,38.753895]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-23","properties":{"name":"Parkland, WA","date":"2009-11-29","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 717.07","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":19.58525276184082,"median_income_tract":43241,"summary":"Nov 29, 2009: 4 killed. Parkland, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Other · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nMaurice Clemmons used a handgun to kill four Lakeview, Wash., police officers as they worked on laptops at a Parkland coffee shop. He was killed two days later by a Seattle officer at a traffic stop. Several people were convicted of aiding his flight.\nCensus Tract 717.07 (ACS 2006-2010): 19.6% in poverty, median household income $43,241, 63.5% white, 2.3% Black, 14.3% Hispanic/Latino, 8.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Franciscan Health St. Clare Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":5.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.2,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":50.55,"nearest_level1_miles":31.41,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.434013,47.155376]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-198","properties":{"name":"Madison, WI","date":"2009-12-03","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 11.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":82.1524887084961,"median_income_tract":14855,"summary":"Dec 3, 2009: 4 killed. Madison, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nTyrone M. Adair, 38, shot himself four days after police found his girlfriend's and infant daughter's bodies in the trunk of his car. His ex-girlfriend and a 2-year-old daughter were shot at their home. Adair was out of work and faced child support costs\nCensus Tract 11.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 82.2% in poverty, median household income $14,855, 90.8% white, 0.4% Black, 1.5% Hispanic/Latino, 17.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Unitypoint Health - Meriter","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":0.87,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.54,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercyhealth Javon Bea Hospital - Riverside Blvd Campus","nearest_level1_km":91.55,"nearest_level1_miles":56.89,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.40123,43.073051]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-411","properties":{"name":"Kennesaw, GA","date":"2010-01-12","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 302.29","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":17.399381637573242,"median_income_tract":49911,"summary":"Jan 12, 2010: 4 killed, 1 injured. Kennesaw, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nOn January 12, 2010, three people were killed and two others critically injured in a workplace shooting at a truck rental business located near Kennesaw, GA.  Another victim died in 2013 from complications related to his injuries. The shooter, a former e\nCensus Tract 302.29 (ACS 2006-2010): 17.4% in poverty, median household income $49,911, 68.7% white, 13.6% Black, 5.5% Hispanic/Latino, 12.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Wellstar Kennestone Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.26,"nearest_level1_center":"Wellstar Atlanta Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":34.72,"nearest_level1_miles":21.58,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.575577,34.026279]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-17","properties":{"name":"Bellville, TX","date":"2010-01-17","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7605.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":5.1766438484191895,"median_income_tract":71118,"summary":"Jan 17, 2010: 5 killed. Bellville, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMaron Thomas spent several months at a state mental hospital after his family was found slain in their home. His 2-year-old niece had been decapitated. Thomas was later tried and convicted of murder. He was sentenced to life without parole eligibility.\nCensus Tract 7605.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 5.2% in poverty, median household income $71,118, 83.6% white, 7.1% Black, 6.6% Hispanic/Latino, 14.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bellville Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":0.43,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.27,"nearest_level1_center":"Texas Childrens Hospital","nearest_level1_km":86.82,"nearest_level1_miles":53.95,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.257187,29.950226]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-18","properties":{"name":"Spout Spring, VA","date":"2010-01-19","killed":8,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 401","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":14.295392990112305,"median_income_tract":40758,"summary":"Jan 19, 2010: 8 killed. Spout Spring, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTwo mental health evaluators found Christopher Brian Speight insane when he killed eight relatives and friends. Speight pleaded guilty to three counts of capital murder and received five life terms plus 18 years in prison.\nCensus Tract 401 (ACS 2006-2010): 14.3% in poverty, median household income $40,758, 73.7% white, 24.5% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 12.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lynchburg General Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":24.36,"nearest_trauma_miles":15.13,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Virginia Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":83.94,"nearest_level1_miles":52.16,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-78.90918,37.349869]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-16","properties":{"name":"Brooklyn, NY","date":"2010-01-30","killed":5,"injured":16,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 824","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":12.801403045654297,"median_income_tract":32482,"summary":"Jan 30, 2010: 5 killed, 16 injured. Brooklyn, NY.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Public · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA toilet paper roll drenched in paint thinner, set ablaze and thrown at the bottom of a crowded Brooklyn tenement's stairs trapped five victims. Daniel Ignacio received 25 years to life in prison. Officers testified that Ignacio told them he was drunk.\nCensus Tract 824 (ACS 2006-2010): 12.8% in poverty, median household income $32,482, 0.0% white, 92.7% Black, 6.4% Hispanic/Latino, 10.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Kings County Hospital Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.83,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.52,"nearest_level1_center":"Kings County Hospital Center","nearest_level1_km":0.83,"nearest_level1_miles":0.52,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.949585,40.650105]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-220","properties":{"name":"Fallbrook, CA","date":"2010-02-04","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Profit","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 98","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":36.14906692504883,"median_income_tract":31078,"summary":"Feb 4, 2010: 4 killed. Fallbrook, CA.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Other · Circumstance: Profit · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nA couple and their two young sons vanished from their home in 2010. In November 2013, authorities discovered their bodies in shallow graves outside Victorville, CA, and a year later charged one victim's business partner, Charles Merritt, with murder. He\nCensus Tract 98 (ACS 2006-2010): 36.1% in poverty, median household income $31,078, 22.3% white, 7.1% Black, 64.0% Hispanic/Latino, 13.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Arrowhead Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":51.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":32.11,"nearest_level1_center":"Loma Linda University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":54.15,"nearest_level1_miles":33.65,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-117.291161,34.536106]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-188","properties":{"name":"Cicero, IL","date":"2010-02-14","killed":7,"injured":3,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Profit","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8138.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":26.067546844482422,"median_income_tract":34250,"summary":"Feb 14, 2010: 7 killed, 3 injured. Cicero, IL.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Profit · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nProsecutors say recordings show a landlord told his handyman to torch a wood-frame house. The fire trapped three adults and four kids in the attic. Lawrence Myers was sentenced to life in prison; maintenance man Marion Cormier was convicted and sentenced\nCensus Tract 8138.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 26.1% in poverty, median household income $34,250, 10.2% white, 1.9% Black, 86.2% Hispanic/Latino, 4.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Loyola Macneal Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.51,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.18,"nearest_level1_center":"Mount Sinai Hospital","nearest_level1_km":5.19,"nearest_level1_miles":3.23,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.753944,41.845589]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-15","properties":{"name":"New Orleans, LA","date":"2010-03-25","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 14.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":51.8112907409668,"median_income_tract":21636,"summary":"Mar 25, 2010: 4 killed. New Orleans, LA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDamian Jordan had a history of violence against women, with multiple arrests for battery. He pleaded guilty to four counts of manslaughter in the shootings of his girlfriend, her sister and her two children. Jordan was sentenced to 80 years in prison.\nCensus Tract 14.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 51.8% in poverty, median household income $21,636, 11.5% white, 87.0% Black, 1.5% Hispanic/Latino, 35.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.31,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.68,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_level1_km":4.31,"nearest_level1_miles":2.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.041466,29.976748]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-14","properties":{"name":"Washington, DC","date":"2010-03-30","killed":4,"injured":5,"offenders":6,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 98.10","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":34.92267990112305,"median_income_tract":26234,"summary":"Mar 30, 2010: 4 killed, 5 injured. Washington, DC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Open space · Offenders: 6\nThe theft of a cheap bracelet ended in three shootings, including a drive-by that sprayed bullets at a funeral crowd, killing four teens. Jeffrey Best, Robert Bost and Orlando Carter received life without parole. Nathaniel Simms, Lamar Williams and Sanqu\nCensus Tract 98.10 (ACS 2006-2010): 34.9% in poverty, median household income $26,234, 1.2% white, 89.9% Black, 4.0% Hispanic/Latino, 18.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"George Washington University Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":8.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.39,"nearest_level1_center":"George Washington University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":8.68,"nearest_level1_miles":5.39,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.007446,38.830921]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-12","properties":{"name":"Los Angeles, CA","date":"2010-04-03","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 1242.04","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":31.552587509155273,"median_income_tract":36645,"summary":"Apr 3, 2010: 4 killed, 2 injured. Los Angeles, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nA gathering of acquaintances at a North Hollywood Mediterranean restaurant ended when a man left and returned with a handgun, firing 50 bullets, killing four and injuring two. Nerses Galstyan was charged with four counts of murder and received a life sen\nCensus Tract 1242.04 (ACS 2006-2010): 31.6% in poverty, median household income $36,645, 29.2% white, 14.8% Black, 53.0% Hispanic/Latino, 7.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Cedar Sinai Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":10.67,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.63,"nearest_level1_center":"Cedar Sinai Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":10.67,"nearest_level1_miles":6.63,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.378967,34.17223]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-13","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2010-04-14","killed":5,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8216","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":9.427105903625488,"median_income_tract":60147,"summary":"Apr 14, 2010: 5 killed, 2 injured. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJames Larry told police he was angry his family were infidels who would not conform to his Muslim culture. He shot and killed his pregnant wife, young son and three other family members. He pleaded guilty and was imprisoned without possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 8216 (ACS 2006-2010): 9.4% in poverty, median household income $60,147, 48.1% white, 38.7% Black, 12.3% Hispanic/Latino, 3.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Advocate Christ Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.42,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.12,"nearest_level1_center":"Advocate Christ Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":3.42,"nearest_level1_miles":2.12,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.693497,41.731739]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-189","properties":{"name":"Peoria, IL","date":"2010-04-21","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 12","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":38.54314041137695,"median_income_tract":19789,"summary":"Apr 21, 2010: 4 killed, 1 injured. Peoria, IL.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAunterrio Barney was arrested in North Carolina months after a purposely set fire killed three adults and a 2-year-old boy. Barney had faced the death penalty, but because Illinois has banned it, he now will serve a mandatory life sentence.\nCensus Tract 12 (ACS 2006-2010): 38.5% in poverty, median household income $19,789, 51.6% white, 23.2% Black, 22.4% Hispanic/Latino, 14.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Methodist Medical Center Of Illinois","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":0.89,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.55,"nearest_level1_center":"Saint Francis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.02,"nearest_level1_miles":0.63,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.588989,40.693649]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-10","properties":{"name":"Winchester, MA","date":"2010-06-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing, Blunt force","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3385","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":2.707275867462158,"median_income_tract":140795,"summary":"Jun 14, 2010: 4 killed. Winchester, MA.\nCause: Stabbing, Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThomas Mortimer IV admitted killing his wife, two young children and mother-in-law and was sentenced to four life terms without parole. According to a letter Mortimer wrote that was found at the scene, he hated his wife's parents, with whom he lived.\nCensus Tract 3385 (ACS 2006-2010): 2.7% in poverty, median household income $140,795, 92.2% white, 0.0% Black, 0.8% Hispanic/Latino, 5.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lahey Hospital And Medical Center - Burlington","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":6.66,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.14,"nearest_level1_center":"Lahey Hospital And Medical Center - Burlington","nearest_level1_km":6.66,"nearest_level1_miles":4.14,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-71.137001,42.452316]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-118","properties":{"name":"Hialeah, FL","date":"2010-06-16","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 6.08","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":26.6451416015625,"median_income_tract":26627,"summary":"Jun 16, 2010: 4 killed, 3 injured. Hialeah, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nGerardo Regalado's wife had moved out and started a new job. The couple fought in the parking lot, where he shot her, and then he ran into the restaurant where she worked, targeting women. Four died and three were injured. Regalado committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 6.08 (ACS 2006-2010): 26.6% in poverty, median household income $26,627, 2.1% white, 0.8% Black, 97.1% Hispanic/Latino, 6.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Jackson Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":9.72,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.04,"nearest_level1_center":"Jackson Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":9.72,"nearest_level1_miles":6.04,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.278107,25.857595]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-11","properties":{"name":"Northampton, PA","date":"2010-06-26","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 162.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":6.183330535888672,"median_income_tract":45840,"summary":"Jun 26, 2010: 4 killed. Northampton, PA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice found three people bleeding from fatal stab wounds, and another body in the basement. Michael Eric Ballard, who had served time for killing a man in 1991, was sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 162.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 6.2% in poverty, median household income $45,840, 91.6% white, 0.2% Black, 4.3% Hispanic/Latino, 3.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Good Shepherd Specialty Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":8.8,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.47,"nearest_level1_center":"Saint Luke'S Hospital Of Bethlehem, Pennsylvania","nearest_level1_km":12.22,"nearest_level1_miles":7.59,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.496849,40.686207]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-9","properties":{"name":"New York, NY","date":"2010-07-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 31","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":12.356322288513184,"median_income_tract":104405,"summary":"Jul 22, 2010: 4 killed. New York, NY.\nCause: Stabbing, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nInvestigators at first thought four children and their mother had died in an accidental house fire. But they discovered the kids had been killed -- three had slashed throats -- by their mother Leisa Jones, 30, who died of smoke inhalation.\nCensus Tract 31 (ACS 2006-2010): 12.4% in poverty, median household income $104,405, 64.2% white, 1.8% Black, 6.5% Hispanic/Latino, 14.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Jersey City Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.77,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.34,"nearest_level1_center":"Bellevue Hospital Center","nearest_level1_km":3.8,"nearest_level1_miles":2.36,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.005974,40.714268]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-6","properties":{"name":"Manchester, CT","date":"2010-08-03","killed":8,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 5144","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":10.755472183227539,"median_income_tract":48503,"summary":"Aug 3, 2010: 8 killed, 2 injured. Manchester, CT.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nJust after Omar S. Thornton was forced to resign from his beer delivery job, he opened fire with a 9 mm pistol, killing eight co-workers and injuring two before killing himself. Supervisors had confronted Thornton over pilferage.\nCensus Tract 5144 (ACS 2006-2010): 10.8% in poverty, median household income $48,503, 70.1% white, 10.8% Black, 9.4% Hispanic/Latino, 0.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hartford Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":13.3,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.27,"nearest_level1_center":"Hartford Hospital","nearest_level1_km":13.3,"nearest_level1_miles":8.27,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-72.521477,41.775932]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-7","properties":{"name":"Lanham, MD","date":"2010-08-06","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8022.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":8.193883895874023,"median_income_tract":50958,"summary":"Aug 6, 2010: 4 killed. Lanham, MD.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nPolice found the bodies of two women and two children in a trash-filled garage apartment. Darrell Lynn Bellard was convicted and sentenced to life in prison without parole eligibility. Tkeisha Nicole Gilmer pleaded guilty in 2011 and was sentenced to lif\nCensus Tract 8022.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 8.2% in poverty, median household income $50,958, 23.1% white, 69.5% Black, 0.1% Hispanic/Latino, 4.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Um Capital Region Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":7.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Howard University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":17.47,"nearest_level1_miles":10.85,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.849693,38.833447]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-8","properties":{"name":"Buffalo, NY","date":"2010-08-14","killed":5,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 165","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":39.5,"median_income_tract":17045,"summary":"Aug 14, 2010: 5 killed, 3 injured. Buffalo, NY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nRicardo M. McCray was sentenced to life without parole in a shooting outside a popular downtown bar. Four people, including a man celebrating his wedding anniversary, died. Four others were injured, one so seriously that he remains hospitalized.\nCensus Tract 165 (ACS 2006-2010): 39.5% in poverty, median household income $17,045, 45.1% white, 35.6% Black, 12.6% Hispanic/Latino, 30.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"John R. Oishei Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.84,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.14,"nearest_level1_center":"Erie County Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.77,"nearest_level1_miles":3.58,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-78.878372,42.886448]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-5","properties":{"name":"Lake Havasu City, AZ","date":"2010-08-28","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9529","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":9.70180606842041,"median_income_tract":37367,"summary":"Aug 28, 2010: 5 killed, 1 injured. Lake Havasu City, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nBrian Diez, 26, barged into his ex-girlfriend's house, shot dead five adults, and took his two young children. He brought the kids to a relative in California before committing suicide. His ex, who was killed, had a restraining order against Diez.\nCensus Tract 9529 (ACS 2006-2010): 9.7% in poverty, median household income $37,367, 78.4% white, 0.3% Black, 19.8% Hispanic/Latino, 33.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Havasu Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":1.55,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.96,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center Of Southern Nevada","nearest_level1_km":201.48,"nearest_level1_miles":125.2,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-114.322456,34.483902]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-1","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2010-09-02","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 306.01","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":23.845685958862305,"median_income_tract":31721,"summary":"Sep 2, 2010: 4 killed. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nPolice tailing suspects in a series of drug-related robberies found four men bound and fatally shot in a garage after the suspects had fled. Police killed Arturo Ibarra after a chase. Raul Segura-Rodriguez faces four counts of murder in the garage shooti\nCensus Tract 306.01 (ACS 2006-2010): 23.8% in poverty, median household income $31,721, 46.3% white, 22.6% Black, 11.7% Hispanic/Latino, 15.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Presence Chicago Hospitals Network","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.88,"nearest_level1_center":"Presence Chicago Hospitals Network","nearest_level1_km":4.63,"nearest_level1_miles":2.88,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.658539,41.987534]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-3","properties":{"name":"Lake Charles, LA","date":"2010-09-04","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 17","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":16.16126823425293,"median_income_tract":39418,"summary":"Sep 4, 2010: 4 killed. Lake Charles, LA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nLee Roy Williams told police in a recorded interview that he ''snapped'' after learning his roommates planned to evict him. He pleaded guilty to four counts of murder in the slayings of two men and two women and received four consecutive life sentences.\nCensus Tract 17 (ACS 2006-2010): 16.2% in poverty, median household income $39,418, 74.2% white, 20.5% Black, 2.6% Hispanic/Latino, 3.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lake Charles Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":5.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.53,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Texas Medical Branch - Galveston","nearest_level1_km":180.79,"nearest_level1_miles":112.34,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-93.177635,30.156162]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-2","properties":{"name":"Jackson, KY","date":"2010-09-11","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9203","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":34.13421630859375,"median_income_tract":26944,"summary":"Sep 11, 2010: 5 killed. Jackson, KY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nWhen Stanley Neace's wife didn't cook his eggs the way he wanted, he became enraged and fatally shot her and her daughter, and then went to other trailer homes and shot three neighbors. Neace, 47, killed himself with a shotgun.\nCensus Tract 9203 (ACS 2006-2010): 34.1% in poverty, median household income $26,944, 97.2% white, 0.0% Black, 0.1% Hispanic/Latino, 19.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Morgan County Arh Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":42.07,"nearest_trauma_miles":26.14,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Kentucky Hospital","nearest_level1_km":112.12,"nearest_level1_miles":69.67,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.383659,37.553425]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-116","properties":{"name":"Riviera Beach, FL","date":"2010-09-27","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 13.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":31.436376571655273,"median_income_tract":26051,"summary":"Sep 27, 2010: 5 killed, 1 injured. Riviera Beach, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice came upon Patrick Dell, 32, as he shot himself on the front steps of his estranged wife's home. Inside, officers found the wife and four of her children shot dead. A fifth boy, 12, was wounded. Dell's biological children were unharmed.\nCensus Tract 13.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 31.4% in poverty, median household income $26,051, 0.0% white, 96.5% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 16.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Mary'S Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.58,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.22,"nearest_level1_center":"St Mary'S Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":3.58,"nearest_level1_miles":2.22,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.073036,26.786613]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-4","properties":{"name":"Boston, MA","date":"2010-09-28","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1011.02","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":34.490135192871094,"median_income_tract":37646,"summary":"Sep 28, 2010: 4 killed, 1 injured. Boston, MA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 3\nAn $1,800 robbery ended in the shootings of five people, four fatally, in a home invasion in the Mattapan neighborhood. Dwayne Moore received a sentence of life in prison without parole. Kimani Washington struck a deal and got 16 to 18 years in prison. E\nCensus Tract 1011.02 (ACS 2006-2010): 34.5% in poverty, median household income $37,646, 0.4% white, 89.3% Black, 9.3% Hispanic/Latino, 11.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Brigham And Women'S Faulkner Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.88,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.41,"nearest_level1_center":"Brigham And Women'S Faulkner Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.88,"nearest_level1_miles":2.41,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-71.089127,42.282017]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-119","properties":{"name":"Tallahassee, FL","date":"2010-11-19","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Drowning","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":26.3157901763916,"median_income_tract":34375,"summary":"Nov 19, 2010: 4 killed. Tallahassee, FL.\nCause: Shooting, Drowning · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice arrested Henry Segura in Minnesota 10 months after his ex-girlfriend and three children were found dead in their home. The ex-girlfriend and one of her children were shot at their Saddle Creek Run home. The other children were drowned and all thre\nCensus Tract 2 (ACS 2006-2010): 26.3% in poverty, median household income $34,375, 85.9% white, 8.2% Black, 4.8% Hispanic/Latino, 20.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Tallahassee Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.78,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.73,"nearest_level1_center":"Uf Health Shands Hospital","nearest_level1_km":206.58,"nearest_level1_miles":128.36,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.280731,30.438255]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-205","properties":{"name":"Bonne Terre, MO","date":"2010-11-30","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Strangulation","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9503","acs_period":"2006-2010","pct_poverty_tract":18.011943817138672,"median_income_tract":38161,"summary":"Nov 30, 2010: 4 killed. Bonne Terre, MO.\nCause: Shooting, Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nNathan Fortner's ex-girlfriend and two of her relatives were shot dead at their home. The body of a fourth victim was found in an abandoned house where the ex-girlfriend said Fortner had sexually assaulted her just days before. Fortner committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 9503 (ACS 2006-2010): 18.0% in poverty, median household income $38,161, 79.7% white, 16.5% Black, 1.4% Hispanic/Latino, 10.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Parkland Health Center - Farmington","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":18.89,"nearest_trauma_miles":11.74,"nearest_level1_center":"Ssm Health St. Clare Hospital - Fenton","nearest_level1_km":67.47,"nearest_level1_miles":41.93,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.554642,37.924229]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-126","properties":{"name":"Tucson, AZ","date":"2011-01-08","killed":6,"injured":14,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 47.14, Pima County, Arizona","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":5.954596042633057,"median_income_tract":85038,"summary":"Jan 8, 2011: 6 killed, 14 injured. Tucson, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nJared Lee Loughner went to an event for Rep. Gabrielle Giffords and shot her and constituents waiting to speak with her. Six died and 13 others, including Giffords, were hurt. Loughner pleaded guilty in 2013 to avoid the death penalty and was sentenced t\nCensus Tract 47.14, Pima County, Arizona (ACS 2011-2015): 6.0% in poverty, median household income $85,038, 72.7% white, 3.6% Black, 13.0% Hispanic/Latino, 14.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Carondelet Marana Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":10.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.54,"nearest_level1_center":"Carondelet Marana Hospital","nearest_level1_km":10.52,"nearest_level1_miles":6.54,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-110.977371,32.335587]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-193","properties":{"name":"Minot, ND","date":"2011-01-28","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 101, Ward County, North Dakota","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":18.147382736206055,"median_income_tract":30656,"summary":"Jan 28, 2011: 4 killed. Minot, ND.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAn oilfield worker killed the mother of his child, then went across town to kill her brother, her mother, and her mother's boyfriend. Omar Kalmio, 27, spared his infant daughter. He will remain in prison for life without the chance for parole.\nCensus Tract 101, Ward County, North Dakota (ACS 2011-2015): 18.1% in poverty, median household income $30,656, 82.4% white, 5.3% Black, 4.7% Hispanic/Latino, 21.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Trinity Hospitals","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":0.17,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.1,"nearest_level1_center":"Sanford Medical Center Fargo","nearest_level1_km":365.86,"nearest_level1_miles":227.34,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-101.296272,48.23251]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-137","properties":{"name":"Willowbrook, CA","date":"2011-02-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5414, Los Angeles County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":34.91884231567383,"median_income_tract":35833,"summary":"Feb 11, 2011: 4 killed. Willowbrook, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThree brothers and a cousin were shot on their patio while watching a Los Angeles Lakers game on TV. Police have said the shooting is gang related. It has not been solved.\nCensus Tract 5414, Los Angeles County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 34.9% in poverty, median household income $35,833, 0.6% white, 16.1% Black, 80.8% Hispanic/Latino, 7.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Francis Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.04,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.89,"nearest_level1_center":"Lac - Harbor Ucla Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":10.9,"nearest_level1_miles":6.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.230736,33.914394]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-238","properties":{"name":"Brooklyn, NY","date":"2011-02-11","killed":4,"injured":5,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing, Vehicle crash","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 854, Kings County, New York","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":8.143153190612793,"median_income_tract":39819,"summary":"Feb 11, 2011: 4 killed, 5 injured. Brooklyn, NY.\nCause: Stabbing, Vehicle crash · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nMaksim Gelman was sentenced to 200 years in prison in connection to a daylong string of stabbing attacks and carjackings. Four people died and four were injured. A manhunt for Gelman ended when police arrested him in Times Square.\nCensus Tract 854, Kings County, New York (ACS 2011-2015): 8.1% in poverty, median household income $39,819, 0.0% white, 86.7% Black, 7.3% Hispanic/Latino, 10.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Kings County Hospital Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.26,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.79,"nearest_level1_center":"Kings County Hospital Center","nearest_level1_km":1.26,"nearest_level1_miles":0.79,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.945,40.645245]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-138","properties":{"name":"Oak Harbor, OH","date":"2011-04-16","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 507, Ottawa County, Ohio","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":12.616278648376465,"median_income_tract":42917,"summary":"Apr 16, 2011: 4 killed. Oak Harbor, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAlan Atwater, 31, used a .22-caliber rifle to shoot his wife and three children, ages 1, 2, and 4, then himself. She had told him and her friends that she wanted to separate, according to court documents.\nCensus Tract 507, Ottawa County, Ohio (ACS 2011-2015): 12.6% in poverty, median household income $42,917, 90.9% white, 0.0% Black, 6.2% Hispanic/Latino, 11.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Health St. Charles Hospital, Llc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":31.58,"nearest_trauma_miles":19.62,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Health St. Vincent Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":37.55,"nearest_level1_miles":23.33,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.146591,41.506718]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-128","properties":{"name":"Vancouver, WA","date":"2011-04-25","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 418, Clark County, Washington","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":20.277935028076172,"median_income_tract":41458,"summary":"Apr 25, 2011: 5 killed. Vancouver, WA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTuan Dao, 37, had separated from his wife and was facing financial problems. His wife had gotten a protective order against him. He and his five children, ages 6 to 12, died in a fire he set in their home. An older daughter and his wife were not home.\nCensus Tract 418, Clark County, Washington (ACS 2011-2015): 20.3% in poverty, median household income $41,458, 67.3% white, 1.4% Black, 17.2% Hispanic/Latino, 9.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Peacehealth Southwest Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.48,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.02,"nearest_level1_center":"Legacy Emanuel Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":10.63,"nearest_level1_miles":6.61,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.661484,45.638729]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-176","properties":{"name":"West Union, OH","date":"2011-04-30","killed":4,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7704, Adams County, Ohio","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":28.361581802368164,"median_income_tract":33482,"summary":"Apr 30, 2011: 4 killed, 4 injured. West Union, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nRandle Lee Roberts spared the life of an 8-year-old girl but gunned down the rest of her family, including her mother and 11-year-old sister, as they slept. Roberts fled but was killed in a shootout with police later that day.\nCensus Tract 7704, Adams County, Ohio (ACS 2011-2015): 28.4% in poverty, median household income $33,482, 98.7% white, 1.1% Black, 0.2% Hispanic/Latino, 9.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Harrison Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":73.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":45.97,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Cincinnati Medicalcenter, Llc","nearest_level1_km":89.45,"nearest_level1_miles":55.58,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.584297,38.76968]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-305","properties":{"name":"Ammon, ID","date":"2011-05-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9705.01, Bonneville County, Idaho","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":5.9174604415893555,"median_income_tract":57799,"summary":"May 11, 2011: 4 killed. Ammon, ID.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nGaylin Leirmoe killed his sons, their mother, and her sister at their home before setting fire to it and killing himself.\nCensus Tract 9705.01, Bonneville County, Idaho (ACS 2011-2015): 5.9% in poverty, median household income $57,799, 84.7% white, 0.5% Black, 11.8% Hispanic/Latino, 1.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Idaho Falls Community Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":3.54,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.2,"nearest_level1_center":"Primary Children'S Hospital","nearest_level1_km":302.17,"nearest_level1_miles":187.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.947723,43.487591]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-165","properties":{"name":"Yuma, AZ","date":"2011-06-02","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 1, Yuma County, Arizona","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":38.85172653198242,"median_income_tract":23958,"summary":"Jun 2, 2011: 5 killed, 1 injured. Yuma, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nOne morning, four years after his fifth divorce, Carey Hal Dyess, 73, drove around Yuma County, shooting six people, five of them fatally: his latest ex-wife, three of her friends, and her divorce lawyer. He then pulled over and killed himself.\nCensus Tract 1, Yuma County, Arizona (ACS 2011-2015): 38.9% in poverty, median household income $23,958, 29.0% white, 4.6% Black, 63.0% Hispanic/Latino, 19.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Yuma Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":4.6,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.86,"nearest_level1_center":"Abrazo West Campus","nearest_level1_km":226.66,"nearest_level1_miles":140.84,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-114.62088,32.722313]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-135","properties":{"name":"Medford, NY","date":"2011-06-19","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 1591.07, Suffolk County, New York","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":3.9682538509368896,"median_income_tract":98947,"summary":"Jun 19, 2011: 4 killed. Medford, NY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 2\nA pharmacy robbery ended with David Laffer shooting four people, including two store employees, before fleeing with 10,000 hydrocodone pills. His wife, a painkiller addict, drove the getaway car. Laffer received four life sentences without parole, and sh\nCensus Tract 1591.07, Suffolk County, New York (ACS 2011-2015): 4.0% in poverty, median household income $98,947, 81.5% white, 0.0% Black, 16.2% Hispanic/Latino, 5.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Long Island Community Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":3.24,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.01,"nearest_level1_center":"Stony Brook University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":15.27,"nearest_level1_miles":9.49,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.003777,40.801105]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-206","properties":{"name":"Wagener, SC","date":"2011-07-03","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 217, Aiken County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":23.065282821655273,"median_income_tract":42687,"summary":"Jul 3, 2011: 4 killed. Wagener, SC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA 7-year-old girl watched as her mother was shot. She then grabbed her brother and walked four miles to a neighbor's house to call 911. Kenneth Lee Myers, 47, shot his wife (the girl's mother), two relatives, and an ex-girlfriend before he killed himself\nCensus Tract 217, Aiken County, South Carolina (ACS 2011-2015): 23.1% in poverty, median household income $42,687, 61.5% white, 31.4% Black, 2.9% Hispanic/Latino, 16.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lexington Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":45.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":28.36,"nearest_level1_center":"Prisma Health Richland","nearest_level1_km":51.83,"nearest_level1_miles":32.21,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.362206,33.651031]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-169","properties":{"name":"Grand Rapids, MI","date":"2011-07-07","killed":7,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 20, Kent County, Michigan","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":44.086021423339844,"median_income_tract":17981,"summary":"Jul 7, 2011: 7 killed, 2 injured. Grand Rapids, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nRodrick Shonte Dantzler shot himself at the end of a rampage that took the lives of seven people, including his wife, her parents, their daughter, and an ex-girlfriend. Dantzler had a history of threats against women, according to court records.\nCensus Tract 20, Kent County, Michigan (ACS 2011-2015): 44.1% in poverty, median household income $17,981, 58.9% white, 28.1% Black, 7.3% Hispanic/Latino, 19.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Spectrum Health - Butterworth Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.73,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.45,"nearest_level1_center":"Spectrum Health - Butterworth Campus","nearest_level1_km":0.73,"nearest_level1_miles":0.45,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.668083,42.96336]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-134","properties":{"name":"Wheatland, WY","date":"2011-07-07","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9594, Platte County, Wyoming","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":14.706342697143555,"median_income_tract":35531,"summary":"Jul 7, 2011: 4 killed, 1 injured. Wheatland, WY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAfter a lengthy mental evaluation, Everett Conant III was ruled competent. He pleaded no contest to murder in the killings of his three sons and their uncle, and one count of attempted murder in the shooting of his wife. He will serve life in prison.\nCensus Tract 9594, Platte County, Wyoming (ACS 2011-2015): 14.7% in poverty, median household income $35,531, 90.1% white, 0.0% Black, 7.0% Hispanic/Latino, 16.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Platte County Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Other designation","nearest_trauma_km":0.82,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.51,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Colorado Hospital Authority","nearest_level1_km":257.23,"nearest_level1_miles":159.83,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.952751,42.054413]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-166","properties":{"name":"Medford, OR","date":"2011-07-18","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns, Strangulation","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1, Jackson County, Oregon","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":60.59850311279297,"median_income_tract":15917,"summary":"Jul 18, 2011: 5 killed. Medford, OR.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns, Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nIn his sentencing hearing, Jordan Adam Criado said he killed his wife only after she killed the couple's four children. Yet a judge said evidence was \"overwhelming\" that Criado had stabbed and smothered his kids. Criado was sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 1, Jackson County, Oregon (ACS 2011-2015): 60.6% in poverty, median household income $15,917, 60.7% white, 0.9% Black, 34.8% Hispanic/Latino, 7.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Providence Medford Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":1.8,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.12,"nearest_level1_center":"Ohsu Hospital And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":353.08,"nearest_level1_miles":219.4,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.875595,42.326515]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-129","properties":{"name":"Grand Prairie, TX","date":"2011-07-23","killed":5,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1219.03, Tarrant County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":45.06404113769531,"median_income_tract":26642,"summary":"Jul 23, 2011: 5 killed, 4 injured. Grand Prairie, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nIn a protective-order affidavit, Tan Do's wife said he threatened to kill her when she tried to leave him. However, she then asked that the order be dismissed. Months later, Do shot and killed her, four of her relatives and himself at their son's birthda\nCensus Tract 1219.03, Tarrant County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 45.1% in poverty, median household income $26,642, 8.0% white, 19.1% Black, 66.5% Hispanic/Latino, 14.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Medical City Arlington","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.34,"nearest_level1_center":"Methodist Dallas Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":20.97,"nearest_level1_miles":13.03,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.044296,32.717445]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-120","properties":{"name":"Ocala, FL","date":"2011-08-05","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 19, Marion County, Florida","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":27.52808952331543,"median_income_tract":31389,"summary":"Aug 5, 2011: 4 killed. Ocala, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nRescue units responding to a house fire found four bodies inside. All, including two children, had been shot. Police arrested James Bannister, one victim's boyfriend, was convicted and given a life sentence.\nCensus Tract 19, Marion County, Florida (ACS 2011-2015): 27.5% in poverty, median household income $31,389, 69.9% white, 15.2% Black, 13.4% Hispanic/Latino, 24.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ocala Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":1.35,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.84,"nearest_level1_center":"Uf Health Shands Hospital","nearest_level1_km":54.04,"nearest_level1_miles":33.58,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.140091,29.187199]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-170","properties":{"name":"Copley Township, OH","date":"2011-08-07","killed":7,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5334, Summit County, Ohio","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":7.494309425354004,"median_income_tract":57017,"summary":"Aug 7, 2011: 7 killed, 1 injured. Copley Township, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nUsing two handguns, Michael Hance went on a shooting spree, killing seven neighbors and relatives of his live-in girlfriend. His girlfriend was injured in the attack. Police fatally shot Hance outside a suburban home 10 minutes after the shooting began.\nCensus Tract 5334, Summit County, Ohio (ACS 2011-2015): 7.5% in poverty, median household income $57,017, 76.9% white, 17.8% Black, 1.7% Hispanic/Latino, 11.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Akron General Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":9.76,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.07,"nearest_level1_center":"Akron General Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":9.76,"nearest_level1_miles":6.07,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.644569,41.098946]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-132","properties":{"name":"Newport News, VA","date":"2011-08-19","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 301, Newport News city, Virginia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":51.44560241699219,"median_income_tract":23611,"summary":"Aug 19, 2011: 4 killed. Newport News, VA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJohn Ragin's wife had taken out a protective order against him, but police hadn't served it before they found her and three of their children stabbed to death. Ragin was convicted of capital murder and sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 301, Newport News city, Virginia (ACS 2011-2015): 51.4% in poverty, median household income $23,611, 16.8% white, 68.8% Black, 10.5% Hispanic/Latino, 17.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Riverside Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":10.69,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.64,"nearest_level1_center":"Sentara Norfolk General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":17.08,"nearest_level1_miles":10.61,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.428001,36.97876]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-237","properties":{"name":"Chesterfield, VA","date":"2011-08-27","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1008.22, Chesterfield County, Virginia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":2.8733222484588623,"median_income_tract":104918,"summary":"Aug 27, 2011: 4 killed, 2 injured. Chesterfield, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nLeonard Egland killed his estranged wife, her boyfriend, and the man's son. He took his own daughter, age 7, to Bucks County, PA, where he killed his mother-in-law, dropped his daughter at a hospital, wounded two policemen, and escaped. He later killed h\nCensus Tract 1008.22, Chesterfield County, Virginia (ACS 2011-2015): 2.9% in poverty, median household income $104,918, 83.6% white, 12.1% Black, 1.5% Hispanic/Latino, 10.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Chippenham Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":15.58,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.68,"nearest_level1_center":"Chippenham Hospital","nearest_level1_km":15.58,"nearest_level1_miles":9.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.507812,37.374561]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-131","properties":{"name":"Morgantown, WV","date":"2011-09-05","killed":5,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 107, Monongalia County, West Virginia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":36.659664154052734,"median_income_tract":27806,"summary":"Sep 5, 2011: 5 killed, 2 injured. Morgantown, WV.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Other · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nShayne Riggleman, 22, had been diagnosed as bipolar. He killed five people -- family and friends of a couple who had taken in his ex-girlfriend. He then hit a woman with his car and shot a gas station attendant before killing himself.\nCensus Tract 107, Monongalia County, West Virginia (ACS 2011-2015): 36.7% in poverty, median household income $27,806, 80.5% white, 13.3% Black, 1.4% Hispanic/Latino, 24.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"West Virginia University Hospitals","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.79,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.74,"nearest_level1_center":"West Virginia University Hospitals","nearest_level1_km":2.79,"nearest_level1_miles":1.74,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.955894,39.629524]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-133","properties":{"name":"Carson City, NV","date":"2011-09-06","killed":4,"injured":7,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 8, Carson City, Nevada","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":10.713111877441406,"median_income_tract":66333,"summary":"Sep 6, 2011: 4 killed, 7 injured. Carson City, NV.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nEduardo Sencion entered an IHOP and fired about 60 rounds from an AK-47, killing three off-duty uniformed National Guard members and another patron. Seven others, including two National Guard members, were injured. Sencion shot himself in the head.\nCensus Tract 8, Carson City, Nevada (ACS 2011-2015): 10.7% in poverty, median household income $66,333, 72.4% white, 5.7% Black, 13.5% Hispanic/Latino, 8.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Barton Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":31.32,"nearest_trauma_miles":19.46,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":159.44,"nearest_level1_miles":99.07,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.769722,39.131317]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-130","properties":{"name":"Laurel, IN","date":"2011-09-25","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9699, Franklin County, Indiana","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":18.823209762573242,"median_income_tract":41709,"summary":"Sep 25, 2011: 5 killed. Laurel, IN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDavid Ison will serve life in prison in the fatal shootings of five people in a rural part of Indiana. According to police reports, Ison had previously purchased drugs from one of his victims. They fought over the price of the prescription medication.\nCensus Tract 9699, Franklin County, Indiana (ACS 2011-2015): 18.8% in poverty, median household income $41,709, 97.2% white, 0.0% Black, 2.0% Hispanic/Latino, 9.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Reid Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":48.01,"nearest_trauma_miles":29.83,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Cincinnati Medicalcenter, Llc","nearest_level1_km":71.23,"nearest_level1_miles":44.26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.186356,39.500881]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-125","properties":{"name":"Seal Beach, CA","date":"2011-10-12","killed":8,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 995.11, Orange County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":7.328833103179932,"median_income_tract":85588,"summary":"Oct 12, 2011: 8 killed, 1 injured. Seal Beach, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nPolice say a custody battle may have sparked the fatal shooting of eight people at a beauty salon. Scott Dekraai pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life without parole in the slayings of his ex-wife and others, including a man parked outside the shop.\nCensus Tract 995.11, Orange County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 7.3% in poverty, median household income $85,588, 72.3% white, 0.0% Black, 19.9% Hispanic/Latino, 11.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Mary Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":8.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.39,"nearest_level1_center":"Lac - Harbor Ucla Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":19.91,"nearest_level1_miles":12.37,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.10479,33.741405]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-139","properties":{"name":"Liberty, SC","date":"2011-10-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Profit","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 110.03, Pickens County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":29.391237258911133,"median_income_tract":34615,"summary":"Oct 14, 2011: 4 killed. Liberty, SC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Profit · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSusan Hendricks received four life sentences after pleading guilty but mentally ill to the slayings of her two sons, her ex-husband, and another family member. Hendricks, who suffered from multiple mental illnesses, committed the crimes for insurance mon\nCensus Tract 110.03, Pickens County, South Carolina (ACS 2011-2015): 29.4% in poverty, median household income $34,615, 94.1% white, 2.4% Black, 1.3% Hispanic/Latino, 8.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Anmed Health Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":25.18,"nearest_trauma_miles":15.64,"nearest_level1_center":"Prisma Health Greenville Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":27.62,"nearest_level1_miles":17.17,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.697029,34.734035]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-190","properties":{"name":"Lander, WY","date":"2011-11-10","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Vehicle crash","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 2, Fremont County, Wyoming","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":6.64946985244751,"median_income_tract":54274,"summary":"Nov 10, 2011: 4 killed. Lander, WY.\nCause: Vehicle crash · Type: Other · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nMatthew Denton, 17, drove his Chevrolet Suburban at 97 mph into a Dodge Caravan moving at 50-55 mph., killing himself and those in the other vehicle: a woman, her ex-husband, their son, and his girlfriend. The coroner ruled the act a murder-suicide.\nCensus Tract 2, Fremont County, Wyoming (ACS 2011-2015): 6.6% in poverty, median household income $54,274, 95.2% white, 0.0% Black, 2.6% Hispanic/Latino, 6.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sagewest Health Care - Lander","nearest_trauma_level":"Other designation","nearest_trauma_km":1.43,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.89,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Utah Hospitals And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":344.66,"nearest_level1_miles":214.16,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-108.730675,42.833015]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-167","properties":{"name":"Greensboro, NC","date":"2011-11-20","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 108, Guilford County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":21.76322364807129,"median_income_tract":43169,"summary":"Nov 20, 2011: 5 killed, 1 injured. Greensboro, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nForty hours after gaining custody of her deceased sister's three kids, Mary Ann Holder allegedly shot and killed two of them, along with two of her own and her son's girlfriend. Police said the stress of the custody case, along with an ended affair, cont\nCensus Tract 108, Guilford County, North Carolina (ACS 2011-2015): 21.8% in poverty, median household income $43,169, 62.2% white, 31.3% Black, 4.7% Hispanic/Latino, 11.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Cone Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.09,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.3,"nearest_level1_center":"North Carolina Baptist Hospital","nearest_level1_km":42.84,"nearest_level1_miles":26.62,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.791977,36.072636]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-140","properties":{"name":"Bay City, TX","date":"2011-11-30","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7303.01, Matagorda County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":24.058473587036133,"median_income_tract":50786,"summary":"Nov 30, 2011: 4 killed, 1 injured. Bay City, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJose Avila-Alva's wife refused to file domestic assault charges after an incident the week before. He opened fire on his four children in the family's front yard, killing them and committing suicide. His wife was injured but survived the shooting.\nCensus Tract 7303.01, Matagorda County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 24.1% in poverty, median household income $50,786, 52.0% white, 1.5% Black, 42.6% Hispanic/Latino, 12.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Matagorda Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":2.19,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.36,"nearest_level1_center":"Texas Childrens Hospital","nearest_level1_km":97.61,"nearest_level1_miles":60.65,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.969398,28.982756]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-136","properties":{"name":"Gargatha, VA","date":"2011-12-15","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 904, Accomack County, Virginia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":20.512392044067383,"median_income_tract":40865,"summary":"Dec 15, 2011: 4 killed. Gargatha, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nEsteban Quintero Gonzales forced his way into a trailer and shot and killed four people inside, including his two children and their mother, before killing himself. The couple had been involved in an ongoing custody dispute, sheriff's deputies said.\nCensus Tract 904, Accomack County, Virginia (ACS 2011-2015): 20.5% in poverty, median household income $40,865, 35.1% white, 38.9% Black, 24.2% Hispanic/Latino, 19.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Tidalhealth Peninsula Regional, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":62.3,"nearest_trauma_miles":38.71,"nearest_level1_center":"Children'S Hospital Of The King'S Daughters","nearest_level1_km":121.87,"nearest_level1_miles":75.73,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.591568,37.801907]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-174","properties":{"name":"Emington, IL","date":"2011-12-16","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9602, Livingston County, Illinois","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":9.805046081542969,"median_income_tract":58201,"summary":"Dec 16, 2011: 4 killed. Emington, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSara McMeen, 30, struggled with bipolar medication and postpartum depression. She shot her live-in boyfriend, two children and her 10-month-old daughter before killing herself. Forty years before, her father shot his first wife in a schizophrenic episode\nCensus Tract 9602, Livingston County, Illinois (ACS 2011-2015): 9.8% in poverty, median household income $58,201, 80.6% white, 12.8% Black, 4.3% Hispanic/Latino, 7.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Riverside Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":43.51,"nearest_trauma_miles":27.04,"nearest_level1_center":"The Carle Foundation Hospital","nearest_level1_km":95.59,"nearest_level1_miles":59.39,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.358109,40.969753]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-127","properties":{"name":"Grapevine, TX","date":"2011-12-25","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1137.05, Tarrant County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":19.005584716796875,"median_income_tract":44761,"summary":"Dec 25, 2011: 6 killed. Grapevine, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA family had just finished opening Christmas presents when a relative dressed as Santa Claus opened fire, killing six before shooting himself. Azizolah \"Bob\" Yazdanpanah faced foreclosure and had recently separated from his wife, one of the victims.\nCensus Tract 1137.05, Tarrant County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 19.0% in poverty, median household income $44,761, 52.6% white, 1.2% Black, 43.8% Hispanic/Latino, 10.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Baylor Scott And White Medical Center - Grapevine","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":1.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.95,"nearest_level1_center":"Parkland Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":26.29,"nearest_level1_miles":16.34,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.078064,32.934292]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-159","properties":{"name":"Villa Park, IL","date":"2012-01-17","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8432, DuPage County, Illinois","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":14.940043449401855,"median_income_tract":52813,"summary":"Jan 17, 2012: 4 killed. Villa Park, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA man facing prison described himself as despondent before he shot his girlfriend and three teenage relatives as they slept. Cedric Anderson, who a month earlier had been found guilty of heroin possession, set the house afire and then committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 8432, DuPage County, Illinois (ACS 2011-2015): 14.9% in poverty, median household income $52,813, 65.3% white, 9.4% Black, 23.4% Hispanic/Latino, 5.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Elmhurst Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":5.28,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.28,"nearest_level1_center":"Good Samaritan Hospital - Advocate","nearest_level1_km":8.08,"nearest_level1_miles":5.02,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.988953,41.889751]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-151","properties":{"name":"Birmingham, AL","date":"2012-01-29","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 37, Jefferson County, Alabama","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":26.155794143676758,"median_income_tract":26678,"summary":"Jan 29, 2012: 5 killed. Birmingham, AL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 3\nFive men playing poker inside a Birmingham home were shot to death. Police said the slayings started as a robbery. Reginald Mims was sentenced to 25 years. Artavius Underwood and Rashad Stoves are serving life in prison.\nCensus Tract 37, Jefferson County, Alabama (ACS 2011-2015): 26.2% in poverty, median household income $26,678, 6.0% white, 84.2% Black, 4.1% Hispanic/Latino, 16.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Princeton Baptist Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":3.31,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.06,"nearest_level1_center":"Children'S Hospital Of Alabama","nearest_level1_km":7.24,"nearest_level1_miles":4.5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.882851,33.497475]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-144","properties":{"name":"Norcross, GA","date":"2012-02-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 503.11, Gwinnett County, Georgia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":9.187408447265625,"median_income_tract":94559,"summary":"Feb 21, 2012: 4 killed. Norcross, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nJeong Soo Paek entered his sisters' suburban Atlanta spa and shot them and their husbands before killing himself. In 2006, one sister had gotten a temporary restraining order against Paek, who had threatened to harm them with guns at the salon.\nCensus Tract 503.11, Gwinnett County, Georgia (ACS 2011-2015): 9.2% in poverty, median household income $94,559, 58.3% white, 19.0% Black, 8.2% Hispanic/Latino, 7.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Children'S Healthcare Of Atlanta At Scottish Rite","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level II","nearest_trauma_km":13.53,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.41,"nearest_level1_center":"Wellstar Atlanta Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":24.71,"nearest_level1_miles":15.36,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.213531,33.941212]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-149","properties":{"name":"San Francisco, CA","date":"2012-03-23","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 201, San Francisco County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":28.246753692626953,"median_income_tract":36951,"summary":"Mar 23, 2012: 5 killed. San Francisco, CA.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFive people were killed in their home with what prosecutors described as a \"blunt instrument.\" No motive has been revealed. Binh Thai Luc, 35, pleaded not guilty to five counts of murder, robbery, burglary and lying in wait. He was convicted and sentence\nCensus Tract 201, San Francisco County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 28.2% in poverty, median household income $36,951, 28.4% white, 4.1% Black, 43.8% Hispanic/Latino, 10.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Priscilla Chan And Mark Zuckerberg San Francisco General Hospital And Trauma Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.37,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.47,"nearest_level1_center":"Priscilla Chan And Mark Zuckerberg San Francisco General Hospital And Trauma Center","nearest_level1_km":2.37,"nearest_level1_miles":1.47,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.419418,37.774929]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-146","properties":{"name":"Oakland, CA","date":"2012-04-02","killed":7,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"College","tract":"Census Tract 4029, Alameda County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":25.018287658691406,"median_income_tract":31319,"summary":"Apr 2, 2012: 7 killed, 3 injured. Oakland, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: College · Offenders: 1\nA former nursing student is accused of using a handgun to kill seven at Oikos University, a small private college in East Oakland. One Goh has been treated in a state mental hospital ever since, but in October 2015 was deemed competent to stand trial. Go\nCensus Tract 4029, Alameda County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 25.0% in poverty, median household income $31,319, 23.2% white, 17.2% Black, 11.2% Hispanic/Latino, 3.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Highland Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.53,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.2,"nearest_level1_center":"Highland Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.53,"nearest_level1_miles":2.2,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.270805,37.804371]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-147","properties":{"name":"Gilbert, AZ","date":"2012-05-02","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4224.02, Maricopa County, Arizona","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":18.381790161132812,"median_income_tract":52866,"summary":"May 2, 2012: 4 killed. Gilbert, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJason \"J.T.\" Ready, a well-known white supremacist who had run for public office, shot his girlfriend, three of her family members and then himself. In February, police told Ready's girlfriend to get a protective order against him; she declined.\nCensus Tract 4224.02, Maricopa County, Arizona (ACS 2011-2015): 18.4% in poverty, median household income $52,866, 60.8% white, 0.5% Black, 29.9% Hispanic/Latino, 4.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Banner Gateway Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":7.09,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.4,"nearest_level1_center":"Banner Desert Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":9.18,"nearest_level1_miles":5.7,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.789024,33.352825]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-154","properties":{"name":"Port St. John, FL","date":"2012-05-15","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 621.08, Brevard County, Florida","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":8.258310317993164,"median_income_tract":53142,"summary":"May 15, 2012: 4 killed. Port St. John, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTonya Thomas killed her four teenage and pre-teen children, shooting them a total of 18 times before killing herself. Three of the kids went to a neighbor's house to say their mother shot them, but Thomas called them back inside.\nCensus Tract 621.08, Brevard County, Florida (ACS 2011-2015): 8.3% in poverty, median household income $53,142, 79.1% white, 7.0% Black, 9.0% Hispanic/Latino, 10.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Holmes Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":47.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":29.63,"nearest_level1_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":57.3,"nearest_level1_miles":35.6,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.792519,28.486328]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-202","properties":{"name":"Summersville, WV","date":"2012-05-19","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 9506, Nicholas County, West Virginia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":13.148660659790039,"median_income_tract":39232,"summary":"May 19, 2012: 4 killed. Summersville, WV.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nThe bodies of a man, his girlfriend and two children were found naked in the woods a mile from their vehicle. Police said the killings occurred over a drug debt. James Roy Belknap received a life sentence for four counts of first-degree murder.\nCensus Tract 9506, Nicholas County, West Virginia (ACS 2011-2015): 13.1% in poverty, median household income $39,232, 98.3% white, 0.0% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 15.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Summersville Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":18.95,"nearest_trauma_miles":11.78,"nearest_level1_center":"Charleston Area Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":84.35,"nearest_level1_miles":52.41,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.690926,38.161224]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-148","properties":{"name":"Salem, OR","date":"2012-05-22","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 16.04, Marion County, Oregon","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":19.048826217651367,"median_income_tract":39568,"summary":"May 22, 2012: 5 killed. Salem, OR.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nNikolay Lazukin shot his wife and two daughters, suffocated his infant and set the house ablaze. He also used a baseball bat to kill a neighbor who was walking nearby. Lazukin killed himself after sending an apologetic text message to his father-in-law.\nCensus Tract 16.04, Marion County, Oregon (ACS 2011-2015): 19.0% in poverty, median household income $39,568, 44.3% white, 3.4% Black, 39.0% Hispanic/Latino, 7.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Salem Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":4.67,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.9,"nearest_level1_center":"Ohsu Hospital And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":64.46,"nearest_level1_miles":40.06,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.988701,44.959801]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-150","properties":{"name":"Seattle, WA","date":"2012-05-30","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 44, King County, Washington","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":36.04084777832031,"median_income_tract":50500,"summary":"May 30, 2012: 5 killed, 1 injured. Seattle, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nIan Lee Stawicki, 40, entered a Seattle coffee shop and shot and killed four. He then killed a woman for her car, leading police on a chase that ended with Stawicki killing himself.\nCensus Tract 44, King County, Washington (ACS 2011-2015): 36.0% in poverty, median household income $50,500, 76.1% white, 3.5% Black, 6.3% Hispanic/Latino, 8.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Seattle Children'S","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric","nearest_trauma_km":2.8,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.74,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":7.53,"nearest_level1_miles":4.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.317078,47.67144]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-161","properties":{"name":"Tempe, AZ","date":"2012-06-02","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3191.04, Maricopa County, Arizona","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":52.89534378051758,"median_income_tract":28966,"summary":"Jun 2, 2012: 4 killed. Tempe, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDealing with a brain tumor and facing a bitter divorce, James Butwin allegedly killed his wife and three children, loaded their bodies in an SUV, took it to the desert and set it on fire. A business partner called police after finding \"blood everywhere\"\nCensus Tract 3191.04, Maricopa County, Arizona (ACS 2011-2015): 52.9% in poverty, median household income $28,966, 44.8% white, 4.0% Black, 22.4% Hispanic/Latino, 22.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Banner Desert Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.07,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.53,"nearest_level1_center":"Banner Desert Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":4.07,"nearest_level1_miles":2.53,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.909309,33.414768]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-179","properties":{"name":"Newton Falls, OH","date":"2012-07-06","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9336, Trumbull County, Ohio","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":16.829666137695312,"median_income_tract":42031,"summary":"Jul 6, 2012: 4 killed. Newton Falls, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA 5-year-old boy escaped and told neighbors that \"Daddy's dead\" right after Robert Brazzon had shot his ex-brother-in-law, his wife, and their teenage son. Brazzon earlier had killed his live-in girlfriend. Brazzon shot himself after a brief standoff wit\nCensus Tract 9336, Trumbull County, Ohio (ACS 2011-2015): 16.8% in poverty, median household income $42,031, 94.3% white, 0.2% Black, 3.5% Hispanic/Latino, 6.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Health St. Joseph Warren Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":17.46,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.85,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Health St. Elizabeth Youngstown Hospital","nearest_level1_km":28.11,"nearest_level1_miles":17.46,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.978149,41.188389]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-122","properties":{"name":"Aurora, CO","date":"2012-07-20","killed":12,"injured":70,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 76, Arapahoe County, Colorado","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":28.424657821655273,"median_income_tract":30060,"summary":"Jul 20, 2012: 12 killed, 70 injured. Aurora, CO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nJames E. Holmes opened fire in an Aurora, Colo., movie theater, killing 12 and injuring 70. Holmes, who had pleaded not guilty by reason of insanity, was found guilty of first-degree murder. He was sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 76, Arapahoe County, Colorado (ACS 2011-2015): 28.4% in poverty, median household income $30,060, 28.3% white, 16.6% Black, 47.7% Hispanic/Latino, 3.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Of Colorado Hospital Anschutz Inpatient","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.02,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Colorado Hospital Anschutz Inpatient","nearest_level1_km":1.63,"nearest_level1_miles":1.02,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.831917,39.729431]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-145","properties":{"name":"Oak Creek, WI","date":"2012-08-05","killed":7,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"House of worship","tract":"Census Tract 1602.02, Milwaukee County, Wisconsin","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":7.198153018951416,"median_income_tract":57264,"summary":"Aug 5, 2012: 7 killed, 3 injured. Oak Creek, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: House of worship · Offenders: 1\nWade M. Page, 40, lead guitarist in a white-power band named End Apathy, entered a Sikh temple in Oak Creek, Wis., and killed six with a handgun. He wounded three, including a police officer. After police shot Page in the stomach, he killed himself. One\nCensus Tract 1602.02, Milwaukee County, Wisconsin (ACS 2011-2015): 7.2% in poverty, median household income $57,264, 81.8% white, 1.4% Black, 9.6% Hispanic/Latino, 7.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Aurora St Lukes Med Ctr South Shore","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":5.7,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.54,"nearest_level1_center":"Childrens Hospital Of Wisconsin","nearest_level1_km":21.78,"nearest_level1_miles":13.54,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.863136,42.885849]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-142","properties":{"name":"Minneapolis, MN","date":"2012-09-27","killed":6,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 1261, Hennepin County, Minnesota","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":18.423076629638672,"median_income_tract":70669,"summary":"Sep 27, 2012: 6 killed, 2 injured. Minneapolis, MN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nAfter he was fired from a Minneapolis sign company, Andrew J. Engeldinger shot and killed five people before killing himself.\nCensus Tract 1261, Hennepin County, Minnesota (ACS 2011-2015): 18.4% in poverty, median household income $70,669, 54.3% white, 22.1% Black, 4.9% Hispanic/Latino, 11.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hennepin County Medical Ctr","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.88,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.55,"nearest_level1_center":"Hennepin County Medical Ctr","nearest_level1_km":0.88,"nearest_level1_miles":0.55,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-93.26384,44.979965]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-123","properties":{"name":"Denver, CO","date":"2012-10-17","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 27.01, Denver County, Colorado","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":17.403945922851562,"median_income_tract":36602,"summary":"Oct 17, 2012: 5 killed. Denver, CO.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 3\nFirefighters responding to a blaze at Fero's Bar & Grill found five people inside stabbed to death. Joseph Hill pleaded guilty to murder and received a life sentence. His brother Lynell was sentenced to 70 years. Dexter Lewis was sentenced to life.\nCensus Tract 27.01, Denver County, Colorado (ACS 2011-2015): 17.4% in poverty, median household income $36,602, 72.0% white, 4.1% Black, 15.8% Hispanic/Latino, 6.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Denver Health Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.33,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Denver Health Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.33,"nearest_level1_miles":0.83,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.984703,39.739155]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-152","properties":{"name":"Park City, TN","date":"2012-10-22","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting, Blunt force","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9754, Lincoln County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":19.726613998413086,"median_income_tract":41685,"summary":"Oct 22, 2012: 5 killed. Park City, TN.\nCause: Shooting, Blunt force · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nOfficials said a financial dispute resulted in two men killing girlfriends and others connected with a drug ring associate. Zakkawanda Moss was convicted and sentenced to life in prison. Henry Lee Burrell was convicted and sentenced to life.\nCensus Tract 9754, Lincoln County, Tennessee (ACS 2011-2015): 19.7% in poverty, median household income $41,685, 85.0% white, 8.8% Black, 0.5% Hispanic/Latino, 10.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Huntsville Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":40.11,"nearest_trauma_miles":24.92,"nearest_level1_center":"The Huntsville Hospital","nearest_level1_km":40.11,"nearest_level1_miles":24.92,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.571106,35.082027]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-157","properties":{"name":"New Town, ND","date":"2012-11-18","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9404, Mountrail County, North Dakota","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":18.623212814331055,"median_income_tract":59250,"summary":"Nov 18, 2012: 4 killed, 1 injured. New Town, ND.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nKalcie Eagle, 21, lived a block away from the family he is accused of killing. A grandmother and three of her grandchildren were shot in their home. A 12-year-old who played dead called 911. Eagle stabbed himself to death in front of police hours later.\nCensus Tract 9404, Mountrail County, North Dakota (ACS 2011-2015): 18.6% in poverty, median household income $59,250, 27.0% white, 0.1% Black, 8.8% Hispanic/Latino, 37.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Trinity Hospitals","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":93.1,"nearest_trauma_miles":57.85,"nearest_level1_center":"Sanford Medical Center Fargo","nearest_level1_km":440.82,"nearest_level1_miles":273.91,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-102.490181,47.980846]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-141","properties":{"name":"Northridge, CA","date":"2012-12-02","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 1113.01, Los Angeles County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":15.321459770202637,"median_income_tract":51592,"summary":"Dec 2, 2012: 4 killed. Northridge, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nFour adults were shot dead in the front yard of an unlicensed boarding house in the Northridge neighborhood of Los Angeles. Ka Pasasouk, on probation at the time, was arrested the next day in Las Vegas. It is believed that he killed one of the victims as\nCensus Tract 1113.01, Los Angeles County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 15.3% in poverty, median household income $51,592, 34.2% white, 8.0% Black, 36.8% Hispanic/Latino, 3.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Northridge Hospital Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":4.57,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.84,"nearest_level1_center":"Providence Cedars - Sinai Tarzana Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":9.84,"nearest_level1_miles":6.12,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.51342,34.257595]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-124","properties":{"name":"Detroit, MI","date":"2012-12-04","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5172, Wayne County, Michigan","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":17.69464111328125,"median_income_tract":42500,"summary":"Dec 4, 2012: 4 killed. Detroit, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nNo arrests have been made in the slayings of four people ages 16 to 34 inside a Detroit home. The day after the bodies were found, the house was torched by an arsonist and destroyed.\nCensus Tract 5172, Wayne County, Michigan (ACS 2011-2015): 17.7% in poverty, median household income $42,500, 31.2% white, 57.5% Black, 3.2% Hispanic/Latino, 8.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Children'S Hospital Of Michigan","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.34,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.46,"nearest_level1_center":"Detroit Receiving Hospital","nearest_level1_km":2.55,"nearest_level1_miles":1.58,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.045753,42.331429]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-156","properties":{"name":"Tule River Reservation, CA","date":"2012-12-08","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 27, Tulare County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":15.068977355957031,"median_income_tract":54118,"summary":"Dec 8, 2012: 4 killed, 2 injured. Tule River Reservation, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nHector Celaya was in a lengthy custody dispute involving his three children. He shot his mother, two uncles and son on the Tule Indian Reservation before fleeing with two daughters. Before he was shot by police, Celaya shot both girls, killing one.\nCensus Tract 27, Tulare County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 15.1% in poverty, median household income $54,118, 63.2% white, 0.2% Black, 15.7% Hispanic/Latino, 39.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Kaweah Health Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":61.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":38.3,"nearest_level1_center":"Community Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":124.33,"nearest_level1_miles":77.25,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.714958,36.031281]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-143","properties":{"name":"Newtown, CT","date":"2012-12-14","killed":27,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"School","tract":"Census Tract 2302, Fairfield County, Connecticut","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":3.3898305892944336,"median_income_tract":123750,"summary":"Dec 14, 2012: 27 killed, 2 injured. Newtown, CT.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: School · Offenders: 1\nAdam Lanza, 20, killed his mother at their Newtown, Conn., home, then drove to nearby Sandy Hook Elementary School. He forced his way in and killed six adults and 20 children with a rifle, firing 154 shots. He killed himself with a handgun.\nCensus Tract 2302, Fairfield County, Connecticut (ACS 2011-2015): 3.4% in poverty, median household income $123,750, 86.9% white, 0.4% Black, 7.5% Hispanic/Latino, 3.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Danbury Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":11.95,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.42,"nearest_level1_center":"Yale New Haven Hospital, Inc","nearest_level1_km":33.03,"nearest_level1_miles":20.53,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.303452,41.413986]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-180","properties":{"name":"Tulsa, OK","date":"2013-01-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 25, Tulsa County, Oklahoma","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":30.512128829956055,"median_income_tract":36511,"summary":"Jan 7, 2013: 4 killed. Tulsa, OK.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nTwo brothers have each been charged with four counts of murder and two counts of robbery in the slayings of four women inside an apartment. Police said robbery was the motive. Cedric D. Poore and James S. Poore were both sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 25, Tulsa County, Oklahoma (ACS 2011-2015): 30.5% in poverty, median household income $36,511, 57.2% white, 17.1% Black, 10.4% Hispanic/Latino, 15.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Oklahoma State University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":1.03,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.64,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Medical Center Edmond-Er","nearest_level1_km":143.46,"nearest_level1_miles":89.14,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.992775,36.15398]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-181","properties":{"name":"Albuquerque, NM","date":"2013-01-19","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 21, Bernalillo County, New Mexico","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":33.72780990600586,"median_income_tract":20577,"summary":"Jan 19, 2013: 5 killed. Albuquerque, NM.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nNehemiah Griego, the 15-year-old son of a pastor,  was charged as an adult for using his parents' guns to shoot his mother, father and three siblings. According to the police, Griego claimed he wanted to die while in a gunfight with authorities. He was c\nCensus Tract 21, Bernalillo County, New Mexico (ACS 2011-2015): 33.7% in poverty, median household income $20,577, 46.2% white, 7.2% Black, 33.2% Hispanic/Latino, 12.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Unm Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.12,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.94,"nearest_level1_center":"Unm Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.12,"nearest_level1_miles":1.94,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-106.651138,35.084492]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-187","properties":{"name":"Herkimer, NY","date":"2013-03-13","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 112, Herkimer County, New York","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":18.566051483154297,"median_income_tract":46024,"summary":"Mar 13, 2013: 4 killed, 2 injured. Herkimer, NY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nKurt Myers, 64, shot four people, two fatally, at a barbershop In Mohawk, NY before killing two others at a car wash in the next town of Herkimer. He held police in an overnight standoff before they swarmed and killed him. Authorities do not know what pr\nCensus Tract 112, Herkimer County, New York (ACS 2011-2015): 18.6% in poverty, median household income $46,024, 91.6% white, 2.6% Black, 2.5% Hispanic/Latino, 9.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Elizabeth Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":23.61,"nearest_trauma_miles":14.67,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospital Suny Health Science Center","nearest_level1_km":93.8,"nearest_level1_miles":58.28,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.985992,43.025627]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-191","properties":{"name":"Akron, OH","date":"2013-04-18","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5083.01, Summit County, Ohio","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":70.70594787597656,"median_income_tract":13106,"summary":"Apr 18, 2013: 4 killed. Akron, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nDerrick Brantley and Deshanon Haywood were charged in the execution-style killings of four people in a townhouse in a public-housing complex. Brantley and Haywood were each sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 5083.01, Summit County, Ohio (ACS 2011-2015): 70.7% in poverty, median household income $13,106, 51.4% white, 32.3% Black, 4.2% Hispanic/Latino, 15.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Children'S Hosp. Med Ctr Of Akron","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level II","nearest_trauma_km":0.55,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.34,"nearest_level1_center":"Akron General Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.1,"nearest_level1_miles":0.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.519005,41.081444]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-192","properties":{"name":"Federal Way, WA","date":"2013-04-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 303.13, King County, Washington","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":27.474267959594727,"median_income_tract":40208,"summary":"Apr 21, 2013: 4 killed. Federal Way, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThree neighbors who tried to intervene in a domestic dispute were killed after a gunman shot a woman inside an apartment. Dennis Clark III, the woman's live-in boyfriend, was killed by police in the complex's parking lot.\nCensus Tract 303.13, King County, Washington (ACS 2011-2015): 27.5% in poverty, median household income $40,208, 46.3% white, 14.8% Black, 19.0% Hispanic/Latino, 4.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Franciscan Health St. Francis Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":1.72,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.07,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":33.46,"nearest_level1_miles":20.79,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.310425,47.303047]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-194","properties":{"name":"Manchester, IL","date":"2013-04-24","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9707, Scott County, Illinois","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":13.982916831970215,"median_income_tract":46111,"summary":"Apr 24, 2013: 5 killed, 1 injured. Manchester, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nRick Odell Smith, 43, was shot by police shortly after the slayings of five family members. Smith carried an injured 6-year-old next door and asked neighbors to take her to the hospital. He had been in a custody dispute with a relative of the victims.\nCensus Tract 9707, Scott County, Illinois (ACS 2011-2015): 14.0% in poverty, median household income $46,111, 98.0% white, 0.0% Black, 0.1% Hispanic/Latino, 11.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Pike County Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":63.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":39.68,"nearest_level1_center":"St. John'S Hospital","nearest_level1_km":65.78,"nearest_level1_miles":40.87,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.332344,39.542271]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-196","properties":{"name":"Percy, IL","date":"2013-05-10","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9511, Randolph County, Illinois","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":8.59630012512207,"median_income_tract":41475,"summary":"May 10, 2013: 4 killed, 1 injured. Percy, IL.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour children sleeping upstairs died after the house was set on fire. Four people, including the children's parents, were able to escape from the lower floors. Derrick J. Twardoski pleaded guilty to one count of murder and received a 53-year sentence.\nCensus Tract 9511, Randolph County, Illinois (ACS 2011-2015): 8.6% in poverty, median household income $41,475, 94.3% white, 0.0% Black, 4.9% Hispanic/Latino, 11.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Perry County Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":38.33,"nearest_trauma_miles":23.82,"nearest_level1_center":"Ssm Health Saint Louis University Hosp","nearest_level1_km":86.45,"nearest_level1_miles":53.72,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.618706,38.016441]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-195","properties":{"name":"Waynesville, IN","date":"2013-05-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 115, Bartholomew County, Indiana","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":13.537537574768066,"median_income_tract":57339,"summary":"May 11, 2013: 4 killed. Waynesville, IN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSamuel Sallee was found guilty of four counts of murder. The sheriff said methamphetamine was found at the rural home where a couple and two of their friends had been shot. Sallee was sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 115, Bartholomew County, Indiana (ACS 2011-2015): 13.5% in poverty, median household income $57,339, 81.9% white, 1.5% Black, 7.9% Hispanic/Latino, 11.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Iu Health Bloomington Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":56.13,"nearest_trauma_miles":34.88,"nearest_level1_center":"Eskenazi Health","nearest_level1_km":77.86,"nearest_level1_miles":48.38,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.891647,39.115051]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-204","properties":{"name":"Santa Monica, CA","date":"2013-06-07","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 7022.01, Los Angeles County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":12.761674880981445,"median_income_tract":76806,"summary":"Jun 7, 2013: 5 killed, 1 injured. Santa Monica, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nA domestic shooting turned public when the gunman left home, carjacked a woman, shot at other vehicles, and then entered the campus of Santa Monica College with a semiautomatic rifle that he assembled from a kit (I.g., a ghost . Police shot John Zawahri,\nCensus Tract 7022.01, Los Angeles County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 12.8% in poverty, median household income $76,806, 67.3% white, 0.9% Black, 19.1% Hispanic/Latino, 5.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ronald Reagan Ucla Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.93,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.69,"nearest_level1_center":"Ronald Reagan Ucla Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.93,"nearest_level1_miles":3.69,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.470665,34.017044]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-208","properties":{"name":"Hialeah, FL","date":"2013-07-26","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 7.06, Miami-Dade County, Florida","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":23.034868240356445,"median_income_tract":32818,"summary":"Jul 26, 2013: 6 killed. Hialeah, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nPedro Alberto Vargas, 42, set a fire in his apartment and shot the building managers who came to see what was wrong. He then shot a man on the street and a family of three before taking two tenants hostage. After negotiations failed, police killed him.\nCensus Tract 7.06, Miami-Dade County, Florida (ACS 2011-2015): 23.0% in poverty, median household income $32,818, 1.3% white, 0.0% Black, 98.3% Hispanic/Latino, 1.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Jackson Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":12.73,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.91,"nearest_level1_center":"Jackson Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":12.73,"nearest_level1_miles":7.91,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.312759,25.863899]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-207","properties":{"name":"Clarksburg, WV","date":"2013-07-26","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 301, Harrison County, West Virginia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":30.25936508178711,"median_income_tract":25125,"summary":"Jul 26, 2013: 4 killed. Clarksburg, WV.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice say the 4:30 a.m. fatal shooting of two men, one of whom reportedly owed the assailant money, appeared to be drug-related. Also killed were a father and son newspaper delivery team that just happened to be in the wrong place at the wrong time. Sid\nCensus Tract 301, Harrison County, West Virginia (ACS 2011-2015): 30.3% in poverty, median household income $25,125, 91.9% white, 4.7% Black, 1.1% Hispanic/Latino, 20.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"United Hospital Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":10.48,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.51,"nearest_level1_center":"West Virginia University Hospitals","nearest_level1_km":53.2,"nearest_level1_miles":33.06,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.344536,39.280643]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-209","properties":{"name":"Dallas, TX","date":"2013-08-07","killed":4,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 31.01, Dallas County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":9.964180946350098,"median_income_tract":71484,"summary":"Aug 7, 2013: 4 killed, 4 injured. Dallas, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nErbie Bowser faces capital murder charges in the slayings of his ex-girlfriend and her daughter in Dallas. Bowser was arrested 15 minutes away, inside the home of his ex-wife, who was found shot dead with her adult daughter. Four children were injured. B\nCensus Tract 31.01, Dallas County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 10.0% in poverty, median household income $71,484, 63.2% white, 10.9% Black, 14.4% Hispanic/Latino, 17.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Baylor University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.16,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.34,"nearest_level1_center":"Baylor University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":2.16,"nearest_level1_miles":1.34,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.800453,32.78014]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-210","properties":{"name":"Oklahoma City, OK","date":"2013-08-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1074.05, Oklahoma County, Oklahoma","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":3.7390942573547363,"median_income_tract":74107,"summary":"Aug 14, 2013: 4 killed. Oklahoma City, OK.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nWhen Daniel Green, who was diagnosed with schizophrenia, stopped taking his meds, he had violent episodes, relatives said. Green has been declared not competent for trial in the shootings of his mother, sister, niece and nephew.\nCensus Tract 1074.05, Oklahoma County, Oklahoma (ACS 2011-2015): 3.7% in poverty, median household income $74,107, 51.9% white, 22.5% Black, 6.6% Hispanic/Latino, 2.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Alliancehealth Midwest","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":9.69,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.02,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Health University Of Oklahoma Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":12.01,"nearest_level1_miles":7.46,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.436241,35.38678]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-211","properties":{"name":"Crab Orchard, TN","date":"2013-09-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 9708, Cumberland County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":18.27147674560547,"median_income_tract":35718,"summary":"Sep 11, 2013: 4 killed. Crab Orchard, TN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 2\nAuthorities said three teens and a young woman were shot in a car. Jacob Allen Bennett was convicted and sentenced to life without parole. His girlfriend, Brittany Moser, pleaded guilty to facilitation of second degree murder and received a ten-year pris\nCensus Tract 9708, Cumberland County, Tennessee (ACS 2011-2015): 18.3% in poverty, median household income $35,718, 97.1% white, 0.0% Black, 1.1% Hispanic/Latino, 18.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Starr Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":57.49,"nearest_trauma_miles":35.72,"nearest_level1_center":"The University Of Tennessee Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":84.15,"nearest_level1_miles":52.29,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.877625,35.908936]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-212","properties":{"name":"Washington, DC","date":"2013-09-16","killed":12,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Government/Transit","tract":"Census Tract 72, District of Columbia, District of Columbia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":12.162161827087402,"median_income_tract":106897,"summary":"Sep 16, 2013: 12 killed, 3 injured. Washington, DC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Government/Transit · Offenders: 1\nAaron Alexis, 34, killed 12 and injured eight in an office building at the Washington Navy Yard. The former Navy reservist was killed by police. Alexis worked for a base subcontractor.\nCensus Tract 72, District of Columbia, District of Columbia (ACS 2011-2015): 12.2% in poverty, median household income $106,897, 65.4% white, 22.5% Black, 4.6% Hispanic/Latino, 7.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Howard University Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.12,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.18,"nearest_level1_center":"Howard University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":5.12,"nearest_level1_miles":3.18,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.998528,38.874638]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-213","properties":{"name":"Rice, TX","date":"2013-09-20","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9701, Navarro County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":26.774629592895508,"median_income_tract":37000,"summary":"Sep 20, 2013: 4 killed. Rice, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA couple and their three children were found shot in their home. Authorities said Guadalupe Ronquillo-Ovalle killed her spouse and children, then herself. Her husband had been arrested Sept. 11 on a family violence assault charge.\nCensus Tract 9701, Navarro County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 26.8% in poverty, median household income $37,000, 55.7% white, 2.5% Black, 38.3% Hispanic/Latino, 15.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ennis Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":13.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.61,"nearest_level1_center":"Methodist Dallas Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":63.21,"nearest_level1_miles":39.28,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.504463,32.260731]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-214","properties":{"name":"Paris, TX","date":"2013-10-09","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5, Lamar County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":39.9246711730957,"median_income_tract":23078,"summary":"Oct 9, 2013: 4 killed. Paris, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA woman called police to report that she heard \"someone got shot.\" Responding officers found four men dead inside the house. Police said the shooting did not appear to be random, but they have made no arrests.\nCensus Tract 5, Lamar County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 39.9% in poverty, median household income $23,078, 40.2% white, 49.6% Black, 3.6% Hispanic/Latino, 23.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Paris Regional Medical Center North Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.47,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.53,"nearest_level1_center":"Medical City Plano","nearest_level1_km":133.75,"nearest_level1_miles":83.11,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.550522,33.665695]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-216","properties":{"name":"Phoenix, AZ","date":"2013-10-26","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1077, Maricopa County, Arizona","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":11.152318000793457,"median_income_tract":43588,"summary":"Oct 26, 2013: 4 killed. Phoenix, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMichael Guzzo, 56, used a shotgun to kill the family next door -- a man, his daughter, her husband, and their son. He also killed two of their five dogs. He crossed a courtyard, fired into a unit where dogs were barking, returned home, and then killed hi\nCensus Tract 1077, Maricopa County, Arizona (ACS 2011-2015): 11.2% in poverty, median household income $43,588, 64.9% white, 10.5% Black, 15.3% Hispanic/Latino, 18.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Joseph'S Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.6,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.86,"nearest_level1_center":"St. Joseph'S Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":4.6,"nearest_level1_miles":2.86,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-112.045326,33.511066]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-215","properties":{"name":"New York, NY","date":"2013-10-27","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 135, New York County, New York","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":18.579843521118164,"median_income_tract":62290,"summary":"Oct 27, 2013: 5 killed. New York, NY.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAn itinerant man is charged with stabbing his cousin's wife and her four children after briefly staying with the family. Police found Mingdong Chen at the scene covered in blood. Chen pleaded guilty and was sentenced to 125 years to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 135, New York County, New York (ACS 2011-2015): 18.6% in poverty, median household income $62,290, 40.9% white, 9.1% Black, 36.3% Hispanic/Latino, 13.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"New York - Presbyterian Hospital - New York Weill Cornell Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.43,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.13,"nearest_level1_center":"New York - Presbyterian Hospital - New York Weill Cornell Center","nearest_level1_km":3.43,"nearest_level1_miles":2.13,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.994041,40.771442]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-217","properties":{"name":"Terrell, TX","date":"2013-10-28","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 504, Kaufman County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":24.70732307434082,"median_income_tract":48295,"summary":"Oct 28, 2013: 5 killed. Terrell, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nCharles Everett Brownlow Jr., 36, is charged with killing five people in three separate homes and a convenience store over a span of six hours. He was arrested after being chased in a vehicle and on foot. He was convicted and sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 504, Kaufman County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 24.7% in poverty, median household income $48,295, 58.9% white, 1.5% Black, 32.5% Hispanic/Latino, 8.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Texas Health Presbyterian Hospital Kaufman","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":18.19,"nearest_trauma_miles":11.31,"nearest_level1_center":"Baylor University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":46.88,"nearest_level1_miles":29.13,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.280823,32.752689]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-218","properties":{"name":"Greenwood, SC","date":"2013-10-29","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9709, Greenwood County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":22.39280128479004,"median_income_tract":49420,"summary":"Oct 29, 2013: 5 killed. Greenwood, SC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice were called by a man saying he wanted to hurt himself. After failing to make contact with anyone inside the home, a SWAT team discovered the bodies of five victims, two of them children. Bryan E. Sweatt, 27, had committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 9709, Greenwood County, South Carolina (ACS 2011-2015): 22.4% in poverty, median household income $49,420, 63.9% white, 25.9% Black, 1.1% Hispanic/Latino, 24.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Self Regional Healthcare","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":18.14,"nearest_trauma_miles":11.27,"nearest_level1_center":"Au Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":61.75,"nearest_level1_miles":38.37,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.125679,34.014568]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-219","properties":{"name":"Jacksonville, FL","date":"2013-11-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 123, Duval County, Florida","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":21.03302764892578,"median_income_tract":36875,"summary":"Nov 7, 2013: 4 killed. Jacksonville, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAuthorities have made no arrests in the case of two sisters and two men shot to death inside a home in Jacksonville's Murray Hill neighborhood. There was no sign of forced entry. Three died at the scene, while a fourth died at the hospital.\nCensus Tract 123, Duval County, Florida (ACS 2011-2015): 21.0% in poverty, median household income $36,875, 56.4% white, 17.7% Black, 18.6% Hispanic/Latino, 11.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Wolfson Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric","nearest_trauma_km":6.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.05,"nearest_level1_center":"Uf Health Jacksonville","nearest_level1_km":8.06,"nearest_level1_miles":5.01,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.729729,30.303095]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-222","properties":{"name":"Parsons, KS","date":"2013-11-23","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Strangulation","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9502, Labette County, Kansas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":26.192893981933594,"median_income_tract":30043,"summary":"Nov 23, 2013: 4 killed. Parsons, KS.\nCause: Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA nurse and her three children -- ages 4, 6 and 9 -- were reported missing after the mom didn't show up for work. Their bodies were found in their home. David Cornell Bennett, Jr., a former boyfriend, pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life without paro\nCensus Tract 9502, Labette County, Kansas (ACS 2011-2015): 26.2% in poverty, median household income $30,043, 84.1% white, 8.2% Black, 6.4% Hispanic/Latino, 23.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Labette Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.16,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.34,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Hospital Springfield","nearest_level1_km":176.65,"nearest_level1_miles":109.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.261086,37.34034]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-221","properties":{"name":"Tulsa, OK","date":"2013-11-23","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 15, Tulsa County, Oklahoma","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":25.48179817199707,"median_income_tract":34049,"summary":"Nov 23, 2013: 4 killed, 1 injured. Tulsa, OK.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice are searching for a suspect after four adults were found shot inside a Tulsa home. Six children were unharmed and placed in foster care. The house had been the scene of several drug arrests in the past year, police said.\nCensus Tract 15, Tulsa County, Oklahoma (ACS 2011-2015): 25.5% in poverty, median household income $34,049, 49.1% white, 10.9% Black, 19.4% Hispanic/Latino, 12.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hillcrest Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":4.34,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.7,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Medical Center Edmond-Er","nearest_level1_km":149.26,"nearest_level1_miles":92.75,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.932854,36.173492]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-223","properties":{"name":"Topeka, KS","date":"2013-12-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4, Shawnee County, Kansas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":47.130558013916016,"median_income_tract":22883,"summary":"Dec 1, 2013: 4 killed. Topeka, KS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAfter finding a woman in an alley with gunshot wounds, police found her car and then her house half a mile away, where her brother, ex-husband and another woman lay dead of gunshots. The first victim died two days later. No arrests have been made.\nCensus Tract 4, Shawnee County, Kansas (ACS 2011-2015): 47.1% in poverty, median household income $22,883, 54.0% white, 23.4% Black, 16.0% Hispanic/Latino, 20.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Stormont Vail Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":1.69,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.05,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Kansas Hospital Transplant Center","nearest_level1_km":93.19,"nearest_level1_miles":57.91,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.690163,39.037617]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-224","properties":{"name":"Spanish Fork, UT","date":"2014-01-16","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 33, Utah County, Utah","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":5.838641166687012,"median_income_tract":60625,"summary":"Jan 16, 2014: 4 killed. Spanish Fork, UT.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAt their home in Spanish Fork, Utah, a police officer shot his wife, 2 young children, his mother-in-law and himself.\nCensus Tract 33, Utah County, Utah (ACS 2011-2015): 5.8% in poverty, median household income $60,625, 81.6% white, 0.5% Black, 14.2% Hispanic/Latino, 1.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mountain View Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":8.48,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.27,"nearest_level1_center":"Intermountain Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":64.01,"nearest_level1_miles":39.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.665131,40.110348]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-225","properties":{"name":"Cypress, TX","date":"2014-01-25","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5544.01, Harris County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":0.9459195137023926,"median_income_tract":125448,"summary":"Jan 25, 2014: 4 killed. Cypress, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA petroleum industry engineer, his wife and two young sons were found shot in their home about a week after they were last seen alive.  Eight years later, Feng Lu, a former business associate of one of the victims, was arrested for the shootings.\nCensus Tract 5544.01, Harris County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 0.9% in poverty, median household income $125,448, 73.2% white, 1.7% Black, 16.5% Hispanic/Latino, 1.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Memorial Hermann Cypress Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":7.61,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.73,"nearest_level1_center":"Memorial Hermann - Texas Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":38.03,"nearest_level1_miles":23.63,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.654816,29.972776]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-226","properties":{"name":"Alturas, CA","date":"2014-02-20","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Government/Transit","tract":"Census Tract 1, Modoc County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":23.23615074157715,"median_income_tract":29651,"summary":"Feb 20, 2014: 4 killed, 2 injured. Alturas, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Government/Transit · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Cherie Rhodes used a handgun to shoot five people, four of them fatally, during a tribal eviction hearing  at an American Indian headquarters in Northern California . She also used a butcher knife to wound a sixth person before b\nCensus Tract 1, Modoc County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 23.2% in poverty, median household income $29,651, 81.8% white, 0.0% Black, 11.9% Hispanic/Latino, 16.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lake District Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":79.2,"nearest_trauma_miles":49.21,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":334.76,"nearest_level1_miles":208.01,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-120.545357,41.483761]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-227","properties":{"name":"Indianapolis, IN","date":"2014-02-20","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3803, Marion County, Indiana","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":38.069969177246094,"median_income_tract":29630,"summary":"Feb 20, 2014: 4 killed. Indianapolis, IN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 4\nTwo men and two women were found shot in a small house in the Southeast side neighborhood. Police said this occurred during a robbery of money and illegal drugs. Kenneth Rackemann was convicted and sentenced to life without parole, while Samatha Bradley,\nCensus Tract 3803, Marion County, Indiana (ACS 2011-2015): 38.1% in poverty, median household income $29,630, 75.2% white, 11.7% Black, 10.8% Hispanic/Latino, 15.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Riley Hospital For Children","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":8.8,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.47,"nearest_level1_center":"Eskenazi Health","nearest_level1_km":9.08,"nearest_level1_miles":5.64,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.113571,39.716808]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-228","properties":{"name":"Petersburg, VA","date":"2014-04-19","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8107, Petersburg city, Virginia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":36.694915771484375,"median_income_tract":21154,"summary":"Apr 19, 2014: 4 killed. Petersburg, VA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA 67-year-old woman and her daughter, granddaughter and great-grandson were found after a house fire. They had been stabbed or died in the blaze. Alexander Hill Jr., who was arrested a year later in Buffalo, was charged with four counts of murder. He was\nCensus Tract 8107, Petersburg city, Virginia (ACS 2011-2015): 36.7% in poverty, median household income $21,154, 6.7% white, 86.4% Black, 5.9% Hispanic/Latino, 24.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bon Secours Southside Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":5.49,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.41,"nearest_level1_center":"Chippenham Hospital","nearest_level1_km":34.81,"nearest_level1_miles":21.63,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.404533,37.216202]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-239","properties":{"name":"Isla Vista, CA","date":"2014-05-23","killed":6,"injured":14,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"College","tract":"Census Tract 29.26, Santa Barbara County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":67.3223648071289,"median_income_tract":20640,"summary":"May 23, 2014: 6 killed, 14 injured. Isla Vista, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: College · Offenders: 1\nA 22-year-old college student frustrated over sexual rejections promised in a video to \"annihilate\" women \"on the day of retribution.\" Elliot Rodger, who was found dead, is suspected of the shootings that killed six and wounded seven others.\nCensus Tract 29.26, Santa Barbara County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 67.3% in poverty, median household income $20,640, 58.7% white, 2.9% Black, 26.5% Hispanic/Latino, 4.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Santa Barbara Cottage Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":12.53,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.79,"nearest_level1_center":"Santa Barbara Cottage Hospital","nearest_level1_km":12.53,"nearest_level1_miles":7.79,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.8592,34.414185]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-240","properties":{"name":"San Carlos Park, FL","date":"2014-06-08","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 502.08, Lee County, Florida","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":19.959115982055664,"median_income_tract":47500,"summary":"Jun 8, 2014: 4 killed. San Carlos Park, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSonny Enrique Medina, 36, fatally shot his common-law wife and their three daughters, ages 10, 6 and 2, and then took his own life. The woman had talked about leaving Medina, according to a police report. She was found with numerous bruises on her arms a\nCensus Tract 502.08, Lee County, Florida (ACS 2011-2015): 20.0% in poverty, median household income $47,500, 80.2% white, 0.5% Black, 18.6% Hispanic/Latino, 12.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lee Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":16.81,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.45,"nearest_level1_center":"Kendall Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":166.03,"nearest_level1_miles":103.16,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.82148,26.484673]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-241","properties":{"name":"Spring, TX","date":"2014-07-09","killed":6,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5534.01, Harris County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":0.8274824619293213,"median_income_tract":102582,"summary":"Jul 9, 2014: 6 killed, 1 injured. Spring, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA man bound and fatally shot six members of a family in their home. A seventh, wounded, played dead and then alerted police, who arrested Ronald Haskell, 33, in a nearby neighborhood after a four-hour standoff. Tried for murder in 2019, Haskell was sente\nCensus Tract 5534.01, Harris County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 0.8% in poverty, median household income $102,582, 72.7% white, 7.3% Black, 16.4% Hispanic/Latino, 3.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hca Houston Healthcare Northwest","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.29,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.42,"nearest_level1_center":"Memorial Hermann - Texas Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":36.57,"nearest_level1_miles":22.72,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.442238,30.041006]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-480","properties":{"name":"Philadelphia, PA","date":"2014-07-25","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Vehicle crash","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 200, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":40.88397979736328,"median_income_tract":24850,"summary":"Jul 25, 2014: 4 killed. Philadelphia, PA.\nCause: Vehicle crash · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Other · Location: Open space · Offenders: 2\nJonathan Rosa and Cornelius Crawford forced a real estate agent into her SUV and sexually assaulted her as they drove off in the vehicle. They lost control of the vehicle and crashed into the fruit stand, striking a family of four. The three children wer\nCensus Tract 200, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2011-2015): 40.9% in poverty, median household income $24,850, 1.6% white, 78.1% Black, 15.9% Hispanic/Latino, 35.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Temple University Hospital, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.49,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.3,"nearest_level1_center":"Temple University Hospital, Inc","nearest_level1_km":0.49,"nearest_level1_miles":0.3,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.148163,40.000996]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-242","properties":{"name":"Saco, ME","date":"2014-07-26","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 53, York County, Maine","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":14.565376281738281,"median_income_tract":44055,"summary":"Jul 26, 2014: 4 killed. Saco, ME.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAccording to a medical examiner's report, Joel Smith, 33, had sought help for anxiety but was not taking antidepressants because he had lost his insurance. Smith shot his wife, stepson, and two children before killing himself.\nCensus Tract 53, York County, Maine (ACS 2011-2015): 14.6% in poverty, median household income $44,055, 92.1% white, 0.0% Black, 4.5% Hispanic/Latino, 4.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Maine Medical Center -Transplant Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":22.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.76,"nearest_level1_center":"Maine Medical Center -Transplant Center","nearest_level1_km":22.15,"nearest_level1_miles":13.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-70.449005,43.49807]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-243","properties":{"name":"Culpeper, VA","date":"2014-08-03","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9301.01, Culpeper County, Virginia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":8.722467422485352,"median_income_tract":61985,"summary":"Aug 3, 2014: 4 killed. Culpeper, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA family member found a couple and their three girls shot dead inside their home. The Culpeper County sheriff said the deaths were apparently a murder-suicide resulting from a \"\"domestic situation\"\" between the two adults.\nCensus Tract 9301.01, Culpeper County, Virginia (ACS 2011-2015): 8.7% in poverty, median household income $61,985, 73.1% white, 8.5% Black, 11.4% Hispanic/Latino, 7.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mary Washington Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":49.05,"nearest_trauma_miles":30.48,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Virginia Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":68.36,"nearest_level1_miles":42.48,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.992081,38.500092]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-244","properties":{"name":"Goleta, CA","date":"2014-08-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 29.13, Santa Barbara County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":4.385504245758057,"median_income_tract":88235,"summary":"Aug 11, 2014: 4 killed. Goleta, CA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThe Santa Barbara County sheriff said dispatchers received a call from a man who calmly told them he had just stabbed his parents and two sons at the home they all shared. Nicholas Holzer was convicted and sentenced to life.\nCensus Tract 29.13, Santa Barbara County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 4.4% in poverty, median household income $88,235, 71.7% white, 0.4% Black, 17.9% Hispanic/Latino, 2.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Santa Barbara Cottage Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":7.41,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.6,"nearest_level1_center":"Santa Barbara Cottage Hospital","nearest_level1_km":7.41,"nearest_level1_miles":4.6,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.801422,34.447887]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-247","properties":{"name":"Kansas City, MO","date":"2014-09-02","killed":5,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 134.08, Jackson County, Missouri","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":4.721505165100098,"median_income_tract":55938,"summary":"Sep 2, 2014: 5 killed, 3 injured. Kansas City, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nPolice said Brandon Howell severely beat an elderly couple and fatally shot three neighbors. The couple died a week later. Howell faced a dozen charges, including three counts of first-degree murder. He was convicted and sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 134.08, Jackson County, Missouri (ACS 2011-2015): 4.7% in poverty, median household income $55,938, 65.7% white, 19.9% Black, 8.7% Hispanic/Latino, 4.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Joseph Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":4.82,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.99,"nearest_level1_center":"Research Medical Center - Brookside C","nearest_level1_km":12.74,"nearest_level1_miles":7.92,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.594627,38.893402]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-245","properties":{"name":"Hudson, FL","date":"2014-09-04","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Blunt force","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 311.01, Pasco County, Florida","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":22.904762268066406,"median_income_tract":33577,"summary":"Sep 4, 2014: 4 killed. Hudson, FL.\nCause: Shooting, Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA 27-year-old woman, her new boyfriend, and her parents were found buried a mile from their home. Adam Matos, her former boyfriend who lived with the family, was convicted and sentenced to life in prison without the possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 311.01, Pasco County, Florida (ACS 2011-2015): 22.9% in poverty, median household income $33,577, 88.4% white, 0.1% Black, 11.1% Hispanic/Latino, 15.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Regional Medical Center Bayonet Point","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":0.49,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.3,"nearest_level1_center":"Tampa General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":51.94,"nearest_level1_miles":32.28,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.690674,28.358143]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-246","properties":{"name":"Red Bank, SC","date":"2014-09-09","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Strangulation","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 210.30, Lexington County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":11.460905075073242,"median_income_tract":55926,"summary":"Sep 9, 2014: 5 killed. Red Bank, SC.\nCause: Blunt force, Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTimothy Ray Jones, Jr. led investigators to the bodies of his five children, ages 1 through 8, buried off a dirt road in Alabama. According to police, the children died days earlier in Lexington County, SC. Jones was convicted and sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 210.30, Lexington County, South Carolina (ACS 2011-2015): 11.5% in poverty, median household income $55,926, 80.3% white, 8.8% Black, 3.5% Hispanic/Latino, 2.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lexington Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":10.72,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.66,"nearest_level1_center":"Prisma Health Richland","nearest_level1_km":18.59,"nearest_level1_miles":11.55,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.220947,33.96785]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-248","properties":{"name":"Bell, FL","date":"2014-09-18","killed":7,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9501, Gilchrist County, Florida","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":34.20908737182617,"median_income_tract":29781,"summary":"Sep 18, 2014: 7 killed. Bell, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDon Charles Spirit called police to say he had killed his adult daughter and six grandchildren, ages 3 months to 11 years, and then killed himself. Authorities had investigated the family for child abuse and neglect charges 18 times from 2006 to 2014.\nCensus Tract 9501, Gilchrist County, Florida (ACS 2011-2015): 34.2% in poverty, median household income $29,781, 95.2% white, 0.2% Black, 3.6% Hispanic/Latino, 18.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Uf Health Shands Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":51.77,"nearest_trauma_miles":32.17,"nearest_level1_center":"Uf Health Shands Hospital","nearest_level1_km":51.77,"nearest_level1_miles":32.17,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.861923,29.756096]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-249","properties":{"name":"Guilderland, NY","date":"2014-10-08","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 146.14, Albany County, New York","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":7.028931617736816,"median_income_tract":80000,"summary":"Oct 8, 2014: 4 killed. Guilderland, NY.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThe bodies of two adults and two young boys were found in their home. They had been stabbed and bludgeoned to death. The case is unsolved.\nCensus Tract 146.14, Albany County, New York (ACS 2011-2015): 7.0% in poverty, median household income $80,000, 80.0% white, 4.6% Black, 1.6% Hispanic/Latino, 4.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Albany Medical Center Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":8.81,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.47,"nearest_level1_center":"Albany Medical Center Hospital","nearest_level1_km":8.81,"nearest_level1_miles":5.47,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.871178,42.69138]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-259","properties":{"name":"McKeesport, PA","date":"2014-10-18","killed":6,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5523, Allegheny County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":43.0402946472168,"median_income_tract":22335,"summary":"Oct 18, 2014: 6 killed, 1 injured. McKeesport, PA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour children, their mother and grandfather died in a house fire that critically injured their father. Court documents say Ryan Williams was angry that the father had turned him in to police on a theft charge. Williams was convicted and sentenced to life\nCensus Tract 5523, Allegheny County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2011-2015): 43.0% in poverty, median household income $22,335, 28.8% white, 58.9% Black, 9.0% Hispanic/Latino, 28.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Forbes Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":13.07,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.12,"nearest_level1_center":"Upmc Presbyterian Shadyside","nearest_level1_km":14.64,"nearest_level1_miles":9.1,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.850922,40.341076]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-251","properties":{"name":"Marysville, WA","date":"2014-10-24","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"School","tract":"Census Tract 528.04, Snohomish County, Washington","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":6.213742256164551,"median_income_tract":68472,"summary":"Oct 24, 2014: 4 killed, 3 injured. Marysville, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: School · Offenders: 1\nA 15-year-old used text messages to draw several cousins and friends to his cafeteria table at Marysville-Pilchuck High School. He shot five, four of them fatally, before killing himself.\nCensus Tract 528.04, Snohomish County, Washington (ACS 2011-2015): 6.2% in poverty, median household income $68,472, 73.2% white, 0.4% Black, 14.3% Hispanic/Latino, 3.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Cascade Valley Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":10.62,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.6,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":56.21,"nearest_level1_miles":34.93,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.154968,48.096455]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-250","properties":{"name":"Cadiz, KY","date":"2014-10-26","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9703, Trigg County, Kentucky","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":12.856515884399414,"median_income_tract":48683,"summary":"Oct 26, 2014: 4 killed. Cadiz, KY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice originally described the slayings of a couple, their daughter, and a family acquaintance as a murder/suicide. But six days later authorities charged Ryan Champion, the couple's adult son, with four counts of murder in the shootings. He was convict\nCensus Tract 9703, Trigg County, Kentucky (ACS 2011-2015): 12.9% in poverty, median household income $48,683, 97.5% white, 0.3% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 30.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Livingston Hospital And Healthcare Services, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":59.17,"nearest_trauma_miles":36.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Vanderbilt University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":120.72,"nearest_level1_miles":75.01,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.851425,36.824192]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-252","properties":{"name":"Springfield, MO","date":"2014-11-15","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Hotel/Motel","tract":"Census Tract 36, Greene County, Missouri","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":37.8405647277832,"median_income_tract":23133,"summary":"Nov 15, 2014: 4 killed. Springfield, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Other · Location: Hotel/Motel · Offenders: 1\nFour acquaintances who had been staying together at an Economy Inn were shot in their room on a Saturday morning. Three died at the scene; a fourth died of his injuries several days later. Scott A. Goodwin-Bey was charged with four counts of murder. Inve\nCensus Tract 36, Greene County, Missouri (ACS 2011-2015): 37.8% in poverty, median household income $23,133, 90.4% white, 7.2% Black, 1.0% Hispanic/Latino, 4.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Hospital Springfield","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":7.3,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.54,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Hospital Springfield","nearest_level1_km":7.3,"nearest_level1_miles":4.54,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-93.26178,37.243744]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-253","properties":{"name":"Cleveland, OH","date":"2014-11-21","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1126, Cuyahoga County, Ohio","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":67.4757308959961,"median_income_tract":12417,"summary":"Nov 21, 2014: 4 killed, 1 injured. Cleveland, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA 9-year-old girl survived a gunshot to call police about a shooting that left five dead at a Wade Park home. James E. Henderson was arrested six months later and charged with aggravated murder. He was convicted and sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 1126, Cuyahoga County, Ohio (ACS 2011-2015): 67.5% in poverty, median household income $12,417, 4.5% white, 91.0% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 16.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Hospitals Cleveland Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.16,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospitals Cleveland Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.86,"nearest_level1_miles":1.16,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.623352,41.515808]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-254","properties":{"name":"Cheat Lake, WV","date":"2014-12-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 117, Monongalia County, West Virginia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":8.172504425048828,"median_income_tract":72740,"summary":"Dec 1, 2014: 4 killed. Cheat Lake, WV.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nPolice said Jody Hunt, 39, drove to three locations around Morgantown and shot an ex-girlfriend, a cousin, and two other acquaintances. He was found that evening in his pickup truck, an apparent suicide. Hunt, a convicted felon, bought his handgun online\nCensus Tract 117, Monongalia County, West Virginia (ACS 2011-2015): 8.2% in poverty, median household income $72,740, 83.9% white, 7.7% Black, 0.1% Hispanic/Latino, 8.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mon Health Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":8.41,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.23,"nearest_level1_center":"West Virginia University Hospitals","nearest_level1_km":9.54,"nearest_level1_miles":5.93,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.849998,39.675999]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-255","properties":{"name":"Souderton, PA","date":"2014-12-15","killed":6,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Blunt force","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2072.01, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":3.706688165664673,"median_income_tract":80096,"summary":"Dec 15, 2014: 6 killed, 1 injured. Souderton, PA.\nCause: Shooting, Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSix people were killed at three locations in suburban Philadelphia. After a daylong manhunt, police found the body of suspect Bradley William Stone, a former Marine, in the woods near his home. Stone's ex-wife and five of her family members died.\nCensus Tract 2072.01, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2011-2015): 3.7% in poverty, median household income $80,096, 90.0% white, 1.3% Black, 6.2% Hispanic/Latino, 2.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Grand View Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.29,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.91,"nearest_level1_center":"Albert Einstein Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":33.57,"nearest_level1_miles":20.86,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.32074,40.306492]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-256","properties":{"name":"Rockford, IL","date":"2014-12-20","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 33, Winnebago County, Illinois","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":37.89940643310547,"median_income_tract":26954,"summary":"Dec 20, 2014: 4 killed. Rockford, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nLate on a Saturday night, neighbors heard pounding on a door, then the sound of someone breaking in, then gunshots. Police found the bodies of a woman, her two young sons, and her boyfriend. Calvin Carter, the woman's ex-boyfriend, was charged with the m\nCensus Tract 33, Winnebago County, Illinois (ACS 2011-2015): 37.9% in poverty, median household income $26,954, 46.7% white, 31.7% Black, 17.1% Hispanic/Latino, 16.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Uw Health Swedishamerican Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":4.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.58,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercyhealth Javon Bea Hospital - Riverside Blvd Campus","nearest_level1_km":12.33,"nearest_level1_miles":7.66,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.107201,42.293877]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-257","properties":{"name":"San Francisco, CA","date":"2015-01-09","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 168.02, San Francisco County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":13.052142143249512,"median_income_tract":76563,"summary":"Jan 9, 2015: 4 killed. San Francisco, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nFour men were shot inside a stolen car that was double-parked on the street. Lee Farley, 26, was arrested in connection with the shootings and awaits trial. The San Francisco police called it a case of Fillmore District gang retaliation as culmination of\nCensus Tract 168.02, San Francisco County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 13.1% in poverty, median household income $76,563, 56.7% white, 7.2% Black, 20.3% Hispanic/Latino, 19.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Priscilla Chan And Mark Zuckerberg San Francisco General Hospital And Trauma Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.59,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.61,"nearest_level1_center":"Priscilla Chan And Mark Zuckerberg San Francisco General Hospital And Trauma Center","nearest_level1_km":2.59,"nearest_level1_miles":1.61,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.425728,37.773682]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-258","properties":{"name":"Port Lavaca, TX","date":"2015-01-12","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4, Calhoun County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":17.715078353881836,"median_income_tract":56910,"summary":"Jan 12, 2015: 4 killed. Port Lavaca, TX.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA fire set to a one-room trailer concealed the fact that a woman and her three young children were stabbed to death inside. Authorities had gone to the home twice the day before because of a domestic dispute. Husband/father Jonathan Camacho was convicted\nCensus Tract 4, Calhoun County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 17.7% in poverty, median household income $56,910, 41.2% white, 0.3% Black, 53.5% Hispanic/Latino, 16.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Memorial Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":2.33,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.45,"nearest_level1_center":"Texas Childrens Hospital","nearest_level1_km":172.12,"nearest_level1_miles":106.95,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.654732,28.612963]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-260","properties":{"name":"LaGrange, GA","date":"2015-01-31","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9609.02, Troup County, Georgia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":8.587672233581543,"median_income_tract":58845,"summary":"Jan 31, 2015: 5 killed. LaGrange, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThomas Jesse Lee pleaded guilty but mentally ill to five counts of malice murder in the slayings of his wife, her parents, her daughter and a family friend. Their bodies were found at a home where Lee had been staying. Lee is sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 9609.02, Troup County, Georgia (ACS 2011-2015): 8.6% in poverty, median household income $58,845, 78.6% white, 17.2% Black, 0.7% Hispanic/Latino, 13.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"East Alabama Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":44.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":27.95,"nearest_level1_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":111.35,"nearest_level1_miles":69.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.141998,32.977562]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-261","properties":{"name":"Douglasville, GA","date":"2015-02-07","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 806.04, Douglas County, Georgia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":17.04486656188965,"median_income_tract":54792,"summary":"Feb 7, 2015: 4 killed, 2 injured. Douglasville, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Cedric Prather approached his ex-wife's home and began shooting. He killed her, another man, and two children, and also wounded two more children before shooting himself fatally.\nCensus Tract 806.04, Douglas County, Georgia (ACS 2011-2015): 17.0% in poverty, median household income $54,792, 36.6% white, 55.1% Black, 3.9% Hispanic/Latino, 6.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Wellstar Cobb Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":17.32,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.76,"nearest_level1_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":26.96,"nearest_level1_miles":16.75,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.669174,33.711147]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-262","properties":{"name":"Tyrone, MO","date":"2015-02-26","killed":7,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4802, Texas County, Missouri","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":23.937488555908203,"median_income_tract":35574,"summary":"Feb 26, 2015: 7 killed, 1 injured. Tyrone, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice found eight people shot, seven fatally, in four homes at a rural crossroads. Police said they suspected Joseph Aldridge, 36. He was soon found dead of a self-inflicted gunshot in his pickup truck on a road about 15 miles east.\nCensus Tract 4802, Texas County, Missouri (ACS 2011-2015): 23.9% in poverty, median household income $35,574, 94.5% white, 0.4% Black, 0.3% Hispanic/Latino, 23.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ozarks Healthcare","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":51.72,"nearest_trauma_miles":32.14,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Hospital Springfield","nearest_level1_km":123.94,"nearest_level1_miles":77.01,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-91.876404,37.2033]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-263","properties":{"name":"Indianapolis, IN","date":"2015-03-24","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3536, Marion County, Indiana","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":50.928504943847656,"median_income_tract":18708,"summary":"Mar 24, 2015: 4 killed. Indianapolis, IN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThree women and a man were found shot \"execution style\" in a home on the northwest side of Indianapolis. Police said someone had forced entry, and that the killings were not random. Nicholas Dunn, 36, was arrested for the crime in 2019. However, the char\nCensus Tract 3536, Marion County, Indiana (ACS 2011-2015): 50.9% in poverty, median household income $18,708, 26.1% white, 67.7% Black, 4.3% Hispanic/Latino, 26.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Eskenazi Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.08,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.67,"nearest_level1_center":"Eskenazi Health","nearest_level1_km":1.08,"nearest_level1_miles":0.67,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.187691,39.787155]}}
