{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-265","properties":{"name":"Tucson, AZ","date":"2015-05-12","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 40.73, Pima County, Arizona","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":2.7922861576080322,"median_income_tract":90988,"summary":"May 12, 2015: 4 killed. Tucson, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA man diagnosed with bipolar disorder and schizophrenia shot his parents, brother and 17-year-old niece at the family's longtime home. He killed himself before police arrived.\nCensus Tract 40.73, Pima County, Arizona (ACS 2011-2015): 2.8% in poverty, median household income $90,988, 71.6% white, 2.2% Black, 19.5% Hispanic/Latino, 2.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Banner - University Medical Center South Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":10.05,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.24,"nearest_level1_center":"Banner - University Medical Center Tucson Campus","nearest_level1_km":15.8,"nearest_level1_miles":9.82,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-110.835243,32.135426]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-267","properties":{"name":"Washington, DC","date":"2015-05-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4, District of Columbia, District of Columbia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":9.885931968688965,"median_income_tract":178750,"summary":"May 14, 2015: 4 killed. Washington, DC.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice arrested Daron Dylan Wint, whose DNA was found on a pizza crust inside the home of a local CEO. Authorities believe the CEO, his wife, 10-year-old son and housekeeper were held captive before they were killed, and their house set ablaze.  The pros\nCensus Tract 4, District of Columbia, District of Columbia (ACS 2011-2015): 9.9% in poverty, median household income $178,750, 66.1% white, 4.9% Black, 16.1% Hispanic/Latino, 9.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"George Washington University Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.82,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.75,"nearest_level1_center":"George Washington University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":2.82,"nearest_level1_miles":1.75,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.067719,38.922894]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-266","properties":{"name":"Waco, TX","date":"2015-05-17","killed":9,"injured":18,"offenders":0,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 26, McLennan County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":10.595694541931152,"median_income_tract":60687,"summary":"May 17, 2015: 9 killed, 18 injured. Waco, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 0\nA meeting between five biker gangs at a restaurant escalated into a shootout that killed nine gang members and wounded 18. Police arrested 177 people and found more than 300 weapons, including an AK-47. Officers received and returned gunfire in the melee\nCensus Tract 26, McLennan County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 10.6% in poverty, median household income $60,687, 69.8% white, 5.7% Black, 21.1% Hispanic/Latino, 5.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Baylor Scott And White Medical Center - Hillcrest","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":7.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Baylor Scott And White Medical Center - Temple","nearest_level1_km":55.49,"nearest_level1_miles":34.48,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.187576,31.553329]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-268","properties":{"name":"Deer Lodge, MT","date":"2015-06-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2, Powell County, Montana","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":14.622153282165527,"median_income_tract":39317,"summary":"Jun 7, 2015: 4 killed. Deer Lodge, MT.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMichael Augustine Bournes killed his wife and toddler inside their remote cabin, then went outside and shot his two young sons. He brought their bodies inside, lay them down together, and then set the building on fire and shot and killed himself.\nCensus Tract 2, Powell County, Montana (ACS 2011-2015): 14.6% in poverty, median household income $39,317, 89.3% white, 0.5% Black, 2.9% Hispanic/Latino, 12.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Deer Lodge Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Other designation","nearest_trauma_km":1.54,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.96,"nearest_level1_center":"Primary Children'S Hospital","nearest_level1_km":630.06,"nearest_level1_miles":391.5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-112.734276,46.400394]}}
