{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-287","properties":{"name":"Suwanee, GA","date":"2015-07-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1306.10, Forsyth County, Georgia","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":4.1277079582214355,"median_income_tract":127143,"summary":"Jul 22, 2015: 4 killed. Suwanee, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nHours after police responded to a domestic violence call at the home, the estranged husband shot his wife and her two children, as well as her father. The father survived until Dec. 4, 2015, making him the fourth death. The offender took his own life.\nCensus Tract 1306.10, Forsyth County, Georgia (ACS 2011-2015): 4.1% in poverty, median household income $127,143, 72.6% white, 3.9% Black, 8.5% Hispanic/Latino, 6.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Northside Hospital Gwinnett","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":16.38,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.18,"nearest_level1_center":"Wellstar Atlanta Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":42.32,"nearest_level1_miles":26.3,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.12339,34.082054]}}
