{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-279","properties":{"name":"Greenwood, MN","date":"2015-09-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 275.01, Hennepin County, Minnesota","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":6.319618225097656,"median_income_tract":71174,"summary":"Sep 7, 2015: 4 killed. Greenwood, MN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFive family members were found dead in their home. Authorities said Brian S. Short, 45, killed his wife and teenagers before killing himself. Acquaintances and family members said Short was depressed because his Internet business was struggling.\nCensus Tract 275.01, Hennepin County, Minnesota (ACS 2011-2015): 6.3% in poverty, median household income $71,174, 93.3% white, 1.1% Black, 2.4% Hispanic/Latino, 10.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Park Nicollet Methodist Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":14.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.09,"nearest_level1_center":"North Memorial Health","nearest_level1_km":21.1,"nearest_level1_miles":13.11,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-93.545753,44.908188]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-280","properties":{"name":"Platte, SD","date":"2015-09-17","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9701, Charles Mix County, South Dakota","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":5.190839767456055,"median_income_tract":50871,"summary":"Sep 17, 2015: 5 killed. Platte, SD.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA fire destroyed a rural home, revealing the bodies of a family of six inside. Autopsies led authorities to conclude that Scott Westerhuis had shot and killed his wife and four school-age children and then set fire to their home before killing himself.\nCensus Tract 9701, Charles Mix County, South Dakota (ACS 2011-2015): 5.2% in poverty, median household income $50,871, 97.7% white, 0.0% Black, 0.4% Hispanic/Latino, 16.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Platte Health Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Other designation","nearest_trauma_km":1.3,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.81,"nearest_level1_center":"The Nebraska Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":334.55,"nearest_level1_miles":207.88,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-98.852165,43.38596]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-281","properties":{"name":"Roseburg, OR","date":"2015-10-01","killed":9,"injured":9,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"College","tract":"Census Tract 900, Douglas County, Oregon","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":25.453397750854492,"median_income_tract":35711,"summary":"Oct 1, 2015: 9 killed, 9 injured. Roseburg, OR.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: College · Offenders: 1\nChristopher Harper-Mercer, 26, opened fire on his writing class at Umpqua Community College in rural Oregon, killing his instructor and eight other people before he was wounded by police. He committed suicide at the scene.\nCensus Tract 900, Douglas County, Oregon (ACS 2011-2015): 25.5% in poverty, median household income $35,711, 90.3% white, 0.0% Black, 4.8% Hispanic/Latino, 7.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":5.97,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.71,"nearest_level1_center":"Ohsu Hospital And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":250.95,"nearest_level1_miles":155.94,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-123.335533,43.290257]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-282","properties":{"name":"Tempe, AZ","date":"2015-10-18","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Drowning","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 3187, Maricopa County, Arizona","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":37.414031982421875,"median_income_tract":60882,"summary":"Oct 18, 2015: 4 killed. Tempe, AZ.\nCause: Drowning · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nPolice say Glenn Edward Baxter, 27, deliberately drove his estranged wife's SUV into a suburban lake with her and their three young children strapped in their car seats. The whole family drowned.\nCensus Tract 3187, Maricopa County, Arizona (ACS 2011-2015): 37.4% in poverty, median household income $60,882, 64.7% white, 4.1% Black, 16.6% Hispanic/Latino, 26.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Honorhealth Scottsdale Osborn Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":6.24,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.88,"nearest_level1_center":"Honorhealth Scottsdale Osborn Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":6.24,"nearest_level1_miles":3.88,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.936775,33.433449]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-569","properties":{"name":"Stillwater, OK","date":"2015-10-24","killed":4,"injured":46,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Vehicle crash","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 103, Payne County, Oklahoma","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":61.93336868286133,"median_income_tract":17930,"summary":"Oct 24, 2015: 4 killed, 46 injured. Stillwater, OK.\nCause: Vehicle crash · Type: Public · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nAdacia Avery Chambers intentionally drove her vehicle into a crowd at an OSU Homecoming Parade, killing four and injuring many others. She plead \"no contest\" and received a life sentence.\nCensus Tract 103, Payne County, Oklahoma (ACS 2011-2015): 61.9% in poverty, median household income $17,930, 80.4% white, 3.7% Black, 4.5% Hispanic/Latino, 14.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Stillwater Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":0.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.32,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Medical Center Edmond-Er","nearest_level1_km":62.31,"nearest_level1_miles":38.71,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.075569,36.119629]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-283","properties":{"name":"Pendleton, SC","date":"2015-11-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 107, Anderson County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":28.629892349243164,"median_income_tract":30088,"summary":"Nov 1, 2015: 4 killed. Pendleton, SC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA married couple and their elderly mothers were shot to death by an unknown assailant inside their mobile home. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 107, Anderson County, South Carolina (ACS 2011-2015): 28.6% in poverty, median household income $30,088, 65.5% white, 25.9% Black, 5.0% Hispanic/Latino, 11.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Anmed Health Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":20.66,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.84,"nearest_level1_center":"Prisma Health Greenville Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":39.94,"nearest_level1_miles":24.82,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.798019,34.649162]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-284","properties":{"name":"Palestine, TX","date":"2015-11-14","killed":6,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Blunt force","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 9509.01, Anderson County, Texas","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":15.74887466430664,"median_income_tract":42065,"summary":"Nov 14, 2015: 6 killed, 1 injured. Palestine, TX.\nCause: Shooting, Blunt force · Type: Other · Circumstance: Other · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nSix people were killed while camping on one of the victim's newly purchased land. Four men and a 6-year-old boy were shot after getting help pulling their vehicle out of mud, and a woman was beaten to death. William Hudson was convicted and sentenced to\nCensus Tract 9509.01, Anderson County, Texas (ACS 2011-2015): 15.7% in poverty, median household income $42,065, 72.1% white, 11.3% Black, 14.4% Hispanic/Latino, 17.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Palestine Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":9.41,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.85,"nearest_level1_center":"Ut Health East Texas Tyler Regional Hospital","nearest_level1_km":76.25,"nearest_level1_miles":47.38,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.722038,31.758347]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-285","properties":{"name":"Murray, KY","date":"2015-11-17","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 107, Calloway County, Kentucky","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":10.634005546569824,"median_income_tract":45268,"summary":"Nov 17, 2015: 4 killed. Murray, KY.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nState police found two adults and two children; the adults were shot while the children died of smoke inhalation from the fire, apparently set to cover up evidence of the murders. The assailant was convicted and given a life sentence.\nCensus Tract 107, Calloway County, Kentucky (ACS 2011-2015): 10.6% in poverty, median household income $45,268, 92.6% white, 1.7% Black, 2.6% Hispanic/Latino, 13.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Livingston Hospital And Healthcare Services, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":73.33,"nearest_trauma_miles":45.57,"nearest_level1_center":"Vanderbilt University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":151.99,"nearest_level1_miles":94.44,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.393669,36.616905]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-286","properties":{"name":"San Bernardino, CA","date":"2015-12-02","killed":14,"injured":24,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Terrorism","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Government/Transit","tract":"Census Tract 124, San Bernardino County, California","acs_period":"2011-2015","pct_poverty_tract":24.11055564880371,"median_income_tract":34760,"summary":"Dec 2, 2015: 14 killed, 24 injured. San Bernardino, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Terrorism · Location: Government/Transit · Offenders: 2\nA radicalized Islamic married couple opened fire at a holiday office party in San Bernardino, Calif., killing 14 and injuring 21. They were shot dead by police later that afternoon; an arsenal of weapons, ammunition and bombs were found in their home.\nCensus Tract 124, San Bernardino County, California (ACS 2011-2015): 24.1% in poverty, median household income $34,760, 12.9% white, 4.0% Black, 79.2% Hispanic/Latino, 4.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Loma Linda University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.28,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.04,"nearest_level1_center":"Loma Linda University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":3.28,"nearest_level1_miles":2.04,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-117.279884,34.076069]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-288","properties":{"name":"Rochester, NY","date":"2016-01-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 59, Monroe County, New York","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":26.233766555786133,"median_income_tract":31705,"summary":"Jan 11, 2016: 4 killed. Rochester, NY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFirefighters responding to a house fire in Rochester, N.Y. discovered four victims and quickly determined the house was a crime scene. No further details are available. police are investigating it as a homicide.\nCensus Tract 59, Monroe County, New York (ACS 2017-2021): 26.2% in poverty, median household income $31,705, 11.7% white, 42.1% Black, 21.1% Hispanic/Latino, 16.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Strong Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.88,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.65,"nearest_level1_center":"Strong Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":5.88,"nearest_level1_miles":3.65,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.570366,43.15815]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-289","properties":{"name":"Chesapeake, VA","date":"2016-01-27","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 214.03, Chesapeake city, Virginia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":22.953737258911133,"median_income_tract":57182,"summary":"Jan 27, 2016: 5 killed. Chesapeake, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice responding to a welfare check found one person dead, and a barricaded gunman in a second home nearby. After several hours of negotiations, police entered and found the suspect dead, along with four others. Police say all victims were related.\nCensus Tract 214.03, Chesapeake city, Virginia (ACS 2017-2021): 23.0% in poverty, median household income $57,182, 53.4% white, 27.4% Black, 15.8% Hispanic/Latino, 10.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sentara Norfolk General Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":8.35,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.19,"nearest_level1_center":"Sentara Norfolk General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":8.35,"nearest_level1_miles":5.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.330597,36.790428]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-290","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2016-02-04","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting, Blunt force","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 6308, Cook County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.734821319580078,"median_income_tract":57538,"summary":"Feb 4, 2016: 6 killed. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting, Blunt force · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nAfter a welfare check, police found the bodies of six family members inside their home. Five of the victims, including children ages 10 and 13, died from sharp or blunt force injuries, while the final victim was shot to death. The motive was robbery, and the murders were designed as a cover-up. Diego Uribe Cruz and Jafeth Ramos both pleaded guilty to the murders. Uribe Cruz received a life sentence while Ramos was sentence to 25 years in prison.\nCensus Tract 6308, Cook County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 16.7% in poverty, median household income $57,538, 2.9% white, 1.6% Black, 95.3% Hispanic/Latino, 8.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The University Of Chicago Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":7.6,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.72,"nearest_level1_center":"The University Of Chicago Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":7.6,"nearest_level1_miles":4.72,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.69622,41.789738]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-292","properties":{"name":"Edgerton, MO","date":"2016-02-19","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 306.02, Platte County, Missouri","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":10.282153129577637,"median_income_tract":82576,"summary":"Feb 19, 2016: 4 killed. Edgerton, MO.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA man and his wife, their granddaughter, and her three-month-old son were found shot to death outside their home. Their bodies had also been set on fire. Grayden Denham was convicted and given four life sentences without parole eligibility plus 115 years.\nCensus Tract 306.02, Platte County, Missouri (ACS 2017-2021): 10.3% in poverty, median household income $82,576, 90.4% white, 0.0% Black, 3.1% Hispanic/Latino, 5.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Liberty Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":30.31,"nearest_trauma_miles":18.83,"nearest_level1_center":"University Health Truman Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":45.64,"nearest_level1_miles":28.36,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.637245,39.492199]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-291","properties":{"name":"Kalamazoo, MI","date":"2016-02-20","killed":6,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 29.11, Kalamazoo County, Michigan","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.908119201660156,"median_income_tract":43449,"summary":"Feb 20, 2016: 6 killed, 2 injured. Kalamazoo, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nJason Dalton, a 45-year-old Uber driver, went on a shooting rampage killing six and seriously wounding two others.  According to police, in between the shootings he continued to pick up and deliver passengers to their destinations. Dalton pled guilty and was sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 29.11, Kalamazoo County, Michigan (ACS 2017-2021): 8.9% in poverty, median household income $43,449, 64.4% white, 20.9% Black, 3.7% Hispanic/Latino, 10.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bronson Methodist Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":7.26,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.51,"nearest_level1_center":"Bronson Methodist Hospital","nearest_level1_km":7.26,"nearest_level1_miles":4.51,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.667191,42.274136]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-293","properties":{"name":"Phoenix, AZ","date":"2016-02-23","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1042.24, Maricopa County, Arizona","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.838556289672852,"median_income_tract":61980,"summary":"Feb 23, 2016: 4 killed. Phoenix, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA 26-year-old shot and killed his mother, father, and two younger sisters in their family home before being killed by police. The suspect also set the house on fire, impeding police efforts to rescue any potential survivors.\nCensus Tract 1042.24, Maricopa County, Arizona (ACS 2017-2021): 8.8% in poverty, median household income $61,980, 61.8% white, 5.1% Black, 24.3% Hispanic/Latino, 3.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Banner Thunderbird Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.35,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.84,"nearest_level1_center":"Banner Thunderbird Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.35,"nearest_level1_miles":0.84,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-112.177406,33.596378]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-294","properties":{"name":"Belfair, WA","date":"2016-02-26","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9603.02, Mason County, Washington","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.11051082611084,"median_income_tract":59343,"summary":"Feb 26, 2016: 4 killed. Belfair, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA husband shot and killed his wife, her two adopted children from a previous marriage, and a neighbor, before killing himself during a standoff with police. A 12-year-old girl survived unharmed.\nCensus Tract 9603.02, Mason County, Washington (ACS 2017-2021): 12.1% in poverty, median household income $59,343, 77.1% white, 1.0% Black, 11.5% Hispanic/Latino, 8.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Franciscan Health Harrison Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":24.8,"nearest_trauma_miles":15.41,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":47.09,"nearest_level1_miles":29.26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.933472,47.503292]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-295","properties":{"name":"Kansas City, KS","date":"2016-03-07","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 435, Wyandotte County, Kansas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":11.242236137390137,"median_income_tract":57292,"summary":"Mar 7, 2016: 5 killed. Kansas City, KS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPablo Serrano-Vitorino walked into his neighbor’s house with an assault rifle and opened fire, killing four. He then fled the scene and killed another man in Montgomery County, Missouri, some 170 miles west of Kansas City, KS. He committed suicide while awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 435, Wyandotte County, Kansas (ACS 2017-2021): 11.2% in poverty, median household income $57,292, 73.9% white, 1.9% Black, 19.7% Hispanic/Latino, 8.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Of Kansas Hospital Transplant Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.38,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.34,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Kansas Hospital Transplant Center","nearest_level1_km":5.38,"nearest_level1_miles":3.34,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.672249,39.046112]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-296","properties":{"name":"Wilkinsburg, PA","date":"2016-03-09","killed":5,"injured":3,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 5647, Allegheny County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":27.1864070892334,"median_income_tract":38101,"summary":"Mar 9, 2016: 5 killed, 3 injured. Wilkinsburg, PA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 2\nIn retaliation for the murder of a friend, two gunmen opened fire at a backyard party, killing five and wounding three. Police have determined the suspect with a handgun shot in a manner that forced party-goers towards a gap in a fence where a suspect with an AK-47 rifle waited. The charges against one of the suspects were dropped while the other was acquitted.\nCensus Tract 5647, Allegheny County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2017-2021): 27.2% in poverty, median household income $38,101, 23.1% white, 64.0% Black, 4.4% Hispanic/Latino, 33.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Upmc Presbyterian Shadyside","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":7.27,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.51,"nearest_level1_center":"Upmc Presbyterian Shadyside","nearest_level1_km":7.27,"nearest_level1_miles":4.51,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.875069,40.438148]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-516","properties":{"name":"Chester, NY","date":"2016-04-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting, Strangulation","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 143.01, Orange County, New York","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.695418834686279,"median_income_tract":98750,"summary":"Apr 11, 2016: 4 killed. Chester, NY.\nCause: Shooting, Strangulation · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 3\nA man was lured to the Likquid Lounge because he owed money from a drug deal. Nicholas Tartaglione allegedly strangled him. According to the authorities, the victim’s three companions were then taken elsewhere by Tartaglione and his accomplices and were fatally shot, their bodies discovered eight months later. Tartaglione was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 143.01, Orange County, New York (ACS 2017-2021): 5.7% in poverty, median household income $98,750, 68.0% white, 6.2% Black, 19.1% Hispanic/Latino, 9.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Garnet Health Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":11.85,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.36,"nearest_level1_center":"Westchester Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":49.82,"nearest_level1_miles":30.96,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.274147,41.36216]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-298","properties":{"name":"Appling, GA","date":"2016-04-22","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 304.01, Columbia County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":4.0182647705078125,"median_income_tract":69712,"summary":"Apr 22, 2016: 5 killed. Appling, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA man shot and killed five people in two locations as a result of a domestic dispute before taking his own life as police closed in.  Some of the victims were reportedly members of his estranged wife's family, though she was not among those killed.\nCensus Tract 304.01, Columbia County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 4.0% in poverty, median household income $69,712, 76.2% white, 19.2% Black, 2.1% Hispanic/Latino, 33.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Doctors Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":17.61,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.94,"nearest_level1_center":"Au Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":26.22,"nearest_level1_miles":16.3,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.226433,33.600052]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-297","properties":{"name":"Piketon, OH","date":"2016-04-22","killed":8,"injured":0,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7701, Adams County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":29.937997817993164,"median_income_tract":37286,"summary":"Apr 22, 2016: 8 killed. Piketon, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 4\nEight family members were shot execution style at four separate locations near their homes in rural Ohio. A newborn, a six-month-old and a three-year-old were discovered unharmed. The case Involved a custody battle over a 3-year-old girl at the time of murder, between her mother and her father as well as their respective families. Angela and Edward Wagner pleaded guilty, while against George Wagner, IV was convicted a was sentenced to life without parole. According to Angela Wagner’s testimony during the trial, the family was concerned that the girl was being sexually abused.\nCensus Tract 7701, Adams County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 29.9% in poverty, median household income $37,286, 96.2% white, 0.3% Black, 0.1% Hispanic/Latino, 21.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Greene Memorial Hospital, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":94.05,"nearest_trauma_miles":58.44,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Cincinnati Medicalcenter, Llc","nearest_level1_km":106.69,"nearest_level1_miles":66.29,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.277161,39.020111]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-299","properties":{"name":"Moultrie, GA","date":"2016-05-15","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9709.02, Colquitt County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":28.411911010742188,"median_income_tract":38515,"summary":"May 15, 2016: 5 killed. Moultrie, GA.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFive friends were shot and killed by a friend who then set the house they were staying in on fire. Jeffrey Peacock told investigators he had gone out to get everyone breakfast and when he returned the house was in flames. However, he was convicted and given a life sentence.\nCensus Tract 9709.02, Colquitt County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 28.4% in poverty, median household income $38,515, 42.3% white, 7.6% Black, 42.0% Hispanic/Latino, 14.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"John D Archbold Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":43.72,"nearest_trauma_miles":27.16,"nearest_level1_center":"Atrium Health Navicent The Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":182.28,"nearest_level1_miles":113.26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.849457,31.204084]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-301","properties":{"name":"Roswell, NM","date":"2016-06-11","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 11.02, Chaves County, New Mexico","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":11.850312232971191,"median_income_tract":64659,"summary":"Jun 11, 2016: 5 killed. Roswell, NM.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA man killed his wife and four daughters before fleeing to Mexico where he was apprehended.  The extradition process is underway. Local police believe a domestic dispute led to the deadly shootings.\nCensus Tract 11.02, Chaves County, New Mexico (ACS 2017-2021): 11.9% in poverty, median household income $64,659, 61.4% white, 0.0% Black, 35.4% Hispanic/Latino, 19.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Eastern New Mexico Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":14.56,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.05,"nearest_level1_center":"Carlsbad Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":110.1,"nearest_level1_miles":68.41,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.671249,33.369862]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-300","properties":{"name":"Orlando, FL","date":"2016-06-12","killed":49,"injured":53,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Terrorism","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 185, Orange County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":11.997426986694336,"median_income_tract":51705,"summary":"Jun 12, 2016: 49 killed, 53 injured. Orlando, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Terrorism · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nA heavily armed gunman shot his way into a gay nightclub killing 49 and injuring 53, many of them critically. The gunman, who was killed by responding SWAT officers, recently pledged allegiance to ISIL.\nCensus Tract 185, Orange County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 12.0% in poverty, median household income $51,705, 26.0% white, 43.3% Black, 23.0% Hispanic/Latino, 17.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.42,"nearest_level1_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":0.68,"nearest_level1_miles":0.42,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.376793,28.519602]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-302","properties":{"name":"Los Angeles, CA","date":"2016-06-13","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Shelter/Drug house","tract":"Census Tract 2094.01, Los Angeles County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":32.76322937011719,"median_income_tract":30530,"summary":"Jun 13, 2016: 5 killed. Los Angeles, CA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Shelter/Drug house · Offenders: 1\nA dispute between two homeless men living in a vacant building led one of them, named Johnny Sanchez, to start a fire that not only killed the man he intended to kill, but four others as well. Cadaver dogs found the other homeless victims after the fire was put out. Sanchez was convicted and sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 2094.01, Los Angeles County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 32.8% in poverty, median household income $30,530, 5.8% white, 11.5% Black, 71.0% Hispanic/Latino, 6.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"California Hospital Medical Center - Los Angeles","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.64,"nearest_level1_center":"Los Angeles General Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":6.9,"nearest_level1_miles":4.29,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.283188,34.056263]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-304","properties":{"name":"Las Vegas, NV","date":"2016-06-29","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 34.20, Clark County, Nevada","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.878549575805664,"median_income_tract":50427,"summary":"Jun 29, 2016: 4 killed. Las Vegas, NV.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nJason Dej-Oudom shot and killed his children in their apartment before chasing his wife through parking lots, killing her. He later committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 34.20, Clark County, Nevada (ACS 2017-2021): 16.9% in poverty, median household income $50,427, 25.5% white, 10.1% Black, 59.4% Hispanic/Latino, 13.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mountainview Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":3.18,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.97,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center Of Southern Nevada","nearest_level1_km":6.47,"nearest_level1_miles":4.02,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-115.223824,36.195835]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-306","properties":{"name":"Shelby County/Memphis, TN","date":"2016-07-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 215.47, Shelby County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.8093976974487305,"median_income_tract":72822,"summary":"Jul 1, 2016: 4 killed. Shelby County/Memphis, TN.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nShanynthia Gardner, reportedly suffering from mental illness, stabbed her children and superficially cut herself. Her seven-year-old son managed to escape and alert the authorities. Garnder was convicted and given a life sentence.\nCensus Tract 215.47, Shelby County, Tennessee (ACS 2017-2021): 7.8% in poverty, median household income $72,822, 3.4% white, 85.1% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 6.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Methodist Healthcare - Olive Branch Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":10.43,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.48,"nearest_level1_center":"Methodist Healthcare - Memphis Hospitals","nearest_level1_km":24.81,"nearest_level1_miles":15.42,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.789803,35.016438]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-303","properties":{"name":"Dallas, TX","date":"2016-07-07","killed":5,"injured":11,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 31.02, Dallas County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":10.679611206054688,"median_income_tract":90458,"summary":"Jul 7, 2016: 5 killed, 11 injured. Dallas, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nAngry over the recent number of police shootings of unarmed black men, Micah Xavier Johnson targeted white police officers during a public protest in Dallas. He fatally shot five officers and wounded 11 other people (9 officers and two bystanders). Johnson later fled to El Centro College, where he was killed by police using a bomb disposal robot.\nCensus Tract 31.02, Dallas County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 10.7% in poverty, median household income $90,458, 69.2% white, 9.4% Black, 18.9% Hispanic/Latino, 21.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Baylor University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.51,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.56,"nearest_level1_center":"Baylor University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":2.51,"nearest_level1_miles":1.56,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.804283,32.77956]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-317","properties":{"name":"Sinking Spring, PA","date":"2016-08-06","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 109.02, Berks County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":14.611228942871094,"median_income_tract":72344,"summary":"Aug 6, 2016: 4 killed. Sinking Spring, PA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMark Short killed his wife, three children, and the family dog before committing suicide.\nCensus Tract 109.02, Berks County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2017-2021): 14.6% in poverty, median household income $72,344, 71.4% white, 4.1% Black, 17.1% Hispanic/Latino, 7.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Reading Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":6.28,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.9,"nearest_level1_center":"Reading Hospital","nearest_level1_km":6.28,"nearest_level1_miles":3.9,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.024254,40.331783]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-307","properties":{"name":"Greenville, NC","date":"2016-08-16","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 16.02, Pitt County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":21.27118682861328,"median_income_tract":47578,"summary":"Aug 16, 2016: 4 killed. Greenville, NC.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDibon Toone beat his wife and their children to death, covering their faces with blankets and clothing. He then stole a company car, drove to Virginia, and turned himself in to police. Toone pleaded guilty to the crimes.\nCensus Tract 16.02, Pitt County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 21.3% in poverty, median household income $47,578, 42.1% white, 41.7% Black, 11.1% Hispanic/Latino, 4.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Vidant Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.6,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.62,"nearest_level1_center":"Vidant Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":2.6,"nearest_level1_miles":1.62,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.432388,35.603909]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-308","properties":{"name":"Citronelle, AL","date":"2016-08-20","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Blunt force","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 60, Mobile County, Alabama","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":17.19917106628418,"median_income_tract":53958,"summary":"Aug 20, 2016: 5 killed. Citronelle, AL.\nCause: Shooting, Blunt force · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nHopped up on meth, Derrick Dearman drove to a home and killed five (including a pregnant woman), before kidnapping his ex-girlfriend and driving her to a relative's home in Mississippi. Dearman was convicted and sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 60, Mobile County, Alabama (ACS 2017-2021): 17.2% in poverty, median household income $53,958, 68.8% white, 16.5% Black, 0.7% Hispanic/Latino, 18.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Greene County Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":26.87,"nearest_trauma_miles":16.7,"nearest_level1_center":"Usa Health University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":43.04,"nearest_level1_miles":26.74,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.308281,31.049582]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-310","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2016-08-23","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4604, Cook County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":23.652942657470703,"median_income_tract":59688,"summary":"Aug 23, 2016: 4 killed, 3 injured. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Reginald Hester had made a deal with a woman living in an apartment building to have sex for $10. After taking his money, the woman went back into her apartment and did not come back out. Hester then allegedly started a fire that killed four. Hester died from a terminal illness while awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 4604, Cook County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 23.7% in poverty, median household income $59,688, 0.2% white, 98.0% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 21.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The University Of Chicago Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.61,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.49,"nearest_level1_center":"The University Of Chicago Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.61,"nearest_level1_miles":3.49,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.563736,41.748104]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-419","properties":{"name":"Temecula, CA","date":"2016-08-29","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Medical facility","tract":"Census Tract 432.92, Riverside County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":3.3450703620910645,"median_income_tract":137547,"summary":"Aug 29, 2016: 4 killed. Temecula, CA.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Medical facility · Offenders: 1\nA drunken James Steven Jennex sent a text message to a friend apologizing in advance for his actions and then fired a bullet into the heads of each of three developmentally disabled men in his care before setting his Temecula-area home ablaze and killing himself with a .357 revolver blast to the head.  The fire at the Renee Jennex Small Family Home killed a fourth developmentally disabled man and burned all five people beyond recognition. Investigators pulled a gas can from the rubble.\nCensus Tract 432.92, Riverside County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 3.3% in poverty, median household income $137,547, 75.1% white, 2.8% Black, 17.6% Hispanic/Latino, 10.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Southwest Healthcare System","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":20.58,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.79,"nearest_level1_center":"Riverside Community Hospital","nearest_level1_km":60.11,"nearest_level1_miles":37.35,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-117.032913,33.519958]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-420","properties":{"name":"Del Valle, TX","date":"2016-09-08","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 24.50, Travis County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.064516067504883,"median_income_tract":66056,"summary":"Sep 8, 2016: 4 killed. Del Valle, TX.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour men were shot and their bodies burned in a deliberately-set house fire, all believed to be connected to narcotics trafficking. The fire appears to have been set to cover-up the murders.  The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 24.50, Travis County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 8.1% in poverty, median household income $66,056, 22.7% white, 0.0% Black, 73.4% Hispanic/Latino, 9.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Davids South Austin Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":20.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.87,"nearest_level1_center":"Dell Seton Medical Center At The University Of Texas","nearest_level1_km":21.06,"nearest_level1_miles":13.09,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.585159,30.137255]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-512","properties":{"name":"Rockford, IL","date":"2016-09-17","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Undetermined","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 33, Winnebago County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":26.861568450927734,"median_income_tract":36847,"summary":"Sep 17, 2016: 4 killed. Rockford, IL.\nCause: Stabbing, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Undetermined · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nEric Jackson allegedly stabbed his neighbor and then set fire to her house, killing her and her three children. Jackson was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 33, Winnebago County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 26.9% in poverty, median household income $36,847, 26.9% white, 40.1% Black, 30.4% Hispanic/Latino, 11.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Uw Health Swedishamerican Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":4.11,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.55,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercyhealth Javon Bea Hospital - Riverside Blvd Campus","nearest_level1_km":11.73,"nearest_level1_miles":7.29,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.100571,42.296959]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-311","properties":{"name":"Dearborn Heights, MI","date":"2016-09-21","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5754.01, Wayne County, Michigan","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":14.469867706298828,"median_income_tract":72262,"summary":"Sep 21, 2016: 4 killed, 1 injured. Dearborn Heights, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAfter serving time for killing his pregnant wife in 1991, Gregory Green married the daughter of the pastor that had helped secure his release. He later tortured and tied her up, making her watch as he killed their children. Green pleaded guilty and was sentenced to prison.\nCensus Tract 5754.01, Wayne County, Michigan (ACS 2017-2021): 14.5% in poverty, median household income $72,262, 87.9% white, 0.4% Black, 7.2% Hispanic/Latino, 6.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Beaumont Hospital - Dearborn","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.09,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.3,"nearest_level1_center":"Henry Ford Hospital","nearest_level1_km":15.65,"nearest_level1_miles":9.72,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.239044,42.285278]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-309","properties":{"name":"Burlington, WA","date":"2016-09-23","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 9518, Skagit County, Washington","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":21.182836532592773,"median_income_tract":49626,"summary":"Sep 23, 2016: 5 killed. Burlington, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nArcan Cetin, an immigrant from Turkey, killed five at the Cascade Mall in Burlington, Washington. A year after being arrested, Cetin hanged himself in his cell.\nCensus Tract 9518, Skagit County, Washington (ACS 2017-2021): 21.2% in poverty, median household income $49,626, 51.8% white, 0.8% Black, 42.5% Hispanic/Latino, 5.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Skagit Valley Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":5.06,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.14,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":95.44,"nearest_level1_miles":59.31,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.339958,48.462143]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-316","properties":{"name":"Los Angeles, CA","date":"2016-10-15","killed":4,"injured":10,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 2197, Los Angeles County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.2769775390625,"median_income_tract":56976,"summary":"Oct 15, 2016: 4 killed, 10 injured. Los Angeles, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Marlon Jones went to a birthday party at a crowded home in Los Angeles and killed a rival Jamaican gang member, resulting in a shootout between rival gangs. Charges against Jones are pending.\nCensus Tract 2197, Los Angeles County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 16.3% in poverty, median household income $56,976, 5.2% white, 19.5% Black, 71.9% Hispanic/Latino, 5.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.97,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.71,"nearest_level1_center":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.97,"nearest_level1_miles":3.71,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.350677,34.027569]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-312","properties":{"name":"Jackson, GA","date":"2016-10-27","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 703.25, Henry County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.226259231567383,"median_income_tract":62941,"summary":"Oct 27, 2016: 4 killed. Jackson, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nJacob Kosky and Matthew Baker attended a bonfire party in Jackson, Georgia. They left the event for a short while and killed four upon their return. Kosky pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life without parole. Baker also pleaded guilty was sentenced to life without parole eligibility.\nCensus Tract 703.25, Henry County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 16.2% in poverty, median household income $62,941, 7.0% white, 83.9% Black, 5.7% Hispanic/Latino, 0.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":40.29,"nearest_trauma_miles":25.03,"nearest_level1_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":40.29,"nearest_level1_miles":25.03,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.146919,33.447041]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-545","properties":{"name":"Flora, IN","date":"2016-11-21","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9598, Carroll County, Indiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.956996917724609,"median_income_tract":48432,"summary":"Nov 21, 2016: 4 killed, 1 injured. Flora, IN.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA mother tried unsuccessfully to save her four daughters when their house was on fire. The mother survived but the children all perished. It was later determined that the fire was intentionally set, however the identity of the arsonist remains unknown.\nCensus Tract 9598, Carroll County, Indiana (ACS 2017-2021): 6.0% in poverty, median household income $48,432, 95.1% white, 3.3% Black, 0.4% Hispanic/Latino, 8.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Indiana University Health Arnett Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":28.99,"nearest_trauma_miles":18.01,"nearest_level1_center":"Ascension St Vincent Hospital","nearest_level1_km":76.17,"nearest_level1_miles":47.33,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.522781,40.546879]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-313","properties":{"name":"Channelview, TX","date":"2016-12-09","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 2525, Harris County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":27.431058883666992,"median_income_tract":48616,"summary":"Dec 9, 2016: 4 killed. Channelview, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nFour people were shot dead in a car that had been set on fire; two of the victims were in the trunk, and the other two were in the backseat. The case is unsolved.\nCensus Tract 2525, Harris County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 27.4% in poverty, median household income $48,616, 20.3% white, 0.0% Black, 78.7% Hispanic/Latino, 11.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hca Houston Healthcare Southeast","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":13.03,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.1,"nearest_level1_center":"Harris Health System Ben Taub Hospital","nearest_level1_km":25.56,"nearest_level1_miles":15.88,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.139183,29.77166]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-314","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2016-12-17","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4910, Cook County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":40.87255859375,"median_income_tract":21940,"summary":"Dec 17, 2016: 5 killed, 1 injured. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nReturning after having bought marijuana, Lionel Parks and an accomplice, both armed, ordered everyone in the home to take off their clothes and hand over cellphones, money and jewelry, prosecutors said.  They then discovered a woman in a back bedroom with a cellphone and reportedly became \"agitated.\" The two \"started executing the victims by shooting them in the head as they were lying on the ground,\" according to a court document detailing the charges. Four victims died at the scene. There were two survivors of the shooting. One escaped by playing dead and was able to later identify Parks. The other remained on life support, unable to respond to touch or sound, until she died more than 10 months later. Parks was arrested for murder, and charges against him are pending trial.\nCensus Tract 4910, Cook County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 40.9% in poverty, median household income $21,940, 0.1% white, 95.3% Black, 3.0% Hispanic/Latino, 34.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Advocate Christ Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":9.07,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.64,"nearest_level1_center":"Advocate Christ Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":9.07,"nearest_level1_miles":5.64,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.6259,41.703453]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-315","properties":{"name":"Wilson, NC","date":"2016-12-24","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7.01, Wilson County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":22.124711990356445,"median_income_tract":42813,"summary":"Dec 24, 2016: 4 killed. Wilson, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDereck Harris allegedly shot and killed four members of a family related to a drug debt. Charges against Harris were dropped because of unreliable and uncooperative witnesses.\nCensus Tract 7.01, Wilson County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 22.1% in poverty, median household income $42,813, 0.6% white, 73.9% Black, 23.8% Hispanic/Latino, 4.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Vidant Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":44.56,"nearest_trauma_miles":27.69,"nearest_level1_center":"Vidant Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":44.56,"nearest_level1_miles":27.69,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.873322,35.731415]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-318","properties":{"name":"Hubbard, OR","date":"2017-01-03","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Blunt force","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 102.02, Marion County, Oregon","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.44616413116455,"median_income_tract":70288,"summary":"Jan 3, 2017: 4 killed. Hubbard, OR.\nCause: Shooting, Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Keith Kroeker shot his wife and three young children before setting their house and barn ablaze and killing himself.\nCensus Tract 102.02, Marion County, Oregon (ACS 2017-2021): 8.4% in poverty, median household income $70,288, 63.1% white, 0.9% Black, 31.5% Hispanic/Latino, 5.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Legacy Silverton Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":21.11,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.12,"nearest_level1_center":"Ohsu Hospital And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":34.52,"nearest_level1_miles":21.45,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.767883,45.193878]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-328","properties":{"name":"Fort Lauderdale, FL","date":"2017-01-06","killed":5,"injured":6,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 802, Broward County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.691588401794434,"median_income_tract":62153,"summary":"Jan 6, 2017: 5 killed, 6 injured. Fort Lauderdale, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nOpening fire at the Fort Lauderdale International Airport, Esteban Santiago-Ruiz killed five people and wounded six others (dozens more sustained injuries in the ensuing panic). After serving in the military, Santiago-Ruiz became withdrawn and exhibited anger issues. A few months prior to the shooting, he went to the FBI office in Anchorage, Alaska claiming that the government was trying to control his mind. Despite prior gun confiscations due to mental health concerns, he was a legal gun owner and had a concealed carry permit.  Santiago-Ruiz pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 802, Broward County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 8.7% in poverty, median household income $62,153, 92.3% white, 0.0% Black, 6.7% Hispanic/Latino, 37.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Broward Health Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.31,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.05,"nearest_level1_center":"Broward Health Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":3.31,"nearest_level1_miles":2.05,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.150581,26.074215]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-319","properties":{"name":"Bremerton, WA","date":"2017-01-27","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 920, Kitsap County, Washington","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.820976257324219,"median_income_tract":87608,"summary":"Jan 27, 2017: 4 killed. Bremerton, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 3\nA woman and her son/stepson were killed in their home, which was then burned. Her husband was found the next day in his car, murdered and the car burned as well. Marijuana plants and $60,000 were found in the home. In January 2020, the Kitsap County Sheriff's Office reported that it believes \"members and associates\" of the Bandidos Motorcycle Club were directly involved in the murders. In 2022, Danie Jay Kelly, Jr., Johnny Watson and Robert Watson were arrested and charged.\nCensus Tract 920, Kitsap County, Washington (ACS 2017-2021): 8.8% in poverty, median household income $87,608, 90.1% white, 0.0% Black, 3.3% Hispanic/Latino, 19.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Franciscan Health Harrison Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":15.42,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.58,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":38.11,"nearest_level1_miles":23.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.828362,47.562481]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-320","properties":{"name":"Yazoo City, MS","date":"2017-02-06","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 9503, Yazoo County, Mississippi","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":47.14511489868164,"median_income_tract":29000,"summary":"Feb 6, 2017: 4 killed. Yazoo City, MS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Briddell Barber was at a nightclub with his girlfriend when one of the four victims offered her a ride home. This started an altercation with Barber opening fire on this person and his friends. There is no indication that Barber knew any of them. He pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 9503, Yazoo County, Mississippi (ACS 2017-2021): 47.1% in poverty, median household income $29,000, 4.4% white, 89.3% Black, 4.4% Hispanic/Latino, 12.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Baptist Medical Center Yazoo","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":0.43,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.27,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Mississippi Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":63.15,"nearest_level1_miles":39.24,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.405083,32.862713]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-321","properties":{"name":"Toomsuba, MS","date":"2017-02-20","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 102.04, Lauderdale County, Mississippi","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":33.485595703125,"median_income_tract":29806,"summary":"Feb 20, 2017: 4 killed. Toomsuba, MS.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nKaron McVay came to his girlfriend's cousin's house and shot/stabbed four to death, leaving the three-year-old daughter of his girlfriend's cousin alive. He later returned to the scene when police arrived and pretended to be a normal concerned citizen. He had a history of arson and possibly domestic violence, and served time in prison. McVay was convicted and sentenced to life without parole eligibility.\nCensus Tract 102.04, Lauderdale County, Mississippi (ACS 2017-2021): 33.5% in poverty, median household income $29,806, 55.7% white, 38.8% Black, 3.6% Hispanic/Latino, 15.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Rush Foundation Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":19.8,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.31,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Mississippi Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":157.35,"nearest_level1_miles":97.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.502357,32.437611]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-322","properties":{"name":"Detroit, MI","date":"2017-03-08","killed":5,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Shelter/Drug house","tract":"Census Tract 5010, Wayne County, Michigan","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":48.444580078125,"median_income_tract":37823,"summary":"Mar 8, 2017: 5 killed, 4 injured. Detroit, MI.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Shelter/Drug house · Offenders: 1\nHenry Johnson lived in a group home for the mentally ill and got into a fight with either his roommate or landlord. He then set fire in his room as revenge. Five men who also lived in the home perished. Johnson was ruled incompetent to stand trial and sent for psychiatric care. Johnson has been ruled incompetent to stand trial.\nCensus Tract 5010, Wayne County, Michigan (ACS 2017-2021): 48.4% in poverty, median household income $37,823, 1.2% white, 98.4% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 27.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ascension St John Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.02,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.88,"nearest_level1_center":"Ascension St John Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.02,"nearest_level1_miles":1.88,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.951752,42.416752]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-323","properties":{"name":"Metairie, LA","date":"2017-03-15","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 296, Jefferson Parish, Louisiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":17.099475860595703,"median_income_tract":41212,"summary":"Mar 15, 2017: 4 killed, 1 injured. Metairie, LA.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nArmande Tart was a local drug dealer who went to his friend's apartment and killed him after realizing he had used his drugs. He then went to a nearby apartment with other friends, known cocaine dealers, asked to use their bathroom, and then shot them all point blank in the head, presumably stealing the drugs. Tart was convicted and given a life sentence.\nCensus Tract 296, Jefferson Parish, Louisiana (ACS 2017-2021): 17.1% in poverty, median household income $41,212, 25.2% white, 41.0% Black, 25.6% Hispanic/Latino, 5.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":9.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.2,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_level1_km":9.98,"nearest_level1_miles":6.2,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.17627,29.9974]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-325","properties":{"name":"Sacramento, CA","date":"2017-03-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 39, Sacramento County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.382978916168213,"median_income_tract":73474,"summary":"Mar 22, 2017: 4 killed. Sacramento, CA.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSalvador Vasquez allegedly bludgeoned his wife and two kids to death and stabbed his niece before fleeing to his cousin's house and telling him that he had done something terrible.  Charges against Vasquez are pending.\nCensus Tract 39, Sacramento County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 6.4% in poverty, median household income $73,474, 41.2% white, 5.6% Black, 31.2% Hispanic/Latino, 5.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":6.56,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.08,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":6.56,"nearest_level1_miles":4.08,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-121.518471,38.522507]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-324","properties":{"name":"Rothschild, WI","date":"2017-03-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 10, Marathon County, Wisconsin","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.504831314086914,"median_income_tract":74471,"summary":"Mar 22, 2017: 4 killed. Rothschild, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nNengmy Vang was going through a contentious divorce with his wife. He demanded that she immediately grant him the divorce within 24 hours, or he would kill her. He killed two of her coworkers before going to kill her lawyer (Vang’s wife was in hiding at this point). After killing the lawyer, Vang returned home to his apartment and engaged in a three-hour standoff with police, killing a cop before himself being killed. Vang had a history of emotional abuse towards his wife, marital problems, potential mental illness, and financial issues.\nCensus Tract 10, Marathon County, Wisconsin (ACS 2017-2021): 6.5% in poverty, median household income $74,471, 96.3% white, 0.3% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 1.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Marshfield Medical Center - Weston","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.55,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.58,"nearest_level1_center":"Childrens Hospital Of Wisconsin","nearest_level1_km":242.38,"nearest_level1_miles":150.61,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.609535,44.899754]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-326","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2017-03-30","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 4314, Cook County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":41.781307220458984,"median_income_tract":38858,"summary":"Mar 30, 2017: 4 killed. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nMaurice Harris allegedly targeted four people after his father was killed the night before, presumably related to gang violence. Charges against Harris were dropped because of insufficient evidence.\nCensus Tract 4314, Cook County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 41.8% in poverty, median household income $38,858, 5.1% white, 88.5% Black, 3.0% Hispanic/Latino, 18.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The University Of Chicago Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.96,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.08,"nearest_level1_center":"The University Of Chicago Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":4.96,"nearest_level1_miles":3.08,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.558197,41.760082]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-327","properties":{"name":"Columbia, SC","date":"2017-04-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 104.08, Richland County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":94.96855163574219,"median_income_tract":0,"summary":"Apr 7, 2017: 4 killed. Columbia, SC.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Other · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nDenver Simmons and Jacob Philip were serving long sentences for double homicide (not together) and decided to kill their dormmates because they were annoying, they were bored, and they wanted to get on death row to end being in prison. Both Simmons and Philip pleaded guilty and were sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 104.08, Richland County, South Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 95.0% in poverty, 42.5% white, 48.0% Black, 3.6% Hispanic/Latino.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lexington Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":7.2,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.48,"nearest_level1_center":"Prisma Health Richland","nearest_level1_km":7.55,"nearest_level1_miles":4.69,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.09848,34.069424]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-329","properties":{"name":"Houston, TX","date":"2017-04-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 3138.01, Harris County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":38.61940383911133,"median_income_tract":15601,"summary":"Apr 7, 2017: 4 killed. Houston, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nDekitta Holmes was recently divorced with three children and was unemployed despite having a college degree in criminal justice. According to the police, she went to three separate locations to kill her recent boyfriend, sister, and mother and stepfather. Holmes then committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 3138.01, Harris County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 38.6% in poverty, median household income $15,601, 0.6% white, 73.8% Black, 23.8% Hispanic/Latino, 13.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Womans Hospital Of Texas","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":3.45,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.15,"nearest_level1_center":"Harris Health System Ben Taub Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.82,"nearest_level1_miles":2.37,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.367584,29.685898]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-330","properties":{"name":"Central Islip, NY","date":"2017-04-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":6,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 1462.03, Suffolk County, New York","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":13.754205703735352,"median_income_tract":95313,"summary":"Apr 11, 2017: 4 killed. Central Islip, NY.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 6\nAccording to the authorities, on the evening of April 11, 2017, two female associates of MS-13 lured five young men, including the four victims, to a community park in Central Islip so that Freiry Martinez and other MS-13 members could attack and kill them. The victims were believed to be members of a rival gang who had offended MS-13. Freiry Martinez and numerous other MS-13 members and associates met in the park where they distributed weapons and discussed the plan to kill the victims. Once the female MS-13 associates led the men to a wooded area, Martinez and the other MS-13 members and associates surrounded, attacked and killed of their rivals with machetes, knives, wooden clubs and an axe. The fifth intended victim escaped. The victims’ bodies were discovered the following evening. Martinez, Josue Portillo, and Alexis Hernandez all pleaded guilty and were sentenced to prison; Leniz Escobar was convicted and is awaiting sentencing; and charges against Omar Villalta and Santos Ortiz-Flores are pending.\nCensus Tract 1462.03, Suffolk County, New York (ACS 2017-2021): 13.8% in poverty, median household income $95,313, 10.2% white, 18.8% Black, 67.0% Hispanic/Latino, 12.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Good Samaritan Hospital Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":13.47,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.37,"nearest_level1_center":"Stony Brook University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":14.99,"nearest_level1_miles":9.32,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.193748,40.787964]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-331","properties":{"name":"Cove, AR","date":"2017-04-23","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Unknown","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 9505, Polk County, Arkansas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":21.99630355834961,"median_income_tract":47417,"summary":"Apr 23, 2017: 4 killed. Cove, AR.\nCause: Unknown · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nA mother and her two children were missing on April 23rd, 2017. Police found the three of them in different locations, as well as the mother's uncle dead in his home. Brian Travis, her supposed live-in boyfriend, confessed to the crimes, pleaded guilty, and was sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 9505, Polk County, Arkansas (ACS 2017-2021): 22.0% in poverty, median household income $47,417, 82.6% white, 0.0% Black, 1.9% Hispanic/Latino, 24.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mena Regional Health System","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":24.39,"nearest_trauma_miles":15.16,"nearest_level1_center":"Uams Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":194.57,"nearest_level1_miles":120.9,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.411324,34.435108]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-332","properties":{"name":"Akron, OH","date":"2017-05-15","killed":7,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5052, Summit County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":32.75434112548828,"median_income_tract":33490,"summary":"May 15, 2017: 7 killed. Akron, OH.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nStanley Ford is accused of setting three fires from 2016 to 2017, including one car fire (no deaths), a house fire that killed two adults, and another house fire of his neighbor that killed seven. Ford was convicted and sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 5052, Summit County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 32.8% in poverty, median household income $33,490, 42.7% white, 53.8% Black, 1.3% Hispanic/Latino, 11.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Akron General Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.57,"nearest_level1_center":"Akron General Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":2.52,"nearest_level1_miles":1.57,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.553238,41.062515]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-333","properties":{"name":"Bogue Chitto, MS","date":"2017-05-27","killed":8,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9504.01, Lincoln County, Mississippi","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":11.910198211669922,"median_income_tract":56607,"summary":"May 27, 2017: 8 killed, 1 injured. Bogue Chitto, MS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nWillie Godbolt's wife had left him three weeks prior. He went to her mother's house, where she and their two children were staying, to get custody of the kids back. They called the local deputy, which prompted Godbolt to start firing; he killed three family members and the deputy while his wife and children escaped. He then forced two different individuals to drive him around in different cars, and shot and killed four more people in two homes. He was shot during the process and claimed that his intention had been suicide by cop. Godbolt was found guilty on all charges: four counts of first-degree murder, two counts of kidnapping, one count of attempted murder and one count of armed robbery. He was sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 9504.01, Lincoln County, Mississippi (ACS 2017-2021): 11.9% in poverty, median household income $56,607, 76.5% white, 22.8% Black, 0.7% Hispanic/Latino, 16.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Southwest Ms Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":17.99,"nearest_trauma_miles":11.18,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Mississippi Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":105.52,"nearest_level1_miles":65.57,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.460495,31.412388]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-334","properties":{"name":"Orlando, FL","date":"2017-06-05","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 164.07, Orange County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":24.620655059814453,"median_income_tract":48750,"summary":"Jun 5, 2017: 5 killed. Orlando, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nJohn Neumann was reportedly a disgruntled employee that had a previous history of arguing with coworkers, and even had the police called on him at work in 2014 for battering a coworker; no charges were filed. After being fired from his job, Neumann allegedly went back to Fiamma Inc. and targeted specific coworkers, killing five before himself\nCensus Tract 164.07, Orange County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 24.6% in poverty, median household income $48,750, 33.3% white, 20.4% Black, 32.3% Hispanic/Latino, 14.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":10.1,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.28,"nearest_level1_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":10.1,"nearest_level1_miles":6.28,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.294136,28.579857]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-335","properties":{"name":"La Madera, NM","date":"2017-06-15","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 4.02, Rio Arriba County, New Mexico","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":34.622222900390625,"median_income_tract":39273,"summary":"Jun 15, 2017: 5 killed. La Madera, NM.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nDamian Herrera got into an argument with his stepfather about using his pickup truck. He then shot and killed his stepfather, his half-brother, and mother when the latter two tried to intervene. His sister escaped. He stole the pickup and fled, eventually killing another man to steal his truck. Herrera then drove to a general store to get gas where he killed another man. He was apprehended after a police chase that ended in a crash. Herrere was convicted and received four consecutive life sentences.\nCensus Tract 4.02, Rio Arriba County, New Mexico (ACS 2017-2021): 34.6% in poverty, median household income $39,273, 5.4% white, 0.0% Black, 92.9% Hispanic/Latino, 35.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Christus St Vincent Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":81.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":50.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Christus St Vincent Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":81.71,"nearest_level1_miles":50.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-106.041969,36.390129]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-336","properties":{"name":"Loganville, GA","date":"2017-07-06","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1105.04, Walton County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":10.877544403076172,"median_income_tract":72365,"summary":"Jul 6, 2017: 5 killed, 1 injured. Loganville, GA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nIsabel Martinez stabbed her husband and five children to death. After being apprehended, she refused a lawyer and was convicted of murder. Martinez was given a life sentence without parole eligibility.\nCensus Tract 1105.04, Walton County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 10.9% in poverty, median household income $72,365, 60.2% white, 13.6% Black, 18.9% Hispanic/Latino, 5.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Piedmont Walton Hospital, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":14.61,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.08,"nearest_level1_center":"Wellstar Atlanta Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":44.48,"nearest_level1_miles":27.64,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.900742,33.838997]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-337","properties":{"name":"Whitakers, NC","date":"2017-08-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9308, Halifax County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":30.74877166748047,"median_income_tract":32805,"summary":"Aug 21, 2017: 4 killed. Whitakers, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 4\nAccording to the police, four men broke into the home of a federally-licensed gun salesman (who ran his business from his home), allegedly killing the salesman, his wife, and a couple that were visiting to play cards. Robbery was the motive and police believe it was gang related. Charges against three of the alleged assailants were dropped, however charges against the fourth--James Powell--stood. Powell took an Alford plea, not admitting guilt, and was given four life sentences without parole eligibility.\nCensus Tract 9308, Halifax County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 30.7% in poverty, median household income $32,805, 15.7% white, 46.3% Black, 2.0% Hispanic/Latino, 20.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Vidant Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":73.23,"nearest_trauma_miles":45.5,"nearest_level1_center":"Vidant Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":73.23,"nearest_level1_miles":45.5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.828857,36.169376]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-338","properties":{"name":"Glasgow Village, MO","date":"2017-08-24","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2102, St. Louis County, Missouri","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":33.34898376464844,"median_income_tract":34331,"summary":"Aug 24, 2017: 4 killed. Glasgow Village, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJa'Vonne DuPree was friends with the victims and was staying at their house at the time of the murders. He shot the four victims, ransacked the house, and stole their car. Dupree was convicted and given a life sentence.\nCensus Tract 2102, St. Louis County, Missouri (ACS 2017-2021): 33.3% in poverty, median household income $34,331, 13.1% white, 85.0% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 16.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Louis Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":13.93,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.65,"nearest_level1_center":"Barnes - Jewish Hospital - North","nearest_level1_km":14.2,"nearest_level1_miles":8.83,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.20108,38.754097]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-339","properties":{"name":"Groton, MA","date":"2017-09-08","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3261.02, Middlesex County, Massachusetts","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":4.693024635314941,"median_income_tract":167941,"summary":"Sep 8, 2017: 4 killed. Groton, MA.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nOrion Krause abruptly left home in Maine, prompting his mother to call the police, fearing he was going to commit suicide. He later called her and told her he was in Massachusetts, so she drove to pick him up and swung by her parents' house to visit them. Orion called his former college professor to say that he thought he might have to kill his mother. Orion then killed his mother, grandparents, and their caretaker with a baseball bat. He then stripped naked and covered himself in mud, and ran to a neighbor's house to confess. Krause pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 3261.02, Middlesex County, Massachusetts (ACS 2017-2021): 4.7% in poverty, median household income $167,941, 88.2% white, 0.5% Black, 5.8% Hispanic/Latino, 4.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Joseph Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":16.13,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.02,"nearest_level1_center":"Lahey Hospital And Medical Center - Burlington","nearest_level1_km":33.7,"nearest_level1_miles":20.94,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-71.572639,42.62104]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-340","properties":{"name":"Plano, TX","date":"2017-09-10","killed":8,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 316.28, Collin County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.684265613555908,"median_income_tract":94276,"summary":"Sep 10, 2017: 8 killed, 1 injured. Plano, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Spencer Hight went to his ex-wife's football party and shot her and seven of their friends. All but one of the victims died. Hight was fatally shot at the scene by the police.\nCensus Tract 316.28, Collin County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 7.7% in poverty, median household income $94,276, 64.5% white, 8.7% Black, 20.3% Hispanic/Latino, 2.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Medical City Plano","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.36,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.33,"nearest_level1_center":"Medical City Plano","nearest_level1_km":5.36,"nearest_level1_miles":3.33,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.726402,33.055832]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-341","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2017-09-15","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 8428, Cook County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":34.92447280883789,"median_income_tract":39808,"summary":"Sep 15, 2017: 4 killed. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nThree known members of the Satan's Disciples gang plus one of their ex-girlfriends were shot in a vehicle by another gang retaliating for a hit two nights earlier. The case is unsolved.\nCensus Tract 8428, Cook County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 34.9% in poverty, median household income $39,808, 7.3% white, 0.0% Black, 88.7% Hispanic/Latino, 15.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mt. Sinai Hospital Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.83,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.62,"nearest_level1_center":"Mt. Sinai Hospital Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.83,"nearest_level1_miles":3.62,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.693085,41.808365]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-342","properties":{"name":"Las Vegas, NV","date":"2017-10-01","killed":60,"injured":867,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 68, Clark County, Nevada","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":22.675933837890625,"median_income_tract":48475,"summary":"Oct 1, 2017: 60 killed, 867 injured. Las Vegas, NV.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the authorities, Stephen Paddock, while perched at the window of a Mandalay Bay hotel room, open fired on concert goers below, killing 60 (two of whom died years later from their injuries). Of the 867 injured victims, 411 were injured by gunfire. Paddock took his own life as police approached.\nCensus Tract 68, Clark County, Nevada (ACS 2017-2021): 22.7% in poverty, median household income $48,475, 16.1% white, 13.3% Black, 53.1% Hispanic/Latino, 6.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sunrise Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":5.3,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.29,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center Of Southern Nevada","nearest_level1_km":7.2,"nearest_level1_miles":4.47,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-115.171669,36.095001]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-345","properties":{"name":"Casa Grande, AZ","date":"2017-10-05","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 14.03, Pinal County, Arizona","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":21.1663875579834,"median_income_tract":55417,"summary":"Oct 5, 2017: 4 killed. Casa Grande, AZ.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nAccording to the police, Alec Perez had repeatedly abused his wife, and she had obtained a restraining order against him. He threatened to kill her and told her he'd be back with the right people. He and Rodney Ortiz allegedly murdered her and three others. Both have been charged with trial pending.\nCensus Tract 14.03, Pinal County, Arizona (ACS 2017-2021): 21.2% in poverty, median household income $55,417, 25.6% white, 2.7% Black, 57.7% Hispanic/Latino, 5.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Banner Casa Grande Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":4.37,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.72,"nearest_level1_center":"Dignity Community Care","nearest_level1_km":47.09,"nearest_level1_miles":29.26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.757278,32.885452]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-346","properties":{"name":"Pedro, OH","date":"2017-10-11","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 507, Lawrence County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":23.7386474609375,"median_income_tract":44667,"summary":"Oct 11, 2017: 4 killed, 1 injured. Pedro, OH.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nArron Lawson shot and stabbed four family members and stabbed another (who survived and alerted the police). Lawson also then sexually abused one of decreased victims. Lawson pleaded guilty and was was sentenced to death.\nCensus Tract 507, Lawrence County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 23.7% in poverty, median household income $44,667, 96.7% white, 0.3% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 15.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Mary'S Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":32.14,"nearest_trauma_miles":19.97,"nearest_level1_center":"Charleston Area Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":95.82,"nearest_level1_miles":59.54,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.667381,38.630356]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-530","properties":{"name":"Elizabeth City, NC","date":"2017-10-12","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Government/Transit","tract":"Census Tract 9605.03, Pasquotank County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.579687118530273,"median_income_tract":56515,"summary":"Oct 12, 2017: 4 killed. Elizabeth City, NC.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Other · Location: Government/Transit · Offenders: 4\nAccording to reports, four employees of the   Pasquotank Correctional Institution were fatally stabbed and several others were wounded during a failing escape attempt by four inmates. The four were charge in the killings.\nCensus Tract 9605.03, Pasquotank County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 16.6% in poverty, median household income $56,515, 59.2% white, 38.8% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 3.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sentara Norfolk General Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":55.62,"nearest_trauma_miles":34.56,"nearest_level1_center":"Sentara Norfolk General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":55.62,"nearest_level1_miles":34.56,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.32093,36.362228]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-348","properties":{"name":"New York, NY","date":"2017-10-31","killed":8,"injured":11,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Vehicle crash","situation":"Terrorism","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 69, New York County, New York","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":4.186265468597412,"median_income_tract":237500,"summary":"Oct 31, 2017: 8 killed, 11 injured. New York, NY.\nCause: Vehicle crash · Type: Public · Circumstance: Terrorism · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the authorities, Sayfullo Saipov planned the attack for almost a year; moved from Uzbekistan where he was an accountant after obtaining a Green Card in 2010. He got married, had kids, and worked for Uber. He rented a truck from Home Depot and allegedly drove into bike lane to hit riders/pedestrians, and claimed it was for ISIS. Saipov was convicted although the jury has not as yet returned a sentencing recommendation.\nCensus Tract 69, New York County, New York (ACS 2017-2021): 4.2% in poverty, median household income $237,500, 81.4% white, 0.8% Black, 8.2% Hispanic/Latino, 23.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bellevue Hospital Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.21,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.99,"nearest_level1_center":"Bellevue Hospital Center","nearest_level1_km":3.21,"nearest_level1_miles":1.99,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.01104,40.729206]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-347","properties":{"name":"Sutherland Springs, TX","date":"2017-11-05","killed":25,"injured":20,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"House of worship","tract":"Census Tract 1.02, Wilson County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":21.395973205566406,"median_income_tract":88986,"summary":"Nov 5, 2017: 25 killed, 20 injured. Sutherland Springs, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: House of worship · Offenders: 1\nDevin Kelley had a history of warning signs, including domestic violence, sexual assault, prison time, military experience and obsession with weapons, obsession with previous mass shootings, restraining order, treatment in a mental health facility, etc. He went to his wife's family's church and killed 25, including her grandmother. A citizen exchanged gunfire with him and pursued him, so he committed suicide and crashed his car.\nCensus Tract 1.02, Wilson County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 21.4% in poverty, median household income $88,986, 66.8% white, 4.7% Black, 23.8% Hispanic/Latino, 16.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Connally Memorial Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":17.17,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.67,"nearest_level1_center":"Brooke Army Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":40.53,"nearest_level1_miles":25.18,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-98.056511,29.273245]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-349","properties":{"name":"Rancho Tehama, CA","date":"2017-11-14","killed":5,"injured":18,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 3, Tehama County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":18.55955696105957,"median_income_tract":61118,"summary":"Nov 14, 2017: 5 killed, 18 injured. Rancho Tehama, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nKevin Neal was suspected to be mentally ill, had just assaulted a neighbor, and was called about possible domestic violence on the day prior to the incident. According to the police, Neal shot and killed his wife before going on a rampage to kill his two neighbors, whom he suspected of cooking meth, and then stole their truck to go to the elementary school that his neighbor's son attended. He was prohibited from having guns because of the restraining order, but illegally manufactured the ghost guns at home. Neal committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 3, Tehama County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 18.6% in poverty, median household income $61,118, 70.6% white, 1.1% Black, 23.7% Hispanic/Latino, 24.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Elizabeth Community Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":22.35,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.89,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":180.08,"nearest_level1_miles":111.9,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.397514,40.001034]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-343","properties":{"name":"Troy, NY","date":"2017-12-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 403, Rensselaer County, New York","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.656514167785645,"median_income_tract":53029,"summary":"Dec 21, 2017: 4 killed. Troy, NY.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nTwo offenders killed a friend and her domestic partner as well as their kids to steal an X-box and a TV. James White was convicted and received a life sentence, while Justin Mann pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 403, Rensselaer County, New York (ACS 2017-2021): 12.7% in poverty, median household income $53,029, 65.7% white, 14.5% Black, 13.7% Hispanic/Latino, 12.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Albany Medical Center Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":14.03,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.72,"nearest_level1_center":"Albany Medical Center Hospital","nearest_level1_km":14.03,"nearest_level1_miles":8.72,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.681702,42.758568]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-344","properties":{"name":"Long Branch, NJ","date":"2017-12-31","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8059, Monmouth County, New Jersey","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":19.213973999023438,"median_income_tract":75389,"summary":"Dec 31, 2017: 4 killed. Long Branch, NJ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nScott Kologi, a 16 year old who was homeschooled by his mother and reportedly had an autism spectrum disorder, killed his parents, sister, and grandfather's girlfriend in their family home on New Year's Eve. Kologi was convicted and was given four life sentences.\nCensus Tract 8059, Monmouth County, New Jersey (ACS 2017-2021): 19.2% in poverty, median household income $75,389, 53.5% white, 4.1% Black, 34.1% Hispanic/Latino, 3.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Jersey Shore University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":9.82,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.1,"nearest_level1_center":"Maimonides Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":38.57,"nearest_level1_miles":23.97,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.002998,40.292595]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-350","properties":{"name":"Reading, PA","date":"2018-01-28","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1, Berks County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":49.26861572265625,"median_income_tract":18204,"summary":"Jan 28, 2018: 4 killed. Reading, PA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 4\nFour young men were shot multiple times each in a first-floor apartment of a Reading, PA row house. The case reportedly involved a drug ring. The police identified Pedro Sanchez-Laporte as a person of interest and announced a reward for information leading to his arrest. He was arrested in Florida in 2021. Charges against Sanchez-Laporte are pending trial.\nCensus Tract 1, Berks County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2017-2021): 49.3% in poverty, median household income $18,204, 27.1% white, 5.3% Black, 64.2% Hispanic/Latino, 16.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Reading Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.6,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.99,"nearest_level1_center":"Reading Hospital","nearest_level1_km":1.6,"nearest_level1_miles":0.99,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.931625,40.333088]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-351","properties":{"name":"Melcroft, PA","date":"2018-01-28","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 2605, Fayette County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.644281387329102,"median_income_tract":55909,"summary":"Jan 28, 2018: 4 killed, 1 injured. Melcroft, PA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nTimothy Smith went to a car wash in the middle of the night to engage in a fight with his ex-girlfriend's new boyfriend. While the victims believed it was supposed to be a fistfight, Smith killed them all before committing suicide. Smith was described as being obsessed with his ex. She had recently posted on Facebook that she needed to be taken out on a date or by a sniper, and Smith commented \"I can do both.\"\nCensus Tract 2605, Fayette County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2017-2021): 12.6% in poverty, median household income $55,909, 99.8% white, 0.1% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 19.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Conemaugh Memorial Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":48.95,"nearest_trauma_miles":30.42,"nearest_level1_center":"Conemaugh Memorial Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":48.95,"nearest_level1_miles":30.42,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.389168,40.052002]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-352","properties":{"name":"Paintsville, KY","date":"2018-02-10","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9604.02, Johnson County, Kentucky","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":18.801170349121094,"median_income_tract":56250,"summary":"Feb 10, 2018: 4 killed. Paintsville, KY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJoseph Nickell had recently lost his sister to drug addiction, and had a history of substance abuse and domestic violence. He drove to his parent's house, where allegedly he killed them, before attempting to kill his son. According to the Authorities, Nickell then drove seven miles to his girlfriend's home and killed her and her mother before committing suicide.\nCensus Tract 9604.02, Johnson County, Kentucky (ACS 2017-2021): 18.8% in poverty, median household income $56,250, 95.7% white, 0.0% Black, 0.6% Hispanic/Latino, 12.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Morgan County Arh Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":41.57,"nearest_trauma_miles":25.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Charleston Area Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":119.27,"nearest_level1_miles":74.11,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.810646,37.816208]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-353","properties":{"name":"Parkland, FL","date":"2018-02-14","killed":17,"injured":17,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"School","tract":"Census Tract 106.01, Broward County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":3.2079391479492188,"median_income_tract":130581,"summary":"Feb 14, 2018: 17 killed, 17 injured. Parkland, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: School · Offenders: 1\nNikolas Cruz reportedly had a history of serious mental health and behavioral problems, switching schools multiple times for disciplinary reasons. He attended specialty schools for students with emotional and behavioral problems, and had been recommended to be involuntarily committed by a SRO and counselors. After being expelled from Marjory Stoneman Douglas High School, he used an AR-15 style rifle that he had legally purchased to kill students and teachers. Cruz pleaded guilty to the murders and was sentenced to life imprisonment  without parole eligibility.\nCensus Tract 106.01, Broward County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 3.2% in poverty, median household income $130,581, 58.6% white, 11.4% Black, 17.2% Hispanic/Latino, 4.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Broward Health North","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":15.12,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.39,"nearest_level1_center":"Delray Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":20.41,"nearest_level1_miles":12.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.26944,26.304562]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-354","properties":{"name":"Detroit, MI","date":"2018-02-26","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 5442, Wayne County, Michigan","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":30.815507888793945,"median_income_tract":22629,"summary":"Feb 26, 2018: 4 killed. Detroit, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nGeorge Davis, on parole, went to a gas station in the morning and got into an argument with the mother of his child, killing her, her passenger, and another male witness. He then went to his cousin's home and killed him before fleeing; he killed himself in Ohio.\nCensus Tract 5442, Wayne County, Michigan (ACS 2017-2021): 30.8% in poverty, median household income $22,629, 15.5% white, 77.5% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 40.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Beaumont Hospital - Farmington Hills","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.96,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.33,"nearest_level1_center":"Beaumont Hospital - Royal Oak","nearest_level1_km":14.09,"nearest_level1_miles":8.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.265869,42.40052]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-371","properties":{"name":"West Brookfield, MA","date":"2018-03-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7241, Worcester County, Massachusetts","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.572868347167969,"median_income_tract":83079,"summary":"Mar 1, 2018: 4 killed. West Brookfield, MA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMatthew Locke allegedly killed his cousin's wife and his cousin's children, while the cousin was working out of state. No motive has been offered, but the police initially charged him with lying about an investigation, as he claimed that his cousin had insinuated that MS-13 was responsible for the murders. Locke has been charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 7241, Worcester County, Massachusetts (ACS 2017-2021): 7.6% in poverty, median household income $83,079, 97.0% white, 0.0% Black, 2.3% Hispanic/Latino, 11.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Umass Memorial Med Ctr - Univ Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":33.55,"nearest_trauma_miles":20.85,"nearest_level1_center":"Umass Memorial Med Ctr - Univ Campus","nearest_level1_km":33.55,"nearest_level1_miles":20.85,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-72.165787,42.238029]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-372","properties":{"name":"Mount Pleasant, SC","date":"2018-03-10","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 46.09, Charleston County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":4.722002029418945,"median_income_tract":79844,"summary":"Mar 10, 2018: 4 killed. Mount Pleasant, SC.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nLovequawn Scott was raised by his grandparents. He did well in school and was liked by classmates. He later played football at two different colleges, but was kicked out for drugs/weapons offenses. It is unclear if Lovequawn had a history of mental illness; he appeared at a church and at an urgent care center where his cousin worked the day before the murders, asking for help. He beat his grandparents, his aunt, and his cousin (who was like a sister to him) to death with dumbbells before being arrested with a hand injury and blood all over him. In a bench, Scott was found not guilty by reason of insanity.\nCensus Tract 46.09, Charleston County, South Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 4.7% in poverty, median household income $79,844, 80.5% white, 15.4% Black, 1.0% Hispanic/Latino, 6.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Musc Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":16.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.33,"nearest_level1_center":"Musc Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":16.63,"nearest_level1_miles":10.33,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.783661,32.843315]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-373","properties":{"name":"Westport, CA","date":"2018-03-26","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Vehicle crash","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 110.04, Mendocino County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.87673568725586,"median_income_tract":68894,"summary":"Mar 26, 2018: 6 killed. Westport, CA.\nCause: Vehicle crash · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 2\nJennifer and Sarah Hart, two white women, adopted six black children. While they appeared to be a happy family, the two reportedly neglected and abused the children. The children were described as obedient \"robots\" who were harshly disciplined for minor infractions, such as laughing at the dinner table. The children apparently complained on multiple occasions that they were not fed as a punishment, and often appeared malnourished. In one instance, one of the girls jumped out of the second story window and fled to a neighbor's house, telling them that she had been whipped by her parents. One of the boys repeatedly went to a neighbor's house to ask for food, requesting also that the neighbor not to tell his parents. After the neighbor called Child Protective Services, the Harts took the six children and, according to the police, drove off a cliff into the Pacific Ocean, killing all eight in the car. Jennifer was the driver, but there is evidence that Sarah googled \"suicide\" and \"drowning\" prior to the incident.\nCensus Tract 110.04, Mendocino County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 8.9% in poverty, median household income $68,894, 82.5% white, 0.0% Black, 7.2% Hispanic/Latino, 28.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Adventist Health Howard Memorial","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":40.53,"nearest_trauma_miles":25.18,"nearest_level1_center":"Priscilla Chan And Mark Zuckerberg San Francisco General Hospital And Trauma Center","nearest_level1_km":212.44,"nearest_level1_miles":132.01,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-123.802391,39.324066]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-374","properties":{"name":"Syracuse, NY","date":"2018-04-05","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 39, Onondaga County, New York","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":56.40449523925781,"median_income_tract":0,"summary":"Apr 5, 2018: 4 killed, 1 injured. Syracuse, NY.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nCharles DuBois was unemployed, living at home, and had a known drug abuse problem. He had previously suffered from suicidal thoughts and was taken to emergency psychiatric care two weeks prior to the incident. He intentionally lit two fires at home in the middle of the night while his family slept. He attempted to use the insanity defense but then later recanted it. DuBois was convicted and sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 39, Onondaga County, New York (ACS 2017-2021): 56.4% in poverty, 19.7% white, 46.7% Black, 21.9% Hispanic/Latino, 32.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Hospital Suny Health Science Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.7,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.68,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospital Suny Health Science Center","nearest_level1_km":2.7,"nearest_level1_miles":1.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.172478,43.037609]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-355","properties":{"name":"Nashville, TN","date":"2018-04-22","killed":4,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 156.30, Davidson County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.179739952087402,"median_income_tract":55805,"summary":"Apr 22, 2018: 4 killed, 4 injured. Nashville, TN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nTravis Reinking had a history of paranoia and mental illness: he believed that he was being stalked by Taylor Swift and his phone was being hacked; he crashed a pool party in a pink dress (with his rifle in the trunk) before exposing himself to the partygoers; and he attempted to break into The White House to get a meeting with President Trump. After being arrested by the Secret Service, his gun license was revoked, and the guns were turned over to his father. When he wanted to move out of state, his father returned the weapons to Reinking, who used them to kill four people at the Waffle House...while naked. He was convicted and sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 156.30, Davidson County, Tennessee (ACS 2017-2021): 12.2% in poverty, median household income $55,805, 27.8% white, 51.7% Black, 3.2% Hispanic/Latino, 1.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Tristar Stonecrest Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":9.54,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.93,"nearest_level1_center":"Vanderbilt University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":19.55,"nearest_level1_miles":12.15,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.615471,36.050568]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-356","properties":{"name":"Ponder, TX","date":"2018-05-16","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 203.14, Denton County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.024409055709839,"median_income_tract":95204,"summary":"May 16, 2018: 4 killed, 1 injured. Ponder, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJustin Painter had been married for over six years. When he filed for divorce, he obtained a temporary restraining order against his wife, was awarded primary custody of their three children, and was being paid child support by his wife. It is alleged that, after failing to reconcile, Painter killed the children and her boyfriend and attempted to kill her before committing suicide.\nCensus Tract 203.14, Denton County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 2.0% in poverty, median household income $95,204, 65.9% white, 11.5% Black, 15.6% Hispanic/Latino, 0.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Medical City Denton","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":17.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":11.17,"nearest_level1_center":"John Peter Smith Hospital","nearest_level1_km":50.35,"nearest_level1_miles":31.29,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.284584,33.178478]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-357","properties":{"name":"Santa Fe, TX","date":"2018-05-18","killed":10,"injured":13,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"School","tract":"Census Tract 7234.03, Galveston County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.29965591430664,"median_income_tract":84223,"summary":"May 18, 2018: 10 killed, 13 injured. Santa Fe, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: School · Offenders: 1\nDimitrios Pagourtzis, 17, allegedly fatally shot 10 (eight fellow students and two teachers) and wounded 13 others at the Santa Fe High School in Texas. Pagourtzis was ruled incompetent to stand trial.\nCensus Tract 7234.03, Galveston County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 9.3% in poverty, median household income $84,223, 82.5% white, 0.0% Black, 17.2% Hispanic/Latino, 11.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hca Houston Healthcare Mainland","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":15.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.41,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Texas Medical Branch - Galveston","nearest_level1_km":36.55,"nearest_level1_miles":22.71,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.142418,29.392282]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-358","properties":{"name":"Scottsdale, AZ","date":"2018-05-30","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 2172.01, Maricopa County, Arizona","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.129411697387695,"median_income_tract":85772,"summary":"May 30, 2018: 6 killed. Scottsdale, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nDwight Jones reportedly had a history of mental illness and domestic violence. He had used abusive language towards his son, and then beat up his wife. After his arrest for domestic violence, he was court-ordered to undergo a mental health evaluation and was involuntarily committed to a behavioral health facility. After nine years, he posted a YouTube video detailing his beliefs that there was a conspiracy between his ex-wife, psychiatrist, the law firm, and the local government to keep his son away from him. According to the authorities, Jones then killed his psychiatrist, two paralegals who worked for his wife's law firm, a man who was renting the office of his son's therapist, and two friends. Jones took his own life.\nCensus Tract 2172.01, Maricopa County, Arizona (ACS 2017-2021): 5.1% in poverty, median household income $85,772, 90.1% white, 1.5% Black, 4.6% Hispanic/Latino, 20.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Honorhealth Scottsdale Osborn Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.53,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.33,"nearest_level1_center":"Honorhealth Scottsdale Osborn Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":0.53,"nearest_level1_miles":0.33,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.919296,33.49202]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-359","properties":{"name":"Orlando, FL","date":"2018-06-11","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 148.12, Orange County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":15.146960258483887,"median_income_tract":43250,"summary":"Jun 11, 2018: 5 killed. Orlando, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nGary Lindsey reportedly had a history of violent, erratic behavior. He was living in an apartment with his girlfriend, their two children, and her two other children. He had previously beaten her, knocked their 7-month-old out of her hands, and held a knife to her throat. Staff members from the Department of Children and Families had come to investigate several times but determined that the children were not in danger. According to the authorities, when his girlfriend next called the police to report abuse, Lindsey shot a responding officer, barricaded himself inside the apartment with the children and killed them. After a 24-hour standoff with police, Lindsey took his own life.\nCensus Tract 148.12, Orange County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 15.1% in poverty, median household income $43,250, 42.9% white, 10.2% Black, 34.1% Hispanic/Latino, 19.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":9.49,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.9,"nearest_level1_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":9.49,"nearest_level1_miles":5.9,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.465309,28.489826]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-360","properties":{"name":"Annapolis, MD","date":"2018-06-28","killed":5,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 7027.02, Anne Arundel County, Maryland","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.194437026977539,"median_income_tract":185972,"summary":"Jun 28, 2018: 5 killed, 2 injured. Annapolis, MD.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nIn 2011, Jarrod Ramos pleaded guilty to criminal harassment of a former high school classmate, and The Capital wrote an article about it. He later filed a defamation lawsuit but lost, and began to harass the newspaper and specific employees online. He repeatedly posted threats hoping that staff members would die, and at least one staff member attempted to get a restraining order. In 2016, he ceased making threats, but then two years later came to the newspaper's office and shot five before being arrested. Ramos pleaded guilty and received a life sentence.\nCensus Tract 7027.02, Anne Arundel County, Maryland (ACS 2017-2021): 7.2% in poverty, median household income $185,972, 88.6% white, 2.1% Black, 2.3% Hispanic/Latino, 10.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Um Capital Region Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":27.97,"nearest_trauma_miles":17.38,"nearest_level1_center":"The Johns Hopkins Hospital","nearest_level1_km":33.82,"nearest_level1_miles":21.01,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.543571,38.994289]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-361","properties":{"name":"Prices Corner, DE","date":"2018-07-09","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 121, New Castle County, Delaware","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.961783409118652,"median_income_tract":68674,"summary":"Jul 9, 2018: 4 killed. Prices Corner, DE.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA man was recently estranged from his wife and had lost his local job, working instead out of state. Their oldest son had Williams syndrome. He killed his wife and three young children before committing suicide.\nCensus Tract 121, New Castle County, Delaware (ACS 2017-2021): 8.0% in poverty, median household income $68,674, 85.2% white, 8.2% Black, 4.2% Hispanic/Latino, 1.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Francis Healthcare","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":4.47,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.78,"nearest_level1_center":"Christiana Care Health Services - Christiana Hospital","nearest_level1_km":7.4,"nearest_level1_miles":4.6,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.617874,39.741051]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-362","properties":{"name":"Robstown, TX","date":"2018-07-27","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 56.04, Nueces County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":13.97679328918457,"median_income_tract":58889,"summary":"Jul 27, 2018: 4 killed. Robstown, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nRichard Starry killed two in-laws at a home owned by himself and his father before heading to a local nursing home to kill his father and stepmother and commit suicide. Starry had served 4 years in prison for drug trafficking and had been charged with money laundering (those were dropped however). One source noted that he became a white supremacist in prison and owned 200+ guns and suggested that the motive may have been related to a property dispute between father and son.\nCensus Tract 56.04, Nueces County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 14.0% in poverty, median household income $58,889, 3.6% white, 0.3% Black, 94.5% Hispanic/Latino, 8.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Corpus Christi Medical Center - Northwest","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":6.61,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.11,"nearest_level1_center":"Doctors Hospital At Renaissance","nearest_level1_km":180.27,"nearest_level1_miles":112.02,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.659821,27.79952]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-363","properties":{"name":"Bakersfield, CA","date":"2018-09-12","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 24.01, Kern County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":27.707372665405273,"median_income_tract":46602,"summary":"Sep 12, 2018: 5 killed. Bakersfield, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nJavier Casarez's 28-year marriage ended four months prior when he believed that his wife was cheating on him (potentially with two of the male victims). His ex-wife claimed a history of verbal abuse, and asked for spousal and child support in addition to the family home. Casarez presumably forced his ex-wife to go to his workplace, where he killed her and two others before driving to the home of a man that had loaned him money in 2010, killing that man and his daughter. The young children in the home were unharmed. He then carjacked a mother and child, telling them that he is \"not a bad guy\" before letting them go. When confronted by police, he committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 24.01, Kern County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 27.7% in poverty, median household income $46,602, 26.2% white, 0.5% Black, 71.7% Hispanic/Latino, 4.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Kern Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.06,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Santa Barbara Cottage Hospital","nearest_level1_km":126.05,"nearest_level1_miles":78.32,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.916512,35.349567]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-364","properties":{"name":"Taft, TX","date":"2018-10-13","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 108, San Patricio County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":22.057193756103516,"median_income_tract":45625,"summary":"Oct 13, 2018: 4 killed, 1 injured. Taft, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nRonnie Rodriguez, Jr. and Sr. were at the birthday party for a one-year-old relative when they accused a man of being a peeping tom. The man then drove off, returning later with his family members. Rodriguez Jr. started shooting but missed, but then his father grabbed the gun, shooting the five men, killing four and wounding one. Rodriguez, Jr. was convicted and received a life sentence without parole, while his father's charges remain pending trial.\nCensus Tract 108, San Patricio County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 22.1% in poverty, median household income $45,625, 13.6% white, 0.0% Black, 86.2% Hispanic/Latino, 18.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Christus Spohn Hospital Corpus Christi","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":21.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.49,"nearest_level1_center":"Brooke Army Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":192.16,"nearest_level1_miles":119.4,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.407944,27.974958]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-365","properties":{"name":"Columbia, TN","date":"2018-10-15","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 102.01, Maury County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.208226203918457,"median_income_tract":96924,"summary":"Oct 15, 2018: 4 killed. Columbia, TN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nCindy Collier had been married for nearly 30 years. In 2007, she separated from her husband, and raised their seven children alone (three biological and four adopted from China). She was described as a loving, Christian mother who home schooled her children. According to the police, Collier shot and killed her four adopted children before killing herself.  In the months prior, she was having arguments with her estranged husband about custody (during divorce proceedings that were later dropped).\nCensus Tract 102.01, Maury County, Tennessee (ACS 2017-2021): 6.2% in poverty, median household income $96,924, 89.0% white, 2.6% Black, 4.5% Hispanic/Latino, 9.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Tristar Stonecrest Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":49,"nearest_trauma_miles":30.44,"nearest_level1_center":"Vanderbilt University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":49.7,"nearest_level1_miles":30.88,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.015999,35.728767]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-366","properties":{"name":"Pittsburgh, PA","date":"2018-10-27","killed":11,"injured":6,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"House of worship","tract":"Census Tract 1403, Allegheny County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":10.375465393066406,"median_income_tract":137688,"summary":"Oct 27, 2018: 11 killed, 6 injured. Pittsburgh, PA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: House of worship · Offenders: 1\nRobert Bowers was a high school dropout who started out as a conservative, but then became active in neo-Nazi circles. According to the authorities, Bowers believed in the white genocide conspiracy theory, made many antisemitic and racist remarks, and eventually shot and killed 11 people at a Pittsburgh synagogue. Charges against Bowers are pending trial.\nCensus Tract 1403, Allegheny County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2017-2021): 10.4% in poverty, median household income $137,688, 74.5% white, 2.1% Black, 4.6% Hispanic/Latino, 7.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Upmc Presbyterian Shadyside","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.38,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.1,"nearest_level1_center":"Upmc Presbyterian Shadyside","nearest_level1_km":3.38,"nearest_level1_miles":2.1,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.92083,40.443771]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-367","properties":{"name":"Thousand Oaks, CA","date":"2018-11-07","killed":12,"injured":12,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 59.11, Ventura County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.6946914196014404,"median_income_tract":84609,"summary":"Nov 7, 2018: 12 killed, 12 injured. Thousand Oaks, CA.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Ian David Long fatally shot 12 victims at the Borderline Bar and Grill in Thousand Oaks and then committed suicide. Long was an honorably discharged Marine Corps vet who moved in with his mother following the end of his service. Neighbors reported that he often fought loudly with his mother, and once called the police because he was acting erratically. A mental health professional who observed him following this incident suggested that he may be suffering from PTSD but declined to bring him in for further observation. Long was described as a loner by some, and a nice guy by his friends. He had previously frequented the Borderline Bar and Grill on multiple occasions.\nCensus Tract 59.11, Ventura County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 2.7% in poverty, median household income $84,609, 71.7% white, 2.1% Black, 13.1% Hispanic/Latino, 0.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Los Robles Hospital And Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.56,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.21,"nearest_level1_center":"Providence Cedars - Sinai Tarzana Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":31.56,"nearest_level1_miles":19.61,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.87484,34.176659]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-368","properties":{"name":"Philadelphia, PA","date":"2018-11-19","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 73, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":26.536401748657227,"median_income_tract":45446,"summary":"Nov 19, 2018: 4 killed. Philadelphia, PA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 4\nTwo stepbrothers were renovating a house when they found a small stash of drugs. One of the brothers contacted one of the offenders, attempting to sell the drugs. The offenders then attempted to rob the brothers but ended up executing everyone in the home. Four suspects were arrested, although charges against one of them were dropped. Jahlil Porter, Keith Garner, and Robert Long all pleaded guilty and were sentenced to prison.\nCensus Tract 73, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2017-2021): 26.5% in poverty, median household income $45,446, 17.1% white, 74.5% Black, 2.0% Hispanic/Latino, 12.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Penn Presbyterian Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.54,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.58,"nearest_level1_center":"Penn Presbyterian Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":2.54,"nearest_level1_miles":1.58,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.225304,39.947708]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-370","properties":{"name":"Colts Neck, NJ","date":"2018-11-20","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Profit","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8099.02, Monmouth County, New Jersey","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.4248926639556885,"median_income_tract":166406,"summary":"Nov 20, 2018: 4 killed. Colts Neck, NJ.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Profit · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPaul Caneiro killed his brother and his family, presumably for a financial motive. The two brothers had established businesses together, but his brother was much more successful than Paul (bigger share of businesses, more money, bigger house, etc.) Several years prior to the incident, Paul was in a car accident that required multiple surgeries and caused immense emotional and physical pain (he was awarded a $120,000 settlement for his medical expenses). The once booming business that the brothers shared had fallen on tough times, and Paul’s brother had recently found out that Paul had stolen $75,000 from the business. the brother indicated that he wanted to sever his business relationship with Paul, and had sent his resume to other companies, especially looking for a job in California. Paul shot and killed his brother and his sister-in-law before stabbing their two children. He then lit their house on fire and drove home, lighting his own home on fire to make it look like a vendetta against the extended family. Caneiro has been charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 8099.02, Monmouth County, New Jersey (ACS 2017-2021): 2.4% in poverty, median household income $166,406, 92.9% white, 0.0% Black, 4.2% Hispanic/Latino, 2.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Jersey Shore University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":18.14,"nearest_trauma_miles":11.27,"nearest_level1_center":"Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":28.98,"nearest_level1_miles":18.01,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.18689,40.32869]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-369","properties":{"name":"St. Charles, MO","date":"2018-12-28","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3112.12, St. Charles County, Missouri","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.7316434383392334,"median_income_tract":89839,"summary":"Dec 28, 2018: 4 killed, 1 injured. St. Charles, MO.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nRichard Emery had been dating his girlfriend for approximately a year and a half. Her husband had passed away after a six-year battle with cancer about six months prior to the beginning of their relationship. He had moved into their home, and no one reported any signs of domestic violence, conflict, or mental illness. He shot and killed his girlfriend, her two children, and her mother before fleeing in a vehicle. When stopped by police, he shot at the officers and ran off on foot, attempting to carjack a woman. When her car wouldn't start, he stabbed her (nonfatally) and was eventually caught the next morning in a convenience store bathroom, suffering from two bullet wounds. Emery was arrested, convicted, and sentenced to death for the murders.\nCensus Tract 3112.12, St. Charles County, Missouri (ACS 2017-2021): 2.7% in poverty, median household income $89,839, 84.6% white, 5.4% Black, 1.6% Hispanic/Latino, 6.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Barnes - Jewish St. Peters Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.05,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.27,"nearest_level1_center":"Barnes - Jewish St. Peters Hospital","nearest_level1_km":2.05,"nearest_level1_miles":1.27,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.563812,38.779915]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-395","properties":{"name":"Clackamas County, OR","date":"2019-01-19","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 238, Clackamas County, Oregon","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":3.2207717895507812,"median_income_tract":96365,"summary":"Jan 19, 2019: 4 killed, 2 injured. Clackamas County, OR.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMark Leo Gregory Gago, 42, used an axe to kill his parents, his girlfriend and their infant daughter before deputies shot him as he was attempting to kill his girlfriend's daughter. Some of the victims were beheaded. The one girl and a 40-year-old roommate were injured but survived the attack.\nCensus Tract 238, Clackamas County, Oregon (ACS 2017-2021): 3.2% in poverty, median household income $96,365, 75.7% white, 0.0% Black, 19.5% Hispanic/Latino, 0.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Legacy Silverton Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":15.28,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.49,"nearest_level1_center":"Ohsu Hospital And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":40.51,"nearest_level1_miles":25.17,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.733452,45.136139]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-379","properties":{"name":"Sebring, FL","date":"2019-01-23","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 9613.04, Highlands County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":11.600688934326172,"median_income_tract":53668,"summary":"Jan 23, 2019: 5 killed. Sebring, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nZephen Xaver had a history of being fascinated with violence, and had previously been kicked out of high school for discussing the idea of committing a school shooting, taking hostages, and dying by suicide by cop. He moved from Indiana to Florida and was living there with his mother. Xaver had dropped out of online college a month prior to the shooting and resigned his job as a correctional officer trainee two weeks prior. After allegedly killing four employees and a customer at a SunTrust Bank, Xaver called the police to let them know that he had killed five people and then barricaded himself inside the bank. Xavier was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9613.04, Highlands County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 11.6% in poverty, median household income $53,668, 89.9% white, 0.0% Black, 10.1% Hispanic/Latino, 24.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lakeland Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":81.73,"nearest_trauma_miles":50.78,"nearest_level1_center":"Tampa General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":111.39,"nearest_level1_miles":69.21,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.458389,27.470608]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-381","properties":{"name":"Rockmart, GA","date":"2019-01-24","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 106, Polk County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":15.584150314331055,"median_income_tract":48974,"summary":"Jan 24, 2019: 4 killed, 1 injured. Rockmart, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nWhile on parole, Daylon Gamble went to his estranged cousin's home. According to the police, he allegedly shot and killed his aunt and a cousin and wounded another cousin, after which he  drove to his best friend's apartment where he killed his friend and his friend's girlfriend. He then fled to Indiana where he was apprehended. Gamble was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 106, Polk County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 15.6% in poverty, median household income $48,974, 80.9% white, 16.8% Black, 1.0% Hispanic/Latino, 9.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Polk Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":12.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.85,"nearest_level1_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":68.42,"nearest_level1_miles":42.51,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.060432,33.999165]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-378","properties":{"name":"Gonzales, LA","date":"2019-01-26","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 301.02, Ascension Parish, Louisiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":11.214146614074707,"median_income_tract":66924,"summary":"Jan 26, 2019: 5 killed. Gonzales, LA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDakota Theriot had a \"violent streak\" and a known problem with drugs. Two weeks prior to the incident, he was kicked out of his parents' trailer because of his drug problem. He then went to live with his girlfriend of a few weeks and her family. It appears that there was some sort of dispute, and he killed his girlfriend and her family (but let her two young siblings live) before stealing their car, driving to his parents’ house, and killing them. He then drove to his grandmother's home, where police apprehended him during a wellness check (she had called the police fearful that she would be the next victim of her grandson). Theriot was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 301.02, Ascension Parish, Louisiana (ACS 2017-2021): 11.2% in poverty, median household income $66,924, 92.5% white, 1.0% Black, 4.0% Hispanic/Latino, 11.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Our Lady Of The Lake Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":27.37,"nearest_trauma_miles":17,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_level1_km":84.01,"nearest_level1_miles":52.2,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.892891,30.240561]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-380","properties":{"name":"Palm Springs, CA","date":"2019-02-03","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 448.04, Riverside County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":13.432835578918457,"median_income_tract":63750,"summary":"Feb 3, 2019: 4 killed. Palm Springs, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nThree teenagers and a 25-year-old man were found shot along the same block, with the three teens inside a crashed car. Some evidence suggests that two of the teens may have been involved in an aborted robbery plot, but details remain unclear. According to the police, the suspect Jose Larin-Garcia  was found hiding under a pickup truck a few blocks away. He was taken for medical attention and left without the police/staff knowing. Larin-Garcia visited a friend, telling him that he had been involved in a traffic accident, and the friend loaned him money and clothing. Larin-Garcia was then arrested at a Greyhound bus station where he appeared to be inebriated. A February 2022 trial ended in a hung jury, after which the prosecution retried the case and got a conviction on four counts of first degree murder with a sentence of death.\nCensus Tract 448.04, Riverside County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 13.4% in poverty, median household income $63,750, 32.3% white, 1.0% Black, 41.4% Hispanic/Latino, 20.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Desert Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":4.55,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Loma Linda University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":74.76,"nearest_level1_miles":46.45,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-116.506004,33.812077]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-377","properties":{"name":"Livingston, TX","date":"2019-02-11","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2102.05, Polk County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.209064483642578,"median_income_tract":45750,"summary":"Feb 11, 2019: 4 killed. Livingston, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nRandy Horn, an amateur boxer and poker enthusiast, allegedly killed his wife (27 years his junior), their child, and her two grandparents after posting an ominous message on Facebook. Horn took his own life.\nCensus Tract 2102.05, Polk County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 12.2% in poverty, median household income $45,750, 80.4% white, 6.7% Black, 7.5% Hispanic/Latino, 51.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Chi St Lukes Health - Memorial Livingston","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":11.2,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.96,"nearest_level1_center":"Memorial Hermann - Texas Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":117.06,"nearest_level1_miles":72.74,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.056404,30.725477]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-376","properties":{"name":"Aurora, IL","date":"2019-02-15","killed":5,"injured":6,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 8547, Kane County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":23.56205940246582,"median_income_tract":51750,"summary":"Feb 15, 2019: 5 killed, 6 injured. Aurora, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nGary Martin had a long history of domestic violence, and had been in prison for stabbing an ex-girlfriend in 1995. He was able to apply successfully for an Illinois FOID (Firearm Owners Identification) card due to the lack of fingerprinting, but failed to secure a concealed carry permit, and was sent a letter indicating that he had to give up his guns and FOID card. It remains unclear if the police ever followed up on his illegal gun ownership. After working at Henry Pratt company for 15 years, he went to a meeting where he was told he was being fired. During the meeting, he shot his coworkers/boss, and hid in the 29,000 sq ft factory until police found him, and exchanged gunfire, killing him.\nCensus Tract 8547, Kane County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 23.6% in poverty, median household income $51,750, 29.7% white, 12.9% Black, 52.6% Hispanic/Latino, 11.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Presence Central And Suburban Hospitals Network","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.32,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.07,"nearest_level1_center":"Good Samaritan Hospital - Advocate","nearest_level1_km":27.78,"nearest_level1_miles":17.26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.332726,41.756374]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-375","properties":{"name":"Clinton, MS","date":"2019-02-16","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 103.04, Hinds County, Mississippi","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":4.053409576416016,"median_income_tract":58906,"summary":"Feb 16, 2019: 4 killed. Clinton, MS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nNam Le owned a nail salon with his wife, and several family members worked there. He shot and killed his wife, sister-in-law, sister-in-law's fiancé, and a family friend/babysitter in his home during a 12-hour standoff with police. Several hours into the standoff, he released his two children (ages 4 and 5) unharmed to the police. He was shot by a sniper and later died at the hospital.\nCensus Tract 103.04, Hinds County, Mississippi (ACS 2017-2021): 4.1% in poverty, median household income $58,906, 53.1% white, 40.8% Black, 3.6% Hispanic/Latino, 11.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Merit Health Central","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":9.44,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.87,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Mississippi Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":13.98,"nearest_level1_miles":8.69,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.31945,32.352554]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-425","properties":{"name":"Morrisville, PA","date":"2019-02-23","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Asphyxiation, Strangulation","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1057.04, Bucks County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":4.238574981689453,"median_income_tract":87045,"summary":"Feb 23, 2019: 5 killed. Morrisville, PA.\nCause: Asphyxiation, Strangulation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nShana and Dominique Decree killed five family members in what was suspected to be some type of religious ritual. According to an affidavit of probable cause, social services representatives came to the apartment for an unannounced visit. After there was no answer, they contacted a maintenance worker at the complex for assistance. When the maintenance worker gained access to the apartment, he found two women, mother and daughter, in bed. The worker reported that the two seemed disoriented and the apartment was in disarray. The Morrisville police were called to the scene and both women were taken to the hospital. The assailants both pleaded guilty and were sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 1057.04, Bucks County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2017-2021): 4.2% in poverty, median household income $87,045, 74.9% white, 15.3% Black, 5.8% Hispanic/Latino, 4.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Capital Health Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.97,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.47,"nearest_level1_center":"Albert Einstein Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":36.31,"nearest_level1_miles":22.56,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.77861,40.206501]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-505","properties":{"name":"Gretna, LA","date":"2019-03-06","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 303.04, Iberia Parish, Louisiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.628180503845215,"median_income_tract":85253,"summary":"Mar 6, 2019: 4 killed, 1 injured. Gretna, LA.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTerrance Leonard, 36, killed four children and injured another with a hammer as they were asleep, and then killed the victims’ mother/aunt when she came home in the morning. Leonard pleaded guilty and was given four consecutive life sentences.\nCensus Tract 303.04, Iberia Parish, Louisiana (ACS 2017-2021): 9.6% in poverty, median household income $85,253, 73.2% white, 11.6% Black, 11.4% Hispanic/Latino, 2.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ochsner Lafayette General Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":35.67,"nearest_trauma_miles":22.16,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center New Orleans","nearest_level1_km":178.65,"nearest_level1_miles":111.01,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-91.934036,29.890539]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-382","properties":{"name":"Sheffield, MA","date":"2019-03-13","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9261, Berkshire County, Massachusetts","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.162145614624023,"median_income_tract":71818,"summary":"Mar 13, 2019: 4 killed. Sheffield, MA.\nCause: Stabbing, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nLuke Karpinski appeared to be a loving family man, but he killed his wife and 3 kids before killing himself and lighting their house on fire. Their two dogs also died.\nCensus Tract 9261, Berkshire County, Massachusetts (ACS 2017-2021): 9.2% in poverty, median household income $71,818, 90.9% white, 0.0% Black, 5.2% Hispanic/Latino, 20.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Berkshire Med Ctr Inc - Berkshire Cam","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":35.85,"nearest_trauma_miles":22.27,"nearest_level1_center":"Baystate Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":60.16,"nearest_level1_miles":37.38,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.3321,42.14352]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-399","properties":{"name":"Mandan, ND","date":"2019-04-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 203.01, Morton County, North Dakota","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.32152271270752,"median_income_tract":70473,"summary":"Apr 1, 2019: 4 killed. Mandan, ND.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Public · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nChad Isaak, a veteran and chiropractor, went to the company that managed his mobile home park and shot and stabbed four employees there. It remains unclear if he had any relationship with the victims or what the precise motive was. Isaak was convicted and sentenced to life in prison.\nCensus Tract 203.01, Morton County, North Dakota (ACS 2017-2021): 12.3% in poverty, median household income $70,473, 88.3% white, 1.8% Black, 1.2% Hispanic/Latino, 17.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sanford Medical Center Bismarck","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":5.05,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.14,"nearest_level1_center":"Sanford Medical Center Fargo","nearest_level1_km":302.17,"nearest_level1_miles":187.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-100.847931,46.81472]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-413","properties":{"name":"Goodfield, IL","date":"2019-04-06","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 306.02, Woodford County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.480661392211914,"median_income_tract":93000,"summary":"Apr 6, 2019: 5 killed. Goodfield, IL.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nKyle Alwood, age 9, was arrested for intentionally setting fire to a mobile home, killing five members of his family, including three children. The boy's mother says her son suffers from schizophrenia, bipolar disorder and ADHD, and takes medication daily. Alwood was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 306.02, Woodford County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 2.5% in poverty, median household income $93,000, 95.5% white, 0.0% Black, 0.1% Hispanic/Latino, 3.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Carle Bromenn Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":27.64,"nearest_trauma_miles":17.17,"nearest_level1_center":"Saint Francis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":29.09,"nearest_level1_miles":18.07,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-89.256248,40.642345]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-570","properties":{"name":"Phoenix, AZ","date":"2019-04-11","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Other","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1096.04, Maricopa County, Arizona","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.05215835571289,"median_income_tract":57862,"summary":"Apr 11, 2019: 4 killed, 2 injured. Phoenix, AZ.\nCause: Shooting, Other · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nBelieving that he had permission from God, Austin Smith killed his wife (whom he suspected of infidelity), and two of his daughters. He then drove to his brother's home seeking out the man he suspected was involved with his wife. There he killed one person and injured two others who were trying to intervene.\nCensus Tract 1096.04, Maricopa County, Arizona (ACS 2017-2021): 16.1% in poverty, median household income $57,862, 5.5% white, 4.1% Black, 87.9% Hispanic/Latino, 6.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Banner Estrella Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":5.1,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.17,"nearest_level1_center":"Banner Thunderbird Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":11.99,"nearest_level1_miles":7.45,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-112.211952,33.503922]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-384","properties":{"name":"Westmoreland, TN","date":"2019-04-25","killed":7,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force, Stabbing","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 201.02, Sumner County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":19.646589279174805,"median_income_tract":46833,"summary":"Apr 25, 2019: 7 killed, 1 injured. Westmoreland, TN.\nCause: Blunt force, Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMichael Cummins reportedly had a history of violence and drug problems. After being released after a year in jail for attempting to burn down his neighbor's house and assaulting her, Cummins violated his parole and was about to be arrested. According to the police, he then killed three family members and his uncle's girlfriend and relatives before attacking another woman, presumably to steal her car. The police found Cummins at a nearby creek bed where he was shot and arrested. Cummins was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 201.02, Sumner County, Tennessee (ACS 2017-2021): 19.6% in poverty, median household income $46,833, 94.3% white, 0.9% Black, 0.1% Hispanic/Latino, 10.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sumner Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":24.84,"nearest_trauma_miles":15.44,"nearest_level1_center":"Vanderbilt University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":66.01,"nearest_level1_miles":41.02,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.331215,36.597557]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-383","properties":{"name":"West Chester, OH","date":"2019-04-28","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 111.22, Butler County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.500170707702637,"median_income_tract":101333,"summary":"Apr 28, 2019: 4 killed. West Chester, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nGurpreet Singh called 911 to report that four members of his well-respected Sikh family were found shot dead in their home. Two months later he was arrested for the murder of his wife and three other relatives. The couple's three children were not at home at the time. The jury in Singh's trial could not reach a unanimous verdict, resulting in a mistrial. However, the prosecutor has vowed to retry the case.\nCensus Tract 111.22, Butler County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 9.5% in poverty, median household income $101,333, 58.6% white, 11.4% Black, 3.6% Hispanic/Latino, 0.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"West Chester Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":8.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.36,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Cincinnati Medicalcenter, Llc","nearest_level1_km":23.83,"nearest_level1_miles":14.81,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.467468,39.350815]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-385","properties":{"name":"St. Louis, MO","date":"2019-05-13","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1269, St. Louis city, Missouri","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":27.12377166748047,"median_income_tract":38869,"summary":"May 13, 2019: 4 killed, 1 injured. St. Louis, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour related men were shot and killed inside an injured victim's home. The police believe the incident was related to drugs, as drugs and weapons were found in the home. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 1269, St. Louis city, Missouri (ACS 2017-2021): 27.1% in poverty, median household income $38,869, 1.5% white, 92.2% Black, 1.6% Hispanic/Latino, 30.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Louis Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.64,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.88,"nearest_level1_center":"Barnes - Jewish Hospital - North","nearest_level1_km":4.92,"nearest_level1_miles":3.06,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.243408,38.677395]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-386","properties":{"name":"Virginia Beach, VA","date":"2019-05-31","killed":12,"injured":5,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Government/Transit","tract":"Census Tract 454.33, Virginia Beach city, Virginia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":0.6752411723136902,"median_income_tract":114395,"summary":"May 31, 2019: 12 killed, 5 injured. Virginia Beach, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Government/Transit · Offenders: 1\nDeWayne Craddock, a 15-year employee with no criminal history, submitted his two weeks’ notice to the Virginia Beach Municipal Government citing \"personal reasons.\" According to the authorities, he then went on a rampage at work a few hours later, killing 12 and injuring five. Craddock was killed by the responding police.\nCensus Tract 454.33, Virginia Beach city, Virginia (ACS 2017-2021): 0.7% in poverty, median household income $114,395, 65.5% white, 19.6% Black, 6.1% Hispanic/Latino, 3.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sentara Virginia Beach General Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":12.54,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.79,"nearest_level1_center":"Children'S Hospital Of The King'S Daughters","nearest_level1_km":24.44,"nearest_level1_miles":15.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.061882,36.755463]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-390","properties":{"name":"White Swan, WA","date":"2019-06-08","killed":5,"injured":2,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9400.03, Yakima County, Washington","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":18.557954788208008,"median_income_tract":58008,"summary":"Jun 8, 2019: 5 killed, 2 injured. White Swan, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nJames and Donovan Cloud (with the possible assistance of two others) fatally shot four victims at a residence in the Yakima Indian Reservation. They then stole a car from there and shot additional victims, killing one, inside a nearby vehicle. The murders appear to be drug related. James Cloud was convicted and Donovan Cloud pleaded guilty. James receive a life sentence and Donovan received a 327-month sentence.\nCensus Tract 9400.03, Yakima County, Washington (ACS 2017-2021): 18.6% in poverty, median household income $58,008, 43.2% white, 0.2% Black, 15.6% Hispanic/Latino, 7.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Virginia Mason Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":28.37,"nearest_trauma_miles":17.63,"nearest_level1_center":"Legacy Emanuel Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":173,"nearest_level1_miles":107.5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-120.823036,46.422691]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-388","properties":{"name":"Santa Maria, CA","date":"2019-06-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 23.08, Santa Barbara County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.8457255363464355,"median_income_tract":65982,"summary":"Jun 21, 2019: 4 killed. Santa Maria, CA.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nStemming from an ongoing dispute and apparently precipitated by his recent eviction from his mobile home, Claude Adams, 64, fatally shot two men at the park’s clubhouse area, police said. Adams then killed his wife and son and set fire to the mobile home before taking his own life.\nCensus Tract 23.08, Santa Barbara County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 6.8% in poverty, median household income $65,982, 25.2% white, 1.2% Black, 69.7% Hispanic/Latino, 3.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Marian Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":3.6,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.24,"nearest_level1_center":"Santa Barbara Cottage Hospital","nearest_level1_km":89.24,"nearest_level1_miles":55.45,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-120.439827,34.97504]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-389","properties":{"name":"San Jose, CA","date":"2019-06-23","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5032.22, Santa Clara County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.575220108032227,"median_income_tract":84958,"summary":"Jun 23, 2019: 4 killed. San Jose, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nUsing a stolen handgun, Chi Dinh Ta allegedly killed his wife's relatives who she had recently arranged to have immigrate from Vietnam. He then committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 5032.22, Santa Clara County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 8.6% in poverty, median household income $84,958, 0.3% white, 0.0% Black, 58.5% Hispanic/Latino, 0.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Regional Medical Center Of San Jose","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.85,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.26,"nearest_level1_center":"Santa Clara Valley Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":8.11,"nearest_level1_miles":5.04,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-121.842491,37.300941]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-391","properties":{"name":"North St. Louis County, MO","date":"2019-07-06","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2106, St. Louis County, Missouri","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":21.33136558532715,"median_income_tract":40310,"summary":"Jul 6, 2019: 5 killed. North St. Louis County, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nFive victims were shot to death in police say was in connection with drug activity.  Terrance Wesley pleaded guilty while Anthony Watkins is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 2106, St. Louis County, Missouri (ACS 2017-2021): 21.3% in poverty, median household income $40,310, 24.1% white, 74.3% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 10.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Louis Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":12.64,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.86,"nearest_level1_center":"Barnes - Jewish Hospital - North","nearest_level1_km":12.93,"nearest_level1_miles":8.03,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.236488,38.750568]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-392","properties":{"name":"Port Angeles, WA","date":"2019-07-06","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8, Clallam County, Washington","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":13.91671085357666,"median_income_tract":59286,"summary":"Jul 6, 2019: 4 killed. Port Angeles, WA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMatthew Timothy Wetherington, a 34-year-old registered sex offender, was arrested for allegedly setting fire to his mobile home in the early morning of July 6, 2019, killing his wife and three children inside. Wetherington and his wife were married two months prior to the incident. Wetherington pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 8, Clallam County, Washington (ACS 2017-2021): 13.9% in poverty, median household income $59,286, 86.2% white, 0.0% Black, 4.6% Hispanic/Latino, 13.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Olympic Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":26.99,"nearest_trauma_miles":16.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":102.38,"nearest_level1_miles":63.61,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-123.47374,48.106373]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-445","properties":{"name":"Cleveland, OH","date":"2019-07-09","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1989, Cuyahoga County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":57.272727966308594,"median_income_tract":23266,"summary":"Jul 9, 2019: 4 killed. Cleveland, OH.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nOn July 8, 2019, Armond Johnson allegedly shot and killed his former girlfriend inside her residence before setting the house on fire (killing their 6-year-old son and her 2-year-old daughter) and then fleeing the scene. According to the police, Johnson returned to the crime scene early the following morning and shot and killed a neighbor in a vacant field adjacent to his residence. Johnson was convicted and sentenced to four consecutive life terms.\nCensus Tract 1989, Cuyahoga County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 57.3% in poverty, median household income $23,266, 28.2% white, 58.0% Black, 8.0% Hispanic/Latino, 41.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Hospitals Cleveland Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.78,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.35,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospitals Cleveland Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":3.78,"nearest_level1_miles":2.35,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.645226,41.521976]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-403","properties":{"name":"Summerfield, FL","date":"2019-07-10","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8.03, Marion County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":29.088991165161133,"median_income_tract":38273,"summary":"Jul 10, 2019: 5 killed. Summerfield, FL.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMichael Jones allegedly killed his wife (allegedly during an argument) and the four children on what is believed to be July 10, 2019. Then on September 15, 2019, after crashing his van in Brantley County, GA, he told responding officers that his dead wife was in the back of the vehicle. He then told police about their children whose bodies were left in wooded area in Charlton County, Ga., off Hwy. 301. All five victims (wife, two stepsons, and two daughters) were apparently killed weeks earlier in the family residence. Jones was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 8.03, Marion County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 29.1% in poverty, median household income $38,273, 79.0% white, 2.0% Black, 13.4% Hispanic/Latino, 0.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ocala Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":22.32,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.87,"nearest_level1_center":"Uf Health Shands Hospital","nearest_level1_km":77.31,"nearest_level1_miles":48.04,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.009155,29.008524]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-426","properties":{"name":"Columbus, GA","date":"2019-07-17","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 27, Muscogee County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":24.17266273498535,"median_income_tract":33912,"summary":"Jul 17, 2019: 4 killed. Columbus, GA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTravane Jackson and his girlfriend  had a years-long violent relationship, according to the police. On the day she was planning to leave with their three young children, Jackson allegedly stabbed her and the kids to death in their apartment. Jackson committed suicide while awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 27, Muscogee County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 24.2% in poverty, median household income $33,912, 2.0% white, 92.1% Black, 3.9% Hispanic/Latino, 16.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Piedmont Columbus Regional Midtown","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.59,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.23,"nearest_level1_center":"Atrium Health Navicent Rehabilitation Hospital","nearest_level1_km":129.74,"nearest_level1_miles":80.62,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.963722,32.452126]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-393","properties":{"name":"San Fernando Valley, CA","date":"2019-07-25","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 3203, Los Angeles County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":11.326658248901367,"median_income_tract":58446,"summary":"Jul 25, 2019: 4 killed, 2 injured. San Fernando Valley, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Gerry Dean Zaragoza, 26, went on a shooting rampage in the San Fernando Valley killing four (including his father and brother) and injuring two others (including his mother). The other two slain victims were a mother of four with whom Zaragoza had been obsessed for some time and a man who was shot on a bus. The shooting spree started in Canoga Park, then to North Hollywood, Sherman Oaks, and Van Nuys where Zaragoza was arrested and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 3203, Los Angeles County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 11.3% in poverty, median household income $58,446, 3.1% white, 0.4% Black, 94.8% Hispanic/Latino, 4.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Providence Holy Cross Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":1.7,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.06,"nearest_level1_center":"Providence Cedars - Sinai Tarzana Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":15.01,"nearest_level1_miles":9.33,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.441742,34.282982]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-394","properties":{"name":"Lake Hallie & Lafayette, WI","date":"2019-07-28","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 9704, Dunn County, Wisconsin","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.622533321380615,"median_income_tract":75139,"summary":"Jul 28, 2019: 4 killed, 2 injured. Lake Hallie & Lafayette, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nPoliced responded to a 911 call in Lafayette, WI, finding two dead (including the suspected assailant Ritchie German, Jr.) and two others injured. The police subsequently went to the home of the suspected assailant, finding three dead victims (the suspected assailant’s mother, brother, and nephew).\nCensus Tract 9704, Dunn County, Wisconsin (ACS 2017-2021): 7.6% in poverty, median household income $75,139, 91.0% white, 0.2% Black, 2.7% Hispanic/Latino, 7.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mayo Clinic Health System In Eau Claire","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":15.41,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.58,"nearest_level1_center":"Regions Hospital","nearest_level1_km":110.67,"nearest_level1_miles":68.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-91.696251,44.859741]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-396","properties":{"name":"El Paso, TX","date":"2019-08-03","killed":23,"injured":23,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 34.03, El Paso County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":18.635255813598633,"median_income_tract":43779,"summary":"Aug 3, 2019: 23 killed, 23 injured. El Paso, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nIn an apparently hate-inspired, anti-immigrant attack, Patrick Crusius traveled over 600 miles from suburban Dallas to an El Paso Walmart where he killed 23 people and wounded 23 others with a semiautomatic rifle. In February 2023, Crusius pleaded guilty.\nCensus Tract 34.03, El Paso County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 18.6% in poverty, median household income $43,779, 16.7% white, 1.6% Black, 80.4% Hispanic/Latino, 5.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Del Sol Medical Center A Campus Of Lpds Healthcare","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":4.11,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.55,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center Of El Paso","nearest_level1_km":4.71,"nearest_level1_miles":2.93,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-106.385933,31.77718]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-397","properties":{"name":"Dayton, OH","date":"2019-08-04","killed":9,"injured":27,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 15.01, Montgomery County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":19.61394691467285,"median_income_tract":48317,"summary":"Aug 4, 2019: 9 killed, 27 injured. Dayton, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nDressed in body armor, Connor Betts allegedly opened fire in Dayton’s Oregon District amid a busy nightlife scene of bars and restaurants killing nine (including his sister) and injuring 27 others. With police already patrolling the area, the shooter was killed fairly quickly, preventing many more casualties.\nCensus Tract 15.01, Montgomery County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 19.6% in poverty, median household income $48,317, 59.2% white, 25.0% Black, 10.0% Hispanic/Latino, 6.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Miami Valley Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.36,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.84,"nearest_level1_center":"Miami Valley Hospital","nearest_level1_km":1.36,"nearest_level1_miles":0.84,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.185638,39.757118]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-400","properties":{"name":"Garden Grove, CA","date":"2019-08-07","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 886.02, Orange County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":17.88035011291504,"median_income_tract":82981,"summary":"Aug 7, 2019: 4 killed, 2 injured. Garden Grove, CA.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the authorities, Zachary Castaneda, 33, fatally stabbed four people (including two at his apartment complex) and injured two others in series of attacks over three hours that involved robbery. He was arrested at a 7/11 where he had allegedly killed a security guard. Castanaeda was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 886.02, Orange County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 17.9% in poverty, median household income $82,981, 17.5% white, 0.7% Black, 36.3% Hispanic/Latino, 3.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Of California Irvine Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.76,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.96,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Irvine Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":4.76,"nearest_level1_miles":2.96,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-117.937881,33.77607]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-401","properties":{"name":"Odessa, TX","date":"2019-08-31","killed":7,"injured":22,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 30.04, Ector County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.400483131408691,"median_income_tract":71931,"summary":"Aug 31, 2019: 7 killed, 22 injured. Odessa, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nAfter being stopped by Texas state troopers for making a left turn without signaling, the Seth Ator shot at the officers and then drove toward Midland. He subsequently abandoned his car and hijacked a postal van. The gunman continued shooting indiscriminately as he went. He was eventually killed in a shootout with police at an Odessa theater parking lot.\nCensus Tract 30.04, Ector County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 8.4% in poverty, median household income $71,931, 70.3% white, 8.3% Black, 16.2% Hispanic/Latino, 10.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Odessa Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":10.79,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.7,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":188.71,"nearest_level1_miles":117.26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-102.287827,31.923904]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-402","properties":{"name":"Elkmont, AL","date":"2019-09-02","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 12, Whitfield County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":18.895931243896484,"median_income_tract":35034,"summary":"Sep 2, 2019: 5 killed. Elkmont, AL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMason Sisk, 14, called 911 about hearing gunshots. Deputies responding to the home in Elkmont, Ala. found one adult and two minors dead at the scene. Another adult and minor were hospitalized with critical injuries and later died. The teenager then reportedly admitted to killing five members of his family: his father, stepmother, and siblings. Sisk was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 12, Whitfield County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 18.9% in poverty, median household income $35,034, 48.5% white, 7.3% Black, 42.8% Hispanic/Latino, 16.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hamilton Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":10.77,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.69,"nearest_level1_center":"Erlanger Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":50.82,"nearest_level1_miles":31.58,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.900261,34.722336]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-405","properties":{"name":"Albuquerque, NM","date":"2019-09-12","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 44.01, Bernalillo County, New Mexico","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":24.723247528076172,"median_income_tract":41974,"summary":"Sep 12, 2019: 4 killed, 2 injured. Albuquerque, NM.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nOfficers responded shortly after 9 p.m. to a call of shots fired at 1028 Lura Place SW. Three people were found dead, a fourth died at the hospital. Two others suffered injuries that were not life-threatening. The victims were all related. Although unsolved, initial interviews revealed that an unknown vehicle drove down Lura Place and fired multiple shots at the male in the roadway. That individual may have been the primary target in a shooting that also claimed his mother, grandmother, and cousin.\nCensus Tract 44.01, Bernalillo County, New Mexico (ACS 2017-2021): 24.7% in poverty, median household income $41,974, 10.2% white, 0.9% Black, 88.9% Hispanic/Latino, 8.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Unm Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":6.66,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.14,"nearest_level1_center":"Unm Hospital","nearest_level1_km":6.66,"nearest_level1_miles":4.14,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-106.68428,35.064259]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-406","properties":{"name":"Cleveland, OH","date":"2019-09-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1208.02, Cuyahoga County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":48.75283432006836,"median_income_tract":14827,"summary":"Sep 21, 2019: 4 killed. Cleveland, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nResponding to complaints of an odor coming from an abandoned home, the police discovered the bodies of four gunshot victims. Because of the extent of decomposition, the date of death could not be determined. The location was known as a drug house.\nCensus Tract 1208.02, Cuyahoga County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 48.8% in poverty, median household income $14,827, 1.2% white, 89.6% Black, 8.4% Hispanic/Latino, 21.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Rainbow Babies And Childrens Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.26,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.27,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospitals Cleveland Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.39,"nearest_level1_miles":3.35,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.581345,41.461033]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-404","properties":{"name":"Beaumont, TX","date":"2019-09-29","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 26, Jefferson County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":41.147254943847656,"median_income_tract":35199,"summary":"Sep 29, 2019: 4 killed. Beaumont, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nLively James Stratton, 22, was arrested and charged with four counts of murder for the fatal shooting of his four roommates inside a duplex in the 4100 block of Highland Avenue. Initially, no motive has been identified other than reports that Stratton may have shot and killed the four men over an altercation that occurred earlier that day. Stratton was convicted and sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 26, Jefferson County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 41.1% in poverty, median household income $35,199, 18.9% white, 56.1% Black, 15.2% Hispanic/Latino, 17.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Baptist Hospitals Of Southeast Texas","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":4.22,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.62,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Texas Medical Branch - Galveston","nearest_level1_km":105.69,"nearest_level1_miles":65.67,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.085449,30.047251]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-407","properties":{"name":"New York, NY","date":"2019-10-05","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Blunt force","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 8, New York County, New York","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":28.832752227783203,"median_income_tract":28269,"summary":"Oct 5, 2019: 4 killed, 1 injured. New York, NY.\nCause: Blunt force · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nRandy Santos, a 24-year-old homeless man, allegedly bludgeoned five other homeless men, 4 fatally, with a metal bar in the Chinatown section of Manhattan. Santos was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 8, New York County, New York (ACS 2017-2021): 28.8% in poverty, median household income $28,269, 10.5% white, 0.2% Black, 4.0% Hispanic/Latino, 0.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bellevue Hospital Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.4,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.11,"nearest_level1_center":"Bellevue Hospital Center","nearest_level1_km":3.4,"nearest_level1_miles":2.11,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-73.99704,40.713486]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-408","properties":{"name":"Kansas City, KS","date":"2019-10-06","killed":4,"injured":5,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 423, Wyandotte County, Kansas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":33.701316833496094,"median_income_tract":33750,"summary":"Oct 6, 2019: 4 killed, 5 injured. Kansas City, KS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 2\nNine people were shot, four fatally, at a private bar (the Tequila KC Bar)  in Kansas City. The incident appears to have been precipitated by the bartender's refusal to serve one of the two assailants. Police said that the shooting may have been motivated by an earlier dispute at the bar and that Hugo Villanueva-Morales and Javier Alatorre allegedly returned to carry out the shooting.  While authorities have not determined the motive, information is coming to light about the two suspects' ties to vast criminal networks. Both men were charged and are awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 423, Wyandotte County, Kansas (ACS 2017-2021): 33.7% in poverty, median household income $33,750, 20.6% white, 19.0% Black, 55.1% Hispanic/Latino, 15.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Children'S Mercy Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.35,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.33,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Kansas Hospital Transplant Center","nearest_level1_km":5.38,"nearest_level1_miles":3.35,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.635452,39.100811]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-409","properties":{"name":"Abington, MA","date":"2019-10-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5201, Plymouth County, Massachusetts","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.0661733150482178,"median_income_tract":112460,"summary":"Oct 7, 2019: 4 killed. Abington, MA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThe bodies of a man, a woman and three children were found by a relative inside their townhouse. All five appeared to have been shot. It has been determined that the man, 43-year-old Joseph Zaccardi, killed his wife and children before killing himself. According to Joseph’s Facebook page, he was out of work, with his employment listed as \"Unemployed and Going Crazy.\" Posts on his Facebook profile showed that he had written and illustrated four self-published children’s books, with the most recent, \"Day is Done No More Fun,\" published in June 2018.\nCensus Tract 5201, Plymouth County, Massachusetts (ACS 2017-2021): 2.1% in poverty, median household income $112,460, 84.8% white, 1.7% Black, 1.0% Hispanic/Latino, 2.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"South Shore Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":7.77,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Brigham And Women'S Faulkner Hospital","nearest_level1_km":26.68,"nearest_level1_miles":16.58,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-70.938698,42.107018]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-415","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2019-10-12","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8432, Cook County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.784141540527344,"median_income_tract":58162,"summary":"Oct 12, 2019: 5 killed. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nKrysztof Marek, a 66-year-old truck driver who had lived in the building for about 15 years, walked into a neighbor's apartment where, according to the police, he fatally shot three men and a woman as they ate dinner. He then went upstairs to the third floor, entered another apartment, and allegedly shot a woman there. That woman was taken to the hospital in critical condition where she died. The assailant was facing eviction for non-payment of condo fees as well as foreclosure on his mortgage. He had filed for bankruptcy in September 2017 in which he reported owing $24,000 to the Internal Revenue Service and more than $60,000 to creditors. The assailant left two notes written in Polish behind in his apartment reflecting his determination to carry out the murders. Marek was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 8432, Cook County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 16.8% in poverty, median household income $58,162, 30.5% white, 3.1% Black, 62.8% Hispanic/Latino, 10.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"John H. Stroger Jr. Hospital Of Cook County","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.2,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.99,"nearest_level1_center":"John H. Stroger Jr. Hospital Of Cook County","nearest_level1_km":3.2,"nearest_level1_miles":1.99,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.650047,41.850029]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-423","properties":{"name":"Philadelphia, PA","date":"2019-10-30","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 80, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":28.82367515563965,"median_income_tract":58355,"summary":"Oct 30, 2019: 4 killed. Philadelphia, PA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMaurice Lewis, 28, was arrested and faces murder charges after confessing to killing his mother, stepfather and two younger half-brothers inside their home.\nCensus Tract 80, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania (ACS 2017-2021): 28.8% in poverty, median household income $58,355, 22.3% white, 67.8% Black, 3.7% Hispanic/Latino, 11.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Penn Presbyterian Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.37,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.47,"nearest_level1_center":"Penn Presbyterian Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":2.37,"nearest_level1_miles":1.47,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.224113,39.949326]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-418","properties":{"name":"Orinda, CA","date":"2019-10-31","killed":5,"injured":9,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3530.01, Contra Costa County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":1.1032863855361938,"median_income_tract":237208,"summary":"Oct 31, 2019: 5 killed, 9 injured. Orinda, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFive people were killed and several more injured in a shooting during a packed Halloween party (with over 100 in attendance) at a rented Airbnb home in Orinda, CA. The sheriff said \"there were rival gangs involved in the altercation inside the home. There was also an attempt to steal property which may have precipitated the initial round of shooting. \" The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 3530.01, Contra Costa County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 1.1% in poverty, median household income $237,208, 60.4% white, 0.3% Black, 4.5% Hispanic/Latino, 7.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ucsf Benioff Children'S Hospital Oakland","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":8.42,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.23,"nearest_level1_center":"Highland Hospital","nearest_level1_km":9.29,"nearest_level1_miles":5.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.18325,37.873276]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-422","properties":{"name":"San Diego, CA","date":"2019-11-16","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 32.11, San Diego County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":3.8520801067352295,"median_income_tract":82449,"summary":"Nov 16, 2019: 5 killed. San Diego, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nInvolved in a bitter divorce, Jose Valdivia allegedly shot his wife and four children before turning the gun on himself. All but one of the children died. About two weeks before the shooting rampage, the assailant reportedly sent his estranged wife a photo of a handgun with the message \"It’s sure happening.\"\nCensus Tract 32.11, San Diego County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 3.9% in poverty, median household income $82,449, 17.1% white, 5.3% Black, 59.8% Hispanic/Latino, 3.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Scripps Mercy Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":12.61,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Scripps Mercy Hospital","nearest_level1_km":12.61,"nearest_level1_miles":7.83,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-117.056976,32.678387]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-421","properties":{"name":"Fresno, CA","date":"2019-11-17","killed":4,"injured":6,"offenders":7,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 30.01, Fresno County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":24.25790023803711,"median_income_tract":44826,"summary":"Nov 17, 2019: 4 killed, 6 injured. Fresno, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 7\nFour men were killed and six others were wounded in southeast Fresno when gunmen broke into a backyard party and opened fire on dozens of people watching football. On December 31, 2019, the police arrested seven suspected gang members who, according to the authorities, had mistakenly believed it was a rival gang’s party and attacked to avenge a murder from earlier that day. Pao Vang, Ger Lee, Jhovanny Delgado, Porge Kue, Anthony Montes, Billy Xiong, Johnny Xiong were charged and are awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 30.01, Fresno County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 24.3% in poverty, median household income $44,826, 16.5% white, 7.6% Black, 38.9% Hispanic/Latino, 1.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Community Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":6.16,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Community Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":6.16,"nearest_level1_miles":3.83,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.718201,36.757462]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-424","properties":{"name":"Jersey City, NJ","date":"2019-12-10","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 55, Hudson County, New Jersey","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":39.227203369140625,"median_income_tract":28241,"summary":"Dec 10, 2019: 4 killed, 3 injured. Jersey City, NJ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 2\nOfficials believe the shooting spree began when a detective approached David Anderson and Francine Graham at a cemetery in connection with a homicide investigation and was shot dead. The assailants then fled in a stolen rental truck and eventually ended up at a nearby kosher market, where they opened fire on police officers and civilians. Three of the civilians were killed. Anderson and Graham were both killed by the police. Subsequent reports suggest the incident may have been inspired by antisemitism.\nCensus Tract 55, Hudson County, New Jersey (ACS 2017-2021): 39.2% in poverty, median household income $28,241, 11.6% white, 67.0% Black, 16.6% Hispanic/Latino, 11.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Jersey City Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.96,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.84,"nearest_level1_center":"Richmond University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":8.13,"nearest_level1_miles":5.05,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.083527,40.707001]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-427","properties":{"name":"Celebration, FL","date":"2019-12-27","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing, Other","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 408.07, Osceola County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.600364923477173,"median_income_tract":80170,"summary":"Dec 27, 2019: 4 killed. Celebration, FL.\nCause: Stabbing, Other · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDeputies went to the home on Reserve Place about 9 a.m. Monday, January 13, 2020, to assist federal agents in arresting Anthony Todt on a warrant, which is when they found the four bodies inside. Todd’s wife and her children are believed to have been killed sometime toward the end of December. They were given an overdose of Benadryl and then stabbed to death. The last time anyone spoke to Todt’s wife was 12/26/2019.  Todt., a physical therapist whose license to practice had expired was under pressure from creditors, landlords, Medicaid investigators and federal agents. Todt was convicted and sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 408.07, Osceola County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 2.6% in poverty, median household income $80,170, 67.2% white, 0.0% Black, 25.4% Hispanic/Latino, 57.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Osceola Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":11.67,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.25,"nearest_level1_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":26.04,"nearest_level1_miles":16.18,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.523315,28.329962]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-428","properties":{"name":"Grantsville, UT","date":"2020-01-17","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1307.06, Tooele County, Utah","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.9390809535980225,"median_income_tract":105783,"summary":"Jan 17, 2020: 4 killed, 1 injured. Grantsville, UT.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAccording to his confession, 16-year-old Colin Haynie, killed his mother first at about 1 pm. He then killed his siblings as they returned home. Haynie pleaded guilty to the murders and is awaiting sentencing.\nCensus Tract 1307.06, Tooele County, Utah (ACS 2017-2021): 2.9% in poverty, median household income $105,783, 94.5% white, 0.0% Black, 3.3% Hispanic/Latino, 3.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Jordan Valley Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":38.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":23.94,"nearest_level1_center":"Intermountain Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":46.11,"nearest_level1_miles":28.65,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-112.431084,40.597809]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-429","properties":{"name":"Vanceboro, NC","date":"2020-01-24","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9602.01, Craven County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":20.939674377441406,"median_income_tract":31834,"summary":"Jan 24, 2020: 4 killed. Vanceboro, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPolice went to check on a family after getting a call from a relative concerned after being unable to reach their loved ones for days. In the living room of the home, deputies found the bodies of four victims, all with fatal gunshot wounds. In the master bedroom deputies found the family's dog shot dead next to Michael Ray Ireland, 39, who they suspect had killed his wife and children before taking his own life.\nCensus Tract 9602.01, Craven County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 20.9% in poverty, median household income $31,834, 63.9% white, 30.4% Black, 4.1% Hispanic/Latino, 16.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Vidant Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":49.41,"nearest_trauma_miles":30.7,"nearest_level1_center":"Vidant Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":49.41,"nearest_level1_miles":30.7,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.110161,35.233578]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-430","properties":{"name":"Indianapolis, IN","date":"2020-02-05","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3302.11, Marion County, Indiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":15.790510177612305,"median_income_tract":36275,"summary":"Feb 5, 2020: 4 killed. Indianapolis, IN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 4\nThe Indianapolis Police were called to an apartment in the 4100 block of Shady Oak Drive just before 10:30 p.m. after a neighbor noticed a back patio door was shattered and saw someone fleeing from the residence. Officers found four victims—three men and a woman—dead inside the apartment. Cameron Banks, Lesean Watkins, Rodreice Anderson, and Desmond Banks were arrested for murder. Anderson pleaded guilty to a reduced charge of robbery in exchange for testifying against his accomplices. The other three were tried and convicted of murder. According to authorities, the murders were connected to robbery.\nCensus Tract 3302.11, Marion County, Indiana (ACS 2017-2021): 15.8% in poverty, median household income $36,275, 24.7% white, 56.6% Black, 13.2% Hispanic/Latino, 8.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Indiana University Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":15.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.76,"nearest_level1_center":"Indiana University Health","nearest_level1_km":15.71,"nearest_level1_miles":9.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.987488,39.83223]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-431","properties":{"name":"Milwaukee, WI","date":"2020-02-26","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 123, Milwaukee County, Wisconsin","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":43.55432891845703,"median_income_tract":22250,"summary":"Feb 26, 2020: 5 killed. Milwaukee, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nFollowing a long-standing dispute with a co-worker, Anthony Ferrill shot and killed 5 fellow employees at the Milwaukee facility of the Molson Coors Beverage Company before turning the gun on himself. Reportedly, he felt that he was being harassed by others on the job.\nCensus Tract 123, Milwaukee County, Wisconsin (ACS 2017-2021): 43.6% in poverty, median household income $22,250, 17.9% white, 71.1% Black, 9.1% Hispanic/Latino, 13.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Aurora Sinai Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":2.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.68,"nearest_level1_center":"Childrens Hospital Of Wisconsin","nearest_level1_km":5.14,"nearest_level1_miles":3.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.960991,43.044498]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-473","properties":{"name":"Alexandria, LA","date":"2020-02-29","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 126, Rapides Parish, Louisiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":25.51898765563965,"median_income_tract":33971,"summary":"Feb 29, 2020: 4 killed. Alexandria, LA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nTamielya Brevelle set fire to a house, killing a woman and her three grandchildren. Brevelle was pregnant by the father of one of the children who died. She and her niece Dorothy Bosby were subsequently charged with second-degree murder. Brevelle pleaded guilty and was sentenced to 40 years in prison, while Bosby is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 126, Rapides Parish, Louisiana (ACS 2017-2021): 25.5% in poverty, median household income $33,971, 42.4% white, 43.7% Black, 4.3% Hispanic/Latino, 10.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Rapides Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.4,"nearest_level1_center":"Ochsner Lsu Health Shreveport","nearest_level1_km":180.84,"nearest_level1_miles":112.37,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-92.465736,31.28318]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-432","properties":{"name":"Springfield, MO","date":"2020-03-15","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 39, Greene County, Missouri","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.029345512390137,"median_income_tract":63194,"summary":"Mar 15, 2020: 4 killed, 2 injured. Springfield, MO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nPolice received reports of a gunman firing shots from a car at several locations in Springfield. The vehicle crashed into the Kum &amp; Go gas station and convenience store and the gunman ran inside and began shooting. The first two officers who arrived were shot. The fatalities included three customers, one police officer, and the assailant. The assailant, Joaquin Roman, was mentally ill, according to his mother.  According to one of the surviving victims, Roman gave a half-gibberish speech about being disrespected throughout his life and wanting to inflict pain on others. There was evidence that Roman had searched online for \"mental illness\" and \"tactical shooting\" a few days before the attack. Roman committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 39, Greene County, Missouri (ACS 2017-2021): 9.0% in poverty, median household income $63,194, 87.7% white, 0.0% Black, 2.7% Hispanic/Latino, 5.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mercy Hospital Springfield","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.72,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.93,"nearest_level1_center":"Mercy Hospital Springfield","nearest_level1_km":4.72,"nearest_level1_miles":2.93,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-93.228912,37.158081]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-433","properties":{"name":"Moncure, NC","date":"2020-03-15","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 207.02, Chatham County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.100171089172363,"median_income_tract":80902,"summary":"Mar 15, 2020: 6 killed. Moncure, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSeven family members found dead in an apparent murder-suicide with Larry Ray believed to be the shooter. The shootings took place in neighboring homes.\nCensus Tract 207.02, Chatham County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 6.1% in poverty, median household income $80,902, 84.1% white, 6.0% Black, 7.5% Hispanic/Latino, 10.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Wakemed Cary Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":27.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":16.87,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of North Carolina Hospitals","nearest_level1_km":35.28,"nearest_level1_miles":21.92,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.016754,35.588348]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-470","properties":{"name":"Laredo, TX","date":"2020-04-16","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing, Asphyxiation","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 18.20, Webb County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":42.21807861328125,"median_income_tract":31731,"summary":"Apr 16, 2020: 4 killed. Laredo, TX.\nCause: Stabbing, Asphyxiation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nResponding to an “unknown traffic call,” the police discovered blood inside the residence and noticed that the family was missing. A search of the area yielded three bodies in the rear empty lot of the residence. Samuel Lopez, 20, pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 18.20, Webb County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 42.2% in poverty, median household income $31,731, 16.4% white, 0.0% Black, 74.6% Hispanic/Latino, 10.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Laredo Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":9.07,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.64,"nearest_level1_center":"Doctors Hospital At Renaissance","nearest_level1_km":183.73,"nearest_level1_miles":114.17,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-99.479813,27.451298]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-434","properties":{"name":"Milwaukee, WI","date":"2020-04-27","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 84, Milwaukee County, Wisconsin","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":29.850746154785156,"median_income_tract":19760,"summary":"Apr 27, 2020: 5 killed. Milwaukee, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThe police receive a 911 call from the person believed to be the assailant. Upon arriving at the home, officers found five victims fatally shot.  In addition, young child was found alive in the house, and investigators believe the shooter decided to spare the infant's life. Christopher Stokes, the suspected shooter who had a criminal record, was arrested. Stokes pleaded guilty and was sentenced to prison for 205 years.\nCensus Tract 84, Milwaukee County, Wisconsin (ACS 2017-2021): 29.9% in poverty, median household income $19,760, 2.5% white, 75.1% Black, 7.1% Hispanic/Latino, 33.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Aurora Sinai Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":3.19,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.98,"nearest_level1_center":"Childrens Hospital Of Wisconsin","nearest_level1_km":8.54,"nearest_level1_miles":5.3,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.926765,43.071163]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-436","properties":{"name":"Valhermoso Springs, AL","date":"2020-06-04","killed":7,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 57.04, Morgan County, Alabama","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":11.838942527770996,"median_income_tract":63824,"summary":"Jun 4, 2020: 7 killed. Valhermoso Springs, AL.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nDeputies responding to a call about a shooting found seven people dead inside a home that had been set afire. Investigators believe the victims, three women and four men, were shot. The victims and offenders were part of a motorcycle club called \"Seven Deadly Sins.\" It is believed the shooting involved a dispute among members of this motorcycle club. It is reported that the two suspects--John Legg and Frederic Rogers--went to the house to \"wipe the slate clean\" because several personal firearms were missing and there had been \"perceived disobedience\" toward a local membership club. Neighbors said the house known for heavy drug activity. Two of the victims were reportedly killed only because the shooters didn’t want to leave behind any witnesses. The other victims were killed because of their association with the Seven Deadly Sins club or its members, according to investigators. Legg and Rogers were both charged and are awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 57.04, Morgan County, Alabama (ACS 2017-2021): 11.8% in poverty, median household income $63,824, 91.8% white, 0.0% Black, 4.5% Hispanic/Latino, 12.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Crestwood Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":21.22,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.19,"nearest_level1_center":"The Huntsville Hospital","nearest_level1_km":23.72,"nearest_level1_miles":14.74,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.676308,34.523109]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-437","properties":{"name":"San Antonio, TX","date":"2020-06-04","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Asphyxiation","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1918.09, Bexar County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.0861456394195557,"median_income_tract":118565,"summary":"Jun 4, 2020: 5 killed. San Antonio, TX.\nCause: Asphyxiation · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSix members of a military family, including four young children, were found dead in their car in the family’s garage in San Antonio, apparently after suffering from intentional carbon monoxide poisoning. Investigators believe it to be murder-suicide. The presumed assailant Jared Harless and his wife plus their four children, ranging in age from 11 months to 4 years, were discovered along with two cats found dead in a basket in the front seat.\nCensus Tract 1918.09, Bexar County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 2.1% in poverty, median household income $118,565, 51.6% white, 1.6% Black, 36.6% Hispanic/Latino, 3.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"North Central Baptist Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":5.77,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.58,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":19.88,"nearest_level1_miles":12.35,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-98.498741,29.671835]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-451","properties":{"name":"Monroe, LA","date":"2020-06-11","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 110, Ouachita Parish, Louisiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":54.56385040283203,"median_income_tract":26541,"summary":"Jun 11, 2020: 5 killed. Monroe, LA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nBrittany Tucker fatally shot her neighbor and then went back to her apartment and shot and killed four of her children. She then committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 110, Ouachita Parish, Louisiana (ACS 2017-2021): 54.6% in poverty, median household income $26,541, 4.3% white, 95.2% Black, 0.4% Hispanic/Latino, 10.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Francis Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":7.26,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.51,"nearest_level1_center":"Ochsner Lsu Health Shreveport","nearest_level1_km":156.8,"nearest_level1_miles":97.43,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-92.091202,32.437584]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-438","properties":{"name":"Charlotte, NC","date":"2020-06-22","killed":4,"injured":5,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting, Vehicle crash","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 48, Mecklenburg County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":29.159961700439453,"median_income_tract":25607,"summary":"Jun 22, 2020: 4 killed, 5 injured. Charlotte, NC.\nCause: Shooting, Vehicle crash · Type: Public · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Open space · Offenders: 2\nA crowd initially gathered on the street for an unrelated Juneteenth celebration. Crowds gathered again nightly through Sunday, and police said there were about 400 people on the scene when shots rang out at about 12:30 am early in the morning. Three victims were initially reported dead and a fourth died a day later at the hospital. A total of 181 shell casings were found at the scene. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 48, Mecklenburg County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 29.2% in poverty, median household income $25,607, 3.7% white, 87.8% Black, 8.1% Hispanic/Latino, 10.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Novant Health Presbyterian Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":6.06,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Atrium Health University City","nearest_level1_km":11.1,"nearest_level1_miles":6.9,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.855186,35.260117]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-439","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2020-07-04","killed":4,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 8391, Cook County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":10.247503280639648,"median_income_tract":112257,"summary":"Jul 4, 2020: 4 killed, 4 injured. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nFour people were killed and four wounded in a shooting in Englewood on the South Side. They were at a large gathering in the street about 11:35 p.m. in the 6100 block of South Carpenter Street when four males walked up and started shooting, according to Chicago police. This case is unsolved.\nCensus Tract 8391, Cook County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 10.2% in poverty, median household income $112,257, 47.0% white, 11.3% Black, 11.5% Hispanic/Latino, 12.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Northwestern Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.58,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.98,"nearest_level1_center":"Northwestern Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":1.58,"nearest_level1_miles":0.98,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.632401,41.883228]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-440","properties":{"name":"Paterson, NJ","date":"2020-07-07","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 1815, Passaic County, New Jersey","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":29.197708129882812,"median_income_tract":33086,"summary":"Jul 7, 2020: 4 killed, 3 injured. Paterson, NJ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nSeven people were shot, four of them fatally, in a hail of gunfire in Paterson, NJ after 11 pm in what has been called a gang-related incident. The case is unsolved.\nCensus Tract 1815, Passaic County, New Jersey (ACS 2017-2021): 29.2% in poverty, median household income $33,086, 1.2% white, 49.3% Black, 48.8% Hispanic/Latino, 4.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St Joseph'S University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":2.25,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.4,"nearest_level1_center":"Hackensack University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":9.86,"nearest_level1_miles":6.13,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.161552,40.922855]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-441","properties":{"name":"Detroit, MI","date":"2020-07-19","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 5334, Wayne County, Michigan","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":42.80500411987305,"median_income_tract":16689,"summary":"Jul 19, 2020: 4 killed. Detroit, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nAccording to authorities, 25-year-old Mickey Dane Douglas, while out on parole for robbery conviction, claims someone made a comment about his gym shoes that made him feel threatened. He then shot four people, three of whom died at the scene and a fourth died days later from his injuries. Douglas was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 5334, Wayne County, Michigan (ACS 2017-2021): 42.8% in poverty, median household income $16,689, 0.0% white, 100.0% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 40.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Henry Ford Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.7,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.68,"nearest_level1_center":"Henry Ford Hospital","nearest_level1_km":2.7,"nearest_level1_miles":1.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.117439,42.369869]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-442","properties":{"name":"Elyira, OH","date":"2020-07-28","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 704, Lorain County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":23.68265151977539,"median_income_tract":45492,"summary":"Jul 28, 2020: 4 killed. Elyira, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nOfficers were called to 537 Willow Park Road just after 8:00 a.m. on July 29, 2020 for a welfare check. When they arrived, they found five people dead inside the house. All five sustained what appeared to be gunshot wounds.  In what appeared to be a murder-suicide, 44-year-old John Nelson fatally shot his wife and three children before turning the gun on himself. It is believed that the deaths occurred on July 28.\nCensus Tract 704, Lorain County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 23.7% in poverty, median household income $45,492, 52.1% white, 23.5% Black, 11.2% Hispanic/Latino, 4.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Specialty Hosp. Of Lorain","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":9.29,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Metrohealth Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":35.77,"nearest_level1_miles":22.23,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.11412,41.383812]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-481","properties":{"name":"Denver, CO","date":"2020-08-05","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 83.88, Denver County, Colorado","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.865622043609619,"median_income_tract":86676,"summary":"Aug 5, 2020: 5 killed. Denver, CO.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 3\nThree adults and two children died when fire swept through their two-story home in the Green Valley Ranch neighborhood in Northeast Denver at about 2:55 a.m. on August 5. Three teenagers were arrested months later and charged with murder, burglary, assault, and arson. The sister of one of the accused was also arrested on gun and drug charges. It was later determined that the house was set on fire by mistake as the teenage suspects were allegedly trying to set fire to a different home after a drug deal gone wrong. Charges against the teenagers are pending trial.\nCensus Tract 83.88, Denver County, Colorado (ACS 2017-2021): 7.9% in poverty, median household income $86,676, 21.1% white, 19.1% Black, 50.2% Hispanic/Latino, 5.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Of Colorado Hospital Anschutz Inpatient","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":7.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.77,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Colorado Hospital Anschutz Inpatient","nearest_level1_km":7.68,"nearest_level1_miles":4.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.78038,39.793156]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-444","properties":{"name":"Belleville, MI","date":"2020-08-15","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5893, Wayne County, Michigan","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.517416954040527,"median_income_tract":90295,"summary":"Aug 15, 2020: 4 killed. Belleville, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour cousins were shot to death allegedly by Raymond Bailey, the former fiancé of one of the victims who had previously been accused of domestic violence. Bailey was arrested, but died prior to trial from injuries he received while fleeing the police.\nCensus Tract 5893, Wayne County, Michigan (ACS 2017-2021): 5.5% in poverty, median household income $90,295, 87.7% white, 8.4% Black, 1.4% Hispanic/Latino, 10.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Beaumont Hospital - Wayne","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":16.33,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.15,"nearest_level1_center":"St Joseph Mercy Hospital","nearest_level1_km":22.01,"nearest_level1_miles":13.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.447594,42.139732]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-446","properties":{"name":"Aguanga, CA","date":"2020-09-07","killed":7,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 444.06, Riverside County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":19.98021697998047,"median_income_tract":50765,"summary":"Sep 7, 2020: 7 killed. Aguanga, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nSeven people were fatally shot at a residence authorities believe was being used \"\"to manufacture and harvest an illicit marijuana operation.\"\" Six of the victims were killed at the scene and a seventh was hospitalized and died later the same day. Sheriff Chad Bianco said that the illegal marijuana growing and processing operation was run by a local Laotian organized crime syndicate believed to be based in the U.S.The case is unsolved.\nCensus Tract 444.06, Riverside County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 20.0% in poverty, median household income $50,765, 68.7% white, 0.0% Black, 27.0% Hispanic/Latino, 22.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Southwest Healthcare System","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":38.12,"nearest_trauma_miles":23.69,"nearest_level1_center":"Riverside Community Hospital","nearest_level1_km":75.28,"nearest_level1_miles":46.78,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-116.859665,33.456596]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-447","properties":{"name":"Palmer, AK","date":"2020-11-30","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 12.01, Matanuska-Susitna Borough, Alaska","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":11.85978889465332,"median_income_tract":69292,"summary":"Nov 30, 2020: 4 killed. Palmer, AK.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMalachi Maxon, 18, just out of jail for assault, allegedly killed four members of his family. The shootings occurred at two locations about 30-minute drive apart. A 6-year-old was apparently spared during the early morning shooting spree north of Anchorage because of defective bullets. Maxon was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 12.01, Matanuska-Susitna Borough, Alaska (ACS 2017-2021): 11.9% in poverty, median household income $69,292, 70.4% white, 1.5% Black, 8.5% Hispanic/Latino, 7.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Mat - Su Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":9.49,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.9,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":2293.99,"nearest_level1_miles":1425.42,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-149.108566,61.609943]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-461","properties":{"name":"Williamsburg, WV","date":"2020-12-08","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9502, Greenbrier County, West Virginia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":37.82243728637695,"median_income_tract":26409,"summary":"Dec 8, 2020: 5 killed. Williamsburg, WV.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nOreanna Myers shot her five children, set the house on fire, and went outside and killed herself. The investigation subsequently concluded that it was murder-suicide.\nCensus Tract 9502, Greenbrier County, West Virginia (ACS 2017-2021): 37.8% in poverty, median household income $26,409, 87.7% white, 1.2% Black, 1.8% Hispanic/Latino, 19.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Pocahontas Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":41.73,"nearest_trauma_miles":25.93,"nearest_level1_center":"Carilion Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":96.48,"nearest_level1_miles":59.95,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.507431,37.994598]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-448","properties":{"name":"Elkview, WV","date":"2020-12-13","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 113.02, Kanawha County, West Virginia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":3.1969521045684814,"median_income_tract":65837,"summary":"Dec 13, 2020: 4 killed. Elkview, WV.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nTwo teenagers, Gavin Smith and Rebecca Walker, reportedly shot four victims to death in their home. The victims were the boy’s family. Smith was convicted and is awaiting sentencing, while Walker pleaded guilty and received a 10-year prison sentence.\nCensus Tract 113.02, Kanawha County, West Virginia (ACS 2017-2021): 3.2% in poverty, median household income $65,837, 93.3% white, 0.5% Black, 0.3% Hispanic/Latino, 5.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Camc - Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":15.51,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.64,"nearest_level1_center":"Charleston Area Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":15.75,"nearest_level1_miles":9.78,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.483299,38.433559]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-449","properties":{"name":"Meridian, MS","date":"2020-12-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 105.01, Lauderdale County, Mississippi","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":10.190839767456055,"median_income_tract":78438,"summary":"Dec 22, 2020: 4 killed. Meridian, MS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nConducting a welfare check, Lauderdale County deputies found three bodies at a residence and another at a nearby location. The assailant Matthew Tucker killed himself during pursuit by law enforcement.\nCensus Tract 105.01, Lauderdale County, Mississippi (ACS 2017-2021): 10.2% in poverty, median household income $78,438, 91.1% white, 4.7% Black, 4.1% Hispanic/Latino, 6.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Rush Foundation Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":8.97,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.58,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Mississippi Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":142.2,"nearest_level1_miles":88.36,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.66053,32.295631]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-450","properties":{"name":"Atkins, AR","date":"2020-12-25","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5502.02, Fulton County, Arkansas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.5,"median_income_tract":40085,"summary":"Dec 25, 2020: 4 killed. Atkins, AR.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFive females were found dead in an apparent murder-suicide. The relationship of the victims was not disclosed, although authorities described the killings as \"domestic related.\" There has also been no report of which was the offender.\nCensus Tract 5502.02, Fulton County, Arkansas (ACS 2017-2021): 16.5% in poverty, median household income $40,085, 96.9% white, 0.6% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 26.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Fulton County Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":26.11,"nearest_trauma_miles":16.22,"nearest_level1_center":"Cox Medical Centers South Hospital","nearest_level1_km":140.51,"nearest_level1_miles":87.31,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-92.089729,36.31588]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-453","properties":{"name":"Evanston, IL","date":"2021-01-09","killed":5,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 8103.01, Cook County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.832236289978027,"median_income_tract":81717,"summary":"Jan 9, 2021: 5 killed, 3 injured. Evanston, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nJason Nightengale shot seven victims, four of them fatally, during a four-hour rampage that started in Chicago and ended in Evanston, where he was shot dead by police.\nCensus Tract 8103.01, Cook County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 9.8% in poverty, median household income $81,717, 30.7% white, 23.1% Black, 38.6% Hispanic/Latino, 1.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Presence Chicago Hospitals Network","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":0.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.44,"nearest_level1_center":"Presence Chicago Hospitals Network","nearest_level1_km":0.71,"nearest_level1_miles":0.44,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.690407,42.01965]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-455","properties":{"name":"Indianapolis, IN","date":"2021-01-24","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2, Howard County, Indiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":17.42048454284668,"median_income_tract":33652,"summary":"Jan 24, 2021: 5 killed, 1 injured. Indianapolis, IN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFive adults, one of whom was pregnant, were found dead inside a residence. Investigators were led to the crime scene after making contact with a 15-year-old male who was found nearby suffering from gunshot wounds. Raymond Childs, 17, was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 2, Howard County, Indiana (ACS 2017-2021): 17.4% in poverty, median household income $33,652, 35.1% white, 44.0% Black, 15.7% Hispanic/Latino, 30.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Community Hospital Of Anderson And Madison County","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":53.85,"nearest_trauma_miles":33.46,"nearest_level1_center":"Ascension St Vincent Hospital","nearest_level1_km":65.81,"nearest_level1_miles":40.89,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.108429,40.497093]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-457","properties":{"name":"Muskogee, OK","date":"2021-02-02","killed":6,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9.02, Muskogee County, Oklahoma","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":31.488121032714844,"median_income_tract":40200,"summary":"Feb 2, 2021: 6 killed, 2 injured. Muskogee, OK.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nOfficers responding to a 911 call about a shooting encountered an armed suspect at the house, The suspect Jarron Pridgeon fled on foot after an officer fired but missed. Pridgeon was arrested after a short pursuit. Found dead inside the house were the suspect's brother and four children. Another child died after being taken by air to a hospital in Tulsa. The children's mother suffered life-threatening injuries and was taken to a Tulsa hospital and was reported to be in stable condition. Three other children in the home were not injured. Pridgeon was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9.02, Muskogee County, Oklahoma (ACS 2017-2021): 31.5% in poverty, median household income $40,200, 47.1% white, 3.6% Black, 8.1% Hispanic/Latino, 13.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Saint Francis Hospital Muskogee","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":5.7,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.54,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Medical Center Edmond-Er","nearest_level1_km":191.05,"nearest_level1_miles":118.71,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.348091,35.732079]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-459","properties":{"name":"Indianapolis, IN","date":"2021-03-13","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 3545, Marion County, Indiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":25.155725479125977,"median_income_tract":41819,"summary":"Mar 13, 2021: 4 killed, 1 injured. Indianapolis, IN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA woman injured by gunfire directed the police to a home where they found four people, including a child, shot dead. The woman was taken to a hospital in stable condition. Police indicated that the incident was the result of a disagreement in the home that escalated to gunfire. Reportedly, the dispute involved the COVID-19 stimulus check. Malik Halfacre reportedly wanted half of the $1,400, but the woman who survived a gunshot refused to share that much. Halfacre was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 3545, Marion County, Indiana (ACS 2017-2021): 25.2% in poverty, median household income $41,819, 63.8% white, 22.0% Black, 7.1% Hispanic/Latino, 20.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Indiana University Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.62,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.25,"nearest_level1_center":"Indiana University Health","nearest_level1_km":3.62,"nearest_level1_miles":2.25,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.128319,39.771397]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-460","properties":{"name":"Acworth, GA","date":"2021-03-16","killed":8,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 910.14, Cherokee County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":17.07526969909668,"median_income_tract":74068,"summary":"Mar 16, 2021: 8 killed, 1 injured. Acworth, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nA 21-year-old Georgia man was arrested in the killings of eight people at three Atlanta-area massage parlors, six of them women of Asian descent. According to authorities, the assailant, Robert Aaron Long, had previously visited the two Atlanta spas. Long claimed he was a sex-addict and was trying to eliminate temptation. Long pleaded guilty and received a sentence of life without parole.\nCensus Tract 910.14, Cherokee County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 17.1% in poverty, median household income $74,068, 53.7% white, 14.9% Black, 25.2% Hispanic/Latino, 4.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Wellstar Kennestone Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":14.22,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Wellstar Atlanta Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":41.31,"nearest_level1_miles":25.67,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.576263,34.094143]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-462","properties":{"name":"Boulder, CO","date":"2021-03-22","killed":10,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 125.08, Boulder County, Colorado","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.346153259277344,"median_income_tract":72266,"summary":"Mar 22, 2021: 10 killed. Boulder, CO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nTen people, including a Boulder police officer, were killed in a shooting at the King Soopers supermarket in Boulder, Colo. Ahmad Al Aliwi Alissa was arrested and treated for injuries. Allissa was ruled incompetent to stand trial.\nCensus Tract 125.08, Boulder County, Colorado (ACS 2017-2021): 16.3% in poverty, median household income $72,266, 74.6% white, 0.7% Black, 11.2% Hispanic/Latino, 0.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Foothills Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.65,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.27,"nearest_level1_center":"Centura Health - St Anthony Hospital","nearest_level1_km":31.13,"nearest_level1_miles":19.34,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-105.237717,39.983521]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-463","properties":{"name":"Baldwin and Essex, MD","date":"2021-03-28","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 4102, Baltimore County, Maryland","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":3.5214085578918457,"median_income_tract":154779,"summary":"Mar 28, 2021: 4 killed, 1 injured. Baldwin and Essex, MD.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nJoshua Green fatally shot his parents. He then drove to the Essex Royal Farms convenience store where he shot three, two of them fatally. He then committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 4102, Baltimore County, Maryland (ACS 2017-2021): 3.5% in poverty, median household income $154,779, 95.4% white, 1.0% Black, 1.6% Hispanic/Latino, 1.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sinai Hospital Of Baltimore","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":20.89,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.98,"nearest_level1_center":"The Johns Hopkins Hospital","nearest_level1_km":23.8,"nearest_level1_miles":14.79,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.514191,39.501492]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-464","properties":{"name":"Orange, CA","date":"2021-03-31","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 762.01, Orange County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.017616271972656,"median_income_tract":129356,"summary":"Mar 31, 2021: 4 killed, 1 injured. Orange, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nAfter locking the courtyard gate, Aminadab Galaxio-Gonzales allegedly entered the office of United Homes, a mobile homes real estate business on West Lincoln Avenue, and opened fire, killing the owner, his daughter, a longtime employee, and a 9-year-old boy. The boy’s mother was wounded and later released from the hospital. She also worked at Unified Homes. When police arrived, they found the woman’s arms wrapped around her son. In addition, the assailant’s ex-wife was a former employee of the company. Galaxio-Gonzales was arrested and subsequently rueled incompetent to stand trial.\nCensus Tract 762.01, Orange County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 5.0% in poverty, median household income $129,356, 34.0% white, 0.7% Black, 31.2% Hispanic/Latino, 0.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Of California Irvine Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":6.07,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.77,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Irvine Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":6.07,"nearest_level1_miles":3.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-117.853783,33.835072]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-465","properties":{"name":"Allen, TX","date":"2021-04-03","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 314.25, Collin County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.31975793838501,"median_income_tract":122926,"summary":"Apr 3, 2021: 4 killed. Allen, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nTwo brothers, Tanvir and Farhan Towhid, formed a suicide pact which included killing the other four family members. The police found the 6 bodies while conducting a welfare check.\nCensus Tract 314.25, Collin County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 7.3% in poverty, median household income $122,926, 60.3% white, 9.4% Black, 16.6% Hispanic/Latino, 0.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Texas Health Presbyterian Hospital Allen","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":4.72,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.93,"nearest_level1_center":"Medical City Plano","nearest_level1_km":14.79,"nearest_level1_miles":9.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.631622,33.091648]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-466","properties":{"name":"Rock Hill, SC","date":"2021-04-07","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 613.02, York County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.2056097984313965,"median_income_tract":80617,"summary":"Apr 7, 2021: 6 killed. Rock Hill, SC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA doctor, his wife, their two grandchildren, and two HVAC workmen were fatally shot in the doctor’s home. After negotiations with the police failed to get him to surrender, the suspect Philip Adams, a former NFL player, committed suicide.\nCensus Tract 613.02, York County, South Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 5.2% in poverty, median household income $80,617, 77.2% white, 19.1% Black, 2.4% Hispanic/Latino, 8.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Piedmont Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":11.62,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.22,"nearest_level1_center":"Atrium Health University City","nearest_level1_km":57.95,"nearest_level1_miles":36.01,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.058563,34.852249]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-467","properties":{"name":"Indianapolis, IN","date":"2021-04-15","killed":8,"injured":4,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 3908.02, Marion County, Indiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":10.849056243896484,"median_income_tract":61765,"summary":"Apr 15, 2021: 8 killed, 4 injured. Indianapolis, IN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the authorities, Brandon Hole, a former employee of FedEx, entered the facility near the Indianapolis airport and started firing outside and then inside, killing 9 and injuring 4, before taking his own life. FedEx said Hole worked at the facility from August to October 2020. His employment was terminated when he failed to return to work.\nCensus Tract 3908.02, Marion County, Indiana (ACS 2017-2021): 10.8% in poverty, median household income $61,765, 73.0% white, 7.9% Black, 15.6% Hispanic/Latino, 12.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Eskenazi Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":15.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.93,"nearest_level1_center":"Eskenazi Health","nearest_level1_km":15.98,"nearest_level1_miles":9.93,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.32235,39.681236]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-468","properties":{"name":"Boone, NC","date":"2021-04-28","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9207.03, Watauga County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.093496322631836,"median_income_tract":68413,"summary":"Apr 28, 2021: 4 killed. Boone, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTwo police officers were fatally shot when conducting a welfare check. After a 13-hour standoff, Isaac Barnes, who had also killed his mother and stepfather, took his own life.\nCensus Tract 9207.03, Watauga County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 12.1% in poverty, median household income $68,413, 88.8% white, 3.3% Black, 5.8% Hispanic/Latino, 14.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Johnson City Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":70.77,"nearest_trauma_miles":43.97,"nearest_level1_center":"Johnson City Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":70.77,"nearest_level1_miles":43.97,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.604187,36.212643]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-469","properties":{"name":"Colorado Springs, CO","date":"2021-05-09","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 65.02, El Paso County, Colorado","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":18.161523818969727,"median_income_tract":61679,"summary":"May 9, 2021: 6 killed. Colorado Springs, CO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTeodoro Macia, 28, killed his girlfriend and others at a birthday party and then took his own life.\nCensus Tract 65.02, El Paso County, Colorado (ACS 2017-2021): 18.2% in poverty, median household income $61,679, 34.1% white, 15.3% Black, 35.8% Hispanic/Latino, 9.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Colo Health Memorial Hospital Central","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":7.89,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.9,"nearest_level1_center":"University Colo Health Memorial Hospital Central","nearest_level1_km":7.89,"nearest_level1_miles":4.9,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.732185,38.79163]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-471","properties":{"name":"West Jefferson, OH","date":"2021-05-24","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 404, Madison County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.930685043334961,"median_income_tract":67446,"summary":"May 24, 2021: 4 killed. West Jefferson, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour people were killed in a shooting at an apartment in West Jefferson, a suburb near Columbus. Three victims were found inside the apartment and one other person was found outside. John Steckel, 35, was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 404, Madison County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 12.9% in poverty, median household income $67,446, 93.2% white, 0.5% Black, 2.0% Hispanic/Latino, 5.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Ohio State University Hospitals","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":22.34,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.88,"nearest_level1_center":"The Ohio State University Hospitals","nearest_level1_km":22.34,"nearest_level1_miles":13.88,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.27346,39.947151]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-472","properties":{"name":"San Jose, CA","date":"2021-05-26","killed":9,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Government/Transit","tract":"Census Tract 5002, Santa Clara County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.274111747741699,"median_income_tract":152118,"summary":"May 26, 2021: 9 killed, 1 injured. San Jose, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Government/Transit · Offenders: 1\nSamuel Cassidy, 57, allegedly opened fire at a light rail yard of the Santa Clara Valley Transportation Authority, killing nine people and then himself.  Cassidy was an employee at the rail yard.\nCensus Tract 5002, Santa Clara County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 6.3% in poverty, median household income $152,118, 28.7% white, 6.3% Black, 36.3% Hispanic/Latino, 14.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Santa Clara Valley Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.2,"nearest_level1_center":"Santa Clara Valley Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.15,"nearest_level1_miles":3.2,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-121.907043,37.354359]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-474","properties":{"name":"Fort Wayne, IN","date":"2021-06-02","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 28, Allen County, Indiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":35.87479782104492,"median_income_tract":26038,"summary":"Jun 2, 2021: 4 killed. Fort Wayne, IN.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThree children and a woman were found killed in a southeast Fort Wayne home. Each was stabbed multiple times. Police arrested 21-year-old Cohen Bennett Hancz-Barron, the ex-boyfriend of one of the victims. Hancz-Barron was convicted and was sentenced to life without parole.\nCensus Tract 28, Allen County, Indiana (ACS 2017-2021): 35.9% in poverty, median household income $26,038, 20.7% white, 49.2% Black, 21.1% Hispanic/Latino, 12.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Parkview Hospital Randallia","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":4.31,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.68,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Toledo Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":140.46,"nearest_level1_miles":87.28,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.124283,41.058929]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-475","properties":{"name":"Portland, OR","date":"2021-06-06","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8.02, Multnomah County, Oregon","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":13.42367172241211,"median_income_tract":73100,"summary":"Jun 6, 2021: 4 killed, 1 injured. Portland, OR.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 3\nFour people were shot and killed at a Southeast Portland home. A man who was wounded called 911 from inside the home to report the shooting. Investigators suspect a shootout occurred inside after three men arrived and attacked the occupants. Michael Lenoire was arrested and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 8.02, Multnomah County, Oregon (ACS 2017-2021): 13.4% in poverty, median household income $73,100, 77.4% white, 1.0% Black, 8.6% Hispanic/Latino, 6.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ohsu Hospital And Clinics","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.28,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.28,"nearest_level1_center":"Ohsu Hospital And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":5.28,"nearest_level1_miles":3.28,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.619011,45.49231]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-476","properties":{"name":"Chicago, IL","date":"2021-06-15","killed":5,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Unsolved","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8348, Cook County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":38.050498962402344,"median_income_tract":18973,"summary":"Jun 15, 2021: 5 killed, 3 injured. Chicago, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Unsolved · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAn argument during a house party resulted in the shooting death of five victims and injury to three others, The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 8348, Cook County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 38.1% in poverty, median household income $18,973, 1.1% white, 89.4% Black, 8.2% Hispanic/Latino, 29.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The University Of Chicago Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.81,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.37,"nearest_level1_center":"The University Of Chicago Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":3.81,"nearest_level1_miles":2.37,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.649384,41.780842]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-477","properties":{"name":"North Bend, OR","date":"2021-06-18","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Vehicle crash","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 3, Coos County, Oregon","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":20.19230842590332,"median_income_tract":52866,"summary":"Jun 18, 2021: 4 killed, 1 injured. North Bend, OR.\nCause: Shooting, Vehicle crash · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Oen Nicholson killed his father and took his truck. The police say that he then ran over several people in an RV park and shot a woman at a marijuana dispensary. He later kidnapped a woman and forced her to drive to Wisconsin. Nicholson was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 3, Coos County, Oregon (ACS 2017-2021): 20.2% in poverty, median household income $52,866, 71.6% white, 2.1% Black, 11.7% Hispanic/Latino, 11.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bay Area Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":1.66,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.03,"nearest_level1_center":"Ohsu Hospital And Clinics","nearest_level1_km":263.74,"nearest_level1_miles":163.88,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-124.219566,43.394665]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-486","properties":{"name":"Hamilton Township, NJ","date":"2021-07-09","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 30.09, Mercer County, New Jersey","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.019783020019531,"median_income_tract":67967,"summary":"Jul 9, 2021: 4 killed, 3 injured. Hamilton Township, NJ.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nIn the early morning of July 9, 2021, Michael Sanders allegedly set the house on fire, killing his 9-month-old daughter and her grandmother. A third victim died two days later and a fourth person died weeks after the blaze. Sanders was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 30.09, Mercer County, New Jersey (ACS 2017-2021): 7.0% in poverty, median household income $67,967, 77.2% white, 3.5% Black, 9.2% Hispanic/Latino, 0.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Capital Health Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":6.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.26,"nearest_level1_center":"Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":36.65,"nearest_level1_miles":22.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.676506,40.214352]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-478","properties":{"name":"Cherokee County, TX","date":"2021-07-20","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9504, Cherokee County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":35.971221923828125,"median_income_tract":34583,"summary":"Jul 20, 2021: 4 killed. Cherokee County, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 3\nFour victims were found shot to death—one in the driveway and three others inside the residence. The three suspects reportedly met up with one of the victims under the pretense of buying a gun from him but actually planned to steal it. Dylan Welch, Billy Phillips, and Jesse Pawlowski were charged and are awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9504, Cherokee County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 36.0% in poverty, median household income $34,583, 14.8% white, 32.8% Black, 48.0% Hispanic/Latino, 10.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ut Health East Texas Jacksonville Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":0.39,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.24,"nearest_level1_center":"Ut Health East Texas Tyler Regional Hospital","nearest_level1_km":41.71,"nearest_level1_miles":25.92,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.2705,31.9638]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-479","properties":{"name":"Wasco , CA","date":"2021-07-25","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 44.03, Kern County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.5136613845825195,"median_income_tract":61196,"summary":"Jul 25, 2021: 4 killed, 1 injured. Wasco , CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the authorities, Jose Ramirez killed his 42-year-old wife and two sons, ages 17 and 24, inside the family home, as well as a Kern County deputy sheriff who had responded to the scene. Ramirez was killed during a stand-off with the police.\nCensus Tract 44.03, Kern County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 7.5% in poverty, median household income $61,196, 7.6% white, 1.1% Black, 90.2% Hispanic/Latino, 5.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Kern Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":41.56,"nearest_trauma_miles":25.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Community Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":133.19,"nearest_level1_miles":82.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.342628,35.600571]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-482","properties":{"name":"Lakeland, FL","date":"2021-09-05","killed":4,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 122.07, Polk County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.175846099853516,"median_income_tract":49211,"summary":"Sep 5, 2021: 4 killed, 2 injured. Lakeland, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, Bryan Riley, an ex-marine, fatally shot four victims and injured another. After exchanging gunfire with responding officers and the SWAT team (during which an officer was injured), the assailant, who had been injured by the police, surrendered. Riley was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 122.07, Polk County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 5.2% in poverty, median household income $49,211, 76.1% white, 2.0% Black, 9.6% Hispanic/Latino, 10.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lakeland Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":5.64,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.51,"nearest_level1_center":"Tampa General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":53.89,"nearest_level1_miles":33.49,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.946175,28.110661]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-483","properties":{"name":"Houston, TX","date":"2021-09-05","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4208, Harris County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":1.3481364250183105,"median_income_tract":247917,"summary":"Sep 5, 2021: 4 killed. Houston, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nResponding to a house fire, the authorities discovered four people—two adults and two children—fatally shot. There was no forced entry, having the police believing it was a domestic incident. The suspect, 23-year-old William Escaño, took his own life.\nCensus Tract 4208, Harris County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 1.3% in poverty, median household income $247,917, 65.0% white, 1.5% Black, 7.5% Hispanic/Latino, 15.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The Womans Hospital Of Texas","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":5.82,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.61,"nearest_level1_center":"Texas Childrens Hospital","nearest_level1_km":6.39,"nearest_level1_miles":3.97,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.461655,29.683626]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-484","properties":{"name":"Saint Paul, MN","date":"2021-09-12","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 360, Ramsey County, Minnesota","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":10.993208885192871,"median_income_tract":85729,"summary":"Sep 12, 2021: 4 killed. Saint Paul, MN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nFour victims were found shot to death inside an SUV in the middle of a Wisconsin cornfield. However, they were killed in Saint Paul, MN. Antoine Suggs was charged in the murders and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 360, Ramsey County, Minnesota (ACS 2017-2021): 11.0% in poverty, median household income $85,729, 76.0% white, 8.7% Black, 7.7% Hispanic/Latino, 11.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Joseph'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":0.7,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.43,"nearest_level1_center":"Regions Hospital","nearest_level1_km":1.35,"nearest_level1_miles":0.84,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-93.094284,44.943718]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-485","properties":{"name":"Riceville, TN","date":"2021-09-25","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9708.02, McMinn County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":14.117091178894043,"median_income_tract":58934,"summary":"Sep 25, 2021: 4 killed. Riceville, TN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nA dispute over custody of a 10-month-old led to the shooting death of four people. Curtis Smith and Jazzmine Hall were both charged and are awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9708.02, McMinn County, Tennessee (ACS 2017-2021): 14.1% in poverty, median household income $58,934, 93.0% white, 0.7% Black, 1.6% Hispanic/Latino, 7.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Starr Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":10.95,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.8,"nearest_level1_center":"Erlanger Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":64.97,"nearest_level1_miles":40.37,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.695099,35.3731]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-487","properties":{"name":"Clare, MI","date":"2021-10-20","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 4, Clare County, Michigan","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":22.795934677124023,"median_income_tract":46782,"summary":"Oct 20, 2021: 4 killed. Clare, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTwo people were shot to death and the bodies of two others were found on a property in central Michigan. Judy Boyer, 54, pleaded guilty and was sentenced to life without parole eligibility.\nCensus Tract 4, Clare County, Michigan (ACS 2017-2021): 22.8% in poverty, median household income $46,782, 93.8% white, 0.0% Black, 4.4% Hispanic/Latino, 26.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Midmichigan Medical Center - Clare","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":5.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.43,"nearest_level1_center":"Spectrum Health - Butterworth Campus","nearest_level1_km":118.63,"nearest_level1_miles":73.71,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.8284,43.8461]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-488","properties":{"name":"Tacoma, WA","date":"2021-10-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Undetermined","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9400.06, Pierce County, Washington","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":38.29560470581055,"median_income_tract":34231,"summary":"Oct 21, 2021: 4 killed. Tacoma, WA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Undetermined · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTwo women and one man were killed in a shooting at a Tacoma residence. At fourth victim died shortly thereafter at the hospital. Maleke Pate, 22, was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9400.06, Pierce County, Washington (ACS 2017-2021): 38.3% in poverty, median household income $34,231, 16.7% white, 28.4% Black, 12.6% Hispanic/Latino, 1.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Franciscan Health St Joseph Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":4.86,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.02,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":43.32,"nearest_level1_miles":26.92,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.399269,47.21759]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-491","properties":{"name":"Tucson, AZ","date":"2021-11-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":0,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 25.04, Pima County, Arizona","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":23.305084228515625,"median_income_tract":47647,"summary":"Nov 14, 2021: 4 killed. Tucson, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 0\nPolice responded to a trailer park and found three people dead. A fourth person died later at the hospital. The authorities did not believe the shooting to be a random act, but a confrontation between two groups. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 25.04, Pima County, Arizona (ACS 2017-2021): 23.3% in poverty, median household income $47,647, 17.5% white, 0.1% Black, 78.6% Hispanic/Latino, 14.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Banner - University Medical Center South Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":6.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.05,"nearest_level1_center":"Banner - University Medical Center Tucson Campus","nearest_level1_km":8.77,"nearest_level1_miles":5.45,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111,32.177502]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-492","properties":{"name":"Waukesha, WI","date":"2021-11-21","killed":6,"injured":61,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Vehicle crash","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 2011.01, Waukesha County, Wisconsin","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":3.9425132274627686,"median_income_tract":107075,"summary":"Nov 21, 2021: 6 killed, 61 injured. Waukesha, WI.\nCause: Vehicle crash · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nFleeing from the police after a domestic disturbance report, Darrell Brooks, 39, allegedly drove his SUV into the city's annual Christmas parade, killing six and injuring dozens of others. Brooks was convicted by a jury of six counts of first-degree intentional homicide and sentenced to life in prison without the possibility of parole.\nCensus Tract 2011.01, Waukesha County, Wisconsin (ACS 2017-2021): 3.9% in poverty, median household income $107,075, 75.0% white, 0.8% Black, 4.9% Hispanic/Latino, 3.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Childrens Hospital Of Wisconsin","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.88,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.66,"nearest_level1_center":"Childrens Hospital Of Wisconsin","nearest_level1_km":5.88,"nearest_level1_miles":3.66,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.094368,43.02951]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-493","properties":{"name":"Lancaster, CA","date":"2021-11-28","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9005.10, Los Angeles County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":30.183090209960938,"median_income_tract":41360,"summary":"Nov 28, 2021: 5 killed. Lancaster, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nGermarcus David, 29, allegedly killed his four children and their grandmother. David was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9005.10, Los Angeles County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 30.2% in poverty, median household income $41,360, 23.6% white, 34.7% Black, 34.5% Hispanic/Latino, 3.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Antelope Valley Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":7.29,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.53,"nearest_level1_center":"Los Angeles General Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":70.75,"nearest_level1_miles":43.96,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.079102,34.686909]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-494","properties":{"name":"Oxford, MI","date":"2021-11-30","killed":4,"injured":7,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"School","tract":"Census Tract 1210, Oakland County, Michigan","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.4347825050354,"median_income_tract":78750,"summary":"Nov 30, 2021: 4 killed, 7 injured. Oxford, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: School · Offenders: 1\nAfter meeting with school counselors and his parents concerning a disturbing drawing a teacher found on his desk, sophomore Ethan Crumbley killed four and wounded seven others at his high school in Oxford, Mich. using a semiautomatic handgun that was hidden inside his backpack. Crumbley pleaded guilty to murder.\nCensus Tract 1210, Oakland County, Michigan (ACS 2017-2021): 6.4% in poverty, median household income $78,750, 90.6% white, 0.4% Black, 6.2% Hispanic/Latino, 2.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ascension Providence Rochester Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":19.94,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.39,"nearest_level1_center":"Beaumont Hospital - Royal Oak","nearest_level1_km":36.42,"nearest_level1_miles":22.63,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.262253,42.838928]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-495","properties":{"name":"Townsend, DE","date":"2021-12-03","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 168.08, New Castle County, Delaware","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.28179407119751,"median_income_tract":126736,"summary":"Dec 3, 2021: 4 killed. Townsend, DE.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDonald Grier allegedly stabbed his father and three others. The three died from their injuries, and the man’s father died two weeks later.  Grier was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 168.08, New Castle County, Delaware (ACS 2017-2021): 5.3% in poverty, median household income $126,736, 61.7% white, 23.4% Black, 11.5% Hispanic/Latino, 0.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bayhealth Hospital Kent Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":30.53,"nearest_trauma_miles":18.97,"nearest_level1_center":"Christiana Care Health Services - Christiana Hospital","nearest_level1_km":30.89,"nearest_level1_miles":19.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.6381,39.410721]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-496","properties":{"name":"Denver, CO","date":"2021-12-27","killed":5,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 20, Denver County, Colorado","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.854907989501953,"median_income_tract":102520,"summary":"Dec 27, 2021: 5 killed, 2 injured. Denver, CO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nLyndon McLeod, 47, went on a shooting spree that started at a Denver tattoo parlor and ended in Lakewood. The assailant killed five victims and wounding two others. The wounded included a police officer. The gunman was killed in a shootout with the police.\nCensus Tract 20, Denver County, Colorado (ACS 2017-2021): 8.9% in poverty, median household income $102,520, 68.3% white, 9.0% Black, 17.1% Hispanic/Latino, 7.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Denver Health Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.24,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Denver Health Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.24,"nearest_level1_miles":0.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.992363,39.739319]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-497","properties":{"name":"Gulfport, MS","date":"2021-12-31","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":4,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9507.02, Bolivar County, Mississippi","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":37.680721282958984,"median_income_tract":19615,"summary":"Dec 31, 2021: 4 killed, 3 injured. Gulfport, MS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 4\nGunfire erupted at a New Year’s Eve party. Three victims perished that night, and another died at the hospital days later. Two other shooting victims survived their injuries. There is evidence of gang connection, according to the police. Xavier Preston, Mario Clark, Vincent Armstrong, and Khalid Williams were charged and are awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9507.02, Bolivar County, Mississippi (ACS 2017-2021): 37.7% in poverty, median household income $19,615, 16.0% white, 83.8% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 7.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Bolivar Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":1.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.23,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Mississippi Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":164.07,"nearest_level1_miles":101.95,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.717422,33.732712]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-498","properties":{"name":"Inglewood, CA","date":"2022-01-23","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 6009.12, Los Angeles County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.787494659423828,"median_income_tract":69859,"summary":"Jan 23, 2022: 4 killed, 1 injured. Inglewood, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour people were killed and one injured at a shooting that occurred at a birthday party. It is believed to be gang related. The case remains unsolved.\nCensus Tract 6009.12, Los Angeles County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 9.8% in poverty, median household income $69,859, 4.5% white, 16.4% Black, 78.5% Hispanic/Latino, 3.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"California Hospital Medical Center - Los Angeles","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":9.74,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.05,"nearest_level1_center":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":11.15,"nearest_level1_miles":6.93,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.345207,33.97945]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-499","properties":{"name":"Milwaukee, WI","date":"2022-01-23","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1854, Milwaukee County, Wisconsin","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":25.56818199157715,"median_income_tract":40577,"summary":"Jan 23, 2022: 6 killed. Milwaukee, WI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFive people were found dead plus another who died soon thereafter at a Milwaukee residence. According to the police, the homicides stemmed from a robbery associated with illicit drug trade. It is believed that the attack occurred three days before the bodies were found. Travis Birkley was subsequently arrested in connection to the crime and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 1854, Milwaukee County, Wisconsin (ACS 2017-2021): 25.6% in poverty, median household income $40,577, 0.5% white, 94.7% Black, 0.2% Hispanic/Latino, 23.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Aurora Sinai Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":2.57,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.59,"nearest_level1_center":"Childrens Hospital Of Wisconsin","nearest_level1_km":7.35,"nearest_level1_miles":4.57,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.938728,43.064152]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-500","properties":{"name":"Corsicana, TX","date":"2022-02-05","killed":5,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9703.02, Navarro County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":13.915355682373047,"median_income_tract":47258,"summary":"Feb 5, 2022: 5 killed, 2 injured. Corsicana, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nKevin Milazzo killed four family members, including a child, and wounded three others in two residences in Navarro County, near Dallas. He then took his own life inside his vehicle.\nCensus Tract 9703.02, Navarro County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 13.9% in poverty, median household income $47,258, 49.9% white, 9.6% Black, 32.6% Hispanic/Latino, 2.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Navarro Regional Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":0.77,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.48,"nearest_level1_center":"Methodist Dallas Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":81.41,"nearest_level1_miles":50.58,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.495438,32.083549]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-501","properties":{"name":"Sacramento, CA","date":"2022-02-28","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"House of worship","tract":"Census Tract 99, Sacramento County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":15.372298240661621,"median_income_tract":63401,"summary":"Feb 28, 2022: 4 killed. Sacramento, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: House of worship · Offenders: 1\nDavid Mora-Rojas, who was under a restraining order obtained by the mother of his children, killed his three daughters plus a chaperone during a supervised visit held inside a church and then took his own life.\nCensus Tract 99, Sacramento County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 15.4% in poverty, median household income $63,401, 45.6% white, 0.6% Black, 47.2% Hispanic/Latino, 17.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Kaiser Foundation Hospital - South Sacramento","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":15.41,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.58,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":23.83,"nearest_level1_miles":14.81,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-121.489258,38.342289]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-502","properties":{"name":"Sacramento, CA","date":"2022-04-03","killed":6,"injured":10,"offenders":3,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 11.03, Sacramento County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":23.46938705444336,"median_income_tract":38424,"summary":"Apr 3, 2022: 6 killed, 10 injured. Sacramento, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Open space · Offenders: 3\nIn a confrontation between rival gangs, six people (three male gang members and three female bystanders) were killed and 10 others wounded in a shooting in Downtown Sacramento, CA. Three men have been arrested in connection to the shooting.\nCensus Tract 11.03, Sacramento County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 23.5% in poverty, median household income $38,424, 49.9% white, 20.4% Black, 18.0% Hispanic/Latino, 12.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":4.26,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.65,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of California Davis Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":4.26,"nearest_level1_miles":2.65,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-121.493759,38.578812]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-503","properties":{"name":"Duluth, MN","date":"2022-04-20","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 13, St. Louis County, Minnesota","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":45.15805435180664,"median_income_tract":36250,"summary":"Apr 20, 2022: 4 killed. Duluth, MN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nConducting a welfare check because of a reported mental health crisis, the police found five people and a dog dead inside a Duluth home.  Brandon Taylor Cole-Skogstad, 29, had shot his aunt, uncle, two young cousins and their dog while the family slept Tuesday night, police said. He later killed himself with the murder weapon when the police arrived at the house the next afternoon.\nCensus Tract 13, St. Louis County, Minnesota (ACS 2017-2021): 45.2% in poverty, median household income $36,250, 83.0% white, 5.2% Black, 4.5% Hispanic/Latino, 6.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Luke'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":0.66,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.41,"nearest_level1_center":"Essentia Health St. Mary'S Med","nearest_level1_km":1.14,"nearest_level1_miles":0.71,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-92.089203,46.802872]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-504","properties":{"name":"Mountain View, AR","date":"2022-04-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9502.03, Stone County, Arkansas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":35.963382720947266,"median_income_tract":24936,"summary":"Apr 21, 2022: 4 killed. Mountain View, AR.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA pair of double homicides occurred in homes one-quarter mile apart. Donnie Trammell was arrested for the crime and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9502.03, Stone County, Arkansas (ACS 2017-2021): 36.0% in poverty, median household income $24,936, 81.3% white, 0.0% Black, 10.2% Hispanic/Latino, 28.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Stone County Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":17.34,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Arkansas Children'S Hospital","nearest_level1_km":117.44,"nearest_level1_miles":72.97,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-91.934036,35.757851]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-506","properties":{"name":"Gulfport, MS","date":"2022-04-27","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Hotel/Motel","tract":"Census Tract 13.02, Harrison County, Mississippi","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.950028896331787,"median_income_tract":63056,"summary":"Apr 27, 2022: 4 killed. Gulfport, MS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Hotel/Motel · Offenders: 1\nJeremy Raynolds fatally shot three victims at a Biloxi hotel, then carjacked a vehicle in Guilford and shot the driver (who died in surgery). The gunman committed suicide during a stand-off with the police.\nCensus Tract 13.02, Harrison County, Mississippi (ACS 2017-2021): 7.0% in poverty, median household income $63,056, 66.0% white, 18.1% Black, 10.9% Hispanic/Latino, 23.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Merit Health Biloxi","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":10.25,"nearest_trauma_miles":6.37,"nearest_level1_center":"Usa Health University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":92.97,"nearest_level1_miles":57.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.996307,30.38916]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-524","properties":{"name":"Worcester, MA","date":"2022-05-14","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 7318.02, Worcester County, Massachusetts","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":46.77530288696289,"median_income_tract":27443,"summary":"May 14, 2022: 4 killed, 3 injured. Worcester, MA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nYvonne Ngoiri, 36, allegedly set fire to an apartment building, killing four occupants inside. In addition to the four counts of second-degree murder, Ngoiri was charged with two counts of arson of a dwelling, two counts of assault and battery with a dangerous weapon and one count of assault and battery with a dangerous weapon causing serious bodily injury.\nCensus Tract 7318.02, Worcester County, Massachusetts (ACS 2017-2021): 46.8% in poverty, median household income $27,443, 37.9% white, 13.8% Black, 41.7% Hispanic/Latino, 11.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Umass Memorial Med Ctr - Univ Campus","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.81,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.74,"nearest_level1_center":"Umass Memorial Med Ctr - Univ Campus","nearest_level1_km":2.81,"nearest_level1_miles":1.74,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-71.791473,42.26548]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-507","properties":{"name":"Buffalo , NY","date":"2022-05-14","killed":10,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 168.01, Erie County, New York","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":29.01982307434082,"median_income_tract":22338,"summary":"May 14, 2022: 10 killed, 3 injured. Buffalo , NY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nDressed in camouflage, Payton Gendron, 18, allegedly started shooting at customers at a supermarket in a predominantly Black neighborhood, killing 10 and wounding three others. He reportedly was shouting racial epithets and live streaming the attack. Gendron pleaded guilty to charges carrying a mandatory sentence of life without parole.\nCensus Tract 168.01, Erie County, New York (ACS 2017-2021): 29.0% in poverty, median household income $22,338, 5.5% white, 82.8% Black, 5.2% Hispanic/Latino, 25.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"John R. Oishei Children'S Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Pediatric Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.31,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.81,"nearest_level1_center":"Erie County Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":2.7,"nearest_level1_miles":1.68,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-78.854347,42.90773]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-508","properties":{"name":"Uvalde, TX","date":"2022-05-24","killed":21,"injured":17,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"School","tract":"Census Tract 9505, Uvalde County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":22.860700607299805,"median_income_tract":36404,"summary":"May 24, 2022: 21 killed, 17 injured. Uvalde, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: School · Offenders: 1\nFiring off hundreds of rounds, 18-year-old Salvador Ramos fatally shot 19 children and two teachers at the Robb Elementary School. Right before the attack at the school, Ramos shot and injured his grandmother. He was killed in a shootout with responding police.\nCensus Tract 9505, Uvalde County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 22.9% in poverty, median household income $36,404, 10.2% white, 1.0% Black, 88.9% Hispanic/Latino, 9.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Uvalde Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":2.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.57,"nearest_level1_center":"University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":122.1,"nearest_level1_miles":75.87,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-99.787857,29.199699]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-509","properties":{"name":"Stanwood, MI","date":"2022-05-27","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9608, Mecosta County, Michigan","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":19.54221534729004,"median_income_tract":46680,"summary":"May 27, 2022: 4 killed. Stanwood, MI.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nCharles Gillard allegedly shot and killed his wife and three children. He then shot himself but survived the injury. Gillard was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9608, Mecosta County, Michigan (ACS 2017-2021): 19.5% in poverty, median household income $46,680, 94.0% white, 1.6% Black, 1.7% Hispanic/Latino, 7.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Spectrum Health Big Rapids Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":12.7,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.89,"nearest_level1_center":"Spectrum Health - Butterworth Campus","nearest_level1_km":70.16,"nearest_level1_miles":43.59,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.451263,43.580978]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-510","properties":{"name":"Tulsa, OK","date":"2022-06-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Medical facility","tract":"Census Tract 69.05, Tulsa County, Oklahoma","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":23.09433937072754,"median_income_tract":43450,"summary":"Jun 1, 2022: 4 killed. Tulsa, OK.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Medical facility · Offenders: 1\nBlaming his doctor for his post-operative back pain, Michael Louis allegedly killed the doctor as well as three others that were in his path. He then took his own life.\nCensus Tract 69.05, Tulsa County, Oklahoma (ACS 2017-2021): 23.1% in poverty, median household income $43,450, 34.2% white, 23.0% Black, 28.6% Hispanic/Latino, 17.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Saint Francis Hospital, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":3.45,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.14,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Medical Center Edmond-Er","nearest_level1_km":148.87,"nearest_level1_miles":92.5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.903809,36.101269]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-511","properties":{"name":"Centerville, TX","date":"2022-06-02","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9503.01, Leon County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":31.12078285217285,"median_income_tract":36525,"summary":"Jun 2, 2022: 5 killed. Centerville, TX.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nEscaped felon Gonzalo Lopez allegedly killed a man and his grandchildren at his ranch near Centerville, Texas. Lopez was pursued and killed by law enforcement officers.\nCensus Tract 9503.01, Leon County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 31.1% in poverty, median household income $36,525, 78.3% white, 4.7% Black, 16.9% Hispanic/Latino, 58.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Chi St Joseph Health Madison Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":35.75,"nearest_trauma_miles":22.21,"nearest_level1_center":"Baylor Scott And White Medical Center - Temple","nearest_level1_km":130.66,"nearest_level1_miles":81.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.005661,31.25321]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-513","properties":{"name":"Portsmouth, VA","date":"2022-06-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2120, Portsmouth city, Virginia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.568435668945312,"median_income_tract":39474,"summary":"Jun 7, 2022: 4 killed. Portsmouth, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nTwo men came to the door of a home and once inside shot four people. Three died at the scene, and a fourth died three days later from his injuries. Raymond Lee Gore, 57, was arrested and awaits trial. Antwann Gore, 40, was arrested bu the charges against him were dropped for lack of evidence.\nCensus Tract 2120, Portsmouth city, Virginia (ACS 2017-2021): 16.6% in poverty, median household income $39,474, 1.5% white, 96.5% Black, 1.2% Hispanic/Latino, 22.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sentara Norfolk General Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.91,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.43,"nearest_level1_center":"Sentara Norfolk General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.91,"nearest_level1_miles":2.43,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.310928,36.82766]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-514","properties":{"name":"Highland Park, IL","date":"2022-07-04","killed":7,"injured":30,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 8654, Lake County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":4.846882343292236,"median_income_tract":98750,"summary":"Jul 4, 2022: 7 killed, 30 injured. Highland Park, IL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nDressed in women's clothing for disguise purposes, Robert Crimo, 21, allegedly opened fire from a rooftop down at a July 4th parade, killing seven and injuring dozens more. He then drove to Madison, WI, where reportedly, he contemplated another attack. Instead, he returned to Illinois and was arrested, having been identified by a trace of the weapon discarded at the scene. Crimo was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 8654, Lake County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 4.8% in poverty, median household income $98,750, 74.3% white, 0.8% Black, 18.9% Hispanic/Latino, 7.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Northshore University Healthsystem","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":0.91,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.57,"nearest_level1_center":"Advocate Condell Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":16.28,"nearest_level1_miles":10.11,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.800858,42.18512]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-515","properties":{"name":"Houston, TX","date":"2022-07-16","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Gang conflict","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 5503.07, Harris County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":24.510181427001953,"median_income_tract":37155,"summary":"Jul 16, 2022: 4 killed. Houston, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Gang conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAn argument inside an apartment resulted in four people being fatally shot. Eric Reyes has been arrested in the case.\nCensus Tract 5503.07, Harris County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 24.5% in poverty, median household income $37,155, 5.5% white, 61.1% Black, 18.3% Hispanic/Latino, 6.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hca Houston Healthcare Northwest","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":2.28,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.42,"nearest_level1_center":"Memorial Hermann - Texas Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":32.33,"nearest_level1_miles":20.09,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.451302,30.001341]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-517","properties":{"name":"Orlando, FL","date":"2022-08-02","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Undetermined","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 167.35, Orange County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.746341228485107,"median_income_tract":115295,"summary":"Aug 2, 2022: 4 killed. Orlando, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nDonovan Ramirez, 45, killed his wife, adult daughter, and two younger daughters, after which he took his own life.\nCensus Tract 167.35, Orange County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 7.7% in poverty, median household income $115,295, 33.2% white, 5.3% Black, 49.4% Hispanic/Latino, 27.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":17.8,"nearest_trauma_miles":11.06,"nearest_level1_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":17.8,"nearest_level1_miles":11.06,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.237221,28.4233]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-518","properties":{"name":"Laurel, NE","date":"2022-08-04","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Profit","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9772, Cedar County, Nebraska","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.678654193878174,"median_income_tract":65164,"summary":"Aug 4, 2022: 4 killed. Laurel, NE.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Profit · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nJason Jones allegedly killed neighbors in two separate homes three blocks apart. The victims were shot and both homes were set on fire with an accelerant. Jones is charged with four counts of first-degree murder, two counts of first-degree arson and four counts of use of a firearm to commit a felony. Authorities allege that Jones was engaged in a burglary attempt. Jones was charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 9772, Cedar County, Nebraska (ACS 2017-2021): 6.7% in poverty, median household income $65,164, 94.1% white, 0.2% Black, 3.0% Hispanic/Latino, 14.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Providence Medical Center, Inc","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":21.34,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.26,"nearest_level1_center":"The Nebraska Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":158.62,"nearest_level1_miles":98.56,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.066643,42.4291]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-519","properties":{"name":"Dayton, OH","date":"2022-08-05","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1102.01, Montgomery County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.1226396560668945,"median_income_tract":90515,"summary":"Aug 5, 2022: 4 killed. Dayton, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAfter creating a video describing his grievances, Stephen Marlow allegedly shot and killed four victims in two separate homes. He was arrested in Kansas and was extradited back to Ohio. Marlow has been charged and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 1102.01, Montgomery County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 5.1% in poverty, median household income $90,515, 82.2% white, 6.4% Black, 0.8% Hispanic/Latino, 3.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Grandview Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":8.99,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.59,"nearest_level1_center":"Miami Valley Hospital","nearest_level1_km":11.99,"nearest_level1_miles":7.45,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.215889,39.85025]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-520","properties":{"name":"Casa Grande, AZ","date":"2022-09-04","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 16, Pinal County, Arizona","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.386404037475586,"median_income_tract":63705,"summary":"Sep 4, 2022: 4 killed. Casa Grande, AZ.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nResponding to a 911 call, the police found four dead inside a Casa Grande, AZ home. Richard Wilson, 21, was arrested at the scene and has been charged with fatally stabbing his parents, sister, and niece.\nCensus Tract 16, Pinal County, Arizona (ACS 2017-2021): 16.4% in poverty, median household income $63,705, 40.5% white, 3.4% Black, 53.5% Hispanic/Latino, 8.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Banner Casa Grande Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":14.19,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.82,"nearest_level1_center":"Dignity Community Care","nearest_level1_km":34.94,"nearest_level1_miles":21.71,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.786064,32.992016]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-522","properties":{"name":"Elk Mills, MD","date":"2022-09-09","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 305.01, Cecil County, Maryland","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":3.125,"median_income_tract":89214,"summary":"Sep 9, 2022: 4 killed. Elk Mills, MD.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nResponding to a report of gunshots inside a home, the police found a man shot dead in a detached garage with a semiautomatic handgun near him. They then entered the residence where they found a woman and three children shot in various locations inside the house. The incident is considered a murder-suicide.\nCensus Tract 305.01, Cecil County, Maryland (ACS 2017-2021): 3.1% in poverty, median household income $89,214, 90.4% white, 0.8% Black, 4.8% Hispanic/Latino, 5.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Christiana Care Health Services - Christiana Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":14.64,"nearest_trauma_miles":9.1,"nearest_level1_center":"Christiana Care Health Services - Christiana Hospital","nearest_level1_km":14.64,"nearest_level1_miles":9.1,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-75.836761,39.661091]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-525","properties":{"name":"McGregor, TX","date":"2022-09-29","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 39.02, McLennan County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":10.937078475952148,"median_income_tract":77777,"summary":"Sep 29, 2022: 5 killed. McGregor, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJaimes-Hernandez allegedly shot and killed his wife, her two children plus their two neighbors. He was arrested and is awaiting trial.\nCensus Tract 39.02, McLennan County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 10.9% in poverty, median household income $77,777, 63.6% white, 1.5% Black, 31.8% Hispanic/Latino, 10.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Baylor Scott And White Medical Center - Hillcrest","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":24.34,"nearest_trauma_miles":15.12,"nearest_level1_center":"Baylor Scott And White Medical Center - Temple","nearest_level1_km":39.74,"nearest_level1_miles":24.7,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.40554,31.43305]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-526","properties":{"name":"Dos Palos, CA","date":"2022-10-03","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"Robbery","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 24.01, Merced County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":14.895105361938477,"median_income_tract":41328,"summary":"Oct 3, 2022: 4 killed, 1 injured. Dos Palos, CA.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Robbery · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the Merced County Sheriff, a family of four was robbed and then kidnapped from their place of business--an incident that was reportedly captured on surveillance video. The three adults were subsequently found dead in a remote open field. According to the authorities, the 8-moth-old girl  was left for dead and died from exposure.” Jesus Manuel Salgado was arrested in connection to the incident.\nCensus Tract 24.01, Merced County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 14.9% in poverty, median household income $41,328, 29.0% white, 2.7% Black, 66.4% Hispanic/Latino, 19.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Memorial Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":72.98,"nearest_trauma_miles":45.35,"nearest_level1_center":"Community Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":81.69,"nearest_level1_miles":50.76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-120.600273,37.083092]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-527","properties":{"name":"Ft. Worth, TX","date":"2022-10-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Vehicle","tract":"Census Tract 1046.04, Tarrant County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":26.17604637145996,"median_income_tract":39479,"summary":"Oct 7, 2022: 4 killed. Ft. Worth, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Vehicle · Offenders: 1\nFour people were shot inside a vehicle. Three were dead on the scene, and the fourth died at the hospital. The police say it appeared to be a robbery associated with drug trade.\nCensus Tract 1046.04, Tarrant County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 26.2% in poverty, median household income $39,479, 2.3% white, 53.0% Black, 43.3% Hispanic/Latino, 4.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"John Peter Smith Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":3.6,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.24,"nearest_level1_center":"John Peter Smith Hospital","nearest_level1_km":3.6,"nearest_level1_miles":2.24,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-97.290146,32.717991]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-532","properties":{"name":"Henryetta, OK","date":"2022-10-09","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 9.02, Okmulgee County, Oklahoma","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":22.7418155670166,"median_income_tract":37273,"summary":"Oct 9, 2022: 4 killed. Henryetta, OK.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nFour friends disappeared and their remains were found days later in a river. According to police, they had been shot at a scrapyard before being dismembered and dumped in the river.\nCensus Tract 9.02, Okmulgee County, Oklahoma (ACS 2017-2021): 22.7% in poverty, median household income $37,273, 70.5% white, 0.5% Black, 7.3% Hispanic/Latino, 21.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hillcrest Hospital Henryetta","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":0.42,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.26,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Medical Center Edmond-Er","nearest_level1_km":133.34,"nearest_level1_miles":82.85,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.01152,35.439751]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-528","properties":{"name":"Inman, SC","date":"2022-10-09","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Undetermined","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 228.06, Spartanburg County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":6.995254993438721,"median_income_tract":63081,"summary":"Oct 9, 2022: 5 killed. Inman, SC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFive people living in a South Carolina drug house were found shot to death. James Drayton, who had stayed at the house for a short period of time, was arrested in Georgia in connection to the shooting.\nCensus Tract 228.06, Spartanburg County, South Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 7.0% in poverty, median household income $63,081, 76.3% white, 19.0% Black, 0.3% Hispanic/Latino, 7.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Spartanburg Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":13.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.47,"nearest_level1_center":"Spartanburg Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":13.63,"nearest_level1_miles":8.47,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-82.07473,35.0191]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-529","properties":{"name":"Raleigh, NC","date":"2022-10-13","killed":5,"injured":2,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 541.19, Wake County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":2.708829164505005,"median_income_tract":93198,"summary":"Oct 13, 2022: 5 killed, 2 injured. Raleigh, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nFive people were fatally shot (including an off-duty police officer) and three others were injured. A juvenile, 16-year-old Austin Thompson, was arrested in connection to the crime. The prosecutor is planning to try him as an adult.\nCensus Tract 541.19, Wake County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 2.7% in poverty, median household income $93,198, 39.1% white, 26.3% Black, 14.5% Hispanic/Latino, 5.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Wakemed","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.5,"nearest_level1_center":"Wakemed","nearest_level1_km":5.63,"nearest_level1_miles":3.5,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-78.53672,35.813492]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-546","properties":{"name":"South Fulton, GA","date":"2022-10-17","killed":4,"injured":5,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 105.17, Fulton County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":13.242105484008789,"median_income_tract":65282,"summary":"Oct 17, 2022: 4 killed, 5 injured. South Fulton, GA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFire investigators believe a fatal house fire was intentionally set.Twelve people from two families were inside the home. Eight people escaped the fire, but four of them died. A suspect has not been identified.\nCensus Tract 105.17, Fulton County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 13.2% in poverty, median household income $65,282, 0.7% white, 96.8% Black, 1.9% Hispanic/Latino, 2.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":22.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.77,"nearest_level1_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":22.15,"nearest_level1_miles":13.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.461983,33.56427]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-531","properties":{"name":"Woodbridge, VA","date":"2022-10-17","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9012.03, Prince William County, Virginia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.09877872467041,"median_income_tract":92671,"summary":"Oct 17, 2022: 4 killed. Woodbridge, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nFour people were found shot to death inside a home in Prince William County, VA in what the police characterized as a “domestic related” incident. David Nathaniel Maine Has been arrested and charged with murder.\nCensus Tract 9012.03, Prince William County, Virginia (ACS 2017-2021): 8.1% in poverty, median household income $92,671, 32.8% white, 12.7% Black, 32.5% Hispanic/Latino, 0.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sentara Northern Virginia Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":4.83,"nearest_trauma_miles":3,"nearest_level1_center":"Inova Fairfax Hospital","nearest_level1_km":24.88,"nearest_level1_miles":15.46,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.338631,38.651878]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-533","properties":{"name":"Hartland, WI","date":"2022-10-21","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2036.02, Waukesha County, Wisconsin","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":5.508550643920898,"median_income_tract":106146,"summary":"Oct 21, 2022: 5 killed. Hartland, WI.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAccording to the police, six people found dead in an apartment fire had been shot, one by his own hand.\nCensus Tract 2036.02, Waukesha County, Wisconsin (ACS 2017-2021): 5.5% in poverty, median household income $106,146, 93.5% white, 0.0% Black, 3.6% Hispanic/Latino, 6.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Aurora Medical Center Summit","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":11.78,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.32,"nearest_level1_center":"Childrens Hospital Of Wisconsin","nearest_level1_km":25.5,"nearest_level1_miles":15.84,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-88.328934,43.097118]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-534","properties":{"name":"Broken Arrow, OK","date":"2022-10-27","killed":7,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 74.15, Tulsa County, Oklahoma","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":14.371257781982422,"median_income_tract":68676,"summary":"Oct 27, 2022: 7 killed. Broken Arrow, OK.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nTwo adults and six children were found dead inside a burning home. According to the police, the children had been shot, while the adults are suspected of suicide.\nCensus Tract 74.15, Tulsa County, Oklahoma (ACS 2017-2021): 14.4% in poverty, median household income $68,676, 69.9% white, 1.9% Black, 9.3% Hispanic/Latino, 9.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Ascension St. John Broken Arrow","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":3.34,"nearest_trauma_miles":2.07,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Medical Center Edmond-Er","nearest_level1_km":155.79,"nearest_level1_miles":96.8,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.802597,36.048351]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-535","properties":{"name":"Aurora, CO","date":"2022-10-30","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 72.01, Arapahoe County, Colorado","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":19.971097946166992,"median_income_tract":48675,"summary":"Oct 30, 2022: 4 killed. Aurora, CO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThree men and one woman were found shot to death inside an Aurora, CO home. The police indicated that the assailant was under a restraining order requiring him to stay away from the residence. The assailant’s ex-girlfriend was not home at the time of the shooting. Joseph Mario Castorena was subsequently arrested in Mexico for extradition back to Colorado to face charges.\nCensus Tract 72.01, Arapahoe County, Colorado (ACS 2017-2021): 20.0% in poverty, median household income $48,675, 31.8% white, 12.8% Black, 44.3% Hispanic/Latino, 8.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"University Of Colorado Hospital Authority","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.63,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.64,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Colorado Hospital Authority","nearest_level1_km":2.63,"nearest_level1_miles":1.64,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.868202,39.730141]}}
