{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-541","properties":{"name":"Colorado Springs, CO","date":"2022-11-20","killed":5,"injured":17,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Hate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 1.04, El Paso County, Colorado","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":18.017057418823242,"median_income_tract":55705,"summary":"Nov 20, 2022: 5 killed, 17 injured. Colorado Springs, CO.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Hate · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nFive people were killed and 25 injured at an LGBTQ night club. Anderson Lee Aldrich, 22, has been arrested and charged.\nCensus Tract 1.04, El Paso County, Colorado (ACS 2017-2021): 18.0% in poverty, median household income $55,705, 76.6% white, 0.2% Black, 18.6% Hispanic/Latino, 5.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Centura Health - Penrose - St Franci","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":5.82,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.62,"nearest_level1_center":"University Colo Health Memorial Hospital Central","nearest_level1_km":5.84,"nearest_level1_miles":3.63,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-104.758202,38.881039]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-542","properties":{"name":"Hennessey, OK","date":"2022-11-20","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 9581, Kingfisher County, Oklahoma","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":13.834447860717773,"median_income_tract":46534,"summary":"Nov 20, 2022: 4 killed, 1 injured. Hennessey, OK.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nDeputies responding to reports of a hostage situation and shooting at a marijuana growing facility found four people dead and one injured. Wu Chen has been charged in the murders.\nCensus Tract 9581, Kingfisher County, Oklahoma (ACS 2017-2021): 13.8% in poverty, median household income $46,534, 72.5% white, 0.4% Black, 22.7% Hispanic/Latino, 19.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Okeene Municipal Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":20.31,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.62,"nearest_level1_center":"Ou Medical Center Edmond-Er","nearest_level1_km":78.39,"nearest_level1_miles":48.71,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-98.091248,36.141232]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-543","properties":{"name":"Chesapeake, VA","date":"2022-11-22","killed":6,"injured":6,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 210.10, Chesapeake city, Virginia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":1.397868275642395,"median_income_tract":111907,"summary":"Nov 22, 2022: 6 killed, 6 injured. Chesapeake, VA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nA gunman, an employee of the Chesapeake Walmart, opened fire in the store shortly before closing, killing six and wounding four others. According to the police, the shooting occurred in the break room and victimized the assailant’s co-workers. The assailant died apparently by suicide.\nCensus Tract 210.10, Chesapeake city, Virginia (ACS 2017-2021): 1.4% in poverty, median household income $111,907, 87.4% white, 3.3% Black, 1.1% Hispanic/Latino, 8.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Sentara Norfolk General Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":17.68,"nearest_trauma_miles":10.98,"nearest_level1_center":"Sentara Norfolk General Hospital","nearest_level1_km":17.68,"nearest_level1_miles":10.98,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-76.255058,36.707878]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-544","properties":{"name":"Buffalo Grove, IL","date":"2022-11-30","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Stabbing","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 8645.12, Lake County, Illinois","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":0.8179959058761597,"median_income_tract":187500,"summary":"Nov 30, 2022: 4 killed. Buffalo Grove, IL.\nCause: Stabbing · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA man killed his wife, who had filed for divorce, their two children and his mother before taking his own life. There has been a history of domestic violence leading up to the murder-suicide.\nCensus Tract 8645.12, Lake County, Illinois (ACS 2017-2021): 0.8% in poverty, median household income $187,500, 59.1% white, 0.4% Black, 8.3% Hispanic/Latino, 1.3% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Advocate Condell Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":8.52,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.29,"nearest_level1_center":"Advocate Condell Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":8.52,"nearest_level1_miles":5.29,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.97934,42.199348]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-547","properties":{"name":"Enoch, UT","date":"2023-01-04","killed":7,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1102.02, Iron County, Utah","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":7.171555042266846,"median_income_tract":61250,"summary":"Jan 4, 2023: 7 killed. Enoch, UT.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nCarrying out a welfare check, the police discovered eight family members—three adults and five children—shot to death. It has been considered a murder-suicide.\nCensus Tract 1102.02, Iron County, Utah (ACS 2017-2021): 7.2% in poverty, median household income $61,250, 89.6% white, 0.1% Black, 7.0% Hispanic/Latino, 3.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Cedar City Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level IV","nearest_trauma_km":8.75,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.44,"nearest_level1_center":"University Medical Center Of Southern Nevada","nearest_level1_km":261.69,"nearest_level1_miles":162.61,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-113.016983,37.767979]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-548","properties":{"name":"High Point, NC","date":"2023-01-07","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Despondency","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 163.06, Guilford County, North Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.410003662109375,"median_income_tract":49077,"summary":"Jan 7, 2023: 4 killed. High Point, NC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Despondency · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nResponding to cries for help, the police broke into a home and found two adults and three children dead inside. The police are considering it a murder-suicide.\nCensus Tract 163.06, Guilford County, North Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 12.4% in poverty, median household income $49,077, 61.4% white, 26.1% Black, 5.2% Hispanic/Latino, 3.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Cone Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":19.33,"nearest_trauma_miles":12.01,"nearest_level1_center":"North Carolina Baptist Hospital","nearest_level1_km":27.7,"nearest_level1_miles":17.21,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-79.976448,36.00943]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-549","properties":{"name":"Cleveland, OH","date":"2023-01-13","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 1054, Cuyahoga County, Ohio","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":44.019412994384766,"median_income_tract":26552,"summary":"Jan 13, 2023: 4 killed, 1 injured. Cleveland, OH.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMartin Muniz was arrested ad charged with killing his step-father, sister, nephew, as well as a friend of his sister. Another victim was shot but survived.\nCensus Tract 1054, Cuyahoga County, Ohio (ACS 2017-2021): 44.0% in poverty, median household income $26,552, 41.3% white, 24.4% Black, 32.9% Hispanic/Latino, 17.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Metrohealth Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":1.33,"nearest_trauma_miles":0.83,"nearest_level1_center":"Metrohealth Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":1.33,"nearest_level1_miles":0.83,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-81.709778,41.453129]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-550","properties":{"name":"Goshen, CA","date":"2023-01-16","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Drug trade","incident_type":"Suspected felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9.01, Tulare County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":20.467275619506836,"median_income_tract":54048,"summary":"Jan 16, 2023: 6 killed. Goshen, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Suspected felony · Circumstance: Drug trade · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nSix people were fatally shot inside and outside a residence. The two suspects who were arrested two weeks later were known members of the Norteño gang The police believe that the shooting was the likely result of a conflict with members of the Sureños, a rival gang.\nCensus Tract 9.01, Tulare County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 20.5% in poverty, median household income $54,048, 10.0% white, 0.0% Black, 81.2% Hispanic/Latino, 1.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Kaweah Health Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":11.5,"nearest_trauma_miles":7.14,"nearest_level1_center":"Community Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":54.87,"nearest_level1_miles":34.1,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-119.421402,36.346291]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-551","properties":{"name":"Monterey Park, CA","date":"2023-01-21","killed":11,"injured":9,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 4822.01, Los Angeles County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":14.969584465026855,"median_income_tract":54141,"summary":"Jan 21, 2023: 11 killed, 9 injured. Monterey Park, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 1\nA gunman opened fire at a ballroom dance studio during a Chinese Lunar New Year celebration. The assailant, identified as Huu Can Tran, 72, then killed himself during a stand-off with the police.\nCensus Tract 4822.01, Los Angeles County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 15.0% in poverty, median household income $54,141, 2.9% white, 2.5% Black, 20.5% Hispanic/Latino, 7.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lac Usc Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":7.82,"nearest_trauma_miles":4.86,"nearest_level1_center":"Lac Usc Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":7.82,"nearest_level1_miles":4.86,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-118.123543,34.06197]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-552","properties":{"name":"Half Moon Bay, CA","date":"2023-01-23","killed":7,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 6137.02, San Mateo County, California","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.542281150817871,"median_income_tract":106667,"summary":"Jan 23, 2023: 7 killed, 1 injured. Half Moon Bay, CA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nSeven people were killed in two related shootings at a mushroom farm and a trucking firm in Half Moon Bay, California. A suspect—66-year-old Chunli Zhao—then drove to a police substation to surrender.\nCensus Tract 6137.02, San Mateo County, California (ACS 2017-2021): 9.5% in poverty, median household income $106,667, 48.7% white, 0.3% Black, 46.3% Hispanic/Latino, 7.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Lucile Salter Packard Children'S Hospital Stanford","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":21.74,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.51,"nearest_level1_center":"Lucile Salter Packard Children'S Hospital Stanford","nearest_level1_km":21.74,"nearest_level1_miles":13.51,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-122.41803,37.469711]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-574","properties":{"name":"Luttrell, TN","date":"2023-01-29","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 401.01, Union County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":16.65817642211914,"median_income_tract":46570,"summary":"Jan 29, 2023: 4 killed. Luttrell, TN.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nCharles Damon Aljumaily, 52, shot four children and then set fire to the house before taking his own life.\nCensus Tract 401.01, Union County, Tennessee (ACS 2017-2021): 16.7% in poverty, median household income $46,570, 96.3% white, 0.0% Black, 3.2% Hispanic/Latino, 16.9% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"The University Of Tennessee Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":37.32,"nearest_trauma_miles":23.19,"nearest_level1_center":"The University Of Tennessee Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":37.32,"nearest_level1_miles":23.19,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-83.7239,36.22514]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-553","properties":{"name":"Arkabutla, MS","date":"2023-02-17","killed":6,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 9503.01, Tate County, Mississippi","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":24.620573043823242,"median_income_tract":48491,"summary":"Feb 17, 2023: 6 killed, 1 injured. Arkabutla, MS.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nRichard Dale Crum, 52, allegedly shot to death his ex-wife and five others at two residences and outside a store in Arkabutla, MS. Crum was arrested and charged with murder.\nCensus Tract 9503.01, Tate County, Mississippi (ACS 2017-2021): 24.6% in poverty, median household income $48,491, 50.5% white, 44.3% Black, 0.7% Hispanic/Latino, 10.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Baptist Memorial Hospital - Desoto","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":28.39,"nearest_trauma_miles":17.64,"nearest_level1_center":"Methodist Healthcare - Memphis Hospitals","nearest_level1_km":45.41,"nearest_level1_miles":28.21,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-90.129356,34.738392]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-554","properties":{"name":"Daphne, AL","date":"2023-02-22","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Stabbing","situation":"","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 107.04, Baldwin County, Alabama","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.821428298950195,"median_income_tract":76154,"summary":"Feb 22, 2023: 4 killed. Daphne, AL.\nCause: Shooting, Stabbing · Type: Family · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThe police were called to investigate a shooting at an home in Daphne, AL. They found one person dead inside the home and three dead in the backyard. Tarant Smith-Bracy, 21, was arrested in connection to the shooting and stabbing deaths of four family members.\nCensus Tract 107.04, Baldwin County, Alabama (ACS 2017-2021): 9.8% in poverty, median household income $76,154, 87.4% white, 7.2% Black, 2.2% Hispanic/Latino, 4.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Thomas Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":14.42,"nearest_trauma_miles":8.96,"nearest_level1_center":"Usa Health University Hospital","nearest_level1_km":22.78,"nearest_level1_miles":14.15,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-87.870461,30.647551]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-555","properties":{"name":"Cocoa, FL","date":"2023-03-01","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 621.13, Brevard County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.045791625976562,"median_income_tract":73986,"summary":"Mar 1, 2023: 4 killed. Cocoa, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nResponding to a 911 call, Sheriff's deputies discovered four victims shot to death and two minor children who were unharmed. Domenico Gigante, who was the ex-boyfriend of one of the victims and the father of another, was arrested and charged with four counts of murder.\nCensus Tract 621.13, Brevard County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 8.0% in poverty, median household income $73,986, 73.4% white, 13.3% Black, 4.8% Hispanic/Latino, 12.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Holmes Regional Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":40.27,"nearest_trauma_miles":25.02,"nearest_level1_center":"Orlando Health Orlando Regional Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":58.23,"nearest_level1_miles":36.18,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.795662,28.412281]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-556","properties":{"name":"Miami Lakes, FL","date":"2023-03-10","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 128.01, Miami-Dade County, Florida","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":8.192155838012695,"median_income_tract":76136,"summary":"Mar 10, 2023: 4 killed. Miami Lakes, FL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nPerforming a welfare check, the police found three women and two men dead in an apparent murder-suicide\nCensus Tract 128.01, Miami-Dade County, Florida (ACS 2017-2021): 8.2% in poverty, median household income $76,136, 2.5% white, 0.1% Black, 97.4% Hispanic/Latino, 4.1% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Jackson Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":18.12,"nearest_trauma_miles":11.26,"nearest_level1_center":"Jackson Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":18.12,"nearest_level1_miles":11.26,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.341049,25.907949]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-557","properties":{"name":"Dallas, TX","date":"2023-03-12","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":2,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 204.02, Dallas County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":23.102367401123047,"median_income_tract":85608,"summary":"Mar 12, 2023: 4 killed. Dallas, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Location: Residence · Offenders: 2\nResponding to a report of gunfire, the police found four people shot dead inside an apartment building. Reportedly the shooting arouse out of a custody dispute between one of the alleged assailants and one of the victims. A child was also found in the apartment who was unharmed.\nCensus Tract 204.02, Dallas County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 23.1% in poverty, median household income $85,608, 47.2% white, 26.8% Black, 19.3% Hispanic/Latino, 16.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Baylor University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":2.12,"nearest_trauma_miles":1.32,"nearest_level1_center":"Baylor University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":2.12,"nearest_level1_miles":1.32,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-96.796997,32.776699]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-558","properties":{"name":"Birmingham/Ragland, AL","date":"2023-03-14","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Undetermined","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 21, Jefferson County, Alabama","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":29.08622932434082,"median_income_tract":26394,"summary":"Mar 14, 2023: 4 killed. Birmingham/Ragland, AL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Undetermined · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nThe police in Alabama arrested Daniel P. Watson, 28, for suspicion of committing two double homicides on the same day, one in Birmingham and the other in Ragland.\nCensus Tract 21, Jefferson County, Alabama (ACS 2017-2021): 29.1% in poverty, median household income $26,394, 22.4% white, 75.3% Black, 1.8% Hispanic/Latino, 25.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Vincent'S East","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":4.99,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.1,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Alabama Hospital","nearest_level1_km":11.03,"nearest_level1_miles":6.85,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.708633,33.567032]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-559","properties":{"name":"Sumter, SC","date":"2023-03-21","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 17.01, Sumter County, South Carolina","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":4.692597389221191,"median_income_tract":79010,"summary":"Mar 21, 2023: 4 killed. Sumter, SC.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nAletha Holliday was in her backyard of her home with a co-worker when her ex-husband, Charles Slacks, Jr., entered the home using a key, walked outside and fatally shot Holiday’s coworker. Slacks then went back inside and began to go upstairs, where his two sons and step-daughter were sleeping. Despite Holiday’s efforts to stop him, Slacks proceeded up the stairs where he shot the three children to death. Slacks then took his own life.\nCensus Tract 17.01, Sumter County, South Carolina (ACS 2017-2021): 4.7% in poverty, median household income $79,010, 69.8% white, 15.0% Black, 7.3% Hispanic/Latino, 1.6% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Regional Medical Center Of Orangeburg And Calhoun Counties","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":57.97,"nearest_trauma_miles":36.02,"nearest_level1_center":"Prisma Health Richland","nearest_level1_km":59.41,"nearest_level1_miles":36.92,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-80.402,33.920799]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-560","properties":{"name":"Nashville, TN","date":"2023-03-27","killed":6,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"School","tract":"Census Tract 179.02, Davidson County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":4.087797164916992,"median_income_tract":116534,"summary":"Mar 27, 2023: 6 killed. Nashville, TN.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Location: School · Offenders: 1\nA woman opened fire at a private religious elementary school, killing three adults and three children. She was killed during an exchange of fire with the police.\nCensus Tract 179.02, Davidson County, Tennessee (ACS 2017-2021): 4.1% in poverty, median household income $116,534, 77.2% white, 1.9% Black, 0.9% Hispanic/Latino, 5.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Vanderbilt University Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.71,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.55,"nearest_level1_center":"Vanderbilt University Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.71,"nearest_level1_miles":3.55,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-86.825897,36.093201]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-572","properties":{"name":"Monroe, LA","date":"2023-03-31","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Arson","incident_type":"Felony","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 106.05, Ouachita Parish, Louisiana","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":40.437957763671875,"median_income_tract":31197,"summary":"Mar 31, 2023: 4 killed. Monroe, LA.\nCause: Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Felony · Circumstance: Arson · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nMichael Jarrod Cooper Was arrested and charged with murder for allegedly setting fire that killed four people.\nCensus Tract 106.05, Ouachita Parish, Louisiana (ACS 2017-2021): 40.4% in poverty, median household income $31,197, 22.2% white, 74.9% Black, 2.5% Hispanic/Latino, 26.2% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"St. Francis Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":8.35,"nearest_trauma_miles":5.19,"nearest_level1_center":"Ochsner Lsu Health Shreveport","nearest_level1_km":160.34,"nearest_level1_miles":99.63,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-92.0531,32.44551]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-561","properties":{"name":"Louisville, KY","date":"2023-04-10","killed":5,"injured":8,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Employment grievance","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Commercial/Retail","tract":"Census Tract 7526.01, Frederick County, Maryland","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":3.4894192218780518,"median_income_tract":130875,"summary":"Apr 10, 2023: 5 killed, 8 injured. Louisville, KY.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Employment grievance · Location: Commercial/Retail · Offenders: 1\nFour people were killed and nine others were injured inside a bank by a employee. The assailant was killed during the confrontation with the police.\nCensus Tract 7526.01, Frederick County, Maryland (ACS 2017-2021): 3.5% in poverty, median household income $130,875, 81.9% white, 0.9% Black, 0.9% Hispanic/Latino, 4.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Meritus Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":23.67,"nearest_trauma_miles":14.71,"nearest_level1_center":"Inova Fairfax Hospital","nearest_level1_km":70.12,"nearest_level1_miles":43.57,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-77.536713,39.441448]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-562","properties":{"name":"Dadeville, AL","date":"2023-04-15","killed":4,"injured":32,"offenders":6,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Bar/Club/Restaurant","tract":"Census Tract 9624, Tallapoosa County, Alabama","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":24.052841186523438,"median_income_tract":32500,"summary":"Apr 15, 2023: 4 killed, 32 injured. Dadeville, AL.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Location: Bar/Club/Restaurant · Offenders: 6\nTwo brothers and a third person have been charged with fatally shooting four victims and injuring as many as 32 others during a \"\"Sweet 16\"\" birthday party inside the Mahogany Masterpiece dance studio.\nCensus Tract 9624, Tallapoosa County, Alabama (ACS 2017-2021): 24.1% in poverty, median household income $32,500, 57.1% white, 39.5% Black, 1.0% Hispanic/Latino, 17.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Russell Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":22.15,"nearest_trauma_miles":13.76,"nearest_level1_center":"University Of Alabama Hospital","nearest_level1_km":122.31,"nearest_level1_miles":76,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.763397,32.83173]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-563","properties":{"name":"Bowdoin, ME","date":"2023-04-18","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9702, Sagadahoc County, Maine","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":9.548554420471191,"median_income_tract":78458,"summary":"Apr 18, 2023: 4 killed, 3 injured. Bowdoin, ME.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nJoseph Eaton, 34, was arrested after he allegedly shot and killed his parents and two of their friends in a Bowdoin, ME residence and then fired at vehicles on Interstate 95 in Yarmouth, injuring three people.\nCensus Tract 9702, Sagadahoc County, Maine (ACS 2017-2021): 9.5% in poverty, median household income $78,458, 91.8% white, 0.5% Black, 4.6% Hispanic/Latino, 5.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Central Maine Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":24.99,"nearest_trauma_miles":15.53,"nearest_level1_center":"Maine Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":57.66,"nearest_level1_miles":35.83,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-69.901711,44.09581]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-564","properties":{"name":"Cleveland, TX","date":"2023-04-28","killed":5,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 2001.06, San Jacinto County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":25.087583541870117,"median_income_tract":49444,"summary":"Apr 28, 2023: 5 killed. Cleveland, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA Texas man went next door with a AR-style rifle and began shooting his neighbors, killing five inside the house. According to the authorities, this occurred after the family asked him to stop firing rounds in his yard because they were trying to sleep. After several days on the run, Francisco Oropeza, 38, was arrested a charged in connection to the murders.\nCensus Tract 2001.06, San Jacinto County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 25.1% in poverty, median household income $49,444, 61.5% white, 12.5% Black, 26.1% Hispanic/Latino, 19.8% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Hca Houston Healthcare Conroe","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":28.73,"nearest_trauma_miles":17.85,"nearest_level1_center":"Memorial Hermann - Texas Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":74.89,"nearest_level1_miles":46.54,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-95.182457,30.36216]}}
