{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-575","properties":{"name":"Nash, TX","date":"2023-05-23","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Other","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 109.05, Bowie County, Texas","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":17.291889190673828,"median_income_tract":55344,"summary":"May 23, 2023: 4 killed. Nash, TX.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Family · Circumstance: Other · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nCesar Olalde, 19, has been charged with fatally shooting four family members. Reportedly, he thought his family members were cannibals and would eat him.\nCensus Tract 109.05, Bowie County, Texas (ACS 2017-2021): 17.3% in poverty, median household income $55,344, 38.8% white, 49.6% Black, 10.4% Hispanic/Latino, 14.5% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Christus St Michael Health System","nearest_trauma_level":"Level III","nearest_trauma_km":5.84,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.63,"nearest_level1_center":"Ochsner Lsu Health Shreveport","nearest_level1_km":112.41,"nearest_level1_miles":69.85,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-94.13284,33.44246]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-576","properties":{"name":"Mesa, AZ","date":"2023-05-27","killed":4,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Multiple","tract":"Census Tract 4214, Maricopa County, Arizona","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":20.16640281677246,"median_income_tract":28750,"summary":"May 27, 2023: 4 killed, 1 injured. Mesa, AZ.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Location: Multiple · Offenders: 1\nIren Byers, 20, is charged with killing four people and injuring another in a series of shootings in Phoenix (one killed) and Mesa (three killed).\nCensus Tract 4214, Maricopa County, Arizona (ACS 2017-2021): 20.2% in poverty, median household income $28,750, 63.7% white, 4.6% Black, 28.3% Hispanic/Latino, 11.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Banner Desert Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":5.57,"nearest_trauma_miles":3.46,"nearest_level1_center":"Banner Desert Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":5.57,"nearest_level1_miles":3.46,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-111.82608,33.415184]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-578","properties":{"name":"Sequatchie, TN","date":"2023-06-15","killed":5,"injured":1,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns","situation":"Family issue","incident_type":"Family","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 502.03, Marion County, Tennessee","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":19.182270050048828,"median_income_tract":60284,"summary":"Jun 15, 2023: 5 killed, 1 injured. Sequatchie, TN.\nCause: Shooting, Smoke inhalation & burns · Type: Family · Circumstance: Family issue · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nGary Don Barnett killed his estranged wife, her daughter, two of their grandchildren, and another child. He also set fire to the house and then took his own life. A sixth victim was shot three times but survived.\nCensus Tract 502.03, Marion County, Tennessee (ACS 2017-2021): 19.2% in poverty, median household income $60,284, 93.6% white, 2.4% Black, 0.0% Hispanic/Latino, 12.7% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Erlanger Medical Center","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":29.18,"nearest_trauma_miles":18.13,"nearest_level1_center":"Erlanger Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":29.18,"nearest_level1_miles":18.13,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-85.60012,35.11575]}}
{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-577","properties":{"name":" Kellogg, ID","date":"2023-06-18","killed":4,"injured":0,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Interpersonal conflict","incident_type":"Other","location_type":"Residence","tract":"Census Tract 9603, Shoshone County, Idaho","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":15.14262866973877,"median_income_tract":35613,"summary":"Jun 18, 2023: 4 killed.  Kellogg, ID.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Other · Circumstance: Interpersonal conflict · Location: Residence · Offenders: 1\nA 31-year-old man has been arrested in connection with the fatal shooting of his neighbors. Reportedly, the incident follows longstanding conflict between the parties. However, the precipitant, according to the police, is that Kaylor was upset that the neighbor’s 18-year-old son had reportedly exposed himself to the man’s children.\nCensus Tract 9603, Shoshone County, Idaho (ACS 2017-2021): 15.1% in poverty, median household income $35,613, 90.4% white, 1.3% Black, 3.7% Hispanic/Latino, 20.4% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Kootenai Health","nearest_trauma_level":"Level II","nearest_trauma_km":52.66,"nearest_trauma_miles":32.72,"nearest_level1_center":"Uw Medicine - Harborview Medical Center","nearest_level1_km":464.73,"nearest_level1_miles":288.77,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-116.12796,47.54417]}}
