{"type":"Feature","id":"mkdb-581","properties":{"name":"Hampton, GA","date":"2023-07-15","killed":4,"injured":3,"offenders":1,"weapon":"Shooting","situation":"Indiscriminate","incident_type":"Public","location_type":"Open space","tract":"Census Tract 705.05, Henry County, Georgia","acs_period":"2017-2021","pct_poverty_tract":12.407940864562988,"median_income_tract":71601,"summary":"Jul 15, 2023: 4 killed, 3 injured. Hampton, GA.\nCause: Shooting · Type: Public · Circumstance: Indiscriminate · Location: Open space · Offenders: 1\nLongmore, 40, fatally shot four of his neighbors. A day later, while on the run, he was killed in a shootout with the police during which three officers were injured.\nCensus Tract 705.05, Henry County, Georgia (ACS 2017-2021): 12.4% in poverty, median household income $71,601, 52.0% white, 45.3% Black, 1.2% Hispanic/Latino, 11.0% vacant housing.","nearest_trauma_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_trauma_level":"Level I","nearest_trauma_km":42.06,"nearest_trauma_miles":26.14,"nearest_level1_center":"Grady Memorial Hospital","nearest_level1_km":42.06,"nearest_level1_miles":26.14,"source_note":"Mass Killing Database (MKDB), 2006–2023: incidents with 4 or more killed; tract context from ACS 5-year estimates."},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-84.26608,33.38619]}}
